E["item:admiral-proudmoore-s-orders"] = {t="item",n="Admiral Proudmoore's Orders",z="durotar",s="Admiral Proudmoore's Orders are written battle plans recovered from Kul Tiras forces entrenching themselves along the coastline of Durotar. Penned before the Grand Admiral's defeat at Theramore, the documents outline persistent military strategies that continue to threaten the nascent orc homeland.",h="Admiral Proudmoore's Orders are written battle plans recovered from Kul Tiras forces entrenching themselves...",sec={{t="A Legacy of Hatred",b="Even after the death of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore at Theramore, his expeditionary forces refuse to yield. Recovered from Lieutenant Benedict's garrison at Tiragarde Keep, these tactical directives detail long-term maneuvers and fortifications designed to undermine the Horde. The orders prove that the Grand Admiral's offensive in Durotar was no hasty raid, but an organized campaign structured to endure long past his own demise. For the Horde, the recovered documents offer vital insight into Kul Tiras operations and potential reinforcements threatening their borders.",sp=0},{t="Delivery to Grommash Hold",b="Recognizing the strategic danger outlined in the plans, Horde scouts dispatch the recovered papers directly to Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar. Delivered to chieftain Vol'jin, who serves as counselor to Warchief Thrall, the orders confirm the Darkspear leader's persistent suspicion that human aggression remains an active peril. The intelligence urges the Horde leadership to prepare for further incursions along the coast.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What are Admiral Proudmoore's Orders?",a="They are military directives drawn up by Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore before his fall at Theramore. They direct the remaining Kul Tiras soldiers in Durotar to fortify coastal footholds and wage war against the Horde.",al={"proudmoores orders","what are the orders","admirals orders item"},it="identity"},{q="Where were these orders recovered?",a="The orders are secured in Durotar during the ongoing struggle against the Kul Tiras remnants stationed at Tiragarde Keep, near the southeastern coast.",al={"where do i find the orders","orders location","who drops the orders"},it="origin"},{q="Who needs to see these orders?",a="They are brought to the Darkspear chieftain Vol'jin, who resides inside Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar's Valley of Wisdom alongside Warchief Thrall.",al={"who do i turn this into","who wants the orders","orders hand in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why are Kul Tiras soldiers still fighting in Durotar?",a="Though Admiral Proudmoore fell in battle, his subordinates, such as Lieutenant Benedict, remained devoted to his mission to exterminate the orcs. The orders provided pre-planned strategies for the garrison to continue harassing Durotar even without the Grand Admiral's direct oversight.",al={"why are humans in durotar","why tiragarde keep hostile","daelin dead why fight"},it="history"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="These documents vindicate those in the Horde who argued human truces would never last, demonstrating that Kul Tiras forces intended to wage a war of extermination from the moment they made landfall.",["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear trolls, these orders are handed straight to their chieftain, Vol'jin, confirming his long-held counsel to Thrall that human presence along the coast remains an immediate danger."},kw={"benedict","durotar","kul tiras","orders","orgrimmar","proudmoore","tiragarde","vol'jin"},rel={"quest:830","npc:vol-jin","zone:durotar","subzone:grommash-hold","zone:orgrimmar","npc:thrall","topic:horde","topic:human"},src={"Admiral Proudmoore's Orders","The Admiral's Orders (2)"}}
E["item:burning-blade-medallion"] = {t="item",n="Burning Blade Medallion",z="durotar",s="The Burning Blade Medallion is a dark talisman carried by cultists lurking within the Valley of Trials. Guarded by dark magic in the depths of the Burning Blade Coven, it serves as direct proof of demonic corruption attempting to subvert the young warriors of Durotar.",h="The Burning Blade Medallion is a dark talisman carried by cultists lurking within the Valley of Trials.",sec={{t="A Mark of Corruption",b="Discovered deep inside the winding caverns of the Burning Blade Coven, the medallion is held by Yarrog Baneshadow, an agent of the sinister Burning Blade cult. Identified through the divinations of Zureetha Fargaze, the trinket channels dark power amidst the cult's impish familiars and felstalkers. Striking down its bearer and seizing the medallion cuts short an insidious attempt to undermine the Horde's training grounds from within Durotar itself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Burning Blade Medallion?",a="It is a magical talisman carried by Yarrog Baneshadow, an operative of the Burning Blade cult hiding within Durotar. The medallion serves as a focus of dark magic and a badge of allegiance among the cultists.",al={"burning blade talisman","coven medallion","yarrog's medallion"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants the medallion retrieved?",a="Zureetha Fargaze, an orc seer stationed outside the Den in the Valley of Trials, seeks the medallion to root out demonic influence and study the cult's local machinations.",al={"who takes the medallion","where do i turn in the medallion","zureetha fargaze quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the medallion found?",a="It is held deep inside the Burning Blade Coven, a hidden cave located northwest of the Den in the Valley of Trials. It is guarded by Yarrog Baneshadow, who lurks along the cave's upper ledges.",al={"where is yarrog baneshadow","burning blade medallion location","how to find the medallion"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does the medallion's presence mean for Durotar?",a="Its discovery confirms that the Burning Blade cult has slipped operatives right into the Horde's proving grounds, signaling that the cultists have far broader and more dangerous ambitions across the orcish homeland.",al={"why are cultists in valley of trials","is burning blade in durotar"},it="threat"}},ang={["race:Orc"]="The medallion represents the lingering shadow of the demonic corruption that once enslaved the orcish race, now threatening young initiates before they even leave the Valley of Trials.",["class:Warlock"]="While dark magic is practiced by Horde warlocks under strict discipline, the medallion represents the rogue, unbound fel craft of the Burning Blade, which threatens the stability of Durotar."},kw={"burning blade coven","burning blade medallion","durotar","felstalker","talisman","valley of trials","yarrog baneshadow","zureetha fargaze"},rel={"npc:zureetha-fargaze","quest:794","subzone:burning-blade-coven","subzone:valley-of-trials","quest:1089","quest:792","zone:durotar"},src={"Burning Blade Medallion","Burning Blade Medallion (Classic)"}}
E["item:cactus-apple"] = {t="item",n="Cactus Apple",z="durotar",s="Cactus Apples are tough, moisture-rich fruits harvested from the rugged flora of Durotar's Valley of Trials. Flourishing in the arid desert heat, they are prized by local orcs as a rare, refreshing source of sustenance.",h="Cactus Apples are tough, moisture-rich fruits harvested from the rugged flora of Durotar's Valley of Trials.",sec={{t="Desert Harvest",b="The sun-scorched earth of Durotar offers little luxury, forcing its inhabitants to make use of whatever hardy plants survive the elements. Cactus apples grow in clusters around the thick cactuses dotting the Valley of Trials. While difficult to gather without catching a few thorns, the fruit provides vital hydration in the sweltering canyon. A local orc named Galgar gathers these fruits to prepare his signature Cactus Apple Surprise, a cooling confection that brings welcome relief to recruits enduring their harsh initial training.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do cactus apples grow?",a="They grow wild across the red dust of the Valley of Trials in southern Durotar, typically resting at the bases of the stout cactus plants scattered through the basin.",al={"cactus apple locations","where to find cactus apple","cactus apple spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Cactus Apple Surprise?",a="It is a chilled, refreshing dish prepared by the Valley of Trials local Galgar. Using freshly gathered cactus apples, he cooks a sweet snack that provides instant relief from Durotar's punishing desert heat.",al={"what is galgars surprise","cactus apple recipe","galgar treat"},it="purpose"},{q="Who asks for these apples?",a="Galgar, an orc stationed in the Valley of Trials, trades portions of his cooling dessert to any young recruit willing to venture out and bring back six fresh apples.",al={"cactus apple quest giver","who wants cactus apples","galgar apples"},it="motive",gp=true},{q="What is a Cactus Apple?",a="A Cactus Apple is a crisp, refreshing wild fruit found flourishing beneath the thorny cactuses of the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Despite the harsh, arid conditions of the orcish homeland, these resilient plants produce succulent fruit that offers much-needed hydration and nourishment under the scorching desert sun.",al={"what is cactus apple","cactus apple lore","what are cactus apples"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where do Cactus Apples come from?",a="Cactus Apples are native desert fruits that grow naturally at the base of cacti scattered across Durotar's Valley of Trials. They are not crafted or cultivated by any single person, but rather sprout directly from the resilient flora adapted to the red canyons and dry climate of the region.",al={"where do cactus apples come from","cactus apple origin","who made cactus apples"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does Galgar want Cactus Apples?",a="Galgar gathers them to whip up batches of his famous Cactus Apple Surprise. The sweltering heat of the Valley of Trials takes a heavy toll on new recruits and seasoned warriors alike, and the sweet, cooling dessert made from these apples offers vital refreshment against the brutal midday sun.",al={"why gather cactus apples","why does galgar want cactus apples","cactus apple purpose"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="For wilderness cooks surviving in Durotar, harvesting desert cactuses is a prime lesson in turning prickly, inhospitable desert vegetation into a hydrating meal.",["race:Orc"]="Young orcs undergoing trials in Durotar quickly learn that enduring the red canyon means taking advantage of every scarce scrap of moisture nature offers."},kw={"cactus apple","cactus apple surprise","desert fruit","durotar","galgar","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:galgar-s-cactus-apple-surprise","npc:galgar","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar"},src={"Cactus Apple","Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise"}}
E["item:canvas-scraps"] = {t="item",n="Canvas Scraps",z="durotar",s="Canvas Scraps are remnants of tough woven fabric carried by human invaders and centaur tribes encroaching upon Durotar. In Razor Hill, aging veteran Furl Scornbrow collects these salvaged swatches to stitch useful travel sacks for fresh Horde recruits.",h="Canvas Scraps are remnants of tough woven fabric carried by human invaders and centaur tribes encroaching...",sec={{t="Trophies of Durotar's Enemies",b="Canvas is not a fabric native to the rough hide-working traditions of the Orcs, but it is abundant among Durotar's enemies. The Kul Tiras marines and sailors entrenched along the eastern shoreline carry heavy canvas gear and sailcloth remnants from their naval excursions. Further inland, the roaming Kolkar centaur repurpose scraps of coarse cloth looted from supply caravans and past conflicts. Defeating these hostiles yields durable remnants that can be salvaged from their camps and gear.",sp=0},{t="A Veteran's Craft",b="Perched atop the Razor Hill watchtower, veteran Furl Scornbrow keeps an eye out for invaders while turning his hands to useful labor. Though past his fighting prime, the old warrior repurposes salvaged enemy fabric into sturdy carrying bags for younger soldiers. By turning the materials of Kul Tiras and the Kolkar against them, Furl equips the new generation of defenders fighting to secure the Horde's borders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do Canvas Scraps come from?",a="They are recovered from human and centaur foes across Durotar. You can take them from the Kul Tiras forces occupying Tiragarde Keep and the eastern shore, or from Kolkar centaur drudges and outrunners prowling near their inland camps.",al={"who drops canvas scraps","where to get canvas scraps","canvas scraps farm"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Furl Scornbrow want these scraps?",a="Furl Scornbrow is an aging Orc veteran stationed in the Razor Hill watchtower who can no longer fight on the front lines. To remain useful to the Horde, he uses the salvaged cloth to sew practical traveling sacks for young adventurers.",al={"who needs canvas scraps","what are canvas scraps used for","furl scornbrow canvas"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why do the Kul Tiras troops and centaur carry canvas?",a="The Kul Tiras expedition arrived in Durotar aboard warships and maintains seaside encampments, making sailcloth and woven canvas everyday essentials. The Kolkar centaur acquire similar coarse fabrics by raiding caravans, scavenging coastlines, and plundering travelers crossing the arid plains.",al={"why do centaur have canvas","human canvas scraps lore"}},{q="What are Canvas Scraps?",a="Canvas Scraps are pieces of heavy, woven fabric salvaged from the camps and gear of enemies across Durotar. Tougher than simple linen, canvas is widely used for heavy-duty military equipment, sails, and rugged tents. While scraps like these might look like mere refuse on the battlefield, their durable fibers can easily be repurposed by a skilled tailor or craftsman into practical supplies, such as sturdy carrying bags for warriors on the march.",al={"what are canvas scraps","canvas scrap item","what is canvas scraps"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Every salvaged scrap taken from Kul Tiras invaders or Kolkar raiders helps supply new defenders answering Thrall's call across Durotar.",["profession:Tailoring"]="While simple woven canvas is primarily gathered as raw salvage by warriors, it serves as a rugged foundation for crafting utilitarian bags in the harsh desert."},kw={"canvas scraps","carry your weight","durotar","furl scornbrow","kolkar","kul tiras","razor hill"},rel={"quest:791","npc:furl-scornbrow","subzone:razor-hill-watchtower","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:kul-tiras","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},src={"Canvas Scraps","Carry Your Weight"}}
E["item:durotar-tiger-fur"] = {t="item",n="Durotar Tiger Fur",z="durotar",s="Durotar Tiger Fur is harvested from the fierce tigers roaming the tropical Echo Isles off the southeastern coast of Durotar. The Darkspear trolls rely heavily on these pelts to craft cold-weather blankets, sturdy tents, and durable armor as their refugee population steadily expands.",h="Durotar Tiger Fur is harvested from the fierce tigers roaming the tropical Echo Isles off the southeastern...",sec={{t="A Vital Resource for the Darkspear",b="In the crowded settlement of Sen'jin Village, resources are perpetually stretched thin. The Darkspear trolls balance the survival of their people against the fragile ecology of their new home, deliberately allowing local tiger populations to thrive until growing needs demand a cull. The thick, hardy furs of the Durotar tigers are carefully cured to produce everyday survival necessities, from basic protective armor to warm blankets that shield the tribe as seasonal weather shifts.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Echo Isles",b="Harvesting these pelts requires crossing open water to the Echo Isles, the lush archipelago south of Durotar that the Darkspear once called home before the witch doctor Zalazane drove them out. Alongside the dangers posed by Zalazane's thralls, stalkers among the thick foliage must contend with the patient, predatory nature of the tigers themselves. Experienced troll hunters like Vel'rin Fang speak of spending entire days motionless in the jungle brush just to secure a single clean kill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are Durotar tiger furs obtained?",a="They are collected by hunting Durotar tigers located across the Echo Isles, the archipelago situated off the southeastern coast of Durotar.",al={"where do tiger furs drop","durotar tiger fur location","how to get tiger furs"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the trolls of Sen'jin Village need these furs?",a="Vel'rin Fang of Sen'jin Village gathers them to supply the growing Darkspear settlement with blankets, tents, and protective leather armor to ensure the tribe does not suffer as seasonal weather changes.",al={"why collect tiger pelts","who needs tiger fur","practical prey purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why don't the trolls overhunt the tigers?",a="The Darkspear deliberately allow the tiger population to thrive naturally, initiating culls only when community supplies run low and shelter or clothing stocks are overwhelmed by their expanding population.",al={"tiger conservation","cull the flock"}},{q="What is Durotar Tiger Fur?",a="Durotar Tiger Fur is the pelt harvested from the wild tigers prowling the Echo Isles off the southeastern coast of Durotar. Tough, warm, and resilient, these hides are an essential raw material for the Darkspear trolls of Sen'jin Village, who work them into everyday necessities to shelter their people from the harsh elements.",al={"what is durotar tiger fur","tiger fur durotar","what is this fur"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does Durotar Tiger Fur come from?",a="These furs are skinned directly from the Durotar tigers that stalk the dense underbrush of the Echo Isles. They are not crafted by artisans, but hunted in the wild by stalkers and scouts braving the waters south of Sen'jin Village.",al={"origin of durotar tiger fur","where do tiger furs come from","who makes durotar tiger fur"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear, securing tiger hides is a dual reminder of their practical struggle for survival in Sen'jin Village and the painful loss of their rightful homeland on the Echo Isles.",["class:Hunter"]="Stalking the tigers of the Echo Isles mirrors classic troll hunting rites, demanding immense patience and camouflage to ambush these stealthy island predators."},kw={"durotar tiger","durotar tiger fur","echo isles","practical prey","sen'jin village","troll pelt","vel'rin fang"},rel={"quest:817","subzone:echo-isles","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","quest:808","subzone:razor-hill"},src={"Durotar Tiger Fur","Practical Prey"}}
E["item:encrypted-parchment"] = {t="item",n="Encrypted Parchment",z="durotar",s="The Encrypted Parchment is a ciphered missive delivered to aspiring orc rogues training in the Valley of Trials. Handed over by Gornek, it discreetly directs promising recruits into the shadows of the Den to meet the covert trainer Rwag.",h="The Encrypted Parchment is a ciphered missive delivered to aspiring orc rogues training in the Valley of...",sec={{t="A Summons from the Shadows",b="Young orcs seeking to prove their martial prowess in the Valley of Trials typically fight out in the open sun. However, those showing an aptitude for stealth, deception, and bladecraft draw a very different kind of attention. The Encrypted Parchment is handed to promising orc rogues by Gornek once they have cut their teeth against the local wildlife. Rather than an open announcement, the message is coded to ensure that only someone with an eye for subterfuge heeds the call.",sp=0},{t="Ties to the Shattered Hand",b="Deciphering the parchment directs the novice deep into the cave known as the Den, past the watchful eye of other clan trainers to find Rwag. There, the recruit learns that the summons was arranged on behalf of the Shattered Hand—an order operating within the Horde's covert network. By answering the parchment, the rogue takes their first step into a world of espionage, shadowcraft, and guarded secrets.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Encrypted Parchment?",a="It serves as a coded summons that introduces novice orc rogues to their class trainer, Rwag, who lurks inside the Den within the Valley of Trials.",al={"what is encrypted parchment","parchment purpose","why encrypted parchment"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends the parchment to you?",a="The message originates from the rogue trainer Rwag, though it is handed to you by Gornek after you complete your initial trials in the valley.",al={"who wrote the parchment","parchment sender","who gave me parchment"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the message written in cipher?",a="Rwag and his contacts within the Shattered Hand favor secrecy over open declarations. A ciphered message ensures that only someone suited for the subtle path of a rogue is guided into their hidden ranks.",al={"why is it encrypted","why encrypted","secret message"},it="motive"},{q="What organization is behind the summons?",a="Rwag reveals that the Shattered Hand asked him to keep an eye out for capable recruits. They offer training in stealth and espionage to serve the Horde from the shadows.",al={"who wants to train me","shattered hand rogue","what faction sent this"},it="ties"},{q="Can troll rogues use this parchment?",a="No. While troll rogues also begin in the Valley of Trials, their secretive summons comes in the form of an Encrypted Tablet rather than this parchment.",al={"troll encrypted parchment","is it for trolls too"},gp=true},{q="What is the Encrypted Parchment?",a="The Encrypted Parchment is a coded letter delivered to promising young orc rogues who prove their mettle in the Valley of Trials. Written using thieves' cant or cipher to avoid prying eyes, it directs you to seek out your trainer, Rwag, concealed within the shadows of the Den.",al={"what is encrypted parchment","encrypted parchment item","what is this parchment"},it="identity",rc="Orc",add=true},{q="Why is the Encrypted Parchment given to you?",a="The parchment is delivered to you because you have caught the attention of the Shattered Hand, the guild of assassins and scouts serving the Horde. They wish to bring you into their fold, instruct you in your lethal craft, and ensure you know where to find their covert operative, Rwag.",al={"why do i need encrypted parchment","why encrypted parchment","purpose of encrypted parchment"},it="why_wanted",rc="Orc",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="The parchment represents your induction into the covert underworld of the Horde, pointing you toward mentors affiliated with the Shattered Hand.",["race:Orc"]="While orc culture typically prizes open, honorable combat, this missive welcomes those whose talents lie in the quieter, deadlier arts of survival."},kw={"durotar","encrypted parchment","gornek","orc rogue","rwag","shattered hand","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:3088","npc:rwag","npc:gornek","subzone:valley-of-trials","quest:1089","quest:1858","quest:cutting-teeth","quest:3083"},src={"Encrypted Parchment","Encrypted Parchment (quest)"}}
E["item:encrypted-tablet"] = {t="item",n="Encrypted Tablet",z="durotar",s="The Encrypted Tablet is a coded message delivered to novice Darkspear troll rogues training in the Valley of Trials. Inscribed by the rogue trainer Rwag, it summons promising cutpurses and scouts to his post inside the Den.",h="The Encrypted Tablet is a coded message delivered to novice Darkspear troll rogues training in the Valley of...",sec={{t="A Hidden Summons",b="Novice troll rogues arriving in the Valley of Trials are handed the Encrypted Tablet as their initial directive. Inscribed with ciphered instructions, the slate directs them directly to Rwag, an orc trainer residing within the shaded caves of the Den. Rather than openly broadcasting guild business, the local shadow operatives use these encrypted slates to test comprehension and discreetly draw new talent under official tutelage.",sp=0},{t="Eyes of the Hand",b="Deciphering the tablet introduces recruits to the larger shadow network of the Horde. Upon reporting to Rwag, scouts learn that their progression is scrutinized by shadowy syndicates like the Shattered Hand, who look to valley trainers to ensure prospective cutpurses, spies, and assassins are sharp enough to serve the new nation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Encrypted Tablet used for?",a="The Encrypted Tablet serves as an encrypted summons instructing young troll rogues to report to Rwag, the local rogue trainer stationed within the Den in the Valley of Trials.",al={"tablet purpose","what does encrypted tablet do","why do i have encrypted tablet"},it="purpose"},{q="Who wrote the message on the tablet?",a="The message was crafted by Rwag, the rogue trainer in the Valley of Trials who oversees the training of thieves, cutpurses, and assassins for the Horde.",al={"who sent encrypted tablet","tablet author","who wrote this"},it="origin"},{q="Where do I find Rwag?",a="Rwag is located deep inside the Den, a cavern complex along the northern ridge of the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",al={"where is rwag","rwag location","find rogue trainer valley of trials"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is 'the Hand' mentioned by Rwag?",a="The Hand refers to the Shattered Hand, a clandestine order operating among the Horde's rogue network. Rwag answers to them regarding the readiness of new operatives emerging from the Valley.",al={"what hand","who are the hand","shattered hand connection"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Encrypted Tablet?",a="The Encrypted Tablet is a coded stone slate delivered specifically to you upon beginning your training in the Valley of Trials. Encrypted to shield its contents from pryin' eyes, it serves as a summons to test your cleverness and direct you to the local rogue trainer.",al={"encrypted tablet","what is encrypted tablet","tablet item"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why is the Encrypted Tablet wanted?",a="The rogue trainer Rwag sent the tablet to ensure that newly arrived scoundrels find their way to his den. By deciphering the encrypted message, you prove you have the wits required of a rogue and learn precisely where to seek his guidance.",al={"why want encrypted tablet","why is tablet needed","who wants encrypted tablet"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="The ciphered slate represents your initial induction into the formal ranks of Horde rogues, pointing you toward Rwag's training in the Den.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear trolls training in Durotar receive this tablet as proof that their agility and stealth have caught the eye of the Valley's trainers."},kw={"durotar","encrypted tablet","rogue trainer","rwag","shattered hand","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:3083","npc:rwag","topic:rogue","subzone:valley-of-trials","topic:troll","zone:durotar","quest:1089"},src={"Encrypted Tablet","Encrypted Tablet (quest)"}}
E["item:etched-parchment"] = {t="item",n="Etched Parchment",z="durotar",s="The Etched Parchment is a written summons delivered to novice hunters training within Durotar's Valley of Trials. Handed over by Gornek, it directs aspiring wilderness stalkers to seek instruction from the troll trainer Jen'shan.",h="The Etched Parchment is a written summons delivered to novice hunters training within Durotar's Valley of...",sec={{t="A Summons to the Hunt",b="Young orcs and Darkspear trolls seeking their place among the Horde begin their rites in the arid basin of the Valley of Trials. While they prove themselves against the local vermin, Gornek serves as a watchful overseer who guides recruits toward their calling. For those destined to wield bow, gun, and fang, Gornek passes along this etched parchment. It bears a direct message from Jen'shan, a skilled hunter trainer seeking fresh eyes and steady hands.",sp=0},{t="The First Lesson",b="Carrying the parchment to Jen'shan marks the true beginning of a hunter's training in Durotar. Jen'shan emphasizes that walking the wild path is no easy task, requiring just as much dedication to master the beasts of the desert as an arcanist devotes to magic or a shaman gives to the spirits. Reading the parchment and answering her call introduces novitiates to proper marksmanship and wilderness survival.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Etched Parchment for?",a="It is an introductory summons intended to guide newly arrived hunters in the Valley of Trials to their class trainer, Jen'shan.",al={"etched parchment use","what does etched parchment do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who hands out this parchment?",a="Gornek, the overseer stationed near the Den in the Valley of Trials, presents the note to young hunters upon their arrival.",al={"who gives etched parchment","etched parchment questgiver"},gp=true},{q="Who wrote the Etched Parchment?",a="The message comes from Jen'shan, a troll hunter trainer stationed within the Valley of Trials who is eager to train new marksmen.",al={"who sent etched parchment","parchment author"},it="origin"},{q="Where can Jen'shan be found?",a="Jen'shan is located in the Valley of Trials in Durotar, waiting near the training grounds to instruct novice orc and troll hunters.",al={"where is jenshan","find jenshan"},gp=true},{q="What is the Etched Parchment?",a="The Etched Parchment is a written summons directed specifically to novice hunters arriving in the Valley of Trials. Handed to you by Gornek, it carries a direct call to seek out the local hunter trainer, Jen'shan, so you can begin learning how to survive the harsh red wastes of Durotar and master the wild beasts that roam them.",al={"what is etched parchment","etched parchment item","about etched parchment"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Jen'shan want the Etched Parchment returned to her?",a="Jen'shan does not keep the parchment as a prized relic; she uses it as a formal summons to bring fledgling hunters before her. Delivering it confirms you have answered her call and are ready to be instructed in the deadly crafts of archery, marksmanship, and surviving alongside the fierce predators of Durotar.",al={"why bring etched parchment","why does jenshan want the parchment","etched parchment purpose"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This missive represents a hunter's very first rite of passage in Durotar, formally connecting them with Jen'shan to begin learning tracking, ranged weaponry, and survival.",["faction:Horde"]="Every young warrior of the Horde must hone their craft; for hunters, this parchment marks their initial step toward feeding their clan and guarding Durotar's borders."},kw={"durotar","etched parchment","gornek","hunter","jen'shan","trainer","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:3087","npc:gornek","npc:jen-shan","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:hunter"},src={"Etched Parchment","Etched Parchment (Classic)"}}
E["item:felstalker-hoof"] = {t="item",n="Felstalker Hoof",z="durotar",s="A Felstalker Hoof is a physical token taken from demonic beasts infesting the Burning Blade Coven in Durotar's Valley of Trials. Young shaman must retrieve these hooves as a trial of readiness before learning to commune with the elemental spirits of the earth.",h="A Felstalker Hoof is a physical token taken from demonic beasts infesting the Burning Blade Coven in...",sec={{t="A Shaman's Trial",b="Within the sun-baked Valley of Trials, the trainer Canaga Earthcaller tasks budding shaman with facing the demonic taint threatening Durotar. The Burning Blade Coven to the north harbors vile familiars and demonic felstalkers. Taking the hooves of these fiends is not merely an act of culling pests, but a rigorous test of endurance, resolve, and spirit. Only by subduing these chaotic beasts can an aspiring shaman prove worthy of receiving the secrets of the earth and preparing the ceremonial sapta needed to commune directly with elemental spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Felstalker Hoof used for?",a="Two Felstalker Hooves are brought to Canaga Earthcaller in the Valley of Trials. They serve as proof that a shaman initiate possesses the strength and spirit required to begin communes with the earth element.",al={"what does felstalker hoof do","hoof quest item","why get felstalker hooves"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do these hooves come from?",a="They are carved from the demonic Felstalkers found inside and around the Burning Blade Coven, located in the northern reaches of the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",al={"where to get felstalker hoof","felstalker hoof location","who drops hooves"},it="origin"},{q="Who requires these hooves?",a="Canaga Earthcaller, the shaman trainer stationed near the Den in the Valley of Trials, requests them during the Call of Earth rite.",al={"who wants felstalker hooves","who turns in hoof","canaga earthcaller quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Can any adventurer collect these hooves?",a="Felstalker Hooves are sought specifically by shaman undergoing their elemental initiation. Warriors, warlocks, and rogues have their own distinct trials within the valley and have no need for them.",al={"can non shaman get hooves","is hoof shaman only"},gp=true},{q="What is a Felstalker Hoof?",a="A Felstalker Hoof is a physical trophy taken from the demonic felstalkers summoned by the Burning Blade cultists in Durotar. Rather than serving as a crafting component, it is taken as proof of combat prowess by young shamans seeking to commune with the spirits of the earth.",al={"what is felstalker hoof","felstalker hoof info","what are felstalker hooves"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Slaying demons and gathering their hooves is your first major step toward communion with the earth spirits, testing the patience and stubborn resilience needed to wield an Earth Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="The presence of demonic felstalkers in Durotar's training grounds is a constant reminder of the Burning Blade's lingering corruption on Horde lands."},kw={"burning blade coven","call of earth","canaga earthcaller","durotar","earth sapta","felstalker","felstalker hoof","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:1516","npc:canaga-earthcaller","subzone:burning-blade-coven","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:shaman","quest:792","quest:794"},src={"Felstalker Hoof","Call of Earth (Durotar)"}}
E["item:fire-tar"] = {t="item",n="Fire Tar",z="durotar",s="Fire Tar is a volatile substance gathered by Razormane quilboar spellcasters across the eastern Barrens. To Horde shamans, it serves as a crucial ritual component used to brew the Fire Sapta, which grants spiritual communion with the element of fire.",h="Fire Tar is a volatile substance gathered by Razormane quilboar spellcasters across the eastern Barrens.",sec={{t="A Concoction of the Bristlebacks",b="Carried almost exclusively by spellcasting Razormane quilboar—including their geomancers, mystics, and thornweavers—fire tar is an alchemical substance tuned closely to flame. While the bristled tribes of the Barrens use it for their own harsh magic and rituals, shamanic instructors recognize it as an essential worldly reagent capable of bridging the gap between mortal senses and raw elemental fury.",sp=0},{t="The Path to the Fire Totem",b="When young orc and troll shamans are sent to Telf Joolam perched high in Durotar's crags, they are charged with forging their fire totem. Telf requires two key elements tied to heat and flame to brew a fire sapta: a reagent pouch stolen from Burning Blade cultists, and fire tar harvested from the Razormane. Drinking the resulting brew allows the shaman to pierce the veil and perceive the elemental spirits of flame awaiting them atop the nearby peaks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Fire Tar used for?",a="Fire Tar is a necessary ritual ingredient brought to the hermit shaman Telf Joolam in Durotar. Combined with reagents from the Burning Blade, it is brewed into a Fire Sapta—a potion that enables a shaman to view and commune with fire spirits to earn their fire totem.",al={"fire tar use","what does fire tar do","why do i need fire tar"},it="purpose"},{q="Who carries Fire Tar?",a="It is carried by spellcasting quilboar of the Razormane tribe in the eastern Barrens, such as Razormane Geomancers, Mystics, Thornweavers, and Water Seekers.",al={"who drops fire tar","fire tar mobs","where to get fire tar"},it="target"},{q="Why do shamans need ingredients tied to hostile spellcasters?",a="Saptas require physical components deeply saturated with the corresponding element. Because both the Razormane casters and Burning Blade warlocks channel intense heat and destructive flame, their everyday materials are already steeped in the fiery essence needed to awaken a shaman's elemental sight.",al={"why quilboar tar","why warlocks and quilboar"}},{q="Where does Telf Joolam brew the Fire Sapta?",a="Telf Joolam resides on a high cliff overlooking the crags of Durotar, near the path between Razor Hill and the Barrens. There he instructs initiates on balancing the destructive and creative nature of flame.",al={"where is telf joolam","turn in fire tar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Fire Tar?",a="Fire Tar is a volatile, elemental substance carried by spellcasters among the Razormane quilboar in the Barrens. Imbued with the fundamental essence of fire, this pungent pitch is prized by practitioners of elemental magic for its natural affinity to flame.",al={"what is fire tar","fire tar info","describe fire tar"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does Fire Tar come from, and who makes it?",a="Fire Tar is harvested from the Razormane quilboar spellcasters inhabiting the eastern Barrens, including their geomancers, mystics, and thornweavers. Whether refined through their primitive earth-and-fire rites or gathered from natural fissures across their bristling briar territories, it remains a closely guarded staple of their shamans and seers.",al={"who makes fire tar","fire tar origin","where does fire tar come from"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Gathering Fire Tar marks an essential rite of passage, teaching you to seek out elemental resonance in the wider world to brew the Fire Sapta and earn your Fire Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="Acquiring Fire Tar takes young Horde adventurers out of Durotar and across the Southfury River into the Barrens, confronting the aggressive Razormane tribes."},kw={"call of fire","fire sapta","fire tar","quilboar","razormane","shaman totem","telf joolam","the barrens"},rel={"quest:1524","npc:telf-joolam","topic:shaman","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens","zone:durotar","item:reagent-pouch-shaman","subzone:dustwind-cave"},src={"Fire Tar","Call of Fire (3)"}}
E["item:fizzle-s-claw"] = {t="item",n="Fizzle's Claw",z="durotar",s="Fizzle's Claw is the severed hand of the goblin warlock Fizzle Darkstorm. Taken from his encampment in Thunder Ridge, it serves as physical proof to the Horde commanders in Razor Hill that a dangerous Burning Blade conspirator has been slain.",h="Fizzle's Claw is the severed hand of the goblin warlock Fizzle Darkstorm.",sec={{t="A Grim Trophy",b="Orgnil Soulscar, tasked with uprooting shadow cults threatening the orcish homeland, identified Fizzle Darkstorm as an instigator spreading corruption in Thunder Ridge. Demand for Fizzle's claw was not merely out of savagery, but practical necessity: the Horde requires indisputable evidence when a covert warlock operating under the banner of the Burning Blade is eliminated.",sp=0},{t="The Threat in Thunder Ridge",b="Thunder Ridge was already disrupted by elemental unrest, making Fizzle's cultist presence an imminent peril to the surrounding territories. By severing the goblin's claw and returning it to Razor Hill, Horde scouts confirmed that the warlock's rituals and his attempts to establish a Burning Blade foothold had been thwarted.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who does this claw belong to?",a="The claw belonged to Fizzle Darkstorm, a treacherous goblin warlock affiliated with the shadow cult known as the Burning Blade.",al={"who is fizzle","fizzle darkstorm","claw owner"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Orgnil Soulscar want Fizzle's Claw?",a="Orgnil Soulscar needs definitive proof of Fizzle's death. The Burning Blade operates from the shadows, so presenting the goblin warlock's claw confirms that this particular threat to Durotar has been permanently purged.",al={"why need claw","orgnil soulscar claw","proof of death"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where was the claw found?",a="It is taken from Fizzle Darkstorm at his camp tucked away in Thunder Ridge, a canyon located to the northwest of Razor Hill in Durotar.",al={"fizzle location","where is fizzle","thunder ridge claw"},it="place"},{q="What is the Burning Blade doing in Durotar?",a="The Burning Blade is a sinister cult seeking to undermine the new orcish homeland through demonic corruption, dark sorcery, and civil unrest. Warlocks like Fizzle establish hidden camps to spread chaos across the region.",al={"burning blade durotar","why are cultists in thunder ridge"},it="threat"},{q="What is Fizzle's Claw?",a="Fizzle's Claw is the severed hand of Fizzle Darkstorm, a treacherous goblin warlock aligned with the Burning Blade cult. It serves as gruesome physical proof of his demise for Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill, confirming that the cultist ringleader stirring up trouble in Thunder Ridge has been permanently eliminated.",al={"what is fizzles claw","fizzles claw item","fizzle claw identity"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Presenting Fizzle's claw to Razor Hill demonstrates an ongoing commitment to cleansing Durotar of the shadow cults threatening the fragile safety of the young nation.",["class:Warlock"]="Fizzle Darkstorm used fel arts to serve the subversive Burning Blade, turning his dark talents toward direct rebellion against the Horde."},kw={"burning blade","dark storms","durotar","fizzle darkstorm","fizzle's claw","orgnil soulscar","razor hill","thunder ridge"},rel={"quest:806","npc:orgnil-soulscar","subzone:thunder-ridge","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:warlock","topic:goblin"},src={"Fizzle's Claw","Dark Storms (quest)"}}
E["item:foreman-s-blackjack"] = {t="item",n="Foreman's Blackjack",z="durotar",s="The Foreman's Blackjack is a heavy leather-wrapped cosh loaned out to fresh Horde recruits in the Valley of Trials. Taskmasters hand it down as an everyday disciplinary tool to wake slumbering peons and enforce the grueling pace of Durotar's early construction.",h="The Foreman's Blackjack is a heavy leather-wrapped cosh loaned out to fresh Horde recruits in the Valley of...",sec={{t="A Tool of Orcish Labor",b="Building a new home in the rugged desert of Durotar requires massive stockpiles of lumber, and the labor falls squarely on the shoulders of the Horde's peons. In the Valley of Trials, Foreman Thazz'ril relies on the Foreman's Blackjack to keep work crews moving. Rather than dealing lethal blows, this weighted bludgeon is designed to deliver a jarring wake-up call to laborers caught napping beneath the valley's shade trees. It serves as a stark reminder of peon life in the new Horde: grueling, unglamorous, and supervised with an iron fist.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Foreman's Blackjack used for?",a="Overseers give the blackjack to young adventurers to discipline sleeping peons throughout the Valley of Trials. Striking a napping peon jolts them awake and sends them straight back to chopping and hauling wood.",al={"blackjack use","why use blackjack","peon club"},it="purpose"},{q="Who owns this blackjack?",a="It belongs to Foreman Thazz'ril, the labor taskmaster stationed in the Valley of Trials who oversees the collection of raw timber for the young Orc settlement.",al={"who gives blackjack","foreman blackjack owner"},it="leader"},{q="Why do the peons keep falling asleep on the job?",a="Orcish peons work relentless, exhausting shifts gathering wood under the harsh sun of Durotar. Whenever they find shade beneath the valley's sparse trees, exhaustion overtakes them, leading to frequent unauthorized naps.",al={"why are peons lazy","lazy peons sleeping"},it="motive"},{q="Can I keep the blackjack after finishing the task?",a="No. The overseer demands the tool be returned immediately once the shirkers have been disciplined, ensuring it remains on hand for future taskmasters to enforce labor quotas.",al={"keep blackjack","can i keep foreman blackjack"},gp=true},{q="What is the Foreman's Blackjack?",a="The Foreman's Blackjack is a heavy leather-wrapped truncheon carried by Foreman Thazz'ril in the Valley of Trials. It is an unglamorous tool of discipline, designed not to inflict grievous wounds in war, but to deliver a sharp, stinging blow that jolts sleeping workers back to their feet.",al={"what is the blackjack","foremans blackjack item","what is foremans blackjack"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Foreman Thazz'ril want the blackjack back?",a="Foreman Thazz'ril relies on the blackjack to run his work crews in the Valley of Trials. Without it, he has little leverage to force the exhausted, unmotivated peons to keep chopping and hauling lumber for the Horde. Once you have helped knock the laborers back to their duties, he expects his essential tool returned.",al={"why return the blackjack","why does thazzril need the blackjack","why want the blackjack"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For young orcs stepping into the Valley of Trials, wielding the blackjack offers an early lesson in Horde hierarchy: those without the strength or spirit of a warrior are relegated to labor and kept in line by force.",["faction:Horde"]="The blackjack highlights the relentless practical effort needed to tame Durotar, where settling a harsh land requires every laborer to work without pause."},kw={"blackjack","durotar","foreman's blackjack","lazy peons","peon","thazzril","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:lazy-peons","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","quest:1089"},src={"Foreman's Blackjack","Lazy Peons"}}
E["item:glowing-ember"] = {t="item",n="Glowing Ember",z="durotar",s="A Glowing Ember is the lingering, elemental core recovered from a defeated Minor Manifestation of Fire atop the crags of Durotar. It serves as a vital ceremonial reagent in a shaman's trials, used to ignite the brazier at the Shrine of Eternal Flame.",h="A Glowing Ember is the lingering, elemental core recovered from a defeated Minor Manifestation of Fire atop...",sec={{t="Core of the Flame",b="When a rising shaman drinks the fire sapta and faces the fiery spirits atop the ridge near Telf Joolam, they confront a Minor Manifestation of Fire. Upon the elemental's defeat, this smoldering remnant is all that remains of its physical form. Still pulsing with raw elemental heat, the ember carries the living spark of fire necessary to awaken the sacred brazier at the Shrine of Eternal Flame.",sp=0},{t="Igniting the Torch",b="Placing the Glowing Ember into the otherwise cool basin of the mountain brazier triggers a sudden, white-hot ignition. Feeding on the residue of the defeated elemental, the brazier allows the initiate to ignite the Torch of the Dormant Flame, binding the unruly essence of fire into a vessel they can carry down the mountain to prove their mastery over the elements.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the Glowing Ember come from?",a="The ember is recovered from the remains of a Minor Manifestation of Fire, a hostile elemental encountered at the summit above the Shrine of Eternal Flame in Durotar.",al={"how to get glowing ember","glowing ember drop","where find glowing ember"},it="origin"},{q="What is the ember used for?",a="Initiates place the ember into the metal brazier at the Shrine of Eternal Flame. It produces an intense, rhythmic flame used to light the ceremonial Torch of the Dormant Flame.",al={"what does glowing ember do","glowing ember use","brazier ember"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why do shamans need the fire sapta to acquire it?",a="The elemental spirits atop the mountain dwell beyond ordinary mortal sight. Consuming the fire sapta attunes a shaman's senses to the elemental plane, revealing the Minor Manifestation of Fire so it can be challenged.",al={"why need sapta","cant see fire elemental","fire sapta ember"}},{q="Who directs shamans to seek this ember?",a="The hermit Telf Joolam, residing in the crags of Durotar, brews the fire sapta and guides shaman initiates through the trial of defeating the flame spirit.",al={"who gives the quest","telf joolam ember","call of fire quest giver"}},{q="What is the Glowing Ember?",a="The Glowing Ember is the smoldering remnant harvested from a Minor Manifestation of Fire upon the peak overlooking Durotar. It is a concentrated piece of living flame left behind once the spirit is overcome, holding enough innate elemental heat to spark the dormant fires atop the mountain's sacred altar.",al={"what is glowing ember","glowing ember lore","glowing ember item"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Obtaining this burning core is a defining rite of passage, forcing an initiate to test their resolve against living fire before commanding its totem."},kw={"call of fire","fire sapta","glowing ember","minor manifestation of fire","shrine of eternal flame","telf joolam","torch of the dormant flame"},rel={"quest:1524","npc:telf-joolam","item:torch-of-the-dormant-flame","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Glowing Ember","Call of Fire (4)"}}
E["item:glyphic-tablet"] = {t="item",n="Glyphic Tablet",z="durotar",s="The Glyphic Tablet is an inscribed slate handed to novice Darkspear troll mages upon beginning their trials in Durotar. Delivered through the overseer Gornek, it directs fledgling spellcasters to seek tutelage from the troll mage trainer, Mai'ah.",h="The Glyphic Tablet is an inscribed slate handed to novice Darkspear troll mages upon beginning their trials...",sec={{t="A Mage's First Summons",b="In the Valley of Trials, new Darkspear troll initiates exhibiting an affinity for arcane power are presented with the Glyphic Tablet. Passed along by Gornek while young recruits handle early tasks around the red canyons, the tablet contains an invitation from Mai'ah, a seasoned troll mage posted outside the Den. For the Darkspear, whose arcane traditions diverge from the scholarly academies of humans or high elves, the tablet serves as a formal call to discipline. Mai'ah uses the meeting to offer both arcane instruction and a solemn warning: raw magic is corruptive, deceptive, and far more hazardous to a practitioner's mind than any enemy soldier.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Glyphic Tablet?",a="It serves as a written summons directing a novice troll mage to report to Mai'ah, the local mage trainer in the Valley of Trials, to commence proper spellcasting training.",al={"what does glyphic tablet do","glyphic tablet use","why do i have glyphic tablet"},it="purpose"},{q="Who sends the Glyphic Tablet?",a="The tablet is authored by the mage trainer Mai'ah and handed to young troll recruits by Gornek within the Valley of Trials.",al={"who wrote glyphic tablet","who gave me glyphic tablet"},it="origin"},{q="Why do troll mages need a warning about magic?",a="Mai'ah stresses that arcane magic is inherently corruptive. She warns that it feeds arrogance and makes spellcasters believe they are invincible, cautioning that the unseen dangers of the arcane are far deadlier than physical rivals.",al={"what does mai'ah say","is magic dangerous"},it="motive"},{q="Can other Horde races receive this tablet?",a="Only troll mages receive the Glyphic Tablet in the Valley of Trials, as the orcs of Durotar do not practice the arcane arts.",al={"can orcs get glyphic tablet","is glyphic tablet troll only"},it="for_you"},{q="What is the Glyphic Tablet?",a="The Glyphic Tablet is an inscribed message sent to novice troll mages beginning their trials in the Valley of Trials. Delivered through Gornek, it summons you to meet with Mai'ah, the local mage trainer, so you may formally commence your instruction in the arcane arts.",al={"what is glyphic tablet","glyphic tablet item","about glyphic tablet"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does anyone want the Glyphic Tablet?",a="The tablet is not sought for power or wealth, but serves as a formal summons and token of introduction. It ensures young troll mages present themselves to Mai'ah, who uses the meeting to deliver crucial warnings regarding the corrupting dangers inherent to wielding arcane magic.",al={"why want glyphic tablet","who needs glyphic tablet","why keep glyphic tablet"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="The tablet marks the start of your arcane instruction among the Darkspear, carrying a reminder from Mai'ah that the corrupting allure of magic is your greatest peril.",["race:Troll"]="As the only race in the Valley of Trials to practice wizardry, Darkspear mages receive this tablet to begin their unique path alongside traditional shamanic and martial ways."},kw={"arcane","durotar","glyphic tablet","gornek","mai'ah","troll mage","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:3086","npc:mai-ah","npc:gornek","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:mage","topic:troll","quest:1089"},src={"Glyphic Tablet","Glyphic Tablet (quest)"}}
E["item:gnomish-tools"] = {t="item",n="Gnomish Tools",z="durotar",s="Gnomish Tools are intricate mechanical implements recovered from the sunken warships of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's fleet off the coast of Durotar. The Horde seeks these salvaged devices to study Alliance engineering and turn their enemies' technological advantages to their own benefit.",h="Gnomish Tools are intricate mechanical implements recovered from the sunken warships of Grand Admiral Daelin...",sec={{t="Sunken Salvage",b="When Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore led Kul Tiras and Alliance forces to the shores of Durotar, his fleet carried vast supplies of modern equipment, including sophisticated gear manufactured by their gnomish allies. Following the destruction of Proudmoore's fleet along the Scuttle Coast, east of Tiragarde Keep, these delicate mechanical kits sank beneath the waves. Today, waterproof toolboxes remain scattered among the rotting timbers and barnacle-encrusted hulls in the shallows.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in Orgrimmar",b="Gar'Thok, overseer of Razor Hill, tasked Horde scouts with securing these tools from the watery grave of Proudmoore's navy. The orcs recognize that humans and gnomes possess advanced technical craftsmanship, particularly in siege engines, shipwrighting, and clockwork mechanics. By collecting and dispatching these kits by caravan to the craftsmen and scholars in Orgrimmar, the Horde intends to dissect Alliance contraptions, learn how to counter their war machines, and adapt foreign innovations for their own survival.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are gnomish tools lying off the coast of Durotar?",a="They were carried aboard the warships of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's fleet when Kul Tiras assaulted Durotar. When Proudmoore's armada was shattered and sunk along the Scuttle Coast east of Tiragarde Keep, their naval cargo settled along the ocean floor.",al={"why gnomish tools here","origin of gnomish tools","how did tools get in durotar"},it="origin"},{q="Why does the Horde want these tools?",a="Gar'Thok of Razor Hill wants them salvaged so they can be sent to Orgrimmar. The Horde recognizes that Alliance engineers possess intricate mechanical knowledge, and studying their tools helps the Horde understand how enemy machines work and how to build better gear of their own.",al={"why does gar'thok want tools","horde use for gnomish tools","what are the tools for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are the tools found?",a="They are stored inside toolboxes scattered in and around the sunken wreckage along the Scuttle Coast, just east of Tiragarde Keep in Durotar. Many rest underwater or across half-submerged broken hulls.",al={"gnomish tools location","where to find gnomish tools","gnomish toolboxes location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are these Gnomish Tools?",a="These are specialized mechanical implements crafted by the gnomes of the Alliance. Highly prized for their precision and intricate design, they represent some of the most sophisticated engineering in Azeroth. Carried aboard Grand Admiral Proudmoore's warships to maintain and repair advanced Alliance machinery, they were scattered across the ocean floor off Durotar's coast when his fleet met its ruin.",al={"what are gnomish tools","gnomish tools info","what are the gnomish tools"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="These kits showcase the precise, intricate craft of Alliance tinkers, offering valuable insights into clockwork assemblies and miniaturization.",["faction:Horde"]="Recovering lost Alliance equipment allows the Horde to study enemy design, reverse-engineer foreign mechanisms, and defend against future naval invasions."},kw={"durotar","engineering","gar'thok","gnomish tools","proudmoore","razor hill","scuttle coast","tiragarde keep"},rel={"quest:825","subzone:scuttle-coast","npc:gar-thok","subzone:tiragarde-keep","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:gnome"},src={"Gnomish Tools","From The Wreckage...."}}
E["item:hallowed-tablet"] = {t="item",n="Hallowed Tablet",z="durotar",s="The Hallowed Tablet is an inscribed message delivered to young Darkspear troll priests training in the Valley of Trials. Sent by the spiritual elder Ken'jai, it bids novices to seek him out and begin learning how to commune with the spirits.",h="The Hallowed Tablet is an inscribed message delivered to young Darkspear troll priests training in the Valley...",sec={{t="A Summons from the Spirits",b="When a promising troll priest takes their first steps in the harsh crimson canyons of the Valley of Trials, Gornek hands them the Hallowed Tablet. Rather than a formal bureaucratic writ, it serves as a personal invitation from Ken'jai, the resident priest trainer residing outside the Den. Ken'jai interprets the signs and whisperings of the spirits, sensing when young Darkspear with spiritual potential arrive in Durotar. The tablet instructs the initiate to read its words and present themselves for guidance on properly channeling spiritual authority.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hallowed Tablet?",a="It is an inscribed stone tablet passed to novice troll priests by Gornek in the Valley of Trials. It contains a message directing the initiate to Ken'jai, their class trainer.",al={"what is this item","hallowed tablet lore","what does the tablet do"},it="identity"},{q="Who sent the tablet?",a="The tablet was sent by Ken'jai, the priest trainer situated outside the Den. The spirits foretold the arrival of a new acolyte, prompting him to send word via Gornek.",al={"who wrote it","who gave me this","tablet author"},it="origin"},{q="Why do troll priests need to see Ken'jai?",a="Darkspear priests rely on communing with and commanding the spirits. Ken'jai guides initiates as their spiritual connection deepens, ensuring the spirits favor teaching them more potent abilities.",al={"what does kenjai do","why see kenjai"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear, priesthood is an intimate communion with the spirits and loa, making the call inscribed on the tablet an invitation into ancestral spiritual traditions.",["class:Priest"]="The tablet marks the start of a priest's formal training in Durotar, establishing their bond with class mentor Ken'jai."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","gornek","hallowed tablet","ken'jai","troll priest","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:3085","npc:gornek","topic:priest","topic:troll","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","quest:1089"},src={"Hallowed Tablet","Hallowed Tablet (quest)"}}
E["item:kron-s-amulet"] = {t="item",n="Kron's Amulet",z="durotar",s="Kron's Amulet is a personal keepsake belonging to Kron, a young orc hunter from Durotar who went missing along the Southfury River.",h="Kron's Amulet is a personal keepsake belonging to Kron, a young orc hunter from Durotar who went missing...",sec={{t="Tragedy on the Southfury",b="Kron was a headstrong young orc from a farmstead northwest of Razor Hill. Eager to prove his prowess and dismissive of danger, he stormed off to hunt the vicious Dreadmaw crocolisks prowling the Southfury River along the border with the Barrens. Ignoring his mother Misha Tor'kren's warnings, his stubborn pride led him directly into the jaws of the river's predators. He never returned, leaving behind only this swallowed trinket as a silent confirmation that he had been slain and devoured.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Kron?",a="Kron was an impulsive young orc hunter who lived with his mother, Misha Tor'kren, on a farmstead northwest of Razor Hill. Determined to test his strength, he went out alone to hunt river beasts despite warnings of their ferocity.",al={"who is kron","kron backstory","kron lore"},it="people"},{q="Where is Kron's Amulet found?",a="The amulet is recovered from the bellies of Dreadmaw Crocolisks and Corrupted Dreadmaw Crocolisks lurking along the banks of the Southfury River in Durotar.",al={"where do i find the amulet","kron's amulet location","who drops kron's amulet"},sp=1,it="item",gp=true},{q="Who wants Kron's Amulet returned?",a="His grieving mother, Misha Tor'kren, awaits word of her son at her farmstead northwest of Razor Hill. The amulet provides her the final, painful closure needed to begin mourning.",al={"who needs the amulet","where to turn in kron's amulet","misha tor'kren"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Kron's Amulet?",a="This personal trinket belonged to Kron, an orc youth from a farmstead northwest of Razor Hill. Driven by pride and eager to prove his strength, he set out alone toward the Southfury River to hunt the ferocious Dreadmaw crocolisks along the border of the Barrens. Instead of returning in triumph, he fell prey to the beasts he sought to slay. Swallowed along with his remains, this talisman is the only surviving piece of the young hunter that can prove his grim demise.",al={"what is the amulet","krons amulet lore","who owns the amulet"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Kron's fate is a tragic reminder that while pride and martial glory drive orcish tradition, recklessness and ignoring the wisdom of elders can bring a swift and needless death.",["class:Hunter"]="A stark lesson for any aspiring tracker on the perils of underestimating vicious beasts in unfamiliar river territory."},kw={"amulet","dreadmaw crocolisk","kron","misha tor'kren","razor hill","southfury river"},rel={"quest:816","npc:misha-tor-kren","subzone:southfury-river","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","zone:barrens"},src={"Kron's Amulet","Lost But Not Forgotten (Classic)"}}
E["item:minshina-s-skull"] = {t="item",n="Minshina's Skull",z="durotar",s="Minshina's Skull contains the bound soul of the Darkspear troll Minshina, brother of Master Gadrin. Trapped by the rogue witch doctor Zalazane on the Echo Isles, the skull serves as a grim vessel used to fuel dark ritual magics.",h="Minshina's Skull contains the bound soul of the Darkspear troll Minshina, brother of Master Gadrin.",sec={{t="A Trapped Spirit",b="When Zalazane seized control of the Echo Isles and drove out the Darkspear tribe, Minshina was among those captured and slain. Rather than letting his victim pass into death, the traitorous witch doctor bound Minshina's soul to his own severed skull. Placed within a foul circle of power on the southernmost isle, the skull became a tether of magical enslavement. Master Gadrin, guided by tormented visions of his brother calling to him in dreams, seeks out brave travelers to venture into the occupied islands, reclaim the relic, and shatter Zalazane's hold over his brother's spirit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Minshina?",a="Minshina was a Darkspear troll and the brother of Master Gadrin of Sen'jin Village. He was murdered during the turmoil surrounding Zalazane's betrayal on the Echo Isles.",al={"minshina lore","who is minshina","master gadrin brother"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Minshina's soul trapped in his skull?",a="Zalazane used dark magics to bind Minshina's spirit directly inside his severed head. Arranged within a ritual circle of power on the main isle, the imprisoned soul remained bound to Zalazane's will rather than moving on to the ancestors.",al={"why trap his soul","zalazane skull ritual","soul trapped in skull"},it="power"},{q="Where is the skull located?",a="The skull is found on the largest, southernmost isle of the Echo Isles. It rests atop a hill within a circle of power adorned with candles, ritual markers, and other skulls guarded by Zalazane's thralls.",al={"where is minshinas skull","circle of power location","skull location echo isles"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens when the skull is brought to Master Gadrin?",a="Returning the skull to Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village breaks the dark enchantment. With the foul tether severed, Minshina's spectral form briefly manifests, bows in gratitude, and peacefully departs to the realm of the ancestors.",al={"freeing minshina","gadrin skull reward","what happens to minshina"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="What is Minshina's Skull?",a="Minshina's Skull is the physical remains of Minshina, a fallen Darkspear troll and the brother of Master Gadrin. Rather than resting peacefully in death, Minshina had his very soul bound into his severed skull through dark voodoo, leaving him trapped and crying out for release.",al={"what is minshina's skull","minshina skull identity","what is this skull"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does Minshina's Skull come from, and who made it?",a="The skull belonged to Minshina, who was captured and killed by the traitorous witch doctor Zalazane on the Echo Isles. Using foul sorcery, Zalazane severed the head and bound Minshina's spirit directly to the bone, placing it within a circle of power alongside other remains to fuel his dark rituals.",al={"where did minshina's skull come from","who made minshina skull","minshina skull origin"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does anyone want Minshina's Skull?",a="Master Gadrin seeks the skull to rescue his brother's tormented spirit. Minshina constantly calls out to Gadrin in his dreams, unable to find rest while imprisoned by Zalazane's magic. Recovering the skull from the circle of power on the Echo Isles is the only way to break the binding and grant his soul freedom.",al={"why want minshina skull","why collect minshina skull","who wants minshina skull"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear, Zalazane's desecration of Minshina is a grievous affront to ancestral tradition, making the retrieval of his skull a vital matter of tribal honor.",["faction:Horde"]="Recovering the skull strikes an early blow against Zalazane's twisted grip over the Echo Isles just off the coast of Durotar."},kw={"circle of power","darkspear","echo isles","gadrin","minshina","sen'jin village","skull","zalazane"},rel={"quest:808","npc:master-gadrin","subzone:echo-isles","quest:826","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Minshina's Skull","Minshina's Skull (quest)"}}
E["item:reagent-pouch-shaman"] = {t="item",n="Reagent Pouch (shaman)",z="durotar",s="A reagent pouch carried by Burning Blade cultists lurking in the crags of Durotar. Shaman seeking to communing with fire require these gathered spell components to distill their initial fire sapta.",h="A reagent pouch carried by Burning Blade cultists lurking in the crags of Durotar.",sec={{t="Components of the Flame",b="To forge a fire sapta and attune a young shaman to the spirits of flame, specific ritual catalysts are vital. Cultists of the Burning Blade carry small satchels stocked with reagents tailored for demonic fire conjurations. The hermit Telf Joolam uses these gathered powders and oils, combined with the fire tar of Razormane quilboar, to craft the draught needed to grant sight into the realm of fire.",sp=0},{t="Tainted Sources, Pure Vision",b="Though the Burning Blade perverts flame for destruction and fel sorcery, the physical elements within their pouches remain bound to the primal nature of heat and combustion. Shamanic philosophy maintains that all elemental forces exist in tension: fire is both creator and destroyer. By taking the cultists' stolen tools, a shaman reclaims the elemental medium to awaken genuine communion with the spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the reagent pouch used for?",a="It serves as an essential material for Telf Joolam to brew a fire sapta. Drinking this elixir grants a shaman the visionary sight needed to seek out the elemental spirits and claim their Fire Totem.",al={"reagent pouch use","what does reagent pouch do","reagent pouch shaman quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where do I find a reagent pouch?",a="The pouch is recovered from Burning Blade cultists nestled inside Dustwind Cave, located in the rocky heights northeast of Razor Hill in Durotar.",al={"reagent pouch drop","where to get reagent pouch","burning blade pouch location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does a shaman need warlock reagents?",a="The Burning Blade stocks their pouches with ingredients steeped in fire magic. Because their rituals rely heavily on flame, their reagents provide ready-made elemental catalysts that can be repurposed to brew the fire sapta.",al={"why warlock items","why burning blade reagents","shaman using fel items"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Reagent Pouch?",a="It is a small satchel carried by cultists of the Burning Blade, packed with the ritual herbs, ashes, and occult catalysts they use to fuel their dark spells. While meant for dark sorcery, the sheer concentration of fiery components makes the entire pouch a potent bundle of raw elemental materials.",al={"what is reagent pouch","reagent pouch lore","burning blade reagent pouch"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does the Reagent Pouch come from?",a="The pouches are assembled and carried by Burning Blade cultists hiding within the caves of Durotar and the Barrens. These warlocks gather and store specific components needed for their destructive rites, keeping them close at hand whenever casting flame and shadow magic.",al={"reagent pouch origin","who made the reagent pouch","where did reagent pouch come from"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Retrieving the pouch is a pivotal rite of passage on the path to earning your Fire Totem, teaching that even corrupted elemental mediums can be reclaimed to serve balance.",["class:Warlock"]="The pouches reflect the standard sorcerous supplies carried by fel cultists, holding ritual elements intended for demonic pyromancy rather than nature communion."},kw={"burning blade","call of fire","durotar","dustwind cave","fire sapta","fire totem","reagent pouch","telf joolam"},rel={"quest:1524","npc:telf-joolam","item:fire-tar","subzone:dustwind-cave","zone:durotar","topic:shaman","topic:warlock"},src={"Reagent Pouch (shaman)","Call of Fire (3)"}}
E["item:rough-quartz"] = {t="item",n="Rough Quartz",z="durotar",s="Rough Quartz is a humble elemental stone gifted to novice shaman by a Minor Manifestation of Earth. Though small and unrefined, it serves as the vital spiritual core needed to craft a shaman's first Earth Totem.",h="Rough Quartz is a humble elemental stone gifted to novice shaman by a Minor Manifestation of Earth.",sec={{t="Heart of the Earth Totem",b="To the untrained eye, rough quartz appears to be nothing more than an ordinary desert pebble. Yet to a shaman communing with the spirits in Durotar or Mulgore, it is an elemental gift offered directly by a Minor Manifestation of Earth. The stone represents endurance, patience, and unwavering strength. When presented to an elder such as Canaga Earthcaller in the Valley of Trials, the quartz is bound into the carved wood of an Earth Totem, acting as the spiritual focus that links the fledgling shaman directly to the living soil of Azeroth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Rough Quartz?",a="It serves as proof that a shaman novice has communed with the elemental earth spirit. An elder shaman uses this pebble as the spiritual core when carving the initiate's very first Earth Totem.",al={"what does rough quartz do","rough quartz use","why do i need rough quartz"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives you the Rough Quartz?",a="It is granted by a Minor Manifestation of Earth after you commune with the spirit during the Call of Earth ritual in Durotar or Mulgore.",al={"where do i get rough quartz","who drops rough quartz"},it="origin"},{q="Who do I bring this stone to in Durotar?",a="Bring it to Canaga Earthcaller, the shaman trainer residing in the Valley of Trials, who will fashion it into your Earth Totem.",al={"where to turn in rough quartz","rough quartz turn in","who takes rough quartz"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Is this quartz used for anything else?",a="No. It is purely a sacred ritual object meant solely for crafting an Earth Totem and holds no use in common trade.",al={"can i sell rough quartz","is rough quartz used in crafting"},it="item",gp=true},{q="What is Rough Quartz?",a="Rough Quartz is a small elemental pebble given to aspiring shaman by a Minor Manifestation of Earth. Though modest in size and appearance, the stone represents an initiate's passing of the rite of earth and communion with the elemental spirit, serving as tangible proof of their bond.",al={"what is rough quartz","rough quartz item","rough quartz meaning"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Canaga Earthcaller want the Rough Quartz?",a="Canaga Earthcaller requires the Rough Quartz as proof that you have heeded the call and communed with the elemental spirit. He uses the pebble as the heart of your first Earth Totem, allowing you to commune further with the earth and cast spells tied directly to its power.",al={"why need rough quartz","rough quartz purpose","why bring rough quartz to canaga"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Rough Quartz represents your very first communion with the element of earth, anchoring your spells and marking your path as a true conduit of the spirits."},kw={"call of earth","canaga earthcaller","earth totem","minor manifestation of earth","rough quartz","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:1516","npc:canaga-earthcaller","npc:minor-manifestation-of-earth","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","zone:mulgore","topic:shaman"},src={"Rough Quartz","Call of Earth (Durotar 3)"}}
E["item:rune-inscribed-parchment"] = {t="item",n="Rune-Inscribed Parchment",z="durotar",s="A written missive delivered to aspiring orc shamans in the Valley of Trials. Penned by the trainer Shikrik and handed out by Gornek, it calls initiates to embrace their role as spiritual leaders and conduits for the elemental spirits.",h="A written missive delivered to aspiring orc shamans in the Valley of Trials.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Spirits",b="Within the sun-baked canyon of the Valley of Trials, new orc shamans begin their training under the watchful gaze of veteran overseers. While performing initial trials for Gornek, an initiate is handed this rune-covered document. Sent directly by Shikrik, the local shamanic instructor, the parchment serves as a formal summons into the deeper mysteries of elemental communion. Orcish culture regards the shaman not merely as a battlefield spellcaster, but as an essential mediator between the living and the ancestors. This brief writ marks the transition from simple brute strength to the disciplined path of ancestral reverence.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Rune-Inscribed Parchment?",a="It is a handwritten message handed to novice orc shamans by Gornek in the Valley of Trials. It directs the reader to report to the shaman trainer Shikrik to begin formal instruction.",al={"rune parchment","what is this item","shaman parchment"},it="identity"},{q="Who wrote the parchment?",a="The parchment was written by Shikrik, the shaman trainer stationed in the Valley of Trials, who wished to instruct young initiates in the ways of the elements and ancestral spirits.",al={"who sent the parchment","parchment author"},it="origin"},{q="Why are shamans considered chosen among the orcs?",a="Orc shamans act as spiritual guides and conduits for their ancestors, listening to elemental spirits to guide their people. Shikrik reminds apprentices that their duty includes both mending allies and wielding the furious wrath of the elements against their foes.",al={"why be a shaman","orc shaman role"}},{q="Why does Shikrik want you to read the Rune-Inscribed Parchment?",a="Shikrik dispatched this message through Gornek to summon you directly to her. Having recognized that you are chosen to guide the spiritual lives of your people, she intends to begin your formal training in communion with ancestors, elemental mastery, and the rites of an orc shaman.",al={"why read rune inscribed parchment","why does shikrik send parchment","purpose of rune-inscribed parchment"},it="why_wanted",rc="Orc",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="This rune-inscribed note marks your very first step along the path of the elements, setting you under Shikrik's tutelage to learn ancestor worship and elemental mastery.",["race:Orc"]="The rediscovery of shamanic tradition is central to the new Horde, and this parchment represents the continuation of ancestral wisdom in Durotar."},kw={"durotar","gornek","parchment","rune-inscribed parchment","shaman","shikrik","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:3089","npc:gornek","topic:shaman","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar"},src={"Rune-Inscribed Parchment","Rune-Inscribed Parchment (Classic)"}}
E["item:rune-inscribed-tablet"] = {t="item",n="Rune-Inscribed Tablet",z="durotar",s="A Rune-Inscribed Tablet is a stone message delivered to young Darkspear troll shamans in the Valley of Trials. Handed over by Gornek, it directs promising mystics to begin formal communion with the elements under the tutelage of the orc trainer Shikrik.",h="A Rune-Inscribed Tablet is a stone message delivered to young Darkspear troll shamans in the Valley of Trials.",sec={{t="A Summons to the Spirits",b="Carved with elemental runes, this tablet serves as a formal invitation for burgeoning troll shamans taking their first steps in Durotar. When an initiate demonstrates their mettle in the Valley of Trials, the overseer Gornek presents the stone, sent by the troll shaman Ishi-yo to direct the initiate to the shaman trainer Shikrik. For the Darkspear trolls—who hold deep spiritual traditions of their own—the tablet marks the beginning of their shared path with the orcs, bridging ancient troll mysticism with the revitalized shamanic heritage championed by Warchief Thrall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Rune-Inscribed Tablet used for?",a="The tablet is an introductory message delivered by Gornek to young troll shamans in the Valley of Trials. It instructs the initiate to present themselves to Shikrik, the local shaman trainer, to begin their formal spiritual education.",al={"tablet purpose","what does the tablet do","rune tablet use"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who sends the tablet?",a="The tablet is signed by Ishi-yo, the troll shaman who taught the initiate their first lessons. It sends them on to Shikrik, the orc shaman trainer stationed just outside the Den in the Valley of Trials, who already knows they are coming.",al={"who wrote the tablet","tablet sender","who carved it"},it="origin"},{q="Who receives this tablet?",a="Only newly arrived Darkspear troll shamans receive this specific tablet from Gornek as their initial class summons in Durotar.",al={"who gets rune-inscribed tablet","which class gets the tablet"},it="target"},{q="What is the Rune-Inscribed Tablet?",a="The Rune-Inscribed Tablet is a written summons directed to aspiring troll shamans training within the Valley of Trials. Marked with shamanic runes, it serves as a personal message passed through Gornek to introduce promising recruits directly to their local trainer.",al={"what is rune-inscribed tablet","rune inscribed tablet lore","what is this tablet"},it="identity",rc="Troll",add=true},{q="Why does Shikrik want you to receive the Rune-Inscribed Tablet?",a="Shikrik sends the tablet to bring young shaman initiates into her tutelage. Recognizing your potential, she wants to ground you in communion with the elements and ancestral spirits, preparing you to eventually guide and protect Horde settlements just as Thrall guides the Horde itself.",al={"why does shikrik send the tablet","why do i need this tablet","shikrik rune inscribed tablet"},it="why_wanted",rc="Troll",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The tablet represents a shaman's first official step toward mastering the elements of earth, fire, water, and air, reminding students that their strength flows from ancestral spirits.",["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, answering the summons of an orc trainer highlights the growing bond and shared spiritual path between the trolls and their new Horde allies."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","gornek","rune-inscribed tablet","shaman","shikrik","trainer","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:3084","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","npc:gornek","topic:shaman","topic:troll","npc:thrall","topic:horde"},src={"Rune-Inscribed Tablet","Rune-Inscribed Tablet (quest)"}}
E["item:sack-of-supplies"] = {t="item",n="Sack of Supplies",z="durotar",s="These supply sacks belong to a caravan shipment intended for the goblin engineer Rezlak outside Orgrimmar. Transported across Durotar, the goods were intercepted by the Dustwind harpies roosting in the crags of Razorwind Canyon.",h="These supply sacks belong to a caravan shipment intended for the goblin engineer Rezlak outside Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Plundered Caravan",b="Rezlak, an engineer contracted out of Ratchet by Gazlowe, relies on regular caravans through Durotar to supply his construction efforts for the Horde. Durotar's wilderness, however, is far from tame. When a promised shipment passed near the canyon road south of Orgrimmar, it was ambushed and pillaged by the local Dustwind harpies. The vicious creatures hauled the cargo deep into their roosts within Razorwind Canyon, scattering the sacks among the dirt and scree alongside harpy nesting sites.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside these supply sacks?",a="The sacks contain construction materials and trade goods shipped on behalf of Gazlowe's engineering operations to support Orcish building projects near Orgrimmar. Without them, Rezlak is stranded with no supplies to finish his work.",al={"supply sack contents","what are in the sacks","rezlak supplies"},it="identity"},{q="Who stole the supplies?",a="The supplies were stolen by the Dustwind harpies, a savage avian race that infests the high crevices and ravines of Razorwind Canyon.",al={"who took the supplies","who stole the sacks"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Rezlak?",a="Rezlak is a goblin engineer dispatched by Gazlowe from Ratchet to assist the Horde with building and line infrastructure in Durotar.",al={"who is rezlak","rezlak lore"},it="people"},{q="Where do these sacks of supplies come from?",a="These sacks were part of a shipment sent to Durotar on behalf of Gazlowe and his goblin engineers. Intended to aid the orcs in building and maintaining their settlements, the caravan carrying them was ambushed and looted along the road before it could reach its destination.",al={"sack of supplies origin","where did the supplies come from","who made supply sack"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does Rezlak want these supply sacks?",a="Rezlak cannot carry out the construction work Gazlowe assigned him without proper gear and materials. Harpies from Razorwind Canyon plundered the caravan carrying his tools and provisions, leaving the goblin foreman completely stalled until someone recovers the stolen cargo.",al={"why rezlak wants supplies","why need supply sacks","winds in the desert supplies why"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Recovering lost supplies from local predators ensures that frontier construction around the fledgling capital of Orgrimmar proceeds without costly delays."},kw={"durotar","dustwind harpies","gazlowe","razorwind canyon","rezlak","sack of supplies"},rel={"quest:834","quest:835","npc:rezlak","subzone:razorwind-canyon","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:razor-hill"},src={"Sack of Supplies","Winds in the Desert"}}
E["item:sarkoth-s-mangled-claw"] = {t="item",n="Sarkoth's Mangled Claw",z="durotar",s="Sarkoth's Mangled Claw is the severed pincer of Sarkoth, a monstrous scorpid stalking the southern bluffs of the Valley of Trials. Heavily scarred by the dying troll Hana'zua, the trophy serves as both proof of the beast's death and a final consolation for a wounded hunter's pride.",h="Sarkoth's Mangled Claw is the severed pincer of Sarkoth, a monstrous scorpid stalking the southern bluffs of...",sec={{t="A Trophy of Vengeance",b="While hunting in the Valley of Trials, a young Darkspear troll named Hana'zua engaged a massive scorpid known as Sarkoth. Before Sarkoth's venomous stinger pierced his chest and left him bleeding under a nearby tree, Hana'zua landed a crushing blow against the creature's massive pincer. Severing this battered limb offers undeniable proof that the monstrous scorpid has been slain. For Hana'zua, holding the mangled claw confirms that his desperate strike left a lasting mark, providing a fleeting spark of warrior's honor as venom courses through his veins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the claw mangled?",a="The claw was crushed during a desperate duel between Sarkoth and the troll hunter Hana'zua. Although Sarkoth landed a mortal sting on Hana'zua's chest, the troll struck a ferocious blow against the beast's pincer before it closed around his leg.",al={"why broken claw","who crushed sarkoth claw","mangled claw lore"}},{q="Who wants Sarkoth's Mangled Claw?",a="Hana'zua asks for the claw. He lies mortally poisoned beneath a tree in the northern reaches of the Valley of Trials, desperate for proof that his final enemy has been slain before he succumbs to the scorpid's venom.",al={"who needs sarkoth claw","who turned in to","hanazua claw"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where did this claw come from?",a="It is taken from Sarkoth, a large, aggressive scorpid that prowls the elevated plateau along the southern cliffs of the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",al={"sarkoth location","where is sarkoth","where to get mangled claw"},it="origin"},{q="What is Sarkoth's Mangled Claw?",a="It is the severed pincer of Sarkoth, an unusually large and vicious scorpid prowling the southern plateau above the Valley of Trials. The claw bears severe, splintering damage inflicted by the dying Darkspear troll Hana'zua during their mortal struggle, serving as undeniable proof that the monstrous beast has finally been slain.",al={"what is sarkoths mangled claw","sarkoth claw identity","mangled claw"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Bringing the mangled claw to Hana'zua grants a dying Darkspear kinsman a measure of dignity, letting him know his final strike scarred the beast before the end.",["faction:Horde"]="For initiates in the Valley of Trials, claiming this trophy marks one of the earliest tests of courage and martial strength in the harsh wilds of Durotar."},kw={"claw","durotar","hana'zua","mangled claw","sarkoth","scorpid","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:804","npc:hana-zua","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Sarkoth's Mangled Claw","Sarkoth (quest)"}}
E["item:searing-collar"] = {t="item",n="Searing Collar",z="durotar",s="Searing Collars are ritual torcs worn by members of the Burning Blade cult hiding within Skull Rock in Durotar. Heated to burn the wearer's flesh, they are used by the cultists to attune themselves to demonic powers.",h="Searing Collars are ritual torcs worn by members of the Burning Blade cult hiding within Skull Rock in...",sec={{t="Instruments of Corruption",b="Within the shadowy cavern of Skull Rock, just east of Orgrimmar, the Burning Blade gathers to perform dark rituals. Cultists, neophytes, and thugs of the cult don Searing Collars around their necks, willingly subjecting themselves to scorching heat that brands and sears their skin. The hermit Margoz studies these cruel devices, theorizing that the burning sensation and dark enchantments bound to the metal serve to attune the wearers directly to demonic energies. Investigating the collars reveals that they are a significant conduit of demonic corruption creeping into orc society right under the Horde's nose.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Searing Collar?",a="A Searing Collar is a ritual band worn around the neck by Burning Blade cultists. It burns into the wearer's flesh and channels demonic energy to attune the cultist to dark magic.",al={"what are searing collars","searing collar lore","what does the collar do"},it="identity"},{q="Who wears these collars?",a="They are worn by members of the Burning Blade cult hiding inside Skull Rock, including cultists, fanatics, thugs, apprentices, and neophytes.",al={"who uses them","who drops searing collars","burning blade collars"},it="people"},{q="Why do the cultists burn their own flesh?",a="The Burning Blade uses the searing metal as a ritual medium. By enduring the burns and demonic enchantment, cultists attune their physical bodies and spirits to demonic power.",al={"why burn their flesh","why wear searing collar","purpose of collar"},it="purpose"},{q="Who wants to inspect the Searing Collars?",a="Margoz, an investigator camping in Durotar, collects the collars to study their enchantments and uncover the secrets behind the Burning Blade's dark influence.",al={"who needs searing collars","who is studying the collars","margoz collars"},it="why_wanted"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks recognize the Searing Collars as crude yet effective conduits for channeling fel corruption directly into mortal flesh.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs striving to free their people from the legacy of demonic servitude, finding cultists using these collars on Durotar's doorstep is a grim reminder that the shadow still lingers."},kw={"burning blade","demon","durotar","fel","margoz","searing collar","skull rock"},rel={"quest:827","quest:828","quest:809","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Searing Collar","Skull Rock (Classic)"}}
E["item:simple-tablet"] = {t="item",n="Simple Tablet",z="durotar",s="The Simple Tablet is a written missive handed to novice troll warriors arriving in the Valley of Trials. Delivered by Gornek, it directs the fledgling combatant to present themselves to Frang, the local warrior trainer.",h="The Simple Tablet is a written missive handed to novice troll warriors arriving in the Valley of Trials.",sec={{t="A Summons to Battle",b="Within the harsh red bounds of the Valley of Trials, new recruits are quickly set to work. For young trolls seeking the path of the warrior, Gornek passes along this simple slate or parchment. Written by the troll Tar'sere and addressed to Frang, the master-at-arms resting near the Den, it serves as an official introduction to martial training in Durotar. It urges the recruit to step forward, present themselves, and prove their willingness to swing weapons under the banner of the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Simple Tablet?",a="It is an introductory written message delivered by Gornek to aspiring troll warriors in the Valley of Trials. It bids them to read it and seek out Frang for professional combat training.",al={"simple tablet","what is this tablet","troll warrior tablet"},it="identity"},{q="Who sends the tablet?",a="The message is signed by the troll Tar'sere, who sends the recruit to Frang, the warrior trainer stationed outside the Den in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who sent simple tablet","who wrote the tablet","tablet sender"},it="origin"},{q="Where do I take the tablet?",a="Bring it to Frang, who can be found resting in the shade outside the entrance of the Den in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who do i give simple tablet to","where to bring tablet","frang location"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who receives this tablet?",a="The Simple Tablet is provided specifically to troll warriors beginning their rites of passage in the Valley of Trials.",al={"can anyone get simple tablet","which class gets simple tablet"},it="target"},{q="Why does Frang send you the Simple Tablet?",a="Frang sends the tablet to summon new troll warriors arriving in the Valley of Trials. As a veteran trainer resting in the shade outside the Den, he wants to welcome you into the Horde's ranks, introduce you to martial discipline, and offer his combat training to prepare you for the challenges ahead.",al={"why simple tablet","why does frang want me","purpose of simple tablet"},it="why_wanted",rc="Troll",add=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="The tablet marks a troll warrior's formal introduction to Frang, initiating their combat instruction within the Horde.",["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls carving out their place alongside the orcs in Durotar, receiving the summons signifies their duty to bolster the frontline ranks."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","frang","gornek","simple tablet","the den","valley of trials","warrior trainer"},rel={"quest:3065","npc:gornek","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:warrior","topic:troll","quest:1089"},src={"Simple Tablet","Simple Tablet (quest)"}}
E["item:taming-rod"] = {t="item",n="Taming Rod",z="durotar",s="A Taming Rod is an instructional tool entrusted to novice hunters by their trainers. Infused with simple binding magic, it allows a student to temporarily pacify and command local wildlife to master the fundamentals of beast handling.",h="A Taming Rod is an instructional tool entrusted to novice hunters by their trainers.",sec={{t="A Guide's Training Implement",b="Novice hunters cannot immediately exert the mental force required to bind a wild creature to their will permanently. To bridge that gap, veteran trainers issue specialized Taming Rods. In places like Razor Hill, mentors such as Thotar give aspiring orc and troll hunters these enchanted implements to subdue regional predators—such as dire mottled boars and armored scorpids. The rod temporarily pacifies the beast, allowing the handler to practice issuing commands and fighting alongside an animal companion without the danger of an unbreakable primal bond forming prematurely.",sp=0},{t="A Step Toward Mastery",b="The control granted by a Taming Rod is fleeting, typically lasting only a short while before the magic fades. Each rod is attuned to specific types of wild beasts, serving as a stepping stone through successive trials. Once a novice has proved they can command various wild temperaments—from docile foragers to aggressive venomous hunters—the rod is returned to the trainer. Having demonstrated proper technique, the student is finally taught the innate art of taming, calling, and dismissing lifelong companions without needing an artifact.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Taming Rod used for?",a="A Taming Rod is a training implement given to young hunters by their class trainers. It temporarily pacifies and charms a targeted beast so the student can practice commanding an animal in battle.",al={"what does taming rod do","taming rod use","why do i have a taming rod"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Do I keep the pet I tame with the rod?",a="No. Creatures tamed with a Taming Rod are only under temporary influence for training purposes. Once the rod's enchantment expires or you hand the rod back to your trainer, the bond ends. You learn to permanently tame your own companion only after completing all your trials.",al={"is the pet permanent","do i keep the boar","do i keep the scorpid"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Can I use any Taming Rod on any animal?",a="No. Each rod is enchanted specifically for a particular stage of training and is attuned to a specific target creature, such as a dire mottled boar or an armored scorpid.",al={"does the rod work on anything","taming rod targets"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Can I keep the Taming Rod after completing the training?",a="No. The rod must be returned to your hunter trainer upon completing your assignment. In exchange for returning it after your final trial, the trainer teaches you how to tame, summon, and dismiss beasts on your own.",al={"keep taming rod","can i save the rod"},it="motive",gp=true},{q="What is a Taming Rod?",a="A Taming Rod is an instructional implement entrusted to novice hunters by their trainers. Enchanted to temporarily bend a wild creature's will to your own, it serves as a training aid. Wielding it allows an aspiring hunter to experience the delicate connection required to command wildlife in battle without permanently bonding before their fundamental skills are fully mastered.",al={"what is a taming rod","taming rod item","taming rod lore"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does a hunter want a Taming Rod?",a="Novice hunters require the rod to prove their developing authority over nature. By successfully subduing dangerous beasts like boars or scorpids, you demonstrate the determination and composure necessary to control a feral mind. Once you have shown your trainer that you can direct these creatures in combat, you are taught the true, lasting arts of beast companionship.",al={"why need taming rod","purpose of taming rod","why use taming rod"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="The Taming Rod is the cornerstone of every young hunter's rite of passage, serving as training wheels until they possess the innate willpower to forge lifelong bonds with wild beasts.",["faction:Horde"]="In Durotar and Mulgore, trainers like Thotar use these rods to test whether young recruits have the discipline required to master Kalimdor's harsh wildlife."},kw={"armored scorpid","dire mottled boar","hunter pet","razor hill","taming rod","taming the beast","thotar"},rel={"quest:6061","npc:thotar","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:6081","quest:6065","topic:hunter"},src={"Taming Rod","Taming the Beast (Orc and Troll 1)","Taming the Beast (Orc and Troll 3)"}}
E["item:torch-of-the-dormant-flame"] = {t="item",n="Torch of the Dormant Flame",z="durotar",s="The Torch of the Dormant Flame is a ritual implement carried by young Horde shaman during their communion with fire in Durotar. Awaiting the defeat of a flame manifestation atop the mountain, it serves as a vessel meant to capture primal elemental fire upon the Shrine of the Eternal Flame.",h="The Torch of the Dormant Flame is a ritual implement carried by young Horde shaman during their communion...",sec={{t="Vessel of Awakening",b="A shaman seeking the favor of fire is entrusted with the unlit Torch of the Dormant Flame before ascending the peaks above Durotar. After drinking a spirit-revealing fire sapta, the shaman sees and challenges a Minor Manifestation of Fire upon the mountaintop. Slaying this elemental spirit yields a glowing ember, which is deposited into the weathered brazier of the Shrine of the Eternal Flame. Touching the head of the dormant torch to the resulting white-hot conflagration awakens the wood, transforming it into a burning emblem of elemental mastery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Torch of the Dormant Flame?",a="It is an unlit ceremonial torch given to shaman undertaking the Call of Fire trial. Once a manifestation of fire is defeated and its ember placed in the shrine's brazier, the torch is dipped into the white-hot flames to ignite it with elemental power.",al={"what is dormant flame torch","why do i have this unlit torch","what does the torch do"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does this torch get lit?",a="It is ignited atop the mountain near Telf Joolam in Durotar, specifically at the brazier upon the Shrine of the Eternal Flame, immediately after defeating the Minor Manifestation of Fire.",al={"where to light torch of dormant flame","shrine of eternal flame torch","how to ignite dormant torch"},gp=true},{q="Who provides the unlit torch?",a="The hermit shaman Telf Joolam grants the torch to initiates who have gathered the necessary ritual reagents to prepare the fire sapta.",al={"who gives torch of dormant flame","dormant torch source","call of fire torch giver"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Torch of the Dormant Flame?",a="It is a ceremonial, unlit torch crafted for a shaman's trial during the Call of Fire. Built to receive the wild essence of elemental flame, it remains completely cold and dormant until plunged into the consecrated brazier atop the Shrine of the Dormant Flame, where it catches fire from the essence of a defeated fire manifestation.",al={"torch of the dormant flame","what is dormant torch","dormant flame torch"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why does Telf Joolam need the Torch of the Dormant Flame?",a="The torch serves as the vessel to capture and prove your mastery over fire. By igniting its dormant tip in the sacred brazier with the ember of a vanquished manifestation, you bind the elemental spark into a portable flame. Carrying that newly kindled torch back completes your spiritual communion with the element of fire.",al={"why need torch of dormant flame","why want dormant torch","purpose of dormant flame torch"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The dormant torch represents the initiate's unproven state; only by conquering a living manifestation of flame can a shaman kindle it and earn the right to summon a Fire Totem."},kw={"call of fire","durotar","fire sapta","shaman","shrine of eternal flame","telf joolam","torch of the dormant flame"},rel={"quest:1524","npc:telf-joolam","item:glowing-ember","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Torch of the Dormant Flame","Call of Fire (4)"}}
E["item:ukor-s-burden"] = {t="item",n="Ukor's Burden",z="durotar",s="Ukor's Burden is a heavy bundle of rations hauled out of Razor Hill by a well-meaning orc peon. Intended to feed hungry novices in the Valley of Trials, the unwanted provisions must be hauled back before the wilderness scorpids and raptors pick up the scent.",h="Ukor's Burden is a heavy bundle of rations hauled out of Razor Hill by a well-meaning orc peon.",sec={{t="A Well-Intentioned Mistake",b="Orc peons rarely act on their own initiative, which makes Ukor's errand unusual. Packing a heavy load of provisions from the inn in Razor Hill, he braved the red dust and aggressive wildlife of Durotar to aid young recruits training in the Valley of Trials. To his dismay, the overseers and instructors turned him away—believing that hardship and lean bellies forge true warriors. Trapped outside the canyon's mouth and terrified of the beasts stalking the trail back, Ukor entrusted the sack to passing travelers to return it to Innkeeper Grosk.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Ukor's Burden?",a="It is a heavy pack packed with food and supplies taken from the Razor Hill inn. Ukor gathered the rations hoping to feed the young orcs and trolls undergoing initiation, unaware that the training grounds deliberately restrict outside comfort.",al={"what is in the pack","ukors burden contents","what food is it"},it="item"},{q="Why did the Valley of Trials reject the food?",a="The overseers running the Valley of Trials believe that endurance and deprivation build character in fledgling warriors. As Innkeeper Grosk puts it, starving recruits in training builds spirit, making outside charity unwelcome.",al={"why valley of trials refused food","why didnt they want the food","why wasnt the food needed"},it="motive"},{q="Where does the burden need to go?",a="The supplies belong back on the shelves of the inn in Razor Hill. You must take the sack directly to Innkeeper Grosk, who safely restocks the provisions and offers a drink to whoever hauled it home.",al={"where do i take ukors burden","who wants ukors burden","ukors burden delivery"},it="target"},{q="What is Ukor's Burden?",a="Ukor's Burden is a heavy load of provisions and foodstuffs originally gathered from the inn in Razor Hill. An earnest peon named Ukor packed the bundle himself, intending to deliver relief to the young warriors training in the harsh crags of the Valley of Trials.",al={"what is ukors burden","ukor's burden","ukors burden item"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does Ukor's Burden come from, and who made it?",a="The burden originated at the Razor Hill inn under the care of Innkeeper Grosk. Ukor, a well-meaning orc peon, hauled the load all the way down the road past dangerous scorpions and spiders to reach the proving grounds, only to find his efforts were unwanted.",al={"where did ukors burden come from","who made ukors burden","origin of ukor burden"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Why does anyone want Ukor's Burden?",a="After the trainers in the Valley of Trials turned down the provisions, Innkeeper Grosk needs the food returned to stock back on the shelves in Razor Hill. Terrified of the wild beasts prowling the Durotar wilderness, Ukor relies on passing travelers to carry it safely home.",al={"why does grosk want ukors burden","why return ukors burden","who wants ukor's burden"},it="why_wanted",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The errand illustrates the rigid, survivalist culture Thrall's Horde enforces in Durotar: even simple kindness must defer to the harsh trials required to temper new soldiers."},kw={"durotar","grosk","peon","rations","razor hill","ukor","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:ukor","npc:innkeeper-grosk","quest:2161","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Ukor's Burden","A Peon's Burden"}}
E["item:uncloven-satyr-hoof"] = {t="item",n="Uncloven Satyr Hoof",z="durotar",s="An Uncloven Satyr Hoof is a swollen, solid hoof harvested from the satyrs lurking in Ashenvale. Saturated with corrupt magical energy leeched from the ancient forest, these grim trophies serve as potent crafting components for Darkspear troll armorers.",h="An Uncloven Satyr Hoof is a swollen, solid hoof harvested from the satyrs lurking in Ashenvale.",sec={{t="Leeched Power",b="Satyrs haunt the corrupted groves of northeastern Ashenvale, feeding directly upon the ancient forest's magical purity. As they gorge themselves on this essence, the corruption distorts their demonic physiology, causing their hooves to swell and lose their natural cleft. These solid, uncloven hooves become dense reservoirs of absorbed energy, holding volatile power that can be harvested by skilled shamans and leatherworkers.",sp=0},{t="Crafting the Brutal Armor",b="Down on the coast of Durotar in Sen'jin Village, the troll armorer Ula'elek knows how to turn demonic corruption into strength for Horde champions. By taking the hooves of these sated satyrs, he leeches out the trapped woodland magic, channeling the stolen power into the forging of brutal gauntlets designed to protect young warriors facing the rigors of Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are these satyr hooves uncloven?",a="Satyrs in Ashenvale feed continuously on the forest's sacred magic, corrupting and leeching its power. Satyrs that have gorged themselves the most develop heavily swollen hooves that lose their cleft, sealing the dense, stolen energy inside.",al={"why are they not cloven","uncloven hoof meaning","swollen hooves"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Uncloven Satyr Hooves be found?",a="They are collected from satyrs inhabiting the corrupted ruins and tainted groves of northeastern Ashenvale, such as Satyrnaar and Night Run.",al={"where to farm hooves","satyr hoof location","which satyrs drop hooves"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who wants these hooves in Durotar?",a="Ula'elek, a craftsman residing in Sen'jin Village along the southern coast of Durotar, requests seven of them to extract their stored magic.",al={"who needs satyr hooves","satyr hoof quest giver","what to do with hooves"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What are the hooves used to craft?",a="Ula'elek draws the corrupt forest power out of the hooves to enchant and forge a pair of sturdy, magic-infused brutal gauntlets.",al={"what are they used for","hoof crafting reward","brutal gauntlets materials"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does an Uncloven Satyr Hoof come from?",a="These hooves are taken directly from the satyrs lurking in northeastern Ashenvale. Rather than being crafted, they are natural body parts warped by dark gluttony. Satyrs in the forest gorge themselves on Ashenvale's pure natural energies, and the demons that consume the greatest surplus of this stolen magic develop distinctive swollen, uncloven hooves.",al={"where do uncloven satyr hooves come from","who made uncloven satyr hoof","source of satyr hooves"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Young warriors seeking renown are directed by Horde trainers to commission specialized armor from Sen'jin Village, hunting down Ashenvale's satyrs to prove their martial prowess.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear crafters like Ula'elek excel at turning dark or hostile energies into functional gear, leeching power from demonic foes rather than letting it go to waste."},kw={"ashenvale","durotar","gauntlets","hoof","satyr","sen'jin","ula'elek","uncloven"},rel={"quest:1842","npc:ula-elek","quest:1843","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:ashenvale","zone:durotar","topic:satyr"},src={"Uncloven Satyr Hoof","Satyr Hooves"}}
E["item:venomtail-antidote"] = {t="item",n="Venomtail Antidote",z="durotar",s="Venomtail Antidote is a specialized concoction brewed to neutralize the lethal toxins of Durotar's venomtail scorpids. Prepared by Kor'ghan in Orgrimmar, it serves as an urgent remedy for Rhinag, an afflicted troll scout stranded near the northwestern border of Durotar.",h="Venomtail Antidote is a specialized concoction brewed to neutralize the lethal toxins of Durotar's venomtail...",sec={{t="A Race Against the Venom",b="The arid expanse of Durotar crawls with dangerous wildlife, none more hazardous to careless wanderers than the local scorpids. A deep sting from a venomtail delivers a virulent poison capable of killing an adult warrior within an hour. When the troll Rhinag found himself envenomed far from aid near the northwestern border, his only survival lay in obtaining a specialized remedy from Kor'ghan, an apothecary sequestered deep within Orgrimmar's subterranean Cleft of Shadow.",sp=0},{t="Kor'ghan's Cure",b="Securing the antidote requires navigating the underbelly of Orgrimmar to locate Kor'ghan. Knowledgeable in desert toxins and harsh remedies, Kor'ghan prepares the vial to purge the venom before it turns fatal. Once delivered, the draught halts the venom's progression, sparing Rhinag a humiliating death in the wilderness—though Kor'ghan demands further trials and hunts from the scout to atone for his carelessness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Venomtail Antidote used for?",a="The antidote neutralizes the deadly venom inflicted by venomtail scorpids. It is specifically sought to cure Rhinag, an envenomed troll stranded along the northwestern border of Durotar who has only a short time left to live.",al={"antidote purpose","who needs venomtail antidote","what does venomtail antidote do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who brews the Venomtail Antidote?",a="The antidote is prepared by Kor'ghan, who resides in the Cleft of Shadow beneath Orgrimmar. He understands the potency of Durotar's scorpids and knows how to counteract their stings.",al={"who makes the antidote","where to get venomtail antidote","kor'ghan antidote"},it="origin"},{q="Why is time so critical when obtaining the antidote?",a="Venomtail poison works rapidly through the blood, leaving Rhinag less than an hour to live from the moment he is stung. Securing the antidote and rushing it back across Durotar is the only way to prevent his death.",al={"why hurry antidote","how long does rhinag have","venomtail poison timer"},it="danger"},{q="Why is Rhinag hesitant to seek help in Sen'jin Village?",a="Rhinag admits that falling victim to a common scorpid is deeply embarrassing. He fears returning to Sen'jin Village in his weakened state, believing his kin would mock his carelessness and stupidity.",al={"why not go to sen'jin","rhinag pride","why hide in durotar"},it="motive"},{q="What is Venomtail Antidote?",a="Venomtail Antidote is a specialized concoction crafted to neutralize the deadly poison of Durotar's venomtail scorpids. Without it, anyone stung deeply by these aggressive beasts faces a rapid and agonizing death as the toxin spreads through their blood.",al={"what is venomtail antidote","venomtail antidote info","venomtail cure"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Troll pride runs deep, and Rhinag would rather risk dying alone in the wastes than face the open mockery of Sen'jin Village for being bested by a scorpid.",["faction:Horde"]="Even within the heart of Durotar, the unforgiving desert tests young Horde adventurers, requiring swift coordination between wilderness scouts and city apothecaries."},kw={"antidote","cleft of shadow","cure","durotar","kor'ghan","orgrimmar","rhinag","scorpid","venomtail"},rel={"quest:812","quest:813","npc:rhinag","npc:kor-ghan","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Venomtail Antidote","Need for a Cure"}}
E["item:venomtail-poison-sac"] = {t="item",n="Venomtail Poison Sac",z="durotar",s="A Venomtail Poison Sac is a biological organ harvested from scorpids native to the arid expanses of Durotar. While containing a virulent toxin capable of incapacitating an unwary hunter, it is also the vital ingredient required to brew an effective counter-agent.",h="A Venomtail Poison Sac is a biological organ harvested from scorpids native to the arid expanses of Durotar.",sec={{t="A Deadly Toxin and Its Remedy",b="The scorpids prowling the red rocks of Durotar—chiefly the Venomtail Scorpid, alongside mutated varieties like the Corrupted Scorpid and the notorious Death Flayer—produce a fast-acting, debilitating venom. Stored within specialized tail sacs, this poison can quickly overwhelm even seasoned warriors if left untreated. Ironically, the very sacs that deliver this lethal sting contain the primary compounds necessary to synthesize an antidote. When the hunter Rhinag fell victim to a sting outside Orgrimmar, local alchemists required four fresh poison sacs to concoct the remedy needed to neutralize the venom coursing through his veins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures carry these poison sacs?",a="They are harvested from scorpids in Durotar, primarily the Venomtail Scorpids found roaming near the outskirts of Orgrimmar, as well as Corrupted Scorpids and the rare Death Flayer.",al={"who drops venomtail poison sac","where to get venomtail poison sac","which scorpids have poison sacs"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="What is the poison sac used for?",a="The sacs are brought to Kor'ghan in Orgrimmar to distill a specialized antidote. This cure is urgently needed to treat the hunter Rhinag, who was stung and poisoned while hunting without proper preparation.",al={"venomtail sac use","why do i need venomtail poison sac"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who can brew the antidote from these sacs?",a="Kor'ghan, located within Orgrimmar, knows the proper method to refine the raw venom from four intact sacs into a curative draft before the poison proves fatal.",al={"who brews the antidote","where to turn in venomtail sacs","kor'ghan venomtail"}},{q="What is a Venomtail Poison Sac?",a="A Venomtail Poison Sac is the venom-producing organ harvested from the dangerous scorpids that prowl Durotar, most notably the venomtail scorpids lurking near the gates of Orgrimmar. The fluid inside carries an exceptionally potent and fast-acting toxin, making the creatures a deadly threat to any careless hunter who wanders the arid red wastes.",al={"what is venomtail poison sac","venomtail poison sac lore","about venomtail sac"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does a Venomtail Poison Sac come from?",a="These sacs are harvested directly from the scorpids indigenous to the harsh plains of Durotar, including venomtail scorpids, corrupted scorpids, and death flayers. They are natural anatomical organs of the beasts, biological reservoirs developed by the scorpids to subdue prey and defend against predators in the unforgiving wasteland.",al={"where do venomtail poison sacs come from","who drops venomtail sac","venomtail poison sac origin"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Young Horde adventurers learning the harsh realities of Durotar quickly discover that survival requires understanding the wildlife, as local toxins can easily kill those who rush unprepared into the red wastes.",["class:Hunter"]="Rhinag's misfortune serves as an object lesson for hunters: pursuing dangerous beasts without understanding their venom or carrying proper remedies beforehand can easily cost a tracker their life."},kw={"antidote","durotar","kor'ghan","poison","rhinag","sac","scorpid","venomtail"},rel={"quest:813","quest:812","item:venomtail-antidote","npc:kor-ghan","npc:rhinag","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Venomtail Poison Sac","Finding the Antidote"}}
E["item:vile-familiar-head"] = {t="item",n="Vile Familiar Head",z="durotar",s="A Vile Familiar Head is a gruesome trophy collected from the feral impish creatures dwelling near the Burning Blade Coven in the Valley of Trials. Young Horde warlocks gather them under the guidance of Ruzan as proof of their combat readiness before learning to bind their first demonic minions. The heads serve as a grim test of discipline, showing that an apprentice understands the lethality of the beings they intend to summon.",h="A Vile Familiar Head is a gruesome trophy collected from the feral impish creatures dwelling near the Burning...",sec={{t="A Gruesome Lesson in Demonology",b="Within the sun-baked canyon of the Valley of Trials, the warlock trainer Ruzan demands six Vile Familiar Heads from novices seeking to learn the art of summoning. The vile familiars that loiter outside the Burning Blade Coven are vicious, fiery imps whose diminutive stature conceals dangerous elemental cunning. Ruzan requires prospective summoners to face these fiends in battle and sever their heads to prove they can subdue and command demonic life rather than be overpowered by it. Because warlocks are barely tolerated within Thrall's Horde, training requires extreme caution; reckless novices who perish to their own conjurations only deepen the dishonor and suspicion cast upon practitioners of the dark arts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Vile Familiar Heads used for?",a="They serve as proof of martial prowess for novice warlocks in the Valley of Trials. The trainer Ruzan requires six of these severed heads before he will instruct an apprentice in the ritual of summoning their first imp minion.",al={"vile familiar head purpose","what are these heads for","ruzan quest item"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where do vile familiars come from?",a="They congregate around the mouth and interior of a cave to the northeast in the Valley of Trials, an encampment harboring the secretive and malevolent Burning Blade Coven.",al={"vile familiar location","where to find vile familiars","burning blade coven cave"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Ruzan make young warlocks collect these heads?",a="Ruzan believes that no one should summon a creature they cannot overpower in combat. Because imps are deceptive and throw volatile fire, defeating them face-to-face ensures the aspiring warlock understands the threat posed by the demonic entities they seek to command.",al={"why collect heads","ruzan motive","why kill familiars first"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How does the Horde view warlocks who collect such trophies?",a="Warlocks are merely tolerated rather than embraced by the modern Horde. Past betrayals tied to fel magic left a legacy of deep distrust, forcing trainers like Ruzan to ensure apprentices are disciplined and quiet in their studies.",al={"are warlocks accepted","horde warlock reputation","distrusted warlocks"},it="conflict"},{q="What is a Vile Familiar Head?",a="It is the severed head of a vile familiar, one of the minor impish demons found lurking outside the Burning Blade Coven in the Valley of Trials. For a novice warlock studying in Durotar, carrying these grisly trophies serves as proof of having defeated an imp in direct combat.",al={"what is vile familiar head","vile familiar head item","vile familiar trophy"},it="identity",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Collecting these heads marks a warlock's very first step toward mastery over the Nether, earning the right to summon and bind an imp into servitude.",["faction:Horde"]="Even in Durotar's training grounds, warlocks practice their arts on the fringes, mindful that the Horde watches their demonic pursuits with lingering suspicion."},kw={"burning blade coven","durotar","imp","ruzan","valley of trials","vile familiar","vile familiar head","warlock quest"},rel={"quest:792","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:burning-blade-coven","topic:warlock","zone:durotar","topic:horde","quest:1089"},src={"Vile Familiar Head","Vile Familiars (Warlock)"}}
E["item:zalazane-s-head"] = {t="item",n="Zalazane's Head",z="durotar",s="Zalazane's Head is the grim trophy brought to Master Gadrin to confirm the fall of the traitorous witch doctor Zalazane. Its retrieval marks a crucial step in freeing the Echo Isles from the dark magic holding the Darkspear tribe's home hostage.",h="Zalazane's Head is the grim trophy brought to Master Gadrin to confirm the fall of the traitorous witch...",sec={{t="Proof of the Traitor's End",b="When the witch doctor Zalazane betrayed the Darkspear tribe, he used mind-enslaving hexes to seize control of their island home, driving Vol'jin's people to the mainland shores of Durotar. From the Echo Isles, Zalazane continued to send hexed thralls across the waters to snatch more victims. To assure the anxious refugees in Sen'jin Village that the tyrant's reign of terror had broken, Master Gadrin demanded absolute physical proof of his demise. Returning the severed head not only confirms Zalazane's defeat in battle, but offers the displaced tribe a rare measure of peace and a hope of one day reclaiming their stolen islands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who asks for Zalazane's Head?",a="Master Gadrin, the witch doctor residing in Sen'jin Village on the southern coast of Durotar, asks adventurers to bring him the head as proof that Zalazane has been slain.",al={"who wants zalazane head","zalazane quest giver","gadrin zalazane"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why was Zalazane targeted?",a="Zalazane was once a respected sorcerer among the Darkspear, but his lust for power led him to enslave his kin through mind-controlling magic. He drove the tribe out of the Echo Isles and continued raiding the mainland to capture more Darkspear for his thrall army.",al={"why kill zalazane","what did zalazane do","zalazane lore"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Zalazane found?",a="Zalazane resides on the largest of the Echo Isles off the southeastern coast of Durotar, surrounded by the hexed and voodoo trolls bound to his service.",al={"where is zalazane","zalazane location","echo isles zalazane"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Does bringing the head reclaim the Echo Isles?",a="While killing Zalazane removes the immediate threat of his raids and brings relief to Sen'jin Village, the Echo Isles remain dangerous and littered with his lingering voodoo thralls, leaving the Darkspear still largely based on the mainland.",al={"do trolls get echo isles back","is echo isles reclaimed","echo isles safe"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Zalazane's Head?",a="It is the severed head of the witch doctor Zalazane, taken after striking him down on the Echo Isles. More than a grim trophy, it serves as undeniable proof that the rogue sorcerer who betrayed the Darkspear tribe and drove them from their island home has finally been slain.",al={"zalazane head what is it","what is zalazanes head","zalazane head item"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Where does Zalazane's Head come from?",a="It comes directly from the traitorous witch doctor Zalazane himself, claiming it after defeating him at his camp on the largest of the Echo Isles. It was not crafted, but taken by force to put an end to his enslavement of fellow Darkspear trolls.",al={"who made zalazane head","where do you get zalazanes head","origin of zalazanes head"},it="origin",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, claiming Zalazane's head is a deeply personal act of vengeance and justice against the traitor who drove their people into exile and enslaved their brothers.",["faction:Horde"]="Eliminating Zalazane secures the southern coastline of Durotar for the Horde, preventing dark magic from undermining Thrall's newly founded territories."},kw={"darkspear","echo isles","gadrin","hexed troll","sen'jin village","voodoo troll","zalazane","zalazane's head"},rel={"quest:826","subzone:echo-isles","subzone:sen-jin-village","topic:darkspear-tribe","quest:808","zone:durotar","npc:vol-jin"},src={"Zalazane's Head","Zalazane (quest)"}}
E["npc:canaga-earthcaller"] = {t="npc",n="Canaga Earthcaller",z="durotar",s="Canaga Earthcaller is a Darkspear troll shaman stationed in the sunbaked Valley of Trials. He instructs novice Horde shamans in communing with the spirits of the land and obtaining their first elemental totems. Beyond ritual guidance, he keeps a watchful eye on wounded scouts and emerging threats near the Den.",h="Canaga Earthcaller is a Darkspear troll shaman stationed in the sunbaked Valley of Trials.",sec={{t="Voice of the Land",b="Perched on the red bluffs of the Valley of Trials, Canaga Earthcaller serves as one of the very first spiritual guides for Darkspear trolls and orcs who walk the path of the shaman. While many trainers focus strictly on martial readiness, Canaga teaches newcomers how to quiet their minds and listen to the rumblings of Kalimdor itself, preparing the earth sapta necessary to commune with the spirits.",sp=0},{t="The First Totem",b="Before any fledgling shaman can truly channel the elemental fury of the earth, they must prove their respect and resolve to the spirits. Canaga directs initiates to gather sacred reagents and journey to the local spirit rock in Durotar. Through his guidance, novices drink the earth sapta, behold the elemental spirits firsthand, and earn their Earth Totem.",sp=0},{t="Trouble in the Valley",b="Canaga does not merely dwell on esoteric rituals; he remains attuned to the valley's immediate dangers. When his friend Hana'zua heads north into the valley where the scorpids hunt and fails to return, Canaga directs capable travelers to search for him, ensuring the tribe's scouts are not left to perish in the wilderness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Canaga Earthcaller?",a="Canaga Earthcaller is a Darkspear troll shaman residing in the Valley of Trials. He mentors young shamans taking their first steps in the Horde and helps coordinate aid for fallen scouts nearby.",al={"canaga lore","who is canaga","canaga earthcaller npc"},it="identity"},{q="What does Canaga teach young shamans?",a="Canaga oversees the Call of Earth ritual chain for Horde shamans starting in Durotar. He brews the Earth Sapta, a mystical draught that allows initiates to perceive and speak with the local earth elemental spirit to earn their first totem.",al={"shaman quest durotar","call of earth durotar","canaga quests"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Earth Sapta Canaga prepares?",a="Earth Sapta is a specially brewed spiritual draught crafted from regional reagents. Shamans drink it to open their senses to the hidden spirits of the land, allowing them to communicate directly with elemental manifestations.",al={"what is earth sapta","sapta lore"},it="item"},{q="Why does Canaga send adventurers to find Hana'zua?",a="Hana'zua, a good friend of Canaga's, went out into the valley heading north, where the scorpids hunt, and never returned. The spirits tell Canaga that his friend is not well, so he asks adventurers to search for him and lend assistance.",al={"canaga hanazua","why find hanazua"},it="motive"},{q="Why is a troll training shamans in an orcish proving ground?",a="Following the Third War, the Darkspear tribe integrated closely with Thrall's Horde and settled alongside the orcs in Durotar. Troll shamans and warriors now train side by side with young orcs within the Valley of Trials.",al={"why troll in valley of trials","darkspear in valley of trials"},it="why_here"},{q="Where can Canaga Earthcaller be found?",a="Canaga sits on the rock plateaus overlooking the eastern paths of the Valley of Trials, just south of the main training hub.",al={"canaga location","where is canaga"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Canaga Earthcaller on?",a="Canaga serves the Horde, guiding fledging shamans of both the Darkspear trolls and the orcs. Stationed in the Valley of Trials, he aids young initiates in forging their initial communion with the elemental spirits of Durotar on behalf of Warchief Thrall's newly established realm.",al={"canaga earthcaller faction","is canaga horde","who does canaga serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Canaga Earthcaller want?",a="Canaga seeks to ensure that emerging shamans properly attune to the spirits of the earth. He tests hopeful initiates by tasking them to gather sacred reagents, drink the Earth Sapta, commune directly with local elemental manifestations, and rescue missing allies like his fellow troll Hana'zua.",al={"what does canaga want","canaga earthcaller goal","canaga purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Who is Canaga Earthcaller tied to?",a="Canaga belongs to the Darkspear tribe and collaborates directly with the orcish shamanic teachers in the Valley of Trials. He also maintains ties to Hana'zua, a scout sent north whose safety concerns him when reports of quillboar aggression arise.",al={"canaga earthcaller ties","who does canaga work with","canaga allies"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Canaga is your very first spiritual mentor in Durotar, preparing the Earth Sapta so you can commune with the elements and claim your Earth Totem.",["race:Troll"]="As one of the prominent Darkspear figures in the Valley of Trials, Canaga ensures that troll recruits are looked after, including dispatched scouts like Hana'zua.",["race:Orc"]="Canaga works side by side with orcish instructors in the valley, helping young orcs bind their spirit to the harsh soil of their new homeland."},kw={"call of earth","canaga","darkspear","durotar","earth sapta","earthcaller","hana'zua","shaman","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:1516","quest:1462","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","npc:hana-zua","topic:troll"},src={"Canaga Earthcaller"}}
E["npc:elder-runetotem"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Runetotem",z="durotar",s="Elder Runetotem is an ancestral tauren spirit appearing outside Razor Hill in Durotar during the Lunar Festival. As one of the revered elders of the Horde, she offers wisdom and her blessing to travelers who seek her out across the red canyons.",h="Elder Runetotem is an ancestral tauren spirit appearing outside Razor Hill in Durotar during the Lunar...",sec={{t="A Spirit in Durotar",b="Though ancestral tauren spirits are typically tied to the grassy plains and sacred burial grounds of Mulgore, Elder Runetotem lingers far from the pastures of her people. She manifests beside the dusty settlement of Razor Hill in Durotar. To young orcs and wandering adventurers, her ethereal presence serves as a bridge between the ancient traditions of the Shu'halo and the harsh new home the Horde has carved along the Great Sea.",sp=0},{t="Ancestral Honors",b="During the Lunar Festival, the spirits of great leaders, shamans, and heroes manifest throughout the world to commune with the living. Elder Runetotem represents the Runetotem line—a lineage known for deep reverence for the Earth Mother and spiritual communion. Travelers honoring her presence are granted ancestral tokens and her spiritual blessing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Runetotem?",a="Elder Runetotem is a ghostly tauren ancestor who manifests near Razor Hill in Durotar. She is one of the honored elders who returns during the Lunar Festival to greet travelers and grant ancestral blessings.",al={"elder runetotem lore","who is the tauren ghost in razor hill","runetotem ghost"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a tauren spirit located in Durotar?",a="While most tauren ancestral spirits are rooted in Mulgore, the spirits of the Lunar Festival wander far and wide across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms. Her presence in Razor Hill allows Horde travelers passing through Durotar to pay their respects to the wisdom of the Earth Mother's children.",al={"why is runetotem in razor hill","tauren ghost durotar"},it="why_here"},{q="What connection does she have to the Runetotem tribe?",a="She bears the name of the Runetotem clan, one of the prominent tauren lineages renowned for their shamans, spiritual guides, and connections to the natural world.",al={"runetotem tribe elder","runetotem family"},it="ties"},{q="What does speaking with her grant?",a="Speaking with Elder Runetotem honors her memory during the Lunar Festival, rewarding adventurers with a Coin of Ancestry and a temporary blessing from the spirits.",al={"what does elder runetotem give","runetotem reward"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Elder Runetotem on?",a="Elder Runetotem stands with the Horde and her tauren kin. As an honored ancestral spirit, she offers her ancient wisdom and blessings to adventurers who respect the ways of the ancestors and walk through Horde lands.",al={"is elder runetotem horde","elder runetotem faction","elder runetotem side"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Elder Runetotem want?",a="She seeks to share the remembrance and reverence of the tauren people with travelers passing through Razor Hill. By reaching out to the living, she reminds travelers of the ancestral spirits watching over the lands and keeping ancient traditions alive.",al={"what does elder runetotem seek","why talk to elder runetotem","elder runetotem goal"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Finding a venerable ancestor of the Runetotem tribe so far from Mulgore is a humbling reminder that the spirits of the Shu'halo watch over their allies across all lands.",["faction:Horde"]="Standing outside the heavily fortified settlement of Razor Hill, her presence embodies the spiritual alliance between the orcs of Durotar and the tauren of Mulgore."},kw={"coin of ancestry","durotar","elder runetotem","lunar festival","razor hill","runetotem","tauren ghost"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:8670","topic:tauren","zone:mulgore","subzone:red-rocks"},src={"Elder Runetotem"}}
E["npc:foreman-thazz-ril"] = {t="npc",n="Foreman Thazz'ril",z="durotar",s="Foreman Thazz'ril is an orc labor supervisor stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Tasked with keeping peons on schedule and maintaining basic infrastructure for young warriors, he is perpetually frustrated by lazy laborers and nearby cultist activity.",h="Foreman Thazz'ril is an orc labor supervisor stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",sec={{t="Keeping the Peons in Line",b="Building a new home in the harsh red rock of Durotar requires unending physical labor. In the Valley of Trials, Foreman Thazz'ril oversees the peons chopping lumber and gathering materials needed to support both the encampment and the wider Horde war effort. Unfortunately for Thazz'ril, peons are notoriously prone to slacking off and taking naps under the desert sun. To keep construction moving, he regularly enlists newly arrived recruits to give the slumbering workers a brisk wallop with his trusty blackjack, instilling obedience through blunt persuasion.",sp=0},{t="A Lost Pick in Dangerous Hands",b="Thazz'ril's responsibilities also involve surveying the valley's mineral resources, though that duty led to an embarrassing misstep. While scouting the cave known as the Burning Blade Coven, he was forced to flee from the dark cultists lurking inside, accidentally abandoning his treasured enchanted pick. Too cautious to retrieve it himself amidst the gathering warlocks and their demonic minions, he relies on young Horde aspirants to venture into the depths and return his tool.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Foreman Thazz'ril?",a="Foreman Thazz'ril is an orc labor overseer in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. He is responsible for managing work crews, chopping lumber, and surveying the region for useful resources to aid the Horde's settlement.",al={"who is thazzril","thazzril valley of trials","foreman thazzril lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Thazz'ril give players a blackjack?",a="The peons under his watch frequently fall asleep under trees rather than harvesting lumber. Thazz'ril provides an enchanted wooden blackjack to knock some discipline into them and send them scurrying back to work.",al={"why hit lazy peons","thazzril blackjack","lazy peons quest lore"}},{q="Why is Thazz'ril's pick inside the Burning Blade cave?",a="While scouting the local caves for mineral veins, Thazz'ril stumbled into the Burning Blade Coven. Spooked by the cultists hiding in the shadows, he beat a hasty retreat and left his valuable enchanted pick behind.",al={"thazzril pick","why is pick in coven","burning blade pick"}},{q="What is his role in the Horde?",a="Thazz'ril is not a frontline soldier or shaman, but a civilian overseer. His duties center on the logistical backbone of Durotar: supervising manual labor, maintaining construction supplies, and keeping peons productive.",al={"is thazzril a soldier","thazzril rank"}},{q="Whose side is Foreman Thazz'ril on?",a="Thazz'ril is loyal to Thrall's Horde. Stationed in the Valley of Trials, he oversees the fundamental labor and resource gathering that helps build Durotar and sustain the training grounds for incoming orc and troll recruits.",al={"foreman thazzril allegiance","thazzril horde","thazzril faction"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Foreman Thazz'ril want?",a="Thazz'ril primarily wants his workers to actually work. Exasperated by lazy peons slacking off around the valley, he recruits young adventurers to wake them up. He also seeks the recovery of his prized enchanted pick, which he unfortunately abandoned near the Burning Blade's coven.",al={"thazzril goals","what does thazzril need","thazzril quest motive"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Foreman Thazz'ril here?",a="He is assigned to the Valley of Trials to direct peon labor and manage local mining and wood-gathering efforts. Maintaining the settlement and keeping raw materials flowing is essential to preparing young warriors before they venture into the wider lands of Durotar.",al={"why is thazzril in the valley of trials","thazzril location reason"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For young orcs coming of age, Thazz'ril provides an early lesson in Horde society: strength on the battlefield is only possible when supported by unglamorous, disciplined labor.",["profession:Mining"]="Thazz'ril values quality mining equipment, as shown by his desperation to recover his enchanted pick from the dark recesses of the Burning Blade Coven."},kw={"blackjack","burning blade","durotar","foreman","lazy peons","thazzril","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:lazy-peons","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:burning-blade-coven","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Foreman Thazz'ril"}}
E["npc:furl-scornbrow"] = {t="npc",n="Furl Scornbrow",z="durotar",s="Furl Scornbrow is an aging orc lookout stationed in the watchtower northwest of Razor Hill. No longer able to fight on the front lines due to his advancing years, he keeps watch over the red canyons of Durotar and crafts sturdy packs for young travelers setting out across the land.",h="Furl Scornbrow is an aging orc lookout stationed in the watchtower northwest of Razor Hill.",sec={{t="Watchman of the Ridge",b="Perched high in the wooden watchtower just northwest of Razor Hill, Furl Scornbrow keeps a quiet vigil over the central plains of Durotar. In the tense early days following the founding of Orgrimmar, sentries like Furl were vital for sounding signal horns against hostile quilboar, centaur, and Kul Tiras interlopers. As Durotar has stabilized and Razor Hill has established firmer borders, emergencies have grown rarer, leaving Furl plenty of quiet hours at his post.",sp=0},{t="A Useful Pair of Hands",b="Furl freely admits that his old bones and fading strength render him useless in battle, but an orc does not easily surrender their purpose. Rather than sitting idle, he puts his hands to work fashioning canvas sacks and packs for fresh recruits who need to carry their supplies. In exchange for coarse thread and practical materials, he equips green adventurers venturing out to prove their worth to the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Furl Scornbrow?",a="Furl Scornbrow is an elderly orc watchman stationed in the lookout tower perched atop the bluffs northwest of Razor Hill. Unable to serve as a front-line warrior due to his age, he watches the horizon for danger and crafts bags for young travelers.",al={"who is furl","furl scornbrow lore","furl in razor hill"},it="identity"},{q="What is Furl's role in Durotar?",a="He mans the signal horn tower watching for invaders approaching Razor Hill. Because Durotar has grown increasingly secure under Horde control, he sounds the alarm far less often, spending his spare time helping incoming recruits organize their gear.",al={"what does furl do","furl purpose"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Furl ask travelers for materials?",a="Furl believes every member of the Horde must carry their weight, regardless of circumstance. Since he can no longer fight, he stitches practical travel packs to aid newer warriors, asking only for basic materials like coarse thread to finish the work.",al={"carry your weight quest lore","why does furl want thread"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Furl Scornbrow on?",a="Furl stands firmly with the Horde. Positioned high above Razor Hill, he keeps watch over Durotar to protect the young orcish realm from potential invaders and aids travelers who serve the Warchief.",al={"furl scornbrow faction","furl scornbrow horde","is furl horde"},it="side",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Furl embodies the orcish belief that even when age robs a warrior of their martial strength, an honorable life means finding another way to serve the clan and Horde.",["faction:Horde"]="Stationed along the ridges outside Razor Hill, Furl represents the vigilance required to protect Durotar's fledgling settlements against lingering threats."},kw={"carry your weight","durotar","furl scornbrow","lookout","orc","razor hill","watchtower"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:791"},src={"Furl Scornbrow"}}
E["npc:galgar"] = {t="npc",n="Galgar",z="durotar",s="Galgar is an orc cook stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. He prepares provisions for young recruits taking their first steps in service to the Horde. To teach newcomers the basics of foraging in the harsh desert, he tasks them with gathering wild cactus apples for his signature dish.",h="Galgar is an orc cook stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Cook in the Valley",b="Situated near the cooking fire of the Den in the Valley of Trials, Galgar provides sustenance for young orcs and trolls undergoing their initial rites of passage. Durotar is a dry, unforgiving red wasteland where every scrap of sustenance must be wrung from the landscape. By putting novice warriors to work gathering ripe cactus fruit, Galgar tests their attention and resilience while keeping his kitchen stocked.",sp=0},{t="Cactus Apple Surprise",b="Galgar's specialty recipe is known as Cactus Apple Surprise. While he openly acknowledges that hunting down spiny desert fruit is an intentionally simple task designed to ease fresh recruits into life as adventurers, the end product remains a staple ration for hungry trainees. Even the most hardened warrior of the Horde must start somewhere, and under Galgar's watchful eye, that journey begins with desert foraging.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Galgar?",a="Galgar is located in the Valley of Trials, the starting canyon for orcs and trolls in southwestern Durotar. He stands near the central campfire and cooking area outside the Den.",al={"galgar location","where is galgar","galgar coordinates"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Galgar ask adventurers to do?",a="He asks new adventurers to scavenge ripe cactus apples from the wild cacti scattered across the Valley of Trials so he can prepare his Cactus Apple Surprise.",al={"galgar quest","what does galgar want"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why does Galgar send new recruits to pick fruit?",a="Galgar admits the task is intentionally straightforward. It serves as an easy initial chore for fledgling fighters to learn the layout of the valley and practice self-sufficiency in the harsh Durotar wilderness.",al={"why cactus apples","galgar test"},it="motive"},{q="What is Cactus Apple Surprise?",a="It is Galgar's signature recipe, made from fresh cactus apples gathered from the native desert flora of Durotar to nourish novice recruits.",al={"what is cactus apple surprise","galgar food"},it="item"},{q="Who is Galgar?",a="Galgar is an orc cook stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Rather than training warriors in brute combat, he supports the settlement by preparing hearty provisions for the young recruits, most notably his well-known cactus apple surprise.",al={"who is galgar","galgar lore","who galgar"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Galgar on?",a="Galgar is loyal to Thrall's Horde. Serving inside the Valley of Trials, he tends directly to the fledgling orcs and trolls taking their first steps in service to Durotar.",al={"galgar faction","is galgar horde","galgar allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Galgar want?",a="Galgar wants fresh ingredients—primarily the ripe cactus apples that grow across the arid valley—so he can brew batches of his signature cactus apple surprise to keep the young recruits fed and energized.",al={"what does galgar need","galgar goal","galgar wants"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Galgar here in the Valley of Trials?",a="Galgar is stationed in the Valley of Trials to support the encampment's kitchen. While trainers instruct aspirants in the art of war, Galgar ensures the grounds remain supplied with food and introduces new arrivals to basic field work.",al={"why is galgar here","galgar valley of trials reason","why is galgar in durotar"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Why is Galgar famous?",a="Galgar is known throughout the Valley of Trials for his famous recipe, Cactus Apple Surprise. Almost every young recruit passing through the den tastes his cooking while performing introductory chores for him.",al={"is galgar famous","what is galgar known for","galgar fame"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Galgar embodies the practical, rustic cooking of the Horde, utilizing Durotar's sparse natural resources to keep recruits fed and battle-ready.",["race:Orc"]="For young orcs taking their first steps in the Valley of Trials, running an errand for Galgar is a familiar rite of passage before facing fiercer wilderness threats."},kw={"cactus apple surprise","cactus apples","cook","durotar","galgar","horde recruit","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:galgar-s-cactus-apple-surprise","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Galgar"}}
E["npc:gar-thok"] = {t="npc",n="Gar'Thok",z="durotar",s="Gar'Thok is a veteran orc warrior and outpost commander stationed at Razor Hill in Durotar. Having fought at Mount Hyjal and survived the initial Kul Tiras landings on Durotar's coast, he now coordinates local defense against human encroachers and native threats. He directs young Horde recruits stepping out of the Valley of Trials to secure the red wastes of the new homeland.",h="Gar'Thok is a veteran orc warrior and outpost commander stationed at Razor Hill in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Veteran of the Red Wastes",b="Before settling in Razor Hill, Gar'Thok defended the orc encampment during the apocalyptic Battle of Mount Hyjal. Following the Third War, he marched to Durotar under Warchief Thrall and served as a lieutenant under Nazgrel during the earliest days of building the new homeland. When the Mok'Nathal wanderer Rexxar first arrived in Durotar, it was Gar'Thok who alerted him to the aggressive quilboar raiding their perimeter, enlisting the beastmaster to safeguard the fragile new settlement.",sp=0},{t="Surviving the Admiral's Invasion",b="Gar'Thok's resolve was tested when Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's Kul Tiras fleet landed along the eastern shores of Durotar. Stationed at an outlying watch post, Gar'Thok witnessed his garrison overwhelmed and brutally slaughtered by naval marines. Though his forces were decimated, Gar'Thok survived the onslaught. The memory of that surprise assault cemented his vigilance against the surviving marines who still occupy Tiragarde Keep and the coastal shipwrecks.",sp=0},{t="Defense of Razor Hill",b="Today, Gar'Thok oversees the martial defense of central Durotar from the barracks of Razor Hill. He wastes no time with pleasantries, immediately tasking emerging Horde warriors, shamans, and scouts with clearing out hostile Kul Tiran remnants, repossessing salvaged supplies, and recovering military orders left in the coastal ruins. To him, the safety of Durotar is far from guaranteed, requiring constant pressure against any who question the Horde's right to this soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gar'Thok?",a="Gar'Thok is an orc officer stationed in Razor Hill who organizes the local military response against hostile forces in Durotar. He is a veteran of the Third War who served under Nazgrel during the founding of Orgrimmar.",al={"garthok lore","who is garthok","razor hill commander"},it="identity"},{q="Where did Gar'Thok fight before coming to Razor Hill?",a="He fought at the Battle of Mount Hyjal, guarding the orc fortifications against the Burning Legion and the Scourge. Later, he served at a frontier outpost in Durotar, working with Rexxar to quell early quilboar raids.",al={"garthok past","garthok mount hyjal","garthok history"},it="history"},{q="Why does Gar'Thok hate the humans in Durotar so much?",a="During the invasion led by Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore, sailors from Kul Tiras ambushed Gar'Thok's outpost on the coast, butchering his men. He survived the assault and remains dedicated to eradicating the remaining marine encampments.",al={"why garthok hates kul tiras","garthok humans","tiragarde keep garthok"},it="motive"},{q="What threats does Gar'Thok send adventurers to fight?",a="Gar'Thok sends recruits to fight the hostile Kul Tiran sailors entrenched at Tiragarde Keep, reclaim supplies from coastal shipwrecks, push back invading quilboar, and uncover any orders left behind by human commanders.",al={"garthok quests","what does garthok want","razor hill quests"},it="threat"},{q="What is his relationship with Nazgrel and Thrall?",a="Gar'Thok served as a trusted lieutenant under Nazgrel during the initial colonizing expeditions in Durotar, operating directly under the authority of Warchief Thrall to secure the borders of the newly claimed territory.",al={"garthok nazgrel","garthok thrall","garthok rank"},it="ties"},{q="Where can Gar'Thok be found?",a="Gar'Thok stands outside the main watchtower and barracks in Razor Hill, the central settlement of Durotar located south of Orgrimmar.",al={"garthok location","where is garthok","find garthok"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Gar'Thok on?",a="Gar'Thok is wholly loyal to the Horde and Warchief Thrall. Stationed in Durotar under the command of Nazgrel, he works tirelessly to defend the nascent orc homeland and ensure newly arrived warriors are prepared to protect the Horde's borders.",al={"gar'thok faction","is gar'thok horde","who does garthok serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Gar'Thok want?",a="Gar'Thok wants Durotar firmly secured against all threats. Having watched his outpost slaughtered by Kul Tiras invaders, he seeks vengeance against the remaining human sailors on the coast and demands the suppression of encroaching quilboar that harass the settlement.",al={"gar'thok goal","what does garthok want","garthok motives"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Gar'Thok here?",a="Following the devastation of his coastal outpost by Kul Tiran forces, Gar'Thok took up a post in Razor Hill. From this central settlement, he organizes the defense of Durotar and directs budding Horde champions against hostile incursions.",al={"why is gar'thok in razor hill","why is garthok here","garthok duty razor hill"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For young orcs leaving the Valley of Trials, Gar'Thok represents the stern, unyielding discipline of the veteran generation that bled at Mount Hyjal to win Durotar.",["faction:Horde"]="Gar'Thok ensures that fresh recruits of all Horde races understand the precariousness of their new territory, directing them to repel invasive Alliance remnants.",["class:Warrior"]="As a frontline commander who survived both demonic legions and brutal naval ambushes, Gar'Thok expects martial fortitude and unhesitating obedience from fellow warriors."},kw={"daelin","durotar","gar'thok","garthok","kul tiras","nazgrel","razor hill","rexxar","tiragarde"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:kul-tiras","quest:784","quest:830","quest:825","topic:quilboar","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Gar'Thok"}}
E["npc:gornek"] = {t="npc",n="Gornek",z="durotar",s="Gornek is an orc overseer stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. He serves as the primary point of intake for fresh orc and Darkspear troll recruits preparing to prove their worth to the New Horde.",h="Gornek is an orc overseer stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",sec={{t="Welcoming the Unproven",b="Standing directly at the heart of the Valley of Trials, Gornek represents the initial test of discipline for aspiring Horde warriors, scouts, and spellcasters. Under Warchief Thrall's order, every youth and newcomer must earn their place through grit and perseverance rather than entitlement. Gornek assesses those stepping into the valley, reading their introductory orders and directing them to trainers throughout the compound. Whether an initiate carries an encrypted scrawl, a glyphic parchment, or a simple tablet, it is Gornek who receives their credentials and sets them upon their harsh path of survival.",sp=0},{t="A Life in Service to Durotar",b="The arid canyons of the valley test more than battle prowess; they instill the communal ethos of the New Horde. Gornek ensures that novices do not linger aimlessly, pointing them toward the trials of the nearby scorpid burrows, the dens of feral boars, and the watchful eyes of veteran instructors. For those who survive the training grounds and slay the threats lurking in the red rock gullies, Gornek offers the final acknowledgment before dispatching them outward into the wider, perilous landscape of Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gornek?",a="Gornek is an orc greeter and taskmaster in the Valley of Trials. He oversees new recruits of the Horde, reading their induction documents and guiding them to their respective class trainers.",al={"gornek","who is this orc","who is gornek"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Gornek?",a="He stands near the center of the Valley of Trials in southwestern Durotar, just outside the Den where young orcs and Darkspear trolls begin their journeys.",al={"gornek location","where is gornek","gornek map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do new recruits report to him?",a="New arrivals carry training scrolls and tablets designating their chosen discipline. Gornek evaluates these letters of introduction, confirms their eligibility, and sends them to the appropriate mentors within the valley.",al={"why visit gornek","parchment quest","tablet quest"},it="why_me"},{q="What is his role in the New Horde?",a="He acts as an entry coordinator for Thrall's New Horde. His duty is to ensure no recruit enters the broader lands of Durotar without first learning the basic tenets of honor, survival, and martial readiness.",al={"gornek horde role","what does gornek do"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Gornek on?",a="Gornek is fiercely loyal to Thrall's New Horde. Stationed in Durotar, he serves as an overseer within the Valley of Trials, ensuring that every newly awakened orc and visiting troll recruit embraces the discipline, strength, and survival mindset necessary to defend their fledgling nation.",al={"gornek faction","who does gornek serve","gornek horde or alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Gornek want?",a="Gornek wants you to prove yourself worthy of the Horde. Durotar is a harsh land crawling with predators and hostile infiltrators, and he refuses to waste resources on undisciplined recruits. He tasks young warriors with hunting dangerous beasts and rooting out local threats to forge them into capable fighters.",al={"gornek goal","what does gornek need","gornek quest motive"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Gornek in the Valley of Trials?",a="The Valley of Trials is the designated proving ground for the Horde's newest blood. Gornek is stationed here to direct fresh arrivals, evaluate their early capabilities, and introduce them to the trainers and trials that will prepare them for the challenges of Durotar and beyond.",al={"why is gornek here","gornek valley of trials role","why is gornek in durotar"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For young orcs, reporting to Gornek is the very first step toward shedding childhood and earning an honorable place in Durotar.",["race:Troll"]="As allies sheltered by Thrall, Darkspear trolls present their credentials to Gornek to prove they stand as capable equals alongside their orc brothers."},kw={"den","durotar","gornek","parchment","the new horde","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","quest:787","quest:1089","quest:98576","topic:new-horde","topic:horde"},src={"Gornek"}}
E["npc:hana-zua"] = {t="npc",n="Hana'zua",z="durotar",s="Hana'zua is a Darkspear troll scout stationed in the Valley of Trials who fell victim to the poisonous beasts prowling the canyon ridges. Stricken and wounded by the monstrous scorpid Sarkoth, he lies awaiting assistance from young Horde initiates seeking to prove their valor.",h="Hana'zua is a Darkspear troll scout stationed in the Valley of Trials who fell victim to the poisonous beasts...",sec={{t="A Scout Fallen to Venom",b="While traversing the arid heights overlooking the Valley of Trials, Hana'zua encountered Sarkoth, an exceptionally vicious and venomous scorpid that stalks the cliffs. Overwhelmed and stung by the beast, the troll barely survived the confrontation. Unable to move or return to camp on his own, he languishes amid the dust, counting on passing recruits to finish the creature and deliver word of his plight back to the Den.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hana'zua?",a="Hana'zua is a Darkspear troll found injured in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. He was ambushed and poisoned while tracking beasts on the ridges.",al={"hanazua","who is hanazua","injured troll valley of trials"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Hana'zua?",a="He was struck down by Sarkoth, a large and deadly scorpid lurking on the crags above the training grounds. Its potent venom left him incapacitated and unable to return to safety.",al={"why is hanazua hurt","who poisoned hanazua","hanazua injury"},it="why_here"},{q="What does he ask travelers to do?",a="Hana'zua asks able adventurers to avenge his wounding by slaying Sarkoth, collecting the beast's claw as proof, and carrying word of his condition back to the instructors at the Den.",al={"hanazua quest","what does hanazua want"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Hana'zua on?",a="Hana'zua is loyal to the Horde and his fellow Darkspear trolls. Like other young orcs and trolls who come through the Valley of Trials, he ventured into the proving grounds to demonstrate his strength and readiness to serve Thrall's new nation.",al={"hanazua faction","who does hanazua serve","is hanazua horde"},it="side",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear initiates just beginning their journey in Durotar, discovering a wounded kinsman underscores the lethal nature of the local wildlife and the need to protect their newfound allies.",["faction:Horde"]="Hana'zua's survival and vengeance serve as one of the earliest tests of loyalty and combat readiness for aspiring champions of the Horde."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","hana'zua","hanazua","sarkoth","scorpid","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:804","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:troll","quest:1089"},src={"Hana'zua"}}
E["npc:innkeeper-grosk"] = {t="npc",n="Innkeeper Grosk",z="durotar",s="Innkeeper Grosk manages the inn at Razor Hill, providing weary travelers with food, drink, and a place to rest in central Durotar. Located on the bustling road between the Valley of Trials and Orgrimmar, his establishment serves as the primary resting point for young Horde adventurers setting out into the wider world.",h="Innkeeper Grosk manages the inn at Razor Hill, providing weary travelers with food, drink, and a place to...",sec={{t="Hospitality in the Red Wastes",b="Razor Hill serves as the vital crossroad settlement connecting the southern training grounds of Durotar to the high walls of Orgrimmar. At the center of this waystation stands Innkeeper Grosk, an orc tasked with sheltering warriors, scouts, and peons alike. His inn offers a respite from the harsh desert heat, stocked with basic provisions, hearty meats, and cool water for any traveler passing beneath its sturdy timbers.",sp=0},{t="A Peon's Respite",b="Beyond serving passing travelers, Grosk assists the local labor force that keeps Durotar running. In the quest 'A Peon's Burden', the timid peon Ukor, who hauled food all the way to the Valley of Trials only to find it was not needed, asks travelers to carry the load back to Grosk's inn in Razor Hill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Innkeeper Grosk located?",a="Innkeeper Grosk stands inside the inn at Razor Hill, situated right in the center of Durotar along the primary road leading north toward Orgrimmar.",al={"innkeeper grosk location","where is grosk","razor hill innkeeper"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services does Innkeeper Grosk provide?",a="Grosk acts as an innkeeper where Horde adventurers can bind their Hearthstone to Razor Hill. He also sells basic food, water, and meat to replenish health and mana between travels.",al={"what does grosk do","grosk vendor","can i bind hearthstone at razor hill"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Does Innkeeper Grosk offer any quests?",a="He is involved in the quest 'A Peon's Burden', receiving the load of food that the peon Ukor was too frightened of Durotar's beasts to carry back to Razor Hill himself.",al={"innkeeper grosk quests","a peons burden turn in"},gp=true},{q="Who is Innkeeper Grosk?",a="Innkeeper Grosk is the orc proprietor of the tavern in Razor Hill. As travelers, grunts, and wandering adventurers pass through Durotar on their way to or from Orgrimmar, Grosk offers them shelter, provisions, and a hearth to rest their weary bones.",al={"who is grosk","innkeeper grosk","who is innkeeper grosk"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Innkeeper Grosk on?",a="Grosk is a steadfast member of the Horde, welcoming orcs, trolls, tauren, and Forsaken into his establishment. He ensures that those fighting for Warchief Thrall's new realm have a reliable base of rest and resupply in Durotar.",al={"is grosk horde","innkeeper grosk allegiance","innkeeper grosk faction"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Innkeeper Grosk want?",a="Grosk wants to keep his inn running smoothly, catering to travelers across the arid plains of Durotar. He trades hearty food and drink, binds wandering adventurers to his hearthstone, and occasionally looks after the needs of the town's laborers and guards.",al={"what does grosk want","grosk motive","innkeeper grosk goals"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Innkeeper Grosk in Razor Hill?",a="Razor Hill serves as the primary crossroad and garrison town between the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, and the capital of Orgrimmar. Grosk established his tavern here to provide essential lodging and supplies at the beating heart of Durotar's frontier life.",al={"why is grosk here","why razor hill innkeeper","grosk razor hill role"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For newly blooded orcs, trolls, and visiting tauren traveling north from the Valley of Trials or Sen'jin Village, Grosk's inn marks the first true town and hearth location on the road toward Orgrimmar."},kw={"durotar","grosk","innkeeper","innkeeper grosk","orgrimmar","peon's burden","razor hill"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:2161","zone:orgrimmar","npc:magga"},src={"Innkeeper Grosk"}}
E["npc:jen-shan"] = {t="npc",n="Jen'shan",z="durotar",s="Jen'shan is a Darkspear jungle troll and hunter trainer stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. She guides fledgling orc and troll marksmen as they take their first steps into the wilds of the Horde. Young hunters are directed to her to learn the basics of tracking, ranged combat, and survival.",h="Jen'shan is a Darkspear jungle troll and hunter trainer stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",sec={{t="Mentor of the Red Sands",b="Perched among the weathered encampments of the Valley of Trials, Jen'shan serves as the primary hunter mentor for new recruits proving their worth to the Horde. Together, young orcs and Darkspear trolls arrive clutching inscribed tablets and parchments directing them straight to her side. With keen eyes sharpened by years in the untamed wilderness, she imparts foundational techniques in archery, marksmanship, and wilderness survival, ensuring no novice falls prey to the scorpids and boars prowling the canyon floor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Jen'shan?",a="Jen'shan is a Darkspear jungle troll hunter trainer located within the Valley of Trials in Durotar. She instructs novice hunters of the Horde in basic wilderness lore, tracking, and ranged weaponry.",al={"jenshan lore","who is jenshan","valley hunter trainer"},it="identity"},{q="What quests involve Jen'shan?",a="Novice hunters are sent to her via introductory training quests. Young orc hunters are directed to her by turning in an Etched Tablet, while young troll hunters seek her out with an Etched Parchment.",al={"jenshan quests","etched tablet jenshan","etched parchment jenshan"},gp=true},{q="Why is a troll training hunters in an orc proving ground?",a="The Valley of Trials serves as the common proving ground for both orc recruits and the displaced Darkspear trolls who share Durotar. As master scouts and stalkers, trolls like Jen'shan play a vital role in preparing new warriors and hunters of both races for service to the Horde.",al={"why is a troll in valley of trials","troll trainer in durotar"},it="why_here"},{q="Whose side is Jen'shan on?",a="Jen'shan is loyal to the Horde and her people, the Darkspear tribe. Stationed in the Valley of Trials, she serves alongside the orcs to ensure that new recruits, whether troll or orc, are properly prepared for the harsh realities of surviving in Durotar and fighting for the warchief.",al={"jenshan faction","is jenshan horde","jenshan loyalty"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Jen'shan want?",a="Jen'shan seeks to drill fledging hunters in marksmanship, survival, and the wild instincts needed to endure. She wants promising young scouts to hone their craft quickly so they can handle the fierce beasts roaming the red wastes and protect the fledgling Horde from its enemies.",al={"jenshan motive","jenshan goal","what does jenshan need"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Who is Jen'shan tied to?",a="Jen'shan belongs to the Darkspear trolls led by Sen'jin's son, Vol'jin. Because the Darkspear share Durotar with Thrall's orcs, she works closely with the trainers of the Valley of Trials to guide fresh recruits of both races into the ranks of the Horde.",al={"jenshan connections","jenshan darkspear ties","who does jenshan serve"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="For young orc and troll hunters, Jen'shan is the very first mentor you encounter, teaching foundational ranged techniques before you venture beyond the red canyons of the Den.",["race:Troll"]="Jen'shan represents the Darkspear tribe's renowned prowess in tracking and scouting, ensuring young trolls retain their ancestral hunting traditions in their new continental home."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","etched parchment","etched tablet","hunter trainer","jen'shan","jenshan","troll","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:troll","quest:3082","quest:3087"},src={"Jen'shan"}}
E["npc:kali-remik"] = {t="npc",n="Kali Remik",z="durotar",s="Kali Remik is a Darkspear troll hunter who spends her time lending guidance to travelers across the Horde's heartland. Familiar with the ways of tracking and survival in Durotar, she directs young hunters to Thotar in Razor Hill to learn the taming of beasts.",h="Kali Remik is a Darkspear troll hunter who spends her time lending guidance to travelers across the Horde's...",sec={{t="A Guide for the Hunt",b="Kali Remik is a seasoned jungle troll tracker well-acquainted with the arid wastes of Durotar and the bustling hubs of the Horde. In coastal settlements like Sen'jin Village, she watches over young scouts taking their first steps outside the Valley of Trials. Knowing when a novice outgrows the local training grounds, she steps in to direct promising marksmen toward Thotar in Razor Hill to begin their path as beastmasters, ensuring the Horde's frontier ranks stay sharp and disciplined.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kali Remik?",a="Kali Remik is a Darkspear troll scout and quest giver. She helps guide fledgling Horde adventurers, especially hunters ready to advance their training beyond local outposts.",al={"kali remik lore","who is kali remik","kali remik npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Kali Remik be found?",a="She can be found aiding her people in Durotar, notably around Sen'jin Village.",al={"where is kali remik","kali remik location","find kali remik"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What guidance does she offer to hunters?",a="Through 'The Hunter's Path', Kali directs young orc and troll hunters who have proven their basic skills to travel to Razor Hill, where Thotar sets them on the path to taming a beast companion of their own.",al={"the hunters path quest","kali remik hunter quest","what does kali teach"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Kali Remik on?",a="Kali Remik is loyal to the Darkspear tribe and stands firmly with Thrall's Horde. She aids her people and their allies by guiding young wilderness scouts and marksmen toward proper training and service to their new homeland.",al={"kali remik faction","who does kali remik serve","kali remik horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Kali Remik in Sen'jin Village?",a="Kali Remik stays in Sen'jin Village to watch over the emerging defenders of the Darkspear tribe. In these coastal shallows, she helps identify promising young hunters among the orcs and trolls who pass through, directing them to the mentors who can hone their survival skills.",al={"why is kali remik here","kali remik sen'jin village role","what brought kali remik here"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="What does Kali Remik want?",a="Kali Remik wants to see Durotar protected by capable scouts and stalkers. She seeks out aspiring hunters to ensure they do not wander unprepared, pointing them along the proper paths to find the trainers who can teach them the ways of the wild.",al={"what does kali remik want","kali remik motive","what is kali remik's goal"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Who is Kali Remik tied to?",a="She is closely bound to the Darkspear trolls of Sen'jin Village and works in tandem with the hunter trainers of Durotar. Her duties link her to the broader survival network of the Horde, ensuring new recruits connect with established mentors across their territory.",al={"who is kali remik tied to","kali remik connections","kali remik allies"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="For young orc and troll marksmen, Kali acts as a stepping stone, recognizing when your skills outstrip village drills and sending you forward to Thotar in Razor Hill.",["race:Troll"]="A fellow member of the Darkspear tribe, Kali keeps watch over her kin as they rebuild their lives along Durotar's coast and settle within Orgrimmar's Valley of Spirits."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","kali remik","sen'jin village","the hunter's path","tracker","valley of spirits"},rel={"quest:6065","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:valley-of-spirits","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:troll","topic:horde","quest:8355"},src={"Kali Remik"}}
E["npc:kaltunk"] = {t="npc",n="Kaltunk",z="durotar",s="Kaltunk is an orc overseer stationed at the heart of the Valley of Trials in Durotar. He serves as the very first point of contact for young orcs taking their opening steps into the world. It is his duty to welcome these aspiring champions and direct them to their initial duties in service to the Horde.",h="Kaltunk is an orc overseer stationed at the heart of the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",sec={{t="The First Step",b="Standing under the harsh sun of the Valley of Trials, Kaltunk watches over the newly arrived hopefuls seeking to prove themselves worthy of the Horde. While other trainers and elders assign grueling trials and hunting rites, Kaltunk ensures that no recruit wanders aimlessly through the red dust. He delivers straightforward orders, pointing newcomers directly toward Gornek and the path of discipline.",sp=0},{t="Keeper of the Valley",b="The Valley of Trials is not an easy proving ground; it was chosen specifically to forge strength and resilience in every youth who walks its canyon floors. Kaltunk embodies this rugged practicality. He offers no grand speeches or coddling, expecting each orc to quickly find their place in the world and pull their weight for the warchief.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kaltunk?",a="Kaltunk is an orc overseer stationed in the Valley of Trials. He is the very first person newly awakened orc adventurers encounter, tasked with pointing them toward their mentors and starting their training.",al={"kaltunk role","who is this orc","kaltunk npc"},it="identity"},{q="What does Kaltunk do for new adventurers?",a="He gives new recruits their initial task, directing them to speak with Gornek elsewhere in the valley so their true training can begin.",al={"kaltunk quest","what does kaltunk want","first quest valley of trials"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can I find Kaltunk?",a="He stands right near the central training tent and campfire within the Valley of Trials, the secluded starting grounds in southern Durotar.",al={"kaltunk location","find kaltunk","where is kaltunk"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is he stationed in the Valley of Trials?",a="He serves as a welcoming overseer to ensure incoming orc recruits are organized and promptly set onto their path of service to Thrall's Horde.",al={"why is kaltunk here","kaltunk purpose"},it="why_here"},{q="Whose side is Kaltunk on?",a="Kaltunk serves the Horde and stands firmly under the authority of Warchief Thrall. He is stationed in the Valley of Trials specifically to welcome fresh orc recruits and guide their first steps into service for the new nation of Durotar.",al={"kaltunk faction","who does kaltunk serve","is kaltunk horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Kaltunk want?",a="Kaltunk wants you to prove yourself to the Horde. He ensures that untested newcomers do not linger idle, directing you immediately to Gornek and the overseers in the Valley of Trials so your training and service to Durotar can begin without delay.",al={"what does kaltunk need","kaltunk goal","kaltunk motive"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For every orc stepping out into Kalimdor, Kaltunk's gruff instructions are the first words they hear as they begin earning their honor.",["faction:Horde"]="Kaltunk helps uphold the practical discipline required to maintain order in the harsh proving grounds of Durotar."},kw={"durotar","gornek","kaltunk","orc starter","valley of trials","your place in the world"},rel={"quest:your-place-in-the-world","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar"},src={"Kaltunk"}}
E["npc:kor-ghan"] = {t="npc",n="Kor'ghan",z="durotar",s="Kor'ghan is a Darkspear jungle troll who can be found lingering in the murky caverns of the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar. Positioned right outside Rekkul's Poisons, he seeks assistance in concocting remedies against venomous wilderness predators.",h="Kor'ghan is a Darkspear jungle troll who can be found lingering in the murky caverns of the Cleft of Shadow...",sec={{t="A Troll in the Shadows",b="Standing before Rekkul's Poisons in the cavernous depths of the Cleft of Shadow, Kor'ghan keeps close watch over remedies and toxins alike. From the capital he dispatches adventurers across the red canyons to gather venomous components from Durotar's scorpids in order to prepare vital antidotes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kor'ghan?",a="Kor'ghan is a Darkspear troll located in the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar, standing outside Rekkul's poison shop.",al={"kor'ghan","who is kor'ghan","korghan npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Kor'ghan?",a="He is located in the subterranean Cleft of Shadow beneath central Orgrimmar, stationed directly in front of Rekkul's Poisons.",al={"kor'ghan location","where is korghan","find korghan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Kor'ghan need help with?",a="He enlists travelers to gather poison sacs from the venomtail scorpids roaming near the entrance of Orgrimmar to help formulate antidotes.",al={"kor'ghan quest","finding the antidote quest","korghan venom"},it="wants"},{q="Was Kor'ghan ever found in Durotar?",a="Not himself. Kor'ghan keeps to his spot near the poison suppliers in Orgrimmar, but he sends adventurers out into Durotar to gather poison sacs from the venomtail scorpids near the city's entrance.",al={"kor'ghan sen'jin","korghan old location"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Kor'ghan on?",a="Kor'ghan is aligned with the Horde. As a Darkspear jungle troll dwelling deep within Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, his allegiances rest firmly with his kin and the new home they share under Warchief Thrall.",al={"korghan faction","is korghan horde","korghan alliance or horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Kor'ghan here?",a="Kor'ghan makes his place just outside Rekkul's Poisons within the shadowy depths of the Cleft of Shadow. Lingering among the city's rogue practitioners and alchemists, he seeks specialized aid and venomous remedies from those who deal in dangerous mixtures.",al={"why is korghan in orgrimmar","why is korghan in cleft of shadow","what brought korghan here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Positioned directly outside Rekkul's Poisons in the Cleft of Shadow, Kor'ghan is a familiar sight to rogues visiting the underbelly of Orgrimmar for reagents and venoms.",["race:Troll"]="Like many Darkspear kin who have left Sen'jin Village, Kor'ghan puts his practical knowledge of Durotar's wild hazards to use in the Horde's fortified capital."},kw={"antidote","cleft of shadow","kor'ghan","korghan","orgrimmar","rekkul's poisons","scorpid venom","sen'jin village"},rel={"subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:orgrimmar","quest:813","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Kor'ghan"}}
E["npc:kzan-thornslash"] = {t="npc",n="Kzan Thornslash",z="durotar",s="Kzan Thornslash is an orc weapon merchant stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. He provides essential starter weaponry and supplies to fresh recruits beginning their training under the Horde.",h="Kzan Thornslash is an orc weapon merchant stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",sec={{t="Armorer to the Recruits",b="Situated within the dusty red canyon of the Valley of Trials, Kzan Thornslash serves as the primary weapon vendor for young orcs and Darkspear trolls taking their first steps as warriors of the Horde. Offering an assortment of basic armaments—ranging from crude hand axes and shortswords to clubs and throwing knives—Kzan ensures that newly awakened aspirants are armed adequately to face the local wildlife and regional hazards.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kzan Thornslash?",a="Kzan Thornslash is an orc merchant stationed in the Valley of Trials. His role is to supply new Horde trainees with standard weapons suited for their initial combat trials.",al={"kzan thornslash","who is kzan","valley of trials weapon vendor"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Kzan Thornslash?",a="He can be found standing in the open training grounds of the Valley of Trials in southwestern Durotar, surrounded by novice adventurers and training instructors.",al={"kzan location","where is kzan thornslash","kzan thornslash map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kind of equipment does Kzan sell?",a="Kzan provides basic starter weaponry, including axes, swords, daggers, staves, bludgeons, and thrown weapons intended for recruits who need reliable iron before acquiring forged or found gear.",al={"what does kzan sell","kzan items","kzan weapons"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Kzan Thornslash on?",a="Kzan Thornslash stands firmly with the Horde. Operating within the Valley of Trials, he answers to the authority of Orgrimmar and Thrall's new nation, outfitting the young orcs and trolls who arrive to prove their strength and loyalty in Durotar.",al={"kzan thornslash faction","who does kzan serve","is kzan horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Kzan Thornslash in the Valley of Trials?",a="Kzan stays in the Valley of Trials to arm aspiring recruits and warriors embarking on their initial trials. In a harsh, arid proving ground overrun by scorpids, boars, and vile familiars, an unproven fighter needs reliable steel, clubs, and blades to survive their testing.",al={"why is kzan thornslash here","kzan valley of trials role","what does kzan do"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="What does Kzan Thornslash want?",a="Kzan aims to supply recruits with the arms they need while maintaining his trade in Durotar. Through his dealings with young warriors, he ensures that the fledgling defenders of the Horde are adequately equipped with basic weaponry to defend their newly settled lands.",al={"what does kzan want","kzan thornslash motive","kzan thornslash goal"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="For young warriors starting with chipped blades, Kzan offers an immediate selection of blunt and edged weaponry to suit different combat disciplines.",["faction:Horde"]="Supplying the nascent armies of Thrall begins at the very bottom, where merchants like Kzan ensure every capable hand has steel to wield for the Horde."},kw={"durotar","horde","kzan","orc","thornslash","valley of trials","weapon vendor","weapons"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","quest:97279"},src={"Kzan Thornslash"}}
E["npc:lar-prowltusk"] = {t="npc",n="Lar Prowltusk",z="durotar",s="Lar Prowltusk is a Darkspear troll sentinel stationed southwest of Sen'jin Village in Durotar. From his post on the frontier, he keeps watch over encroaching threats to the young troll settlement, directing adventurers to blunt the advances of nearby enemies.",h="Lar Prowltusk is a Darkspear troll sentinel stationed southwest of Sen'jin Village in Durotar.",sec={{t="Watcher on the Coast",b="Situated southwest of Sen'jin Village along the rugged Durotar coastline, Lar Prowltusk stands as one of the Darkspear tribe's forward sentinels. With the trolls still working to secure a permanent home after fleeing their sunken island chain, Sen'jin Village faces constant harassment from hostile neighbors. Lar coordinates scouts and warriors to monitor coastal movements and curb the aggression of hostile forces—particularly the Kolkar centaur—ensuring the fragile settlement has room to breathe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lar Prowltusk?",a="Lar Prowltusk is a Darkspear troll quest giver stationed just southwest of Sen'jin Village in Durotar. He helps guard the settlement's outskirts by enlisting capable Horde travelers to strike at regional threats before they reach the village proper.",al={"lar prowltusk","who is lar prowltusk","lar prowltusk durotar"},it="identity"},{q="What threats does Lar Prowltusk focus on?",a="Lar focuses on frontier dangers that threaten southern Durotar, notably the marauding Kolkar centaur packs pushing into troll territory.",al={"lar prowltusk quests","what does lar prowltusk want"},it="wants"},{q="Where can Lar Prowltusk be found?",a="He is located in southern Durotar, keeping watch along the paths southwest of Sen'jin Village.",al={"lar prowltusk location","where is lar prowltusk"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Lar Prowltusk on?",a="Lar Prowltusk is loyal to the Darkspear tribe and the Horde. Stationed along the harsh coast of Durotar southwest of Sen'jin Village, he acts in defense of his people's new home, looking out for encroaching enemies that threaten the safety of the Darkspear trolls and their orc allies.",al={"lar prowltusk faction","who does lar prowltusk serve","lar prowltusk horde or alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Lar Prowltusk out here?",a="You find Lar Prowltusk keeping watch southwest of Sen'jin Village to guard the Darkspear settlement from regional perils. Durotar's southern reaches face constant pressure from aggressive neighbors, and Lar stays posted near the wild coast to help direct defenders against these local threats before they strike the village.",al={"why is lar prowltusk in durotar","lar prowltusk location reason","why is lar southwest of senjin"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Lar Prowltusk tied to?",a="Lar Prowltusk is closely tied to the troll settlement of Sen'jin Village and is companion to Tai'tasi, a fellow Darkspear troll dwelling there. Beyond his personal bonds, he coordinates with the village defenders and wandering Horde adventurers to safeguard troll territory.",al={"lar prowltusk allies","lar prowltusk relations","lar prowltusk mate"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear, scouts like Lar Prowltusk are vital to safeguarding the tribe's fragile new home in Durotar against aggressive centaur clans and encroaching human forces.",["faction:Horde"]="Lar Prowltusk represents the Horde's struggle to secure the borders of Durotar against external threats right outside their fledgling capital's backyard."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","kolkar","lar prowltusk","northwatch","sen'jin village","troll"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","quest:786","topic:troll","topic:alliance"},src={"Lar Prowltusk"}}
E["npc:magga"] = {t="npc",n="Magga",z="durotar",s="Magga is an orc resident living in the dusty settlement of Razor Hill within Durotar. Stationed near the town's lively tavern, she serves as a welcoming face for newly arrived Horde adventurers making their way out of the Valley of Trials.",h="Magga is an orc resident living in the dusty settlement of Razor Hill within Durotar.",sec={{t="A Welcoming Face in Razor Hill",b="Razor Hill serves as the first real taste of the wider world for young orcs and darkspear trolls emerging from the Valley of Trials. Positioned right beside the local inn, Magga helps orient new arrivals to the outpost, introducing them to local amenities and the hospitality of Innkeeper Grosk. While she keeps a low profile among the outpost's busy grunts and tradespeople, she helps bind the small settlement together.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Magga?",a="Magga is an orc civilian stationed in Razor Hill, Durotar. She stands near the inn, welcoming new Horde travelers and pointing them toward lodging and rest.",al={"magga durotar","magga razor hill","who is magga"},it="identity"},{q="What is Magga's connection to Innkeeper Grosk?",a="Magga directs weary travelers to Innkeeper Grosk inside the Razor Hill inn so they can bind their hearthstones and rest after their journey from the Valley of Trials.",al={"magga and grosk","magga innkeeper"},it="ties"},{q="Does Magga offer any quests?",a="Yes, Magga offers a brief introductory greeting task titled 'Welcome!', which directs new adventurers to speak directly with the local innkeeper.",al={"magga quests","welcome quest"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Magga on?",a="Magga is a loyal member of the Horde, dwelling alongside her fellow orcs in the settlement of Razor Hill. She welcomes travelers who come through the crossroads, proudly supporting the people and defense of Durotar under Thrall's leadership.",al={"magga faction","is magga horde","magga allegiance"},it="side",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For fresh recruits leaving the harsh trials of the Valley of Trials behind, Magga provides a reassuring welcome to Durotar's first true settlement."},kw={"durotar","horde","innkeeper grosk","magga","orc","razor hill","welcome"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","npc:innkeeper-grosk"},src={"Magga"}}
E["npc:mai-ah"] = {t="npc",n="Mai'ah",z="durotar",s="Mai'ah is a jungle troll mage trainer stationed within the sun-scorched basin of the Valley of Trials in Durotar. She mentors fledgling spellcasters among the Darkspear trolls who step into the red canyons to hone their command of the arcane. For young trolls beginning the path of wizardry, she offers early guidance and instruction in the foundational arts of magic.",h="Mai'ah is a jungle troll mage trainer stationed within the sun-scorched basin of the Valley of Trials in...",sec={{t="Arcane Mentor of the Den",b="While orcs overwhelmingly favor the primal call of the elements or the physical dominance of the warrior, Darkspear trolls possess a rare affinity for arcane study. Standing within the Valley of Trials, Mai'ah serves as an instructor for young troll mages arriving to undertake their rites of adulthood. She receives candidates carrying glyphic inscriptions and begins shaping their chaotic raw power into disciplined incantations, ensuring they learn the control required to survive Durotar's perils.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mai'ah?",a="Mai'ah is a Darkspear troll mage trainer situated in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. She provides initial guidance, training, and foundational spells to newly arrived troll spellcasters before they venture out into the wider lands of the Horde.",al={"who is maiah","maiah lore","troll mage trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Why is there a troll mage trainer in an orc starting area?",a="After the Darkspear fled their sinking island home and resettled in Durotar alongside Thrall's orcs, young Darkspear trolls undergo their coming-of-age trials alongside orc youths. Because orc culture largely shuns arcane magic due to past demon corruption, troll mages like Mai'ah step in to guide their own kind.",al={"why troll mage here","valley of trials troll trainer","troll mage durotar"},it="why_here"},{q="What role does she play in training new mages?",a="Mai'ah welcomes new troll mages bearing written instructions such as glyphic parchments. She initiates their formal training, teaching the fundamentals of spellcasting so they can defend the Valley of Trials from local beasts and rogue Burning Blade infiltrators.",al={"what does maiah do","glyphic parchment maiah","maiah quests"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Mai'ah on?",a="Mai'ah is loyal to the Darkspear tribe and the Horde. Stationed in the Valley of Trials, she works under Warchief Thrall's new regime to foster the Horde's future spellcasters, dedicating her arcane knowledge to bolstering young troll and allied mages.",al={"mai'ah allegiance","who does mai'ah serve","is mai'ah horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Mai'ah want?",a="Mai'ah wants to train aspiring practitioners in the fundamentals of the arcane. She seeks to guide young novices through their introductory spells and glyphs, ensuring they possess the discipline and magical power needed to survive Durotar and serve the Horde.",al={"what does mai'ah need","mai'ah goals","why does mai'ah teach"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For Darkspear spellcasters, Mai'ah represents the beginning of their magical journey, teaching the discipline needed to weave fire, frost, and arcane energy under the harsh sun of Durotar.",["race:Troll"]="Mai'ah provides Darkspear youths in the Valley of Trials with cultural mentorship in an art rarely practiced by their orcish allies."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","mage trainer","mai'ah","maiah","troll","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","quest:98576","topic:troll"},src={"Mai'ah"}}
E["npc:master-gadrin"] = {t="npc",n="Master Gadrin",z="durotar",s="Master Gadrin is an elderly jungle troll and a venerable witch doctor of the Darkspear tribe, currently residing in Sen'jin Village. Having once trained the tribe's priests and mages alongside the renegade witch doctor Zalazane, he now coordinates efforts to aid his displaced people and break the dark curse gripping their stolen home on the Echo Isles.",h="Master Gadrin is an elderly jungle troll and a venerable witch doctor of the Darkspear tribe, currently...",sec={{t="Mentor of the Darkspear",b="Long before the Darkspear arrived on Kalimdor, Master Gadrin served as a witch doctor of his tribe in their ancestral South Seas islands, where he guided the mystical training of generations of Darkspear trolls.",sp=0},{t="The Betrayal of Zalazane",b="When the Darkspear settled the Echo Isles alongside the Horde, Gadrin and the young witch doctor Zalazane led the mystical training of the tribe's priests and mages together. Tragically, Zalazane succumbed to madness, intoxicated by the dark voodoo forces he sought to wield. The rogue practitioner enslaved his brethren's minds and drove Vol'jin and the uncorrupted Darkspear onto the mainland of Durotar. Now based in Sen'jin Village, Gadrin carries the personal sorrow of seeing a former companion become a tyrannical monster, working tirelessly to lay slain tribesfolk to rest and end Zalazane's reign.",sp=0},{t="Keeper of Ancient Lore",b="Beyond the crisis on the Echo Isles, Gadrin stands as one of the Horde's greatest living authorities on troll spiritualism and loa lore. Scholars, shamans, and even the Royal Apothecary Society seek his insight on arcane and alchemical mysteries. When strange threats like the Burning Blade brush against Durotar, or distant researchers require forgotten rituals—such as deciphering ancient tablets in Zul'Farrak to invoke Shadra the spider loa—it is Gadrin who possesses the knowledge to craft the necessary bindings.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Master Gadrin?",a="Master Gadrin is a witch doctor and an elder spiritual leader of the Darkspear trolls. Located in Sen'jin Village on the coast of Durotar, he serves as a senior advisor to Chieftain Vol'jin.",al={"master gadrin lore","who is gadrin","gadrin npc"},it="identity"},{q="What is Gadrin's history with Zalazane?",a="On the Echo Isles, Gadrin and the young witch doctor Zalazane led the mystical training of the Darkspear's priests and mages together, only for Gadrin to watch in horror as Zalazane fell to dark magic, went mad, and drove the Darkspear from their island home.",al={"gadrin and zalazane","how does gadrin know zalazane","zalazane mentor"},it="ties"},{q="Why is Gadrin staying in Sen'jin Village?",a="When Zalazane's curse drove the Darkspear off the Echo Isles, the survivors established Sen'jin Village on the southern coast of Durotar as a refuge. Gadrin remains in the village to counsel refugees, track local threats, and direct strikes against Zalazane's forces.",al={"why is gadrin here","what is gadrin doing in senjin village"},it="why_here"},{q="Who is Minshina?",a="Minshina was Master Gadrin's brother. He perished during the turmoil on the Echo Isles, and his restless spirit began calling to Gadrin in dreams. Gadrin asks trusted adventurers to recover his brother's skull so his soul may finally find peace.",al={"minshina brother","minshinas skull quest lore","who was minshina"}},{q="Does Gadrin help with the Burning Blade cult?",a="Yes. After receiving word from Zureetha Fargaze about the Burning Blade infiltrating the Valley of Trials, Gadrin monitors the cult's presence near Sen'jin Village. Seeing the wider danger to Durotar, he sends recruits north to report to Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill.",al={"burning blade durotar gadrin","orgnil soulscar gadrin"}},{q="What does Gadrin know about the loa Shadra?",a="Gadrin is a master of ancient troll theology. When the Forsaken Apothecary Lydon seeks a potent venom used by the Hinterlands Witherbark trolls, Gadrin identifies it as a gift from Shadra the spider loa, directing adventurers to Zul'Farrak to read the tablet bearing her true name, which he needs to write a spell of summoning.",al={"shadra spider loa gadrin","gadrin spider god"}},{q="Whose side is Master Gadrin on?",a="Master Gadrin is loyal to the Darkspear tribe and the Horde. Having journeyed from the Darkspear islands after Thrall saved his people from the Sea Witch, he serves as a senior elder, mystical teacher, and trusted advisor to Chieftain Vol'jin.",al={"gadrin faction","is gadrin horde","who does gadrin serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Master Gadrin want?",a="Master Gadrin seeks the death of the traitorous witch doctor Zalazane and the liberation of the Echo Isles. He wishes to free his cursed kin from Zalazane's mind control, reclaim his deceased brother Minshina's skull so the spirits may rest, and protect Sen'jin Village from emerging dangers across Durotar.",al={"what does gadrin want","gadrin goal","master gadrin motive"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, Master Gadrin is a living connection to your ancestral home and the traditions of Sen'jin. He has shaped your tribe's spiritual leadership for generations and feels a fatherly grief over the tragedy of the Echo Isles.",["class:Priest"]="As the elder who instructed Darkspear priests in communing with the spirits and the loa, Gadrin embodies the shadow and faith traditions of the jungle trolls.",["class:Mage"]="Gadrin broke ground by tutoring Darkspear trolls in the arcane arts after the Third War, proving that troll magic could expand far beyond raw ritual mojo.",["faction:Horde"]="Master Gadrin is one of Vol'jin's most trusted advisors, keeping watchful eyes on coastal Durotar and warning Razor Hill when dark cults threaten the fledgling nation of Durotar."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","echo isles","gadrin","master gadrin","minshina","sen'jin village","vol'jin","witch doctor","zalazane"},rel={"npc:vol-jin","subzone:sen-jin-village","quest:826","subzone:echo-isles","quest:808","npc:orgnil-soulscar","topic:darkspear-tribe","zone:durotar"},src={"Master Gadrin"}}
E["npc:master-vornal"] = {t="npc",n="Master Vornal",z="durotar",s="Master Vornal is an elderly Darkspear jungle troll who resides in Sen'jin Village along the southern coast of Durotar. Despite his advancing years and extensive knowledge of alchemical concoctions, he stubbornly refuses to take on any apprentices.",h="Master Vornal is an elderly Darkspear jungle troll who resides in Sen'jin Village along the southern coast of...",sec={{t="The Stubborn Brewer of Sen'jin",b="Master Vornal is a fixture of Sen'jin Village, known for brewing potent draughts and spirits for his fellow Darkspear trolls. Though age is visibly catching up with him, Vornal remains intensely independent and stubbornly refuses to train any apprentices, preferring to mix his remedies and volatile mixtures entirely by his own hand.",sp=0},{t="A Solvent Spirit",b="Vornal occasionally tasks young adventurers with gathering harsh or peculiar ingredients from the surrounding lands, such as potent materials needed for solvents and mixtures. While he is willing to reward those who assist him, he keeps his precise methods and recipes guarded, treating his craft as a solitary pursuit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Master Vornal?",a="Master Vornal is an elderly Darkspear jungle troll residing in Sen'jin Village. He brews potent spirits and remedies for the tribe but insists on working without an apprentice.",al={"master vornal","vornal","sen'jin master vornal","who is vornal"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Master Vornal?",a="He can be found standing among the huts in Sen'jin Village, situated along the southern coast of Durotar just north of the Echo Isles.",al={"vornal location","where is master vornal","find master vornal"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Master Vornal refuse to take apprentices?",a="Vornal is famously stubborn. Despite his advanced age and the community's need for his craft, he prefers to handle his concoctions alone rather than pass his secrets down to headstrong novices.",al={"vornal apprentice","why no apprentice","vornal students"}},{q="What tasks does he offer adventurers?",a="Vornal sends wanderers to gather raw components across the region for his solvent mixtures, relying on travelers for materials while keeping the brewing process strictly to himself.",al={"master vornal quest","a solvent spirit","vornal quest"},it="wants",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Master Vornal on?",a="Master Vornal is loyal to the Darkspear tribe and the Horde. He makes his home in Sen'jin Village, lending his craft and experience to help secure the young settlement against surrounding perils.",al={"vornal allegiance","who does master vornal serve","master vornal faction"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Master Vornal in Sen'jin Village?",a="Master Vornal resides along the coast of Durotar to aid his kin as they carve out a new existence in exile. From his home in Sen'jin Village, he practices his trade and tasks travelers with gathering the potent reagents he requires.",al={"why is master vornal here","why is vornal in senjin village","vornal purpose in durotar"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="What does Master Vornal want?",a="Though aging, Master Vornal prefers to work independently and refuses to burden himself with apprentices. Instead, he looks to capable adventurers to run his errands and collect rare distillations and solvents across Durotar.",al={"what does vornal want","master vornal goal","what is vornal looking for"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, Master Vornal represents the stubborn, elder craftspeople who helped establish Sen'jin Village after the tribe fled their island home.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Those skilled with raw flora will recognize Vornal's keen eye for rare catalysts and harsh natural reagents required for his solvents."},kw={"a solvent spirit","darkspear","durotar","master vornal","sen'jin village","troll","vornal"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village","quest:818","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Master Vornal"}}
E["npc:misha-tor-kren"] = {t="npc",n="Misha Tor'kren",z="durotar",s="Misha Tor'kren is an orc mother dwelling at the Tor'kren Farm in western Durotar, southeast of Thunder Ridge. Plagued by anxiety over her missing son Kron, she appeals to passing travelers for aid in discovering his fate.",h="Misha Tor'kren is an orc mother dwelling at the Tor'kren Farm in western Durotar, southeast of Thunder Ridge.",sec={{t="A Mother's Vigil",b="Tucked away near the edge of Thunder Ridge, Misha Tor'kren works her isolated farmstead while enduring a parent's worst fear. Her son Kron ventured west toward the Southfury River to hunt crocolisks and prove his mettle, but he never returned. With Durotar's frontier dangers stretching orcish watchtowers thin, Misha is left alone to hope for word of his whereabouts, desperate for anyone willing to search the riverbanks for signs of her boy.",sp=0},{t="A Grim Token",b="The Southfury River is unforgiving to young hunters. Those who comb the muddy banks inevitably discover that Kron fell victim to the river's vicious crocolisks. Returning his salvaged amulet is the only closure Misha can receive—a bitter reminder of the brutal trials young orcs face to establish their strength in Kalimdor's harsh wilderness.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Misha Tor'kren?",a="Misha Tor'kren is an orc settler residing at the Tor'kren Farm in western Durotar, situated just southeast of Thunder Ridge.",al={"misha torkren","who is misha","torkren farm owner"},it="identity"},{q="Where did her son Kron go?",a="Kron traveled west toward the Southfury River to hunt river crocolisks, eager to prove himself as an able hunter, but failed to return home.",al={"where is kron","what happened to kron","misha son"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens when you look for Kron?",a="A search of the Southfury River reveals that Kron did not survive his hunt. Slain by the beasts of the river, only his amulet remains to be recovered and brought back to his mother.",al={"is kron dead","find kron","lost but not forgotten"},sp=1},{q="Is she related to Rexxar's bear Misha?",a="No. While they share the name Misha, she is an orc farmer living in Durotar, entirely distinct from Rexxar's loyal bear companion.",al={"misha bear","rexxar bear misha","is she the bear"}},{q="Whose side is Misha Tor'kren on?",a="Misha Tor'kren is a loyal member of the Horde, living as a humble orc settler in Durotar. She makes her home at Tor'kren Farm, working the harsh red soil and relying on Horde travelers and local champions to assist her family in times of crisis.",al={"misha tor'kren faction","who does misha tor'kren serve","misha torkren horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Misha Tor'kren want?",a="Misha wants desperately to find her lost son, Kron. The young orc went missing while out hunting along the dangerous banks of the Southfury River, and she pleads with passing adventurers to search the waters, discover what became of him, and bring back any sign of his fate.",al={"what does misha want","misha tor'kren goal","why does misha need help"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Who is Misha Tor'kren tied to?",a="Misha is deeply tied to her family, most notably her missing son Kron. She manages the Tor'kren homestead southeast of Thunder Ridge, where their livelihoods depend on surviving the perils of Durotar's wilderness.",al={"misha tor'kren family","who is misha related to","misha torkren son"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Kron's reckless desire to prove his warrior prowess against Durotar's wildlife serves as a somber reminder of the steep cost of youthful pride.",["class:Hunter"]="The fate of Misha's son shows the danger of underestimating river predators before a hunter has truly mastered the wild."},kw={"crocolisk","kron","lost but not forgotten","misha","misha tor'kren","southfury river","thunder ridge","tor'kren farm"},rel={"quest:816","subzone:tor-kren-farm","subzone:southfury-river","subzone:thunder-ridge","zone:durotar","npc:misha"},src={"Misha Tor'kren"}}
E["npc:orgnil-soulscar"] = {t="npc",n="Orgnil Soulscar",z="durotar",s="Orgnil Soulscar is an orc investigator stationed at Razor Hill in central Durotar. He serves as an informal officer of the peace, coordinating defense and intelligence against internal threats to the fledgling nation. His primary concern is the shadow cast by the Burning Blade cult within Durotar's canyons.",h="Orgnil Soulscar is an orc investigator stationed at Razor Hill in central Durotar.",sec={{t="Watcher of Razor Hill",b="Positioned at Razor Hill, Orgnil Soulscar takes on the grim responsibility of tracking subversion and insidious threats across Durotar. While grunt patrols look outward toward Alliance footholds and centaur raiding parties, Orgnil focuses on rot brewing from within. He collects reports from scouts across the region, piecing together evidence of ritual corruption and illicit gatherings.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Shadow Council's Remnants",b="Orgnil's chief focus is the clandestine resurgence of the Burning Blade cult, whose warlocks hide in caves such as Skull Rock. Knowing the devastation fel magic brought upon the orcish people in past generations, Orgnil refuses to let demon worship gain another foothold near Orgrimmar. He directs trusted recruits to strike down cultists, gather ritual talismans, and consult with local hermits and shamans like Margoz to understand the dark magics at play.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Orgnil Soulscar?",a="Orgnil Soulscar is an orc official based in Razor Hill who acts as an investigator and coordinator for Durotar's defense. He directs warriors and scouts against covert dangers threatening the newly settled orc lands.",al={"who is orgnil","orgnil soulscar lore","razor hill quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="What threat is Orgnil most worried about?",a="Orgnil is dedicated to rooting out the Burning Blade cult. He sees their presence in Durotar's hidden caverns and their corruptive fel magic as a lethal threat to the fresh start Thrall envisions for the Horde.",al={"what does orgnil want","orgnil enemies","who does orgnil fight"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Orgnil send travelers to Margoz?",a="Margoz is a knowledgeable hermit living north of Razor Hill who understands the dark signs and rituals of the Burning Blade. Orgnil directs scouts to Margoz to decipher the cult's movements and unravel the brewing magical corruption.",al={"why margoz","orgnil and margoz","who is margoz to orgnil"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can Orgnil Soulscar be found?",a="Orgnil is stationed outdoors in the settlement of Razor Hill, near the central crossroads of Durotar.",al={"orgnil location","where is orgnil","find orgnil soulscar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Burning Blade in Durotar?",a="The Burning Blade is a sinister cult beholden to demonic masters and the Shadow Council. They hide in ravines like Skull Rock and the Dustwind Cave, attempting to poison Durotar's wildlife and seduce young orcs back to demonic subservience.",al={"burning blade durotar","burning blade cult","who are burning blade"}},{q="Does Orgnil work directly for Thrall?",a="Orgnil operates as part of the regional defense apparatus centered in Razor Hill, carrying out the Warchief's mandate to safeguard Durotar from sedition and demonic influence.",al={"orgnil thrall","is orgnil warchief guard"},it="leader"},{q="Whose side is Orgnil Soulscar on?",a="Orgnil is entirely loyal to the Horde and the defense of Durotar. Stationed in Razor Hill, he acts as an enforcer of local order and security, dedicating his efforts to protecting young orcish settlements from insidious internal threats like the Burning Blade cultists lurking in the canyon shadows.",al={"orgnil soulscar faction","who does orgnil serve","orgnil allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Orgnil Soulscar want?",a="Orgnil wants to root out and eradicate the shadow of the Burning Blade within Durotar. He seeks reliable intelligence on cultist activity, tasking capable adventurers with cutting down their warlocks, reclaiming stolen talismans, and consulting local hermits like Margoz to untangle the demonic corruption spreading across the land.",al={"what does orgnil want","orgnil goals","orgnil purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Orgnil Soulscar here in Razor Hill?",a="Razor Hill serves as the central hub of defense and logistics in Durotar outside of Orgrimmar. Orgnil is stationed here as an investigative authority and protector, perfectly positioned to monitor suspicious stirrings across the dry valleys and mobilize travelers against encroaching cultists and tainted beasts.",al={"why is orgnil in razor hill","orgnil role razor hill","why is orgnil here"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Orgnil Soulscar tied to?",a="Orgnil works alongside the local defenders of Razor Hill and coordinates with Margoz, an orc knowledgeable in dark arts living on a ridge to the southeast. He directs trusted scouts to Margoz to decipher strange cultist artifacts and combat demonic corruption spreading across Durotar.",al={"orgnil allies","orgnil connections","who does orgnil work with"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For young orcs, Orgnil represents the frontline against the demonic taint that once enslaved the clans, reminding new recruits of the vigilance required to keep their new homeland pure.",["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks must tread carefully around Orgnil, as his entire focus is hunting down and eradicating unchecked demonic corruption within Durotar's borders.",["faction:Horde"]="Orgnil ensures that while the Horde looks outward to build a new nation, its heartland is not hollowed out by cultists from within."},kw={"burning blade","durotar","margoz","orgnil soulscar","razor hill","shadow council","skull rock"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:828","quest:823","quest:806"},src={"Orgnil Soulscar"}}
E["npc:ormak-grimshot"] = {t="npc",n="Ormak Grimshot",z="durotar",s="Ormak Grimshot is an experienced orc hunter trainer residing in the Hunter's Hall within Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. Accompanied by his loyal wolf, Grimfang, he instructs young hunters of the Horde in tracking, marksmanship, and bonding with wild beasts.",h="Ormak Grimshot is an experienced orc hunter trainer residing in the Hunter's Hall within Orgrimmar's Valley...",sec={{t="Master of the Hunt",b="Stationed within the Hunter's Hall in the Valley of Honor, Ormak Grimshot serves as a cornerstone of martial instruction for the Horde's trackers and marksmen. Alongside his companion wolf, Grimfang, Ormak imparts the foundational discipline needed to survive Kalimdor's harsh wilderness. For orc and troll hunters arriving from their trials in Durotar, he provides vital guidance on the sacred art of taming and commanding wild beasts, ensuring every hunter forms an enduring bond with their animal partner.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ormak Grimshot?",a="Ormak Grimshot is a veteran orc hunter trainer stationed in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. He teaches new Horde hunters advanced skills in ranged combat and beast mastery.",al={"who is ormak","ormak grimshot lore","ormak hunter trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Ormak Grimshot?",a="Ormak is located inside the Hunter's Hall, nestled in the Valley of Honor in eastern Orgrimmar. He stands near his pet wolf, Grimfang.",al={"ormak location","where is grimshot","find ormak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is the wolf beside him?",a="The wolf at his side is Grimfang, Ormak's loyal companion animal, illustrating the tight bond between a skilled hunter and their pet.",al={"ormak wolf","grimfang","ormak pet"}},{q="What role does he play for new hunters?",a="Ormak directs novice orc and troll hunters on how to train, feed, and manage their newly tamed beasts once they finish their basic trials in Durotar.",al={"hunter pet quest orgrimmar","taming quest ormak","training the beast ormak"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose side is Ormak Grimshot on?",a="Ormak is entirely devoted to the Horde and the defense of Durotar. Standing among the ranks of trainers in the Valley of Honor, his loyalty lies with Warchief Thrall's new nation and the hunters who safeguard its borders.",al={"ormak faction","ormak horde or alliance","who does ormak serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Ormak Grimshot want?",a="Ormak wants to ensure that the hunters of the Horde are disciplined, skilled marksmen capable of surviving the wilds. Alongside his pet wolf, Grimfang, he seeks to hone the talents of promising scouts and test their resourcefulness through demanding trials.",al={"ormak goal","what does ormak need","ormak grimshot purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Ormak Grimshot in the Valley of Honor?",a="Ormak is stationed in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor to train marksmen in the Hunter's Hall. He remains close to the heart of the Horde's military hub, where seasoned scouts and young trainees alike come seeking guidance on beast mastery and fieldcraft.",al={"why is ormak here","ormak grimshot location why","why is ormak in orgrimmar"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Ormak is an essential mentor for Horde hunters, guiding them through the responsibilities of taming and maintaining a loyal animal companion.",["race:Orc"]="Reflecting classic orcish survival skills, Ormak exemplifies how orcs work alongside wolves and native predators to defend Durotar."},kw={"beast training","grimfang","hunter trainer","hunter's hall","orgrimmar","ormak grimshot","valley of honor"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-honor","quest:6081","topic:horde","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Ormak Grimshot"}}
E["npc:rezlak"] = {t="npc",n="Rezlak",z="durotar",s="Rezlak is a goblin entrepreneur and member of the Tinkers' Union stationed along the dusty roads of Durotar south of Orgrimmar. He hires traveling adventurers to salvage his missing supplies and clear out the harpy nests disrupting regional communications.",h="Rezlak is a goblin entrepreneur and member of the Tinkers' Union stationed along the dusty roads of Durotar...",sec={{t="A Pragmatic Tinkers' Union Agent",b="Perched beside the canyon roads connecting Razor Hill to Orgrimmar, Rezlak represents the Tinkers' Union—a goblin syndicate focused on engineering, supply lines, and industrial pragmatism. Rezlak cares little for the factional tensions of Kalimdor so long as business runs smoothly. When the fierce Dustwind harpies raided his cargo caravans and disrupted local communication lines, Rezlak stayed put, preferring to contract out the dangerous work of extermination and recovery to any passerby willing to turn a profit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rezlak?",a="Rezlak is an independent goblin merchant and engineer affiliated with the Tinkers' Union. Stationed along the main northern road through Durotar, he seeks willing mercenaries to secure his supply lines and reclaim lost gear from regional pests.",al={"rezlak lore","who is rezlak","rezlak durotar"},it="identity"},{q="What is Rezlak doing in Durotar?",a="Rezlak works along the trade routes between the central plains and the canyon pass leading to Orgrimmar. His supply caravans were ambushed by the Dustwind harpies, leaving his cargo strewn across the arid canyons and his vital communication lines severed.",al={"why is rezlak in durotar","rezlak purpose","rezlak mission"},it="why_here"},{q="Which quests does Rezlak offer?",a="Rezlak offers two primary tasks: 'Winds in the Desert', which tasks adventurers with retrieving sacks of lost supplies scattered across the canyon floor, and 'Securing the Lines', which requires thinning out the aggressive Dustwind harpies nesting nearby.",al={"rezlak quests","what quests does rezlak give"},gp=true},{q="What is the Tinkers' Union?",a="The Tinkers' Union is an enterprising goblin trade organization that oversees mechanics, inventors, and logistical operations. Like many goblin cartels and guilds, its members prioritize profitable commerce and practical problem-solving above political loyalty.",al={"tinkers union","rezlak faction"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Rezlak on?",a="Rezlak represents goblin commercial enterprise rather than partisan loyalty. Although he is stationed along a major Durotar roadway deep within Horde territory and is affiliated with the Tinkers' Union, he maintains the pragmatic neutrality typical of his race, prioritizing engineering contracts and salvaged equipment over factional politics.",al={"rezlak faction","is rezlak horde","rezlak horde or alliance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Rezlak want?",a="Rezlak needs assistance securing his operations along the Durotar roadway. Strong desert winds and local troublemakers constantly disrupt his equipment and supply lines, so he employs able adventurers to recover scattered supplies and secure the surrounding area against threats that jeopardize his work.",al={"what does rezlak need","rezlak goals","rezlak quest motive"},it="wants",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As a representative of the Tinkers' Union, Rezlak values mechanical efficiency, practical tools, and salvaged components above all else.",["faction:Horde"]="Though stationed right outside Orgrimmar, Rezlak represents the purely transactional relationship between neutral goblin guilds and the fledgling Horde."},kw={"durotar","dustwind harpies","rezlak","securing the lines","tinkers union","winds in the desert"},rel={"quest:834","quest:835","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:goblin","topic:horde"},src={"Rezlak"}}
E["npc:rhinag"] = {t="npc",n="Rhinag",z="durotar",s="Rhinag is an afflicted jungle troll seeking shelter within a modest homestead at Rocktusk Farm in Durotar. Paralyzed by the harsh venom of the region's scorpions, he relies entirely on passing travelers to secure him a timely remedy.",h="Rhinag is an afflicted jungle troll seeking shelter within a modest homestead at Rocktusk Farm in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Venomous Peril",b="While traversing the arid terrain of Durotar, Rhinag fell victim to the vicious sting of a local Venomtail Scorpid. Overwhelmed by the potent poison, he managed to drag himself into the dilapidated shelter at Rocktusk Farm. Incapacitated and isolated, his survival hinges on anyone who happens by with the resolve to procure a venomtail antidote before the toxins take their final toll.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rhinag?",a="Rhinag is a jungle troll traveler who found himself stranded and paralyzed at Durotar's Rocktusk Farm after suffering a venomous sting from a native scorpion.",al={"who is rhinag","rhinag lore","troll at rocktusk"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Rhinag be found?",a="He is resting inside the small building at Rocktusk Farm, situated in central Durotar south of Razor Hill.",al={"rhinag location","where is rhinag","rocktusk farm troll"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happened to him?",a="While traversing the plains of Durotar, Rhinag was stung by a dangerous Venomtail Scorpid. The virulent toxin left him incapacitated, requiring an antidote to neutralize the poison before it proves fatal.",al={"why is rhinag sick","what poisoned rhinag","need for a cure backstory"}},{q="Whose side is Rhinag on?",a="Rhinag is allied with the Horde. As a jungle troll resting within the borders of Durotar, he relies on travelers and Horde champions passing through Rocktusk Farm to assist him in his time of need.",al={"rhinag faction","is rhinag horde","rhinag allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Rhinag want?",a="Rhinag desperately needs an antidote. Having suffered the sting of a local venomtail scorpid, he requires a timely cure before the venom takes full toll on his body.",al={"rhinag quest","what does rhinag need","rhinag help"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Rhinag at Rocktusk Farm?",a="Rhinag has taken shelter inside the farmstead at Rocktusk Farm after falling victim to a venomtail scorpid sting, waiting inside the building for aid before the poison completely overwhelms him.",al={"why is rhinag here","rhinag rocktusk farm why","what brought rhinag here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Finding a kinsman struck down by native wildlife in the arid wastes of Durotar is a stark reminder of the trials the Darkspear tribe faces in carving out a home alongside the Horde."},kw={"antidote","durotar","need for a cure","rhinag","rocktusk farm","venomtail scorpid"},rel={"quest:812","subzone:rocktusk-farm","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Rhinag"}}
E["npc:rwag"] = {t="npc",n="Rwag",z="durotar",s="Rwag is the orc rogue trainer stationed in the Den, tucked within Durotar's Valley of Trials. He instructs newly arrived orcs and trolls in the arts of stealth, subterfuge, and dirty fighting under the watchful gaze of the Horde.",h="Rwag is the orc rogue trainer stationed in the Den, tucked within Durotar's Valley of Trials.",sec={{t="Shadows of the Valley",b="Operating deep within the cave known as the Den, Rwag trains fledgling rogues, cutpurses, and thieves before they step out into the wider world of Durotar. While the new Horde champions martial honor and battlefield valor, Rwag understands that subtlety, poisons, and a well-placed dagger remain invaluable tools for survival in an unforgiving desert. He keeps a sharp eye on Valley business and harbors deep suspicions regarding the dark practitioners also sheltering in the cave, particularly the warlock Nartok.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rwag?",a="Rwag is an orc rogue trainer situated inside the Den in the Valley of Trials. He instructs novice orc and troll rogues as they begin their training in Durotar.",al={"who is rwag","rwag valley of trials","orc rogue trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Rwag?",a="Rwag is located deep inside the Den, a cavern cut into the rocky cliffs of the Valley of Trials in Durotar, standing among several other class trainers.",al={"rwag location","where is rwag","find rwag"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Rwag think of the warlocks in the Den?",a="Rwag openly distrusts the warlocks who share the Den, specifically keeping a cautious eye on the fel practitioner Nartok, noting that dark magic and secretive cultists require constant vigilance.",al={"rwag nartok","why does rwag distrust warlocks","rwag encrypted parchment"},it="conflict"},{q="Which classes does Rwag train?",a="Rwag exclusively trains rogues, offering early martial instruction in abilities like Eviscerate and, at the Shattered Hand's request, keeping an eye on new recruits and passing along anything the Hand might need of them.",al={"what does rwag teach","can rwag train me"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Rwag on?",a="Rwag serves the Horde, stationed right in the heart of Durotar to instruct fledgling orc and troll cutpurses. Though his craft thrives on deception, his allegiance lies firmly with the new nation Thrall has founded.",al={"rwag faction","is rwag horde","who does rwag serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Rwag want?",a="Rwag aims to hone the stealth, cunning, and martial skill of aspiring rogues starting out in the Valley of Trials. He expects his pupils to master silent footfalls, precise strikes, and keen vigilance—all while keeping a wary eye on untrustworthy figures lurking nearby.",al={"what does rwag want","rwag goal","rwag motives"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Rwag here?",a="Rwag makes his post inside the Den so he can evaluate and instruct new recruits eager to walk the path of shadows. Durotar requires scouts and discreet blades just as much as frontline warriors, and he ensures those with a knack for theft and subterfuge are properly disciplined.",al={"why is rwag in the den","rwag valley of trials role","why is rwag in durotar"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Rwag tied to?",a="Rwag works alongside the other class mentors in the Valley of Trials, though he keeps a suspicious distance from the warlock trainer Nartok, whom he openly distrusts. His ties remain with the Horde's network of rogue trainers and the young scouts he sends out across Durotar.",al={"rwag connections","who does rwag know","rwag nartok"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="For young orc and troll rogues stepping into the Valley of Trials, Rwag is the very first mentor in basic skulduggery, teaching early offensive techniques and deciphering secret ciphers.",["race:Orc"]="Rwag represents the practical, unsanitized edge of orcish survival, proving that even in Thrall's honorable new Horde, shadows and cold steel remain vital."},kw={"durotar","nartok","rogue","rwag","the den","trainer","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","quest:1089","quest:3083","quest:3088","zone:durotar"},src={"Rwag"}}
E["npc:thotar"] = {t="npc",n="Thotar",z="durotar",s="Thotar is a seasoned orc hunter trainer stationed in the settlement of Razor Hill in Durotar. He guides aspiring Horde scouts and marksmen in the ancient traditions of tracking, archery, and bonding with wild beasts. For young orcs and trolls taking their first steps outside the Valley of Trials, he provides the foundational rites needed to master Kalimdor's rugged fauna.",h="Thotar is a seasoned orc hunter trainer stationed in the settlement of Razor Hill in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Mentor in Razor Hill",b="Perched within the fortified hub of Razor Hill, Thotar serves as a veteran instructor for marksmen of the Horde. While new recruits learn the very basics in the Valley of Trials, it falls to Thotar to guide hunters as they face the harsher predatory wilderness of Durotar. Drawing upon traditions passed down through countless generations of orcs, he teaches not only marksmanship, but the deeper respect required to live alongside and direct Kalimdor's deadliest creatures.",sp=0},{t="Taming the Wilds",b="Thotar plays a crucial role in introducing young hunters to the ancient art of beast taming. Through a sequence of trials, he sends novices into the arid canyons to pacify and commune with native beasts, such as venomous scorpid, armored surf crawlers, and cunning boars. By guiding these young scouts through the sacred rites of taming, Thotar ensures the Horde's trackers build a loyal bond with nature rather than merely attempting to dominate it by force.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Thotar?",a="Thotar is a veteran orc hunter trainer stationed in Razor Hill in Durotar. He educates young hunters in traditional wilderness lore, marksmanship, and animal taming.",al={"who is thotar","thotar lore","what does thotar do"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Thotar be found?",a="He is located in the Horde settlement of Razor Hill, situated in central Durotar just north of the Valley of Trials.",al={"thotar location","where is thotar","find thotar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What traditions does Thotar teach?",a="Thotar teaches the ancient survival and tracking traditions passed down through generations of orcs. He emphasizes weapon mastery, wilderness survival, and learning to bond with animal companions through patience and ritual.",al={"what does thotar teach","hunter traditions","thotar training"},it="purpose"},{q="Does Thotar only train orcs?",a="While he is an orc steeped in his people's ways, Thotar instructs any hunter aligned with the Horde who arrives in Razor Hill, regularly mentoring Darkspear trolls and wandering tauren passing through Durotar.",al={"can trolls train with thotar","thotar tauren","who does thotar train"},it="people"},{q="What tasks does Thotar give to young hunters?",a="Thotar directs novice hunters on the rites of 'Taming the Beast,' tasking them with tracking down native Durotar wildlife—such as boars, surf crawlers, and scorpids—and using a taming rod to earn their trust and obedience.",al={"thotar quests","taming the beast thotar","what does thotar send you to do"},it="target"},{q="Why is beast taming so important in his training?",a="For Horde hunters, a beast companion is a vital partner on the battlefield and in the wild. Thotar teaches that properly bonding with a beast ensures mutual survival, transforming raw predators into loyal defenders of the Horde.",al={"why tame beasts","hunter pet lore","purpose of beast taming"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Whose side is Thotar on?",a="Thotar stands firmly with the Horde. Stationed in Razor Hill, he dedicates his craft to strengthening the Horde's ranks by training newly arrived orc, troll, and tauren hunters to survive the wild and defend their lands.",al={"thotar faction","is thotar horde","thotar allegiance"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Thotar want?",a="Thotar seeks to pass down ancestral hunting traditions to a new generation. He expects aspiring hunters to prove their respect for the wilderness by mastering the arts of tracking, survival, and beast taming.",al={"what does thotar want","thotar goal","thotar purpose"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Thotar in Razor Hill?",a="Razor Hill serves as the primary gathering settlement for young adventurers venturing out of the Valley of Trials. Thotar remains here alongside other trainers to prepare emerging hunters before they head deeper into the perils of Durotar and the wider world.",al={"why is thotar here","why is thotar in razor hill","thotar razor hill"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Thotar represents a key milestone for young Horde hunters, teaching the vital rites of beast taming and wilderness mastery once novices step out of the starter valleys.",["race:Orc"]="Thotar preserves and passes down traditional orcish hunting customs, ensuring that life on Kalimdor remains anchored in deep ancestral respect for tracking and beast companionship.",["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear hunters setting out from Sen'jin Village, Thotar offers vital instruction that blends ancestral Horde survival skills with the predatory challenges of Durotar.",["faction:Horde"]="As a frontline trainer in Razor Hill, Thotar ensures that scouts and marksmen patrolling Durotar's borders are disciplined, sharp-eyed, and well-bonded with combat beasts."},kw={"durotar","hunter","hunter trainer","kaplak","orc","razor hill","taming the beast","thotar"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:6061","quest:6081","quest:6065","npc:kaplak","topic:troll","topic:tauren"},src={"Thotar"}}
E["npc:ukor"] = {t="npc",n="Ukor",z="durotar",s="Ukor is an orc peon resting near the eastern path outside the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Eager to help his people, he carried supplies all the way from Razor Hill, only to find the training grounds already had plenty of provisions.",h="Ukor is an orc peon resting near the eastern path outside the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Peon's Errand",b="While many orc peons spend their lives under the watchful eye of harsh taskmasters cutting lumber or hauling rocks, Ukor attempted to perform a service of his own initiative. Tasked or inspired to bring food from Razor Hill to the recruits training in the Valley of Trials, he made the dangerous trek across Durotar's red plains past prowling scorpid and boars. Upon arrival, he discovered the Valley was already well-stocked and had no need for his bundle. Exhausted and somewhat disheartened by the roadside, he relies on passing young adventurers to return the unused provisions back north to Innkeeper Grosk.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ukor?",a="Ukor is an earnest orc peon stationed along the road leading east out of the Valley of Trials in southern Durotar.",al={"ukor lore","who is ukor","what does ukor do"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Ukor standing by the road with a sack of food?",a="Ukor carried a heavy bundle of rations down from Razor Hill to feed the young warriors training in the Valley of Trials. When he arrived, he found they had no shortage of provisions, leaving him stranded with unneeded food.",al={"why is ukor here","ukor quest reason","ukor food bundle"},it="why_here"},{q="What does Ukor ask passing travelers to do?",a="Too afraid of the beasts along the road to carry the sack back himself, Ukor asks fledgling adventurers heading north toward Razor Hill to return the bundle to Innkeeper Grosk.",al={"ukor task","what does ukor want","peons burden quest"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Ukor on?",a="Ukor is a loyal peon of the Horde. Humble and dutiful, he serves Durotar and his kin by hauling supplies and running errands between settlements like Razor Hill and the Valley of Trials, braving wild beasts without a complaint.",al={"ukor faction","is ukor horde","who does ukor serve"},it="side",add=true},{q="Who is Ukor tied to?",a="Ukor answers to Innkeeper Grosk back in Razor Hill. He undertook the journey to the Valley of Trials on Grosk's behalf to deliver fresh provisions, and he relies on passing adventurers to return surplus stock to the innkeeper.",al={"ukor allies","who does ukor know","ukor innkeeper grosk"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Orc peons bear the hard physical labor that builds the new Horde, and Ukor shows that even humble laborers possess a strong desire to support the warriors of Durotar.",["faction:Horde"]="For new recruits emerging from their trials, aiding Ukor marks one of the first opportunities to support everyday Horde logistics between settlements."},kw={"a peon's burden","durotar","grosk","peon","razor hill","ukor","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:2161","npc:innkeeper-grosk","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar"},src={"Ukor"}}
E["npc:vol-jin"] = {t="npc",n="Vol'jin",z="durotar",s="Vol'jin is the chieftain of the Darkspear trolls and a master shadow hunter. Residing in Grommash Hold alongside Warchief Thrall, he acts as a trusted advisor to the Horde while working to secure his displaced people a permanent home in Durotar.",h="Vol'jin is the chieftain of the Darkspear trolls and a master shadow hunter.",sec={{t="Chieftain of the Darkspear",b="Vol'jin took up leadership of the Darkspear tribe following the tragic death of his father, Sen'jin, on their ancestral island home. When sea witch-worshipping murlocs and human forces nearly destroyed the isolated tribe, Thrall's orcs intervened, forging a deep bond between the two peoples. After evacuating the ruins of their islands, Vol'jin pledged his trolls to the New Horde and brought them across the Great Sea to Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="Council in the Valley of Wisdom",b="Though the Darkspear established settlements in Durotar, internal betrayals—namely the treachery of Zalazane on the Echo Isles—forced many refugees to the mainland at Sen'jin Village. Vol'jin spends much of his time inside Grommash Hold in Orgrimmar, lending his sharp strategic counsel and shadow hunter prowess directly to Thrall. From the heart of the orcish capital, he watches over the fledgling Horde while striving to reclaim his people's rightful lands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Vol'jin?",a="Vol'jin is the leader and chieftain of the Darkspear troll tribe. He is a skilled shadow hunter who represents his people within the Horde leadership, serving as one of Warchief Thrall's closest counselors in Orgrimmar.",al={"who is the troll leader","voljin lore","darkspear leader"},it="identity"},{q="Where does Vol'jin live?",a="Vol'jin is located in Grommash Hold, in the Valley of Wisdom within Orgrimmar, standing right beside Warchief Thrall.",al={"where is voljin","voljin location","find voljin"},it="place"},{q="Why did the Darkspear join the Horde?",a="During the Third War, Thrall's fleet washed ashore on the Darkspear Islands. The orcs allied with the trolls against hostile humans and a fanatical murloc army. When Sen'jin fell in battle, Vol'jin honored his father's vision by pledging his tribe to Thrall and accompanying the orcs to Kalimdor.",al={"why are trolls horde","darkspear horde history","thrall and voljin"}},{q="Why aren't the Darkspear living on their own islands?",a="After settling off the coast of Durotar on the Echo Isles, Vol'jin's childhood friend and witch doctor Zalazane was driven mad by dark magic. Zalazane enslaved his fellow tribesmen, forcing Vol'jin and the surviving Darkspear to flee to the mainland at Sen'jin Village.",al={"what happened to echo isles","why are trolls in senjin village","zalazane betrayal"}},{q="Whose side is Vol'jin on?",a="Vol'jin is entirely devoted to the Horde and his own exiled Darkspear trolls. Ever since Thrall and the orcs rescued his tribe from slaughter in their island homeland, Vol'jin has honored his father's oath of allegiance. He serves as one of Thrall's most trusted confidants, offering wise counsel and tactical guidance from within the heart of Orgrimmar.",al={"voljin faction","who does voljin serve","is voljin horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="What does Vol'jin want?",a="Vol'jin wants above all to secure a stable and prosperous future for the Darkspear tribe, fulfilling the dying vision of his father, Sen'jin. He works closely with Thrall to cement the Horde's foothold across Durotar, striving to protect his displaced people from the hostile threats of Kalimdor and preserve their ancestral traditions.",al={"voljin goals","what are voljin's motives","what does voljin seek"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Why is Vol'jin in Orgrimmar?",a="Vol'jin resides in Grommash Hold beside Thrall to represent the Darkspear trolls at the very center of Horde leadership. In addition to guiding his people, he acts as a chief strategist and spiritual advisor to the Warchief, coordinating tribal defenses and strengthening the vital alliance between troll and orc.",al={"why is voljin in orgrimmar","why is voljin here","what is voljin doing in orgrimmar"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="Who is Vol'jin tied to?",a="Vol'jin is the son and successor of the revered witch doctor Sen'jin, whose sacrifice saved the Darkspear. He shares an unshakeable bond with Warchief Thrall, whom he advises daily. Among his own kin, he was raised alongside Zalazane and studied under Master Gadrin, though his ties to the loa guide his path as a shadow hunter.",al={"voljin allies","voljin connections","who is voljin related to"},it="ties",add=true},{q="Why is Vol'jin famous?",a="Vol'jin is renowned as both the chieftain of the Darkspear tribe and an accomplished shadow hunter, deeply attuned to the loa. He led his people through devastating murloc raids, human invasions, and exile, earning the eternal respect of trolls and the highest esteem among the founders of the new Horde.",al={"why is voljin revered","voljin reputation","is voljin famous"},it="fame",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Vol'jin is your chieftain, guiding the Darkspear through displacement and hardship with spiritual wisdom and tactical resolve.",["faction:Horde"]="Alongside Thrall, Vol'jin serves as a pillar of the New Horde, offering cunning advice and the fierce loyalty of the jungle trolls."},kw={"darkspear","grommash hold","orgrimmar","sen'jin","shadow hunter","thrall","vol'jin","zalazane"},rel={"npc:thrall","topic:darkspear-tribe","topic:troll","zone:orgrimmar","quest:826","npc:master-gadrin","topic:horde","zone:durotar"},src={"Vol'jin"}}
E["npc:zjolnir"] = {t="npc",n="Zjolnir",z="durotar",s="Zjolnir is a Darkspear troll mount breeder stationed in Sen'jin Village along the southern coast of Durotar. He provides trained riding raptors to the Darkspear and trustworthy champions of the Horde. For troll riders, his stable of vicious, loyal beasts is a point of deep cultural pride.",h="Zjolnir is a Darkspear troll mount breeder stationed in Sen'jin Village along the southern coast of Durotar.",sec={{t="Breeder of the Darkspear Raptors",b="Situated near the pens of Sen'jin Village, Zjolnir tends to the fierce raptors favored as mounts by the Darkspear trolls. Raptors are temperamental and predatory by nature, requiring an expert hand to raise and saddle for war. Zjolnir freely provides these prized whistled mounts to fellow trolls who have learned the necessary riding arts. Outsiders belonging to the wider Horde must first earn the exalted trust of the Darkspear tribe before Zjolnir will consider trusting them with one of his pack.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Zjolnir?",a="Zjolnir is located in Sen'jin Village, a coastal Darkspear settlement found in the southern reaches of Durotar, standing beside the village's raptor pens.",al={"zjolnir location","where is zjolnir","raptor vendor location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Zjolnir sell?",a="Zjolnir sells whistle-summoned raptors, the signature racial mounts of the Darkspear trolls. His stock includes various breeds and colors suited for both newly trained riders and experienced veterans.",al={"zjolnir vendor","what does he sell","troll mount vendor"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Can non-trolls buy raptors from him?",a="Yes, but non-trolls must earn exalted standing with the Darkspear Trolls before Zjolnir will sell to them. Trolls can purchase from him immediately once they possess the required riding skill.",al={"can orcs buy raptors","who can buy mounts from zjolnir","horde raptor mount"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Who is Zjolnir?",a="Zjolnir is a Darkspear jungle troll handler and breeder who tends to the tribe's prized raptors. Stationed in Sen'jin Village on the Durotar coast, he provides sturdy raptor mounts to his fellow trolls and trusted champions of the Horde who have proven their dedication to the Darkspear tribe.",al={"who is zjolnir","zjolnir lore","who is the raptor vendor"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Whose side is Zjolnir on?",a="He is fiercely loyal to the Darkspear tribe and the Horde. Residing in Sen'jin Village under the leadership of Chieftain Vol'jin, he offers his carefully trained beasts exclusively to his kin and to outsiders who have earned exalted standing with the Darkspear.",al={"zjolnir faction","who does zjolnir serve","is zjolnir horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Zjolnir here?",a="Sen'jin Village serves as the primary coastal haven for the Darkspear trolls following their exile from the Echo Isles. Zjolnir stays here to raise, care for, and supply the tribe's fierce raptor mounts for scouts, raiders, and riders defending their new home in Durotar.",al={"why is zjolnir in senjin village","what is zjolnir doing here"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="What does Zjolnir want?",a="Zjolnir aims to see the Darkspear tribe well-mounted and strong. He seeks capable riders worthy of handling the tribe's predatory raptors, entrusting the deadly beasts only to fellow trolls or allies whose service and loyalty to the Darkspear have been proven beyond question.",al={"what does zjolnir want","zjolnir goals"},it="wants",add=true},{q="Who is Zjolnir tied to?",a="He is bound directly to the Darkspear trolls and serves the community established in Sen'jin Village. His work directly supports the tribe's defense and mobility under Chieftain Vol'jin and the wider Horde alliance founded alongside Thrall.",al={"zjolnir affiliations","who does zjolnir work with"},it="ties",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, Zjolnir provides the swift, clawed beasts central to their heritage and fighting traditions.",["faction:Horde"]="Any Horde warrior who proves their steadfast devotion to the Darkspear tribe can earn the privilege of riding one of Zjolnir's raptors into battle."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","mount","raptor","sen'jin village","troll mount","zjolnir"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Zjolnir"}}
E["npc:zureetha-fargaze"] = {t="npc",n="Zureetha Fargaze",z="durotar",s="Zureetha Fargaze is an orc mentor stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar alongside Foreman Thazz'ril. Vigilant against corruption, she directs young Horde recruits to investigate and root out the dark influence of the Burning Blade cult hiding within the valley.",h="Zureetha Fargaze is an orc mentor stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar alongside Foreman Thazz'ril.",sec={{t="Eyes in the Valley",b="While Foreman Thazz'ril oversees the labor and discipline of young orcs and Darkspear trolls, Zureetha Fargaze keeps watch for subtler, more insidious threats. The Burning Blade cult has secretly infiltrated the Valley of Trials, corrupting lesser demons and gathering strength in the nearby cavern of Burning Blade Coven. Zureetha tasks untested adventurers with retrieving medallions from the cultists to confirm their presence and dismantle their early operations before directing seasoned recruits outward into Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zureetha Fargaze?",a="Zureetha Fargaze is an orc questgiver stationed in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. She stands near Foreman Thazz'ril and monitors the hidden threats creeping into the training grounds.",al={"zureetha fargaze lore","who is zureetha","fargaze valley of trials"},it="identity"},{q="Why is she concerned about the Burning Blade?",a="The demonic Burning Blade cult has taken root inside a nearby cave, drawing foul familiars and corrupting the peaceful trial grounds. Zureetha seeks proof of their presence through their cultist medallions and sends recruits to thin their numbers.",al={"burning blade valley of trials","why does zureetha want medallions","burning blade cult durotar"},it="wants"},{q="Where does she send recruits after their initial trials?",a="Once young orcs and trolls prove their competence against the local threats, Zureetha dispatches them southeast across the ridge to Sen'jin Village to aid the Darkspear tribe.",al={"where do i go after zureetha","zureetha next quest","report to sen'jin"},it="next_step"},{q="Whose side is Zureetha Fargaze on?",a="Zureetha stands firmly with Thrall's Horde. Stationed in the Valley of Trials alongside Foreman Thazz'ril, her duty is to guide young recruits and safeguard the training grounds from internal corruption and hidden enemies.",al={"zureetha fargaze faction","who does zureetha serve","is zureetha horde"},it="side",add=true},{q="Why is Zureetha Fargaze here in the Valley of Trials?",a="She is posted in the Valley of Trials to watch over the newly arrived orcs and trolls as they begin their training. More urgently, she remains vigilant against the shadowy reach of the Burning Blade cult, which has begun creeping into the valley's nearby caves.",al={"why is zureetha in valley of trials","zureetha purpose durotar","why is zureetha here"},it="why_here",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For young orcs taking their first steps into the world, Zureetha represents the watchful vigilance required to keep the demonic taint of the past from polluting their new homeland.",["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks in the Valley of Trials cross paths with Zureetha's tasks early on, dealing with the loose, corrupt vile familiars tied to the Burning Blade's dark summonings."},kw={"burning blade","burning blade medallion","durotar","foreman thazz'ril","valley of trials","zureetha fargaze"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","subzone:sen-jin-village"},src={"Zureetha Fargaze"}}
E["quest:1462"] = {t="quest",n="Earth Sapta",z="durotar",s="Earth Sapta is a replenishment ritual offered by Seer Ravenfeather in Camp Narache. Young shaman undertaking their initiation to commune with the spirits of the stone require this draught to open their inner sight. Should a novice lose or spill their prepared brew before finishing their rite, the seer prepares another to ensure their trial may continue.",h="Earth Sapta is a replenishment ritual offered by Seer Ravenfeather in Camp Narache.",sec={{t="A Visionary Draught",b="The path of the shaman begins with attuning the mortal senses to forces beyond physical sight. To perceive the elemental spirits of the land, an initiate must ingest a potent ritual brew known as a sapta. Infused with natural essences bound to the element of stone and soil, the Earth Sapta lifts the veil between the physical realm and the spiritual plane, allowing a novice to commune directly with the earth elementals of Mulgore.",sp=0},{t="A Second Chance at Sight",b="The spiritual arts demand discipline, but seasoned seers recognize that young initiates often falter or misplace sacred reagents while braving the wilds. Seer Ravenfeather keeps a steady vigil at Camp Narache, ensuring that any pupil who loses their brew before their communion at the stone monument can renew their preparation. With quiet patience, she provides another vessel so the novice may face the spirits unbroken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is an Earth Sapta?",a="An Earth Sapta is a sacred herbal preparation brewed by shamanic elders. When drunk by an initiate, it awakens their inner senses, granting them the spiritual sight required to perceive and commune with earth elementals that are otherwise invisible to ordinary eyes.",al={"what is sapta","earth sapta lore","what does the brew do"},it="item"},{q="Why would an initiate need another Earth Sapta?",a="Trainees undertaking their trials in the wilds sometimes lose, spill, or consume their draught prematurely before reaching the designated sacred site. Seer Ravenfeather provides another dose so their spiritual training is not permanently halted by a simple mistake.",al={"lost my sapta","why get another sapta","lost earth sapta"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Seer Ravenfeather?",a="Seer Ravenfeather is a tauren spiritual guide stationed at Camp Narache in Mulgore. She oversees the earliest trials of young tauren shaman, guiding them through their first communion with the spirits of the earth.",al={"who is ravenfeather","seer ravenfeather lore","camp narache seer"},it="identity"},{q="Why must shaman drink a sapta to see elementals?",a="Novice shaman have not yet honed their innate bond with the elements to perceive them at will. The sapta acts as a bridge, altering the drinker's spiritual perception until they learn to listen and commune with the elements through their own power.",al={"why need a potion to see spirits","why drink sapta"},it="power"},{q="Where does the trial of the Earth Sapta take place?",a="The ritual trial is conducted in the hills of Red Cloud Mesa in Mulgore, near Camp Narache. Novices carry the draught to a sacred stone monument where the local earth spirits dwell.",al={"where do i use sapta","call of earth location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Do all shaman use saptas?",a="Both tauren and orcish shamanic traditions employ saptas during their initial elemental initiations. Each element they first commune with, such as earth, fire and water, has its own sapta to help align the shaman's senses to that specific elemental plane.",al={"do orcs use saptas","are saptas only tauren"}},{q="Why does Seer Ravenfeather give you another Earth Sapta?",a="Seer Ravenfeather is tasked with guiding young tauren initiates through their elemental trials. Without drinking the Earth Sapta, an initiate cannot commune with the spirit of the earth or complete their communion. Should you misplace or spill your draught, Ravenfeather provides another so that your sacred journey is not halted before you ever reach the elemental.",al={"why ravenfeather earth sapta","seer ravenfeather motive","why give sapta again"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The sapta is the foundational tool of your early training, serving as the spiritual catalyst that first opens your eyes to the elemental forces guiding the world.",["race:Tauren"]="Honoring the Earth Mother begins with learning to hear the land, and the elders of Camp Narache take great care to ensure no youth is turned away from the sacred path.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde's reliance on shamanic traditions is nurtured in places like Mulgore, where tribal seers patiently cultivate the next generation of spiritual leaders."},kw={"call of earth","camp narache","draught","earth sapta","elemental","mulgore","seer ravenfeather","shaman"},rel={"npc:seer-ravenfeather","quest:1516","zone:mulgore"},m={start="Seer Ravenfeather",level="4",faction="Horde",id=1462},src={"Earth Sapta (Mulgore)"}}
E["quest:1463"] = {t="quest",n="Earth Sapta",z="durotar",s="This errand serves as a test of responsibility for an initiate shaman in the Valley of Trials. If an acolyte misplaces the consecrated Earth Sapta before communing with the spirits of the land, Canaga Earthcaller provides a replacement with a stern reminder to treat sacred draughts with care.",h="This errand serves as a test of responsibility for an initiate shaman in the Valley of Trials.",sec={{t="A Second Chance with the Elements",b="The path of a shaman requires absolute mindfulness and respect for the spirits of the world. Prepared through specific rituals, the Earth Sapta is an elemental brew intended to thin the veil between the physical realm and the spirits of stone and soil. When an initiate inadvertently misplaces or spills this draught while traveling through Durotar, Canaga Earthcaller is willing to prepare another in good faith, though not without warning the novice to be far more vigilant with sacred gifts.",sp=0},{t="Canaga's Guidance",b="Canaga Earthcaller watches over the fledgling shamans emerging from the Den in the Valley of Trials. While understanding that young orcs and trolls are prone to the chaos of early trials, he stresses that the elemental spirits do not take kindly to negligence. Accepting a second sapta is a small lesson in humility, ensuring the young shaman remembers that power granted by the earth must be guarded and respected.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is an Earth Sapta?",a="An Earth Sapta is a specially prepared ceremonial draught used by shaman initiates. Ingesting it grants spiritual sight, allowing the drinker to perceive and speak with elemental earth spirits that remain unseen to ordinary eyes.",al={"what is sapta","earth sapta use","purpose of sapta"},it="item"},{q="Why does Canaga Earthcaller offer this quest?",a="Canaga Earthcaller provides this replacement if an initiate loses or misplaces their Earth Sapta before completing the communion ritual during the Call of Earth trials. He grants another in good faith so the acolyte can finish their spiritual task.",al={"why canaga gives sapta","lost my earth sapta"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this ritual take place?",a="This exchange occurs in the Valley of Trials, the sun-scorched canyon in southwestern Durotar where young orcs and trolls begin their journeys of discipline and honor.",al={"where is canaga","valley of trials sapta location"},it="place"},{q="Is losing the sapta seen poorly by the spirits?",a="While the spirits are patient, Canaga reminds initiates that treating sacred draughts carelessly demonstrates a lack of focus. A true shaman must treat every elemental gift with absolute reverence.",al={"does losing sapta matter","lore of losing sapta"}},{q="Who can undertake this communion?",a="The preparation and drinking of the Earth Sapta is restricted to practicing shamans seeking to attune themselves to their first elemental totem, the Earth Totem.",al={"who can get earth sapta","classes for sapta"},it="people"},{q="What happens after an initiate drinks the sapta?",a="Drinking the draught opens the initiate's inner vision, allowing them to locate and converse with a local manifestation of the earth spirit tucked away in the crags of the Valley of Trials.",al={"what does sapta do when drunk","after earth sapta"},it="next_step"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="For an initiate, losing the sapta is an early lesson in discipline: communion with the elements requires steady focus, not careless hands.",["race:Orc"]="In the arid crags of Durotar, young orcs learning the ancient ways of shamanism must prove their dedication to the ancestors and the earth beneath their boots.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear trolls walking the path of the elements in the Valley of Trials learn to balance their traditional loa worship with direct reverence for the elemental spirits."},kw={"call of earth","canaga earthcaller","draught","durotar","earth sapta","shaman","totem","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:canaga-earthcaller","quest:1516","quest:1462","zone:durotar"},m={start="Canaga Earthcaller",level="4",faction="Horde",id=1463},src={"Earth Sapta (Durotar)"}}
E["quest:1485"] = {t="quest",n="Vile Familiars",z="durotar",s="In the arid valley of the Valley of Trials, the warlock trainer Ruzan tasks aspiring practitioners of the dark arts with proving their mettle against vile familiars. To earn the knowledge of demon summoning, initiates must face these impish creatures in combat and claim their severed heads. It marks the humble, dangerous first step toward mastering fel power under the watchful eyes of the Horde.",h="In the arid valley of the Valley of Trials, the warlock trainer Ruzan tasks aspiring practitioners of the...",sec={{t="A Precarious Place in the Horde",b="Warlocks hold an uneasy place within Thrall's newly forged Horde. The legacy of demonic corruption and blood pacts that once brought ruin to the orcish race left deep scars and lingering distrust. Though practitioners of fel magic are tolerated in Durotar, they are neither loved nor widely embraced. Many choose reclusive lives in shadowy corners like the Den, practicing their art away from prying eyes while teaching those rare initiates daring enough to walk the path.",sp=0},{t="The Trial of Mastery",b="Before granting an apprentice the dangerous rites required to bend an imp to their will, Ruzan demands evidence of dominance. Near a cave northeast of the Den, vile familiars skulk and hurl bolts of flame at any who approach. By slaying these lesser demons and claiming their heads, an initiate proves they can overpower the fiery adversaries they seek to control, ensuring they will not be consumed by the very magic they intend to command.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Ruzan send warlocks to fight vile familiars?",a="Ruzan requires initiates to face vile familiars so they understand the fiery nature and danger of imps before attempting to summon one. Because warlocks are few and distrusted, he refuses to risk an apprentice's life by teaching the art of demon summoning before they have proven they can best such creatures in direct combat.",al={"why kill vile familiars","ruzan test","imp trial"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the vile familiars found?",a="They gather around and inside a cave to the northeast of the Den in the Valley of Trials, beyond the roaming boars and scorpids. This cavern serves as an encampment for the sinister Burning Blade Coven.",al={"vile familiar location","where are familiars","ruzan cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How does the Horde view warlocks in Durotar?",a="Warlocks are viewed with deep suspicion and distrust throughout the Horde due to the demonic history that previously corrupted the orcish people. While Thrall's government tolerates their presence and recognizes their combat utility, they are kept at arm's length, leading many practitioners to live solitary lives.",al={"are warlocks hated","horde warlock lore","why distrust warlocks"},it="conflict"},{q="What reward does completing this trial offer?",a="Slaying the creatures and returning their severed heads to Ruzan proves you possess the discipline and strength needed to command demons, leading directly into learning how to summon an imp minion.",al={"what do i learn","quest reward ruzan","imp spell"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Are vile familiars actual demons?",a="Yes, vile familiars are minor demonic imps associated with fel magic. Though small in stature, they are formidable adversaries capable of slinging fireballs at their enemies.",al={"what are vile familiars","are familiars imps","familiar demon type"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Ruzan?",a="Ruzan is an orc warlock trainer stationed inside the Den in the Valley of Trials. He instructs new orc and troll warlocks on how to safely harness fel energies and control summoned servants.",al={"ruzan","who is ruzan","valley of trials warlock"},it="people"},{q="What are the Vile Familiar Heads for?",a="Ruzan requires the heads as physical proof of your triumph over the creatures in combat. Because so few novices choose the warlock's path, he refuses to teach you the hazardous art of demon summoning until you can prove you possess the power and will to dominate them.",al={"vile familiar head use","why collect vile familiar heads","ruzan vile familiar heads"},it="item",add=true},{q="What are the vile familiars doing in the Valley of Trials?",a="These vicious, imp-like creatures cluster around a cave northeast of the Den known as the Burning Blade Coven. Drawn by corrupt magics or bound by lurking cultists, they serve as a lethal proving ground for fledgling warlocks to test their resolve against minor demonic minions.",al={"why are vile familiars here","vile familiars valley of trials","cave vile familiars"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Ruzan send you instead of dealing with the familiars himself?",a="This is a personal trial of mastery, not a public defense task. If Ruzan or the Grunts dispatched the familiars, it would teach you nothing. A warlock who cannot overpower a basic demon in direct combat will inevitably be consumed or destroyed the moment they attempt to summon one.",al={"why doesn't ruzan kill them","why me ruzan","why does ruzan test me"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="This trial marks your inaugural rite of passage as a warlock, proving you can subdue demonic fire before invoking the ritual to summon an imp of your own.",["race:Orc"]="Orcish warlocks must confront the dark history of their people every day, proving their control and loyalty in a society that remembers the horrors of fel corruption.",["faction:Horde"]="Though the Horde allows warlocks to train within Durotar, their dark arts are kept tightly contained within isolated areas like the Den."},kw={"burning blade coven","durotar","imp","ruzan","the den","valley of trials","vile familiars","warlock"},rel={"quest:792","subzone:burning-blade-coven","quest:1089","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},m={start="Ruzan",level="4",faction="Horde",id=1485,ri={"Vile Familiar Head"}},src={"Vile Familiars (Warlock)"}}
E["quest:1499"] = {t="quest",n="Vile Familiars",z="durotar",s="This task marks the completion of a young warlock's first foray against the demonic minions hiding in the Valley of Trials. After slaying vile familiars under Ruzan's guidance, the neophyte reports their deed to Zureetha Fargaze, who oversees the culling of the encroaching Burning Blade.",h="This task marks the completion of a young warlock's first foray against the demonic minions hiding in the...",sec={{t="A Matter of Discipline",b="While other young warriors and scouts in the Valley of Trials are dispatched directly by Zureetha Fargaze to curb the infestation in the Burning Blade Coven, warlock initiates answer first to their shadowy mentors. Ruzan demands proof of strength and control over lesser demons before directing his pupils back into the fold of the Horde's general defense, ensuring their efforts serve both the coven of warlocks and the safety of the Den.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of the Coven",b="Zureetha Fargaze keeps a watchful eye on the northern cavern overlooking the Valley of Trials. The vile familiars skulking within are merely the weakest pets of the Burning Blade cultists, yet their open presence within the sacred training grounds represents a brazen insult and a growing danger. Reporting your success against them confirms that even those pursuing the fel arts remain dedicated to defending Durotar from genuine corruption.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Ruzan send me to Zureetha Fargaze instead of rewarding me himself?",a="Zureetha Fargaze is coordinating the overall defense and culling efforts against the Burning Blade in the Valley of Trials. Ruzan tests your mastery over lesser fel creatures first, but directs you to Zureetha so your service is formally recognized and integrated with the Valley's broader defense.",al={"why see zureetha","ruzan to zureetha","why talk to zureetha"},it="motive"},{q="Who are the vile familiars?",a="Vile familiars are minor demonic imps and minions bound to the service of the Burning Blade Coven. Though individually weak, they serve darker masters who lurk deep within the cavern overlooking the Valley of Trials.",al={"what are vile familiars","vile familiar lore","familiars burning blade"},it="target"},{q="Where can I find Zureetha Fargaze?",a="Zureetha Fargaze is stationed right out in the open near the center of the Den in the Valley of Trials, just a short walk up from the trainers' camp where Ruzan resides.",al={"where is zureetha","zureetha fargaze location","zureetha map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is there another quest with the exact same name?",a="Most adventurers receive the quest 'Vile Familiars' directly from Zureetha Fargaze to hunt the creatures. Warlocks, however, are given their own class-specific task by Ruzan, which leads into this brief hand-off back to Zureetha upon completion.",al={"two vile familiars quests","duplicate vile familiars","warlock vile familiars"},gp=true},{q="What is the Burning Blade doing in the Valley of Trials?",a="The Burning Blade cult operates in secret pockets across Durotar, seeking to undermine Thrall's new Horde from within. Taking root in a cavern right inside the Valley of Trials allows them to prey upon unproven novices and spread demonic corruption right under the eyes of the orcish overseers.",al={"burning blade valley of trials","why are cultists in the den"},it="threat"},{q="Does slaying these familiars wipe out the cult?",a="No. As Zureetha notes, the vile familiars are merely pets and scouts for the darker powers within the coven. Their defeat is simply the first step in uncovering and cleansing the deeper cultist threat festering in the Valley.",al={"is burning blade defeated","are cultists gone"},it="next_step"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="For an initiate of the dark arts, confronting the vile familiars is an essential trial, proving you can dominate and dismantle wild fel entities rather than falling prey to them.",["race:Orc"]="The presence of demonic familiars is a foul reminder of the dark pacts that once enslaved the orcish race, making their removal from Durotar's soil a matter of cultural survival.",["race:Troll"]="The Darkspear trolls sharing the Valley of Trials view demonic magic with deep suspicion, making it vital for young practitioners to demonstrate their loyalty against rogue cultists."},kw={"burning blade coven","durotar","imps","ruzan","the den","valley of trials","vile familiars","warlock quest","zureetha fargaze"},rel={"npc:zureetha-fargaze","quest:792","quest:1089","subzone:burning-blade-coven","zone:durotar"},m={start="Ruzan",["end"]="Zureetha Fargaze",level="4",faction="Horde",id=1499},src={"Vile Familiars (Warlock 2)"}}
E["quest:1516"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Earth",z="durotar",s="Call of Earth is the initial trial for novice Horde shaman training within the Valley of Trials. Bestowed by Canaga Earthcaller, the trial tests a shaman's endurance and patience by requiring them to hunt demonic felstalkers in order to prepare a ritual sapta.",h="Call of Earth is the initial trial for novice Horde shaman training within the Valley of Trials.",sec={{t="The First Bond",b="Before a shaman can call upon the elements, they must form an enduring relationship with each one in turn. In orc and troll culture, this spiritual path begins with the earth, the bedrock of life, endurance, and patience. Canaga Earthcaller serves as the guide for fledglings in the Valley of Trials, teaching that the earth demands supreme respect and steadfastness before granting its protection.",sp=0},{t="A Cleansing Hunt",b="To demonstrate their readiness to commune with the stubborn spirits of the land, initiates are sent into the northern ravines where the Burning Blade cult festers. By hunting felstalkers—corrupt extraplanar hounds summoned by dark magic—the shaman proves their ability to defend the land against unnatural decay. Canaga uses the harvested hooves as components to brew an Earth Sapta, a sacred draft that opens mortal eyes to the elemental plane.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this trial?",a="The trial initiates a shaman into the elemental mysteries, proving their patience and spiritual discipline to the earth spirits so they can eventually commune directly with them and earn an Earth Totem.",al={"why do call of earth","what does call of earth give","purpose of quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Canaga Earthcaller?",a="Canaga Earthcaller is a troll shaman trainer residing in the Valley of Trials within Durotar. He guides young orc, troll, and visiting tauren shaman on their foundational steps toward elemental mastery.",al={"who is canaga","canaga earthcaller lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Canaga need felstalker hooves?",a="Canaga uses the hooves as essential ingredients to prepare an Earth Sapta, a specialized potion that allows a mortal shaman's senses to perceive and speak with elemental spirits.",al={"why felstalker hooves","hooves purpose"},it="item"},{q="Where are the felstalkers located?",a="Felstalkers are found just north of the training grounds in the Valley of Trials, haunting the cave and surrounding bluffs belonging to the Burning Blade Coven.",al={"felstalker location","where to find felstalkers"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can other Horde races undertake this version of the trial?",a="Yes. While primarily intended for orc and troll shaman coming of age in Durotar, tauren shaman who travel away from Red Cloud Mesa can also undertake Canaga's trial in the Valley of Trials.",al={"can tauren do this","is this orc only"},gp=true},{q="What virtues does the earth represent to a shaman?",a="According to shamanic tradition, earth represents the foundation of life, embodying immense strength, stamina, and eternal patience, though it can prove stubbornly fickle if not respected.",al={"virtues of earth","shaman earth meaning"},it="power"},{q="Why does Canaga Earthcaller want this done?",a="Canaga serves as a guide for young shaman taking their first steps on the spiritual path. He senses that a time of conflict approaches and that you possess the enduring spirit required to commune with the earth. Before he can prepare the sacred sapta and share the earth's mysteries, he must test your resolve, strength, and patience against dangerous adversaries to ensure you are ready to heed the element's call.",al={"canaga earthcaller motive","why does canaga test you","canaga earthcaller why"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why are the felstalkers in the Valley of Trials?",a="These demonic hounds haunt the northern reaches of the valley, summoned and bound by the shadowy warlocks of the Burning Blade Coven who have hidden themselves within the local caverns. Their foul presence defiles the surrounding land, making them both an immediate threat to young initiates and a fitting test of courage and martial strength for a budding shaman.",al={"why are there felstalkers here","felstalkers valley of trials","what are the felstalkers"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why must you face the felstalkers instead of the valley's guards?",a="This is a personal spiritual trial, not a standard military operation. A shaman must establish their own harmony with the elements through personal trial and demonstrated strength. Having warriors or guards gather the hooves would prove nothing to the stubborn spirits of the earth, who demand that you face danger directly and prove your own patience, endurance, and capability before granting their power.",al={"why me call of earth","why not send guards felstalkers","why must i hunt the felstalkers"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="This rite marks your first formal communion with the elements, laying the foundation for your Earth Totem.",["race:Orc"]="Under Thrall's Horde, returning to the shamanic path honors ancient clan traditions that predate the demonic corruption.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear witch doctors and spiritualists embrace the earth spirits to support their newfound home alongside the orcs."},kw={"burning blade","call of earth","canaga earthcaller","earth totem","felstalker","sapta","shaman trial","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:canaga-earthcaller","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:burning-blade-coven","quest:792","quest:794","zone:durotar","zone:mulgore"},m={start="Canaga Earthcaller",["end"]="Canaga Earthcaller",level="4",faction="Horde",id=1516,ri={"Felstalker Hoof"}},src={"Call of Earth (Durotar)"}}
E["quest:1517"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Earth",z="durotar",s="This sacred rite marks an initiate's first spiritual communion with the elements in Durotar. Guided by Canaga Earthcaller, young shaman consume a potent Earth Sapta atop Spirit Rock to pierce the veil and stand directly before the Minor Manifestation of Earth.",h="This sacred rite marks an initiate's first spiritual communion with the elements in Durotar.",sec={{t="The Power of the Sapta",b="A sapta is a mystical concoction known only to a select few shaman masters. Brewed with elemental magic, the draught serves to bridge mortal perception with the spiritual plane, granting 'Sapta Sight' to the strong-willed. Because its power binds the drinker's spirit directly to an element, tradition demands that it never be consumed outside of consecrated holy ground.",sp=0},{t="Pilgrimage to Spirit Rock",b="To commune with earth, initiates leave the Valley of Trials and ascend the Hidden Path into the southern crags of Durotar. At the trail's end sits Spirit Rock, an elevated sanctuary overlooking the rugged wasteland. Drinking the sapta here allows the initiate to perceive what mundane eyes cannot: an elemental presence waiting quietly among the stone.",sp=0},{t="Patience of the Earth",b="The Minor Manifestation of Earth does not demand bloodshed or subjugation, asking only that the petitioner stand humbly before the world. While the other elemental forces—fire, water, and air—possess turbulent, volatile, and often chaotic spirits, the earth imparts steadiness. It welcomes the petitioner by reminding them that mountains provide endurance and the plains offer boundless patience.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is an Earth Sapta?",a="An Earth Sapta is a specialized potion brewed by veteran shaman that temporarily attunes a drinker's spirit to the element of earth. Drinking it grants the inner vision required to see and speak with hidden elemental spirits.",al={"what is sapta","earth sapta meaning","what does sapta do"},it="item"},{q="Where is Spirit Rock located?",a="Spirit Rock sits in the craggy mountains southwest of the Den in the Valley of Trials. Initiates reach it by following the Hidden Path up into the hills south of the valley floor.",al={"where is spirit rock","spirit rock location","how to find spirit rock"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why must the sapta be consumed at Spirit Rock?",a="Shamanic tradition dictates that a sapta must only be drunk in designated holy places. Sacred sites like Spirit Rock serve as natural thin spots between the mortal realm and the elemental spirits.",al={"why drink at spirit rock","can i drink sapta anywhere"},it="place"},{q="Who is the Minor Manifestation of Earth?",a="It is an elemental spirit of the earth that inhabits Spirit Rock. Visible only through the heightened perception of Sapta Sight, it greets young shaman to test their humility and impart the first foundational lessons of elemental balance.",al={"manifestation of earth","who is the earth spirit"},it="identity"},{q="Can any Horde shaman undertake this trial?",a="While it is primarily the rite of passage for young orc and Darkspear troll shaman training in Durotar, tauren shaman who travel here may also complete it, though they have their own equivalent rite on Red Cloud Mesa.",al={"can tauren do this quest","who can do call of earth"},it="people"},{q="How does the earth spirit react to the initiate?",a="Unlike the volatile manifestations of fire or air, the earth spirit is welcoming and passive. It accepts initiates who approach with humble respect, bestowing its blessing without demanding a contest of strength.",al={"what does the earth spirit say","is the earth spirit hostile"}},{q="Why does Canaga Earthcaller want this done?",a="Canaga Earthcaller is guiding you along the spiritual path of the shaman. Having proven your readiness by gathering the necessary ritual components, he now requires you to drink the Earth Sapta at Spirit Rock. His purpose is to forge your bond with the elemental spirits of the land, allowing your vision to pierce the veil and commune directly with the earth.",al={"canaga motive","why send to spirit rock","why drink earth sapta"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Canaga Earthcaller send you instead of going himself?",a="This journey is a sacred rite of passage that every aspiring shaman must undertake personally. The Earth Sapta binds the drinker's own spirit to the element, granting vision that cannot be experienced through a surrogate. Canaga already commands this communion; you must stand before the earth humbly yourself to earn its blessing.",al={"why me canaga","why send player to spirit rock","why must i drink the sapta"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="This rite represents your very first step along the path of elemental attunement, teaching that true mastery begins with the quiet patience of the earth.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs returning to ancestral ways after generations of fel corruption, communion through the Earth Sapta is a sacred rediscovery of their people's traditional bond with the spirits.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear witch doctors and spiritualists embrace these earthen rites to adapt their deep ancestral ties to the harsh, sun-baked landscape of Durotar."},kw={"call of earth","canaga earthcaller","earth sapta","hidden path","minor manifestation of earth","sapta sight","spirit rock","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:canaga-earthcaller","npc:minor-manifestation-of-earth","subzone:spirit-rock","subzone:hidden-path","quest:1462","quest:1516","quest:1089","zone:durotar"},m={start="Canaga Earthcaller",["end"]="Minor Manifestation of Earth",level="4",faction="Horde",id=1517},src={"Call of Earth (Durotar 2)"}}
E["quest:1518"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Earth",z="durotar",s="Call of Earth is the culminating rite in the trial of earth for young shaman in Durotar. After communing with a manifestation of the earth spirit, an initiate returns to Canaga Earthcaller with rough quartz to receive their first elemental totem.",h="Call of Earth is the culminating rite in the trial of earth for young shaman in Durotar.",sec={{t="Heart of the Stone",b="To commune with the earth, a novice shaman must look beyond brute strength. Upon demonstrating patience and humility before the Minor Manifestation of Earth, the initiate is granted a modest token: a piece of rough quartz. Though unassuming in appearance, this tiny stone serves as an enduring seed of power and proof that the spirit has accepted the petitioner's pledge.",sp=0},{t="The First of Four Paths",b="Bringing the quartz back to Canaga Earthcaller in the Valley of Trials completes the trial. Canaga crafts the stone into an Earth Totem, the physical focus through which the shaman channels the ground's steadfast protection and strength. This rite marks the initiate's formal entrance into the first of the four elemental disciplines, laying the foundation for a lifetime of communion with the natural world.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the rough quartz used for?",a="The rough quartz is gifted by the Minor Manifestation of Earth as proof that you have communed with the spirit. Canaga Earthcaller embeds this pebble into your newly carved Earth Totem, where it acts as the heart and focus for your earth spells.",al={"rough quartz","what does quartz do","purpose of quartz"},it="item"},{q="Who is Canaga Earthcaller?",a="Canaga Earthcaller is a shaman trainer located in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. He guides young orc and troll initiates through their earliest trials, preparing them to commune with elemental spirits and crafting their first totems.",al={"canaga","canaga earthcaller","who is canaga"},it="identity"},{q="Can tauren do this quest?",a="Yes. While tauren typically complete their trial of earth with their own elders at Red Cloud Mesa in Mulgore, any Horde shaman who travels to the Valley of Trials can undergo the ritual with Canaga Earthcaller.",al={"can tauren do durotar call of earth","tauren shaman durotar","tauren call of earth"},gp=true},{q="What does receiving the Earth Totem signify?",a="Receiving an Earth Totem signifies that the spirit of the earth has recognized you. It serves both as a badge of your status among the shaman and as a necessary physical focus to cast earth-based blessings and wards.",al={"why get earth totem","shaman earth totem meaning"},it="purpose"},{q="What virtues does the earth demand from a shaman?",a="The spirit asks an initiate to remain patient, stay strong, and seek wisdom. It teaches that even the smallest pebble can outlast mountains if it endures, urging shaman to respect the ground so that it will support them in turn.",al={"earth spirit lessons","what does earth ask"}},{q="Where does the shaman path go after this?",a="Earth is only the first of the four elements a shaman must master. As your training continues, you will eventually be called to seek communion with the spirits of fire, water, and air.",al={"what totem next","after earth totem","four paths shaman"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does the Minor Manifestation of Earth give you the rough quartz?",a="Having tested your resolve and acknowledged your communion, the spirit grants you the rough quartz as tangible proof of your bond. It wants you to take this small stone back to Canaga Earthcaller so it can serve as the living heart of your first totem, binding the enduring strength and patience of the earth directly to your spiritual practice.",al={"minor manifestation of earth motive","why rough quartz","manifestation of earth why send"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="This rite provides your very first totem, unlocking the ability to ground yourself in the elements and call upon the soil for aid.",["race:Orc"]="The trial represents the continued revival of orcish shamanism in Durotar, turning back toward elemental balance after decades of demonic corruption.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear witch doctors and spiritualists learn beside the orcs in the Valley of Trials, adapting their traditional communion to include the four elemental paths.",["faction:Horde"]="The elements of Kalimdor are wild and untamed, making the bond forged by Horde shaman essential for the survival of their new settlements."},kw={"call of earth","canaga earthcaller","durotar","earth totem","minor manifestation","rough quartz","shaman","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:canaga-earthcaller","npc:minor-manifestation-of-earth","quest:1516","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:troll","zone:mulgore","topic:tauren"},m={start="Minor Manifestation of Earth",["end"]="Canaga Earthcaller",level="4",faction="Horde",id=1518},src={"Call of Earth (Durotar 3)"}}
E["quest:1525"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="durotar",s="This trial marks the critical preparation in a shaman's communion with fire, tasking the initiate with gathering the volatile ingredients needed to brew a Fire Sapta. Telf Joolam requires components saturated with heat and magical power: tar from Razormane geomancers and a pouch of dark reagents from Burning Blade cultists hiding in Durotar.",h="This trial marks the critical preparation in a shaman's communion with fire, tasking the initiate with...",sec={{t="Brewing the Fire Sapta",b="To perceive and speak to the spirits of fire, a shaman cannot rely on mortal vision alone. Just as earth required its own draught, opening the senses to the Eternal Flame demands a specialized Fire Sapta. The potion requires reagents innately bound to heat and flame. The hermit Telf Joolam sends initiates across Durotar and into the eastern Barrens to harvest these specific elements from those who wield primal heat and corrupting sorcery.",sp=0},{t="Enemies and Elements",b="The required ingredients reveal how different factions tap into fire. The Razormane quilboar spellcasters of the eastern Barrens carry fire tar, a viscous, flammable byproduct of their earthy rituals. In contrast, the reagent pouch must be seized from the Burning Blade cultists lurking in Dustwind Cave, nestled in the ravines northeast of Razor Hill. Though the warlock cultists wield fire as an instrument of destruction and demonic chaos, the raw reagents in their pouches remain naturally resonant with the element itself.",sp=0},{t="The Nature of Flame",b="Upon brewing the sapta, Telf Joolam imparts an essential truth of the elements: fire is far more than mere destruction and ruin. While it burns and consumes, it is also the heart of warmth, light, and creation. True balance requires understanding that opposing forces give one another meaning, and that a wise shaman uses contrasting elemental powers in tandem rather than treating fire solely as a weapon.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is a Fire Sapta?",a="A sapta is a ritual draught prepared by shamans using ingredients tied to a specific element. Drinking a Fire Sapta temporarily aligns the shaman's spirit and vision with the plane of fire, allowing them to perceive and speak with elemental fire spirits that are otherwise invisible to ordinary senses.",al={"what is fire sapta","fire sapta meaning","why drink sapta"},it="item"},{q="Where do I find the Fire Tar?",a="Fire tar is carried by Razormane quilboar spellcasters inhabiting the eastern plains of the Barrens, just across the Southfury River from Durotar. Geomancers, Seers, Mystics, and Thornweavers frequently carry pots of this thick, flammable concoction for their tribal rituals.",al={"fire tar location","who drops fire tar","fire tar quilboar"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where is the Reagent Pouch found?",a="The reagent pouch is carried by Burning Blade cultists in Dustwind Cave. This cave is located above the ravines northeast of Razor Hill in Durotar, not to be confused with Skull Rock further to the north near the coast.",al={"reagent pouch location","which cave has reagent pouch","burning blade pouch"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why does a shaman use items from warlocks?",a="Saptas require ingredients that are naturally saturated with the targeted element. Because Burning Blade cultists constantly invoke destructive demonic flames, their spell pouches are densely packed with potent reagents tied directly to fire, providing the exact catalyst Telf Joolam needs to craft the draught.",al={"why use burning blade reagents","warlock items for shaman","warlock fire"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Telf Joolam?",a="Telf Joolam is a solitary troll shaman who makes his camp atop the crags of Durotar, south of Razor Hill. He oversees the harsh trials of fire for Horde initiates, guiding them in mastering the dangerous balance between destruction and creation.",al={"telf joolam lore","who is telf joolam"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="Once Telf Joolam crafts the Fire Sapta from the gathered reagents, he sends you up to the fiery heights of the dormant peak nearby. There, you must drink the concoction to face the elemental spirit and earn your fire totem.",al={"next quest call of fire","after getting reagents","what to do with fire sapta"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Telf Joolam send you on this quest?",a="Telf Joolam is guiding your initiation into the deeper arts of the elements. To wield the power of fire and earn your Fire Totem, you must drink a specialized concoction known as a fire sapta, which temporarily aligns your spiritual senses with the realm of fire. Telf cannot brew this draught from thin air; he requires you to retrieve reagents deeply attuned to flame so he can prepare the mixture and set you upon the path of the Eternal Flame.",al={"why does telf joolam want this","telf joolam purpose","why help telf joolam"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Fire Tar for?",a="Fire tar is one of two vital catalysts required by Telf Joolam to brew a fire sapta. Carried by the spellcasting quilboar of the Razormane tribe in the eastern Barrens, the tar carries inherent volatile properties aligned with fire magic, giving the draught the potency needed to attune your senses to the elemental spirits.",al={"why do i need fire tar","fire tar purpose","use of fire tar"},it="item",add=true},{q="What is the Reagent Pouch for?",a="The reagent pouch provides the volatile components needed to complete the fire sapta. Telf Joolam has you claim it from the Burning Blade cultists lurking northeast of Razor Hill because these warlocks regularly gather materials intrinsically tied to fire for their own dark sorcery. Rather than hunting across the lands for rare, scattered catalysts, the cultists' personal caches contain the exact reagents required to bridge your spirit to flame.",al={"why need reagent pouch","reagent pouch purpose","shaman reagent pouch use"},it="item",add=true},{q="Who are the Burning Blade cultists in Durotar?",a="The cultists are mortal agents of the Burning Blade, a shadowy remnant of the old demonic cults that once served the Shadow Council. Lurking in hidden caves above the ravines northeast of Razor Hill, these warlocks practice forbidden fel magic right beneath the Horde's nose, drawing on chaotic fire powers that make their reagent pouches prime sources for elemental brewing.",al={"burning blade target","who are the cultists","burning blade durotar"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why must you gather the reagents yourself instead of Telf Joolam?",a="The journey itself is part of your spiritual trial. A shaman must prove capable of facing danger, confronting corrupt magic, and demonstrating resolve before claiming communion with fire. Telf Joolam serves as a mentor and guide on this remote peak, but the communion with the element cannot be handed to you—you must personally seize the components that bind you to the flame.",al={"why can't telf get them","why me fire quest","why shaman gather reagents"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="This rite tests a young shaman's ability to balance opposing forces, demonstrating that flame is not merely fuel for wrath, but an instrument of vitality and light when guided by wisdom.",["faction:Horde"]="The trial sends Horde defenders to strike at two pressing threats right on their borders: encroaching Razormane quilboar in the Barrens and the insidious Burning Blade cultists burrowed within Durotar.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, dealing with the Burning Blade is a bitter reminder of the dark warlock magic that once corrupted their people, making reclaiming fire as a pure, natural element a vital act of cultural restoration."},kw={"burning blade","call of fire","dustwind cave","fire sapta","fire tar","razormane","reagent pouch","telf joolam"},rel={"npc:telf-joolam","subzone:dustwind-cave","subzone:razor-hill","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens","zone:durotar","quest:1524","quest:827"},m={start="Telf Joolam",level="12",faction="Horde",id=1525,ri={"Fire Tar","Reagent Pouch (shaman)"}},src={"Call of Fire (3)"}}
E["quest:1526"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Fire",z="durotar",s="This trial marks the critical moment in a shaman's attunement to fire atop the peaks of Durotar. Guided by the hermit Telf Joolam, the initiate must drink a potent fire sapta to perceive and confront a Minor Manifestation of Fire. Slaying the spirit yields a glowing ember, used to kindle the brazier at the Shrine of Eternal Flame and light the ceremonial torch.",h="This trial marks the critical moment in a shaman's attunement to fire atop the peaks of Durotar.",sec={{t="Eyes of the Flame",b="Fire spirits rarely linger in plain sight for the uninitiated. To commune with them, a shaman must alter their perception using a fire sapta, an elemental draught steeped from reagents gathered across the barrens and coast. Imbibing the draught opens the senses to the unseen, revealing minor spirits and manifestations dancing across the crags of the summit.",sp=0},{t="Confronting the Manifestation",b="Fire does not yield to passive devotion; it demands strength, decisiveness, and respect. Waiting atop the mountain is a Minor Manifestation of Fire. Aware of the shaman's piercing gaze once the sapta takes hold, the spirit waits for the challenge to begin. Initiates are taught to strike swiftly and without hesitation, as elemental fire feeds on lingering combat, swelling in ferocity and heat the longer the contest drags on.",sp=0},{t="The Brazier of the Dormant Flame",b="With the manifestation subdued, the shaman claims its lingering heat in the form of a glowing ember. Returning to the summit shrine, the ember is placed into the Brazier of the Dormant Flame. Despite being exposed to the harsh sun and winds of Durotar, the inscribed metal remains pristine and cool until the ember meets the bowl, bursting into a rhythmic, white-hot blaze that ignites the ritual torch.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this trial?",a="This trial tests an aspiring shaman's worthiness to command elemental fire. By confronting a manifestation and capturing its raw heat in a ritual torch, the initiate proves their strength and earns the right to fashion a Fire Totem.",al={"why do call of fire","fire totem quest meaning","call of fire trial"},it="purpose"},{q="Why do I need to drink the fire sapta?",a="Elemental spirits often dwell slightly beyond ordinary mortal sight. Drinking the fire sapta thins the veil, allowing the shaman to perceive and physically interact with the fire elementals gathered atop the mountain.",al={"what does fire sapta do","why sapta","cant see fire elemental"}},{q="Where is the Minor Manifestation of Fire found?",a="The manifestation resides at the absolute peak of the mountain ridge above Telf Joolam's perch in Durotar, near the Shrine of Eternal Flame.",al={"manifestation location","where is the fire elemental","where do i go"},gp=true},{q="Who is Telf Joolam?",a="Telf Joolam is an eccentric shaman hermit living high on a rocky ridge in Durotar. He guides young Horde initiates through the dangerous and temperamental rites required to understand fire.",al={"telf joolam role","telf joolam lore","who is the hermit"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the manifestation grow stronger during the fight?",a="Fire naturally builds, spreads, and feeds on energy over time. Shamans are cautioned to strike decisively because prolonged hesitation allows the spirit to gather strength and burn ever hotter.",al={"why is the fire elemental so strong","manifestation scaling","swift strike fire"}},{q="What happens after the brazier is lit?",a="Lighting the brazier kindles the ceremonial torch. The initiate carries this sacred flame back down the mountain to complete the creation of their Fire Totem.",al={"what after dormant flame","next quest call of fire","where to take lit torch"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Telf Joolam send you on this trial?",a="Telf Joolam is your mentor in the ways of the elements, tasked with guiding young shamans through their communion with fire. Fire is tempestuous, destructive, and unpredictable; the spirits will not grant you their power or respect unless you prove yourself capable of confronting and commanding their essence directly. Telf sends you up the peak not to rid the mountain of a threat, but to forge your spirit in battle and earn the right to carry the flame.",al={"telf joolam motive","why does telf joolam want this","why do this trial"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Glowing Ember for?",a="The Glowing Ember is the pure elemental remnant harvested from the slain Minor Manifestation of Fire. To complete your rite, you must carry this fiery core to the Shrine of Eternal Flame and place it within the dormant brazier. Rekindling the cold basin with the elemental's living essence ignites a sacred, white-hot flame, which in turn lights your Dormant Torch and seals your connection to the element of fire.",al={"glowing ember use","why do i need glowing ember","purpose of glowing ember"},it="item",add=true},{q="What is the Minor Manifestation of Fire, and why is it here?",a="The Minor Manifestation of Fire is an elemental spirit lingering atop the mountain peak near the Shrine of Eternal Flame. Visible only to those whose senses are opened by the sacred fire sapta, it embodies the raw, aggressive nature of the flame. It remains perched upon the crag as an eternal guardian and test for aspiring shamans, challenging all who seek to master fire to subdue its burning wrath.",al={"minor manifestation of fire lore","who is the manifestation","why is the fire elemental here"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Unlike the solid, unyielding earth, fire is volatile and destructive. This trial teaches that fire will consume an indecisive caller, demanding unwavering focus and authority to master.",["faction:Horde"]="Orc and troll shamans make the pilgrimage up the red crags of Durotar to prove their communion with the fiery spirits of the land."},kw={"brazier of the dormant flame","call of fire","durotar","fire sapta","fire totem","minor manifestation of fire","shaman trial","shrine of eternal flame","telf joolam"},rel={"npc:telf-joolam","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},m={start="Telf Joolam",["end"]="Brazier of the Dormant Flame",level="13",faction="Horde",id=1526,ri={"Glowing Ember"}},src={"Call of Fire (4)"}}
E["quest:1842"] = {t="quest",n="Satyr Hooves",z="durotar",s="Satyr Hooves is a quest given by the troll craftsman Ula'elek in Sen'jin Village. In pursuit of forging a pair of empowered brutal gauntlets, warriors must journey north into Ashenvale to hunt satyrs and harvest their magically bloated, uncloven hooves.",h="Satyr Hooves is a quest given by the troll craftsman Ula'elek in Sen'jin Village.",sec={{t="Harnessing Corrupted Essence",b="To forge armor capable of rivaling the most brutal forces on Kalimdor, the Darkspear craftsman Ula'elek looks beyond mundane iron and leather. He directs aspiring warriors north to the ancient woods of Ashenvale, where lingering demonic corruption festers within the local satyr covens.",sp=0},{t="The Bloat of Ashenvale's Magic",b="According to Ula'elek, the satyrs in northeastern Ashenvale sustain themselves by leeching the forest's latent purity and twisting it into foul power. Those demons that have gorged themselves the deepest on this borrowed life manifest abnormal, swollen hooves that have lost their natural cloven split. Ula'elek intends to drain this concentrated magical energy and weave it directly into the gauntlets he crafts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Ula'elek need satyr hooves?",a="Ula'elek requires the hooves to empower the brutal gauntlets he is crafting. He intends to siphon the concentrated forest magic that the satyrs have drained and corrupted into their swollen feet.",al={"why satyr hooves","hoof purpose","what are the hooves for"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the satyrs found?",a="They inhabit northeastern Ashenvale, where they roost among corrupted ancient ruins and leech off the residual magical energy of the deep forest.",al={"where are satyrs","satyr location","where to find satyr hooves"},gp=true},{q="What makes an uncloven hoof special?",a="The lack of a cloven split indicates that a satyr has engorged itself on excessive amounts of Ashenvale's pure magic, swelling its extremities with stolen power.",al={"uncloven hoof lore","why uncloven","swollen hooves"},it="item"},{q="Who is Ula'elek?",a="Ula'elek is a skilled Darkspear troll armor craftsman residing in Sen'jin Village in southern Durotar, known for assisting warriors with crafting trial gear.",al={"who is ulaelek","quest giver","troll in senjin"},it="identity"},{q="What armor is Ula'elek forging?",a="He is preparing to craft a pair of Brutal Gauntlets, heavy protective handwear imbued with stolen magical potency for rising Horde warriors.",al={"what are brutal gauntlets","gauntlet quest","reward armor"},it="purpose"},{q="Do the satyrs serve the Burning Legion here?",a="Yes. Satyrs are ancient night elves transformed by demonic pacts, and the lingering covens in Kalimdor's woodlands continue to practice fel corruption in service to demonic powers.",al={"satyr allegiance","are satyrs legion"},it="threat"},{q="Why are the satyrs in northeastern Ashenvale?",a="Satyrs haunt northeastern Ashenvale to gorge themselves on the ancient forest's purity. By leeching and corrupting its latent enchantments, they empower their wicked rituals and warp their own bodies. The ones who feast most heavily on Ashenvale's natural magic develop grotesque, swollen uncloven hooves, becoming living vessels of concentrated arcane strength.",al={"why satyrs ashenvale","satyr hooves target lore","who are we hunting for hooves"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="This task is part of a warrior's rite of progression, testing their martial resilience against cunning demonic ambushers to earn personalized armor.",["faction:Horde"]="Undertaking this hunt pushes Horde warriors out of Durotar's arid plains and deep into contested night elf territory in Ashenvale.",["race:Troll"]="Ula'elek's methods demonstrate the pragmatic nature of Darkspear craftsmanship, siphoning raw essence from fallen magical foes rather than relying purely on conventional smithing."},kw={"ashenvale","brutal gauntlets","durotar","hooves","satyr","sen'jin village","ula'elek","uncloven"},rel={"npc:ula-elek","quest:1843","quest:1839","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:ashenvale","zone:durotar","topic:satyr"},m={start="Ula'elek",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1842,ri={"Uncloven Satyr Hoof"}},src={"Satyr Hooves"}}
E["quest:1843"] = {t="quest",n="Brutal Gauntlets",z="durotar",s="Brutal Gauntlets is the culmination of an artisan's craft for seasoned Horde warriors. After gathering rare components across distant lands, the craftsman Ula'elek fashions a formidable pair of handguards designed to bring honor to both the maker and the bearer.",h="Brutal Gauntlets is the culmination of an artisan's craft for seasoned Horde warriors.",sec={{t="A Craftsman's Masterpiece",b="Forging armor fit for a seasoned frontline warrior is more than simple metalworking—it is a spiritual undertaking for Horde artisans. Ula'elek, a craftsman residing in Durotar, pours his lineage and skill into shaping these brutal gauntlets. By employing hardened trophies harvested from dangerous adversaries, he constructs armor tailored to withstand ferocious blows while enhancing the wearer's offensive might.",sp=0},{t="Ancestral Honor",b="In orcish and troll traditions, fine arms and armor carry the prestige of the forge and the spirit of the maker into battle. When Ula'elek presents the finished gauntlets to a warrior, he entrusts them with the legacy of his ancestors. A champion who wears them into combat is expected to display courage, martial discipline, and strength worthy of the craftsmanship.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ula'elek?",a="Ula'elek is a craftsman based in Durotar who aids Horde warriors in securing tailored, high-grade armor. He demands exotic materials to ensure that his smithing honors both his trade and his ancestral traditions.",al={"ulaelek","who gives brutal gauntlets","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why were satyr hooves needed for these gauntlets?",a="The satyrs' swollen, uncloven hooves hold the power they leeched from Ashenvale's magic. Ula'elek draws that power out of the hooves and harnesses it into his crafting, so the gauntlets hold great magic.",al={"why satyr hooves","satyr parts","materials used"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What does wearing the gauntlets signify to Ula'elek?",a="To Ula'elek, crafting these gauntlets represents his pinnacle work. Entrusting them to a worthy warrior brings deep honor to his craft and his ancestors, linking his labor directly to the Horde's martial victories.",al={"honor ancestors","ula'elek honor"},it="motive"},{q="Where does this task take place?",a="The forging concludes in Durotar, the arid heartland of the orcs and Darkspear trolls, where Ula'elek inspects the recovered materials and presents the completed armor.",al={"location","where is brutal gauntlets turned in"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is this trial intended for all adventurers?",a="This path is forged specifically for frontline warriors who have proven their stamina and martial dedication, marking their ascent into more seasoned combat roles within the Horde.",al={"is this warrior only","class requirement"},it="why_me"},{q="What comes after receiving the gauntlets?",a="The delivery of the gauntlets marks the completion of this specific crafting trial, leaving the warrior fully equipped to face greater threats across Azeroth's war-torn battlefields.",al={"next quest","brutal gauntlets follow up"},it="next_step"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="These gauntlets represent a warrior's transition into disciplined martial leadership, serving as a trusted piece of protective kit forged specifically for heavy melee engagements.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde craftsmanship relies on enduring tradition and martial pride, ensuring champions carry the spiritual weight and honor of their craftspeople into battle."},kw={"armor forging","brutal gauntlets","durotar","horde","satyr hooves","ula'elek","warrior armor"},rel={"quest:1842","npc:ula-elek","zone:durotar"},m={start="Ula'elek",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1843},src={"Brutal Gauntlets (quest)"}}
E["quest:2161"] = {t="quest",n="A Peon's Burden",z="durotar",s="A Peon's Burden is an introductory delivery task given by Ukor, an anxious orc laborer stranded along the trail outside the Valley of Trials. After attempting to deliver provisions to new recruits who turned out not to need them, Ukor entrusts travelers with returning the heavy load safely to Razor Hill.",h="A Peon's Burden is an introductory delivery task given by Ukor, an anxious orc laborer stranded along the...",sec={{t="A Misplaced Delivery",b="Ukor is an earnest peon who set out from Razor Hill with good intentions, hauling a heavy pack of provisions toward the Valley of Trials. Believing the fresh recruits training in the red canyon were in dire need of rations, he braved the road only to be turned away. The taskmasters overseeing the trials deliberately keep supplies lean—as Innkeeper Grosk later notes, surviving on meager sustenance is seen as a way to forge discipline and endurance in young Horde warriors.",sp=0},{t="Perils of the Red Waste",b="Though he managed to make it to the pass, Ukor finds himself terrified of retracing his steps across the sun-baked soil of Durotar. The crags along the trail teem with aggressive scorpids, venomous spiders, and prowling boars. Lacking weapons, armor, or the fighting spirit expected of orcish grunts, the frightened laborer waits along the path, pleading for any passing adventurer departing the proving grounds to shoulder his burden and return it to the inn.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ukor?",a="Ukor is an orc peon stationed along the road leading out of the Valley of Trials. Well-meaning but timid, he ventured out to deliver provisions from Razor Hill before realizing he was too terrified of local wildlife to make the return journey on his own.",al={"ukor","who is the peon on the road","peon near valley of trials"},it="identity"},{q="Why didn't the trainers in the Valley of Trials want the food?",a="The overseers in the Valley of Trials believe in rigorous discipline for fledgling recruits. As Innkeeper Grosk humorously points out, the instructors prefer to keep the trainees hungry to test their mettle and build their spirit, rendering Ukor's charitable shipment unwelcome.",al={"why refuse food","why did ukor carry food","innkeeper grosk starvation"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does this delivery need to go?",a="The burden must be carried north along Durotar's main thoroughfare to Razor Hill, where it is handed over to Innkeeper Grosk inside the settlement's tavern.",al={"where is razor hill","who do i give the food to","where to deliver ukor's burden"},it="place"},{q="What makes the journey dangerous for a peon?",a="Durotar's rocky wastes are filled with territorial scorpids, venomous crawler spiders, and wild boars. While seasoned recruits can handle such vermin, an unarmored and untrained laborer like Ukor stands little chance if set upon.",al={"why is ukor scared","durotar road dangers"},it="danger"},{q="What is the role of peons in the Horde?",a="Peons occupy the lowest rung of orcish society, handling menial labor such as hauling supplies, chopping timber, and erecting fortifications. While grunts and champions receive praise and glory, peons are often overlooked despite keeping settlements fed and maintained.",al={"orc peons lore","peon status","what are peons"},it="people"},{q="Who is Innkeeper Grosk?",a="Innkeeper Grosk runs the inn in Razor Hill. He manages the town's lodgings and supplies, offering food, drink, and hearth to traveling warriors and reminding recruits that resting is vital before taking on the wider world.",al={"innkeeper grosk","grosk razor hill","razor hill innkeeper"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Ukor want the food delivered back to Razor Hill?",a="Ukor genuinely meant well when he hauled supplies out from Razor Hill, hoping to aid the young recruits training under the harsh sun of the Valley of Trials. Finding that the trainers turned the rations away, he cannot simply abandon the supplies or let them spoil on the road. The food belongs back on the shelves of Innkeeper Grosk's pantry, but after barely surviving the trek past the region's scorpids and spiders, Ukor is terrified of making the perilous return trip alone.",al={"why return the food","ukor motive","why give food to grosk"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Ukor ask you to carry the burden instead of doing it himself?",a="Ukor is an ordinary peon, unaccustomed to violence and unarmed against the wilderness. While he managed to brave the scorpions and spiders on the road leading out from Razor Hill, the sheer terror of facing those savage predators again has frozen him in place. Spotting you emerging victorious from the Valley of Trials, he sees a capable hero who fears nothing, hoping you will gladly carry the burden on your way to the crossroads.",al={"why can't ukor carry it","why me peon's burden","why ask me ukor"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Orcish culture prizes physical might and courage, leaving peons like Ukor at the very bottom of the social hierarchy; taking on his errand shows how even humble labor keeps the fledgling nation of Durotar functioning.",["faction:Horde"]="This trek serves as a transition out of the proving grounds, introducing travelers to Razor Hill, the central hub for Horde defense and logistics in southern Durotar."},kw={"durotar","food","innkeeper grosk","peon","razor hill","supplies","ukor","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:ukor","npc:innkeeper-grosk","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},m={start="Ukor",["end"]="Innkeeper Grosk",level="5",faction="Horde",id=2161},src={"A Peon's Burden"}}
E["quest:3065"] = {t="quest",n="Simple Tablet",z="durotar",s="Simple Tablet is an introductory rite of passage for fledgling warriors entering the Valley of Trials. Delivered into your hands after proving your mettle against local beasts, it directs you toward Frang, the local veteran tasked with honing raw brawn into martial discipline.",h="Simple Tablet is an introductory rite of passage for fledgling warriors entering the Valley of Trials.",sec={{t="A Summons to Arms",b="After proving you can hold your own against the Mottled Boars of the valley, Gornek hands over a parchment specifically marked for you. In the harsh environment of Durotar, the Horde does not leave its fighters without guidance for long. The tablet serves as an invitation to seek out Frang, the warrior trainer stationed outside the Den.",sp=0},{t="Under the Shade of the Den",b="Frang takes shelter in the shade just outside the Den, watching recruits trickle in from the red scrubland. He assesses fresh recruits with a seasoned eye, ready to impart fundamentals—whether hefting a heavy axe or wielding a spear—to ensure each new soldier can defend the fragile settlements of the young Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Simple Tablet?",a="It is an introductory directive handed to young warriors in the Valley of Trials. Gornek passes it along to guide martial recruits to Frang, the resident warrior trainer.",al={"simple tablet","what is this tablet","warrior note"}},{q="Who sends the tablet?",a="The message originates from Frang, the veteran warrior trainer resting outside the Den, who keeps an eye out for emerging fighters.",al={"who wrote the tablet","who sent simple tablet"}},{q="Where can I find Frang?",a="Frang is posted outside the Den within the Valley of Trials, taking shelter from the desert sun under the rock overhangs.",al={"frang location","where is frang","find warrior trainer"}},{q="Why does Frang mention spears and axes?",a="Frang notes the diverse fighting styles among Horde recruits. While orcs favor heavy choppers like greataxes, trolls and other fighters often prefer spears and lighter polearms, both of which serve well in battle.",al={"frang spear quote","why spears"}},{q="Do other classes get this quest?",a="No. The Simple Tablet is specifically given to warriors. Other classes receive their own parchment, rune, or scroll directing them to their respective mentors.",al={"is simple tablet warrior only","class quests in valley of trials"}},{q="What is the purpose of the Den?",a="The Den is a sheltered cavern complex in the Valley of Trials where trainers, supplies, and resting recruits gather away from the blazing heat and wandering beasts.",al={"what is the den","the den durotar"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="This summons marks your very first step onto the warrior's path in Durotar, pointing you directly to Frang to learn foundational stances and strikes.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde relies on a steady stream of hardened front-line fighters to secure Durotar's precarious borders against centaur, quilboar, and human interlopers.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear trolls training in the valley may receive Frang's gruff observations regarding their preference for spears over orcish axes, though he respects anything that kills."},kw={"durotar","frang","gornek","simple tablet","the den","valley of trials","warrior"},rel={"npc:gornek","quest:cutting-teeth","quest:1089","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Frang",level="1",faction="Horde",id=3065},src={"Simple Tablet (quest)"}}
E["quest:3082"] = {t="quest",n="Etched Tablet",z="durotar",s="Etched Tablet is an introductory hunter quest delivered in the Valley of Trials after completing initial trials. It directs aspiring troll hunters to report to the hunter trainer Jen'shan to begin their formal training in the wilderness.",h="Etched Tablet is an introductory hunter quest delivered in the Valley of Trials after completing initial...",sec={{t="A Summons to the Hunt",b="After proving their early mettle against the local boars of the Den, novice hunters are intercepted by Gornek with a carved message. The stone tablet bears the mark of Jen'shan, a skilled troll huntswoman stationed nearby. Gornek passes it along as a sign that the young hunter has demonstrated sufficient grit to catch the eye of seasoned survivalists, marking the transition from basic brute survival to disciplined wilderness training.",sp=0},{t="The Sharing of Survival",b="When reporting to Jen'shan, the troll trainer speaks of the deep history between orcs and trolls within the Horde. While orcs possessed renowned traditions of warriors and shamans, the Darkspear trolls brought ancient stalking, tracking, and survival skills that helped the newcomers endure Kalimdor's rugged wilds. Jen'shan views the training of new hunters as an ongoing exchange of survival knowledge, binding the allied races closer together through shared respect for the hunt.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends the Etched Tablet?",a="The hunter trainer Jen'shan sends the inscribed stone, which is delivered directly by Gornek once you have proven yourself in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who wrote etched tablet","tablet sender","who gave me this tablet"}},{q="Where can Jen'shan be found?",a="Jen'shan is located in the northern area of the Valley of Trials in Durotar, positioned among the other class instructors near the Den.",al={"jen'shan location","where is jenshan","find jenshan"}},{q="Why do troll trainers teach orc hunters here?",a="When the orcs arrived on Kalimdor, they were formidable warriors and shamans, but the Darkspear trolls shared their ancient tracking, trapping, and wilderness lore to help both peoples survive the new frontier.",al={"why troll hunter trainer","troll teaching orc","darkspear hunters"}},{q="What happens after turning in this tablet?",a="Jen'shan accepts you as her student, offering to instruct you in the fundamental techniques, shots, and survival practices required of Horde hunters as you gain experience.",al={"what next after tablet","etched tablet reward lore","jenshan follow up"}},{q="What prerequisite must be finished before getting this tablet?",a="You must first complete the initial task Cutting Teeth for Gornek by slaying mottled boars to prove your basic endurance.",al={"tablet prereq","how to unlock etched tablet","prerequisites for etched tablet"}},{q="Can any class complete this quest?",a="No, this quest is specifically for novice hunters starting their journey in the Valley of Trials. Other classes receive their own distinct training summons from Gornek.",al={"who can get etched tablet","etched tablet class requirement","is this hunter only"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This quest marks your official entry into the ranks of Horde hunters, establishing your bond with the wilderness and your local trainer.",["race:Troll"]="Jen'shan takes pride in how Darkspear hunting lore helped ground the Horde on Kalimdor, reaffirming the vital role troll traditions play in the survival of their allies.",["race:Orc"]="For young orcs, receiving the tablet represents learning refined wilderness stalking and tracking from their Darkspear allies, supplementing traditional warrior might.",["faction:Horde"]="The exchange between Jen'shan and young recruits demonstrates how the Horde blends the distinct cultural strengths of orcs and trolls to ensure their mutual survival."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","etched tablet","gornek","hunter","jen'shan","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:jen-shan","npc:gornek","quest:cutting-teeth","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Jen'shan",level="1",faction="Horde",id=3082},src={"Etched Tablet (quest)"}}
E["quest:3083"] = {t="quest",n="Encrypted Tablet",z="durotar",s="The Encrypted Tablet is a summons delivered by Gornek to aspiring rogues training within the Valley of Trials. Written in cipher, the message directs novice cutpurses to Rwag, the covert operative in the Den who oversees rogue instruction and ties to the Shattered Hand.",h="The Encrypted Tablet is a summons delivered by Gornek to aspiring rogues training within the Valley of Trials.",sec={{t="A Coded Summons",b="Once an initiate proves their mettle against the local wildlife, Gornek hands over an Encrypted Tablet delivered specifically for them. Rather than plain speech, the message is locked in cipher—a test and a precaution fitting for those who practice the arts of stealth, poison, and subterfuge. It invites the recruit to descend into the Den to meet Rwag, the trainer responsible for shaping rogues, thieves, and cutpurses for the Horde.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow of the Hand",b="Upon decoding the instructions and entering the Den, initiates find Rwag, an agent aligned with the Shattered Hand. While he assures newly recruited rogues that the guild will not dictate their every breath, he warns that the Hand holds him accountable should an apprentice fail to perform. In a fledgling nation surrounded by foes, the Horde relies heavily on silent scouts and agile cutpurses to gather intelligence and eliminate threats from the shadows.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Encrypted Tablet?",a="It serves as an introductory summons for novice rogues in the Valley of Trials, directing them to seek out their class trainer, Rwag, inside the Den.",al={"what does the tablet do","encrypted tablet purpose","why encrypted tablet"}},{q="Who delivers the tablet to the player?",a="Gornek, the overseer of trials in the valley, gives the tablet to you once you have completed your initial combat trial killing Mottled Boars.",al={"who gives the encrypted tablet","tablet quest giver","gornek tablet"}},{q="Where can Rwag be found?",a="Rwag is located deep inside the Den, the dark cavern complex nestled along the northern cliffside of the Valley of Trials.",al={"rwag location","where is rwag","find rwag"}},{q="What is 'the Hand' mentioned by Rwag?",a="Rwag is referring to the Shattered Hand, the covert network and guild of assassins, spies, and rogues serving Warchief Thrall's Horde.",al={"what is the hand","shattered hand rwag","who is the hand"}},{q="Why is the tablet written in an encrypted cipher?",a="The cipher ensures that sensitive rogue business and the identities of their handlers remain hidden from prying eyes, testing the initiate's ability to handle discreet missives.",al={"why encrypted","why cipher","rogue tablet code"}},{q="Can any class undertake this quest?",a="No. The Encrypted Tablet is specifically reserved for troll rogues beginning their journey in the Valley of Trials.",al={"is encrypted tablet rogue only","can warriors do encrypted tablet","tablet class restriction"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="This tablet marks your formal induction into the covert operations of Durotar, putting you in direct contact with your first mentor, Rwag, and introducing the subtle reach of the Shattered Hand.",["race:Orc"]="While traditional orc culture honors open battlefield combat, orc rogues play an indispensable role as scouts and infiltrators under the modern Horde.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear rogues combine jungle tracking instincts with the bladecraft taught by mentors in the Den, establishing their quiet utility among their orc allies."},kw={"durotar","encrypted tablet","gornek","rogue trainer","rwag","shattered hand","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:rwag","npc:gornek","quest:cutting-teeth","subzone:valley-of-trials","quest:1089","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Rwag",level="1",faction="Horde",id=3083},src={"Encrypted Tablet (quest)"}}
E["quest:3084"] = {t="quest",n="Rune-Inscribed Tablet",z="durotar",s="The Rune-Inscribed Tablet is a summoning missive delivered to aspiring shamans training in the Valley of Trials. Sent by Shikrik, it invites promising initiates to begin formal instruction in communing with the spirits and commanding the elemental forces of earth, fire, water, and air.",h="The Rune-Inscribed Tablet is a summoning missive delivered to aspiring shamans training in the Valley of...",sec={{t="A Call to the Spirits",b="After proving their early discipline in the dusty training grounds of the Valley of Trials, fledgling shamans are handed a carved stone tablet by Gornek. The runes upon it serve as an invitation from Shikrik, the local shaman trainer, signaling that the initiate is ready to look beyond simple physical combat and heed the deeper currents of the natural world.",sp=0},{t="Spiritual Leadership in the New Horde",b="Shamanism occupies a sacred place in the revitalized Horde. As Shikrik teaches, shamans draw their power from the four elemental forces and their strength from ancestral spirits. Emulating Warchief Thrall, shamans are expected to be spiritual guides and bulwarks of wisdom for their communities, offering protection to the settlements taking root across Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Rune-Inscribed Tablet?",a="It is an inscribed stone tablet passed to novice shamans by Gornek in the Valley of Trials. It carries a summons from the shaman trainer Shikrik, urging the young adventurer to formalize their training in spiritual and elemental arts.",al={"rune inscribed tablet","tablet item","shaman tablet"}},{q="Who is Shikrik?",a="Shikrik is the shaman trainer stationed near the mouth of the Den in the Valley of Trials. She guides new orc and troll shamans in mastering the elements and understanding their duty as spiritual leaders within the Horde.",al={"shikrik","who is shikrik","shaman trainer valley of trials"}},{q="Why does Shikrik invoke Thrall when speaking to new shamans?",a="Warchief Thrall led the revival of ancestral shamanism after the demonic corruption of the Old Horde. Shikrik points to Thrall as the quintessential example of a shaman's duty: balancing elemental harmony with guiding and protecting his people.",al={"why thrall","shikrik mentioning thrall"}},{q="Where is Shikrik located?",a="Shikrik stands just outside the entrance to the Den on the eastern side of the Valley of Trials, ready to teach novice shamans their early techniques.",al={"where is shikrik","find shikrik"}},{q="Who hands out the tablet?",a="Gornek, who oversees the initial trials of newcomers arriving in the Valley of Trials, delivers the tablet once an initiate has proven their basic mettle.",al={"who gives the tablet","gornek tablet"}},{q="What core philosophy does Shikrik teach?",a="Shikrik stresses that a shaman's raw power is drawn from fire, earth, water, and air, while their endurance and resolve stem from the ancestral spirits. Shamans are expected to offer wisdom and defense to whatever towns or warbands they join.",al={"shikrik philosophy","shaman teachings"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="This tablet marks your formal initiation into the shamanic path, charging you to balance the elemental powers and serve as a beacon of ancestral guidance.",["race:Orc"]="The tablet reflects the modern orcish return to ancestral shamanism championed by Thrall, leaving behind the dark warlock legacies of the demonic past.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear trolls practicing shamanism find common ground with orc mentors like Shikrik, blending their ancestral communion with the Horde's shared elemental traditions.",["faction:Horde"]="Shamanism is the moral and spiritual backbone of the new Horde, offering a compass of honor and balance across the harsh frontier."},kw={"durotar","elements","gornek","shaman","shikrik","tablet","thrall","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:gornek","subzone:valley-of-trials","quest:cutting-teeth","quest:1089","zone:durotar","npc:thrall","topic:horde"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Shikrik",level="1",faction="Horde",id=3084},src={"Rune-Inscribed Tablet (quest)"}}
E["quest:3085"] = {t="quest",n="Hallowed Tablet",z="durotar",s="A simple summons delivered to fledgling priests in the Valley of Trials after their initial trial of strength. The inscribed tablet directs young spiritualists to Ken'jai, the resident troll priest trainer, who introduces them to the deeper communion with the spirits.",h="A simple summons delivered to fledgling priests in the Valley of Trials after their initial trial of strength.",sec={{t="A Message from Ken'jai",b="After proving their mettle against the local boars under Gornek's supervision, young priests training in the Valley of Trials receive an inscribed stone known as the Hallowed Tablet. Delivered through Gornek, the message bears the mark of Ken'jai, a Darkspear mystic positioned outside the Den who watches over newcomers called to the path of faith and spiritual magic.",sp=0},{t="Communing with the Spirits",b="Unlike the Holy Light practiced by their human or dwarven counterparts across the sea, priesthood among the Horde's Darkspear trolls centers on communion with the spirits and loa. Ken'jai welcomes fledgling acolytes to Durotar by reminding them that their power stems from spiritual discipline, promising to instruct them in greater rites only as their spiritual bond matures.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Hallowed Tablet?",a="It is an inscribed message sent by the troll priest trainer Ken'jai to young priests training in the Valley of Trials. Gornek holds onto it until the initiate proves their basic capabilities in the valley.",al={"what is hallowed tablet","hallowed tablet item","tablet lore"}},{q="Who is Ken'jai?",a="Ken'jai is a Darkspear troll priest trainer stationed outside the Den in the Valley of Trials. He mentors young initiates in communion with the spirits and guides them as they learn to wield both healing and shadowy spiritual arts.",al={"kenjai","who is kenjai","ken'jai trainer"}},{q="Why does a priest start out fighting mottled boars?",a="Every initiate in the Valley of Trials, regardless of their calling, must prove basic self-reliance and physical survival skills before specialized instructors will invest time in training them.",al={"why kill boars","cutting teeth connection"}},{q="How does Ken'jai's priesthood differ from the Holy Light?",a="Darkspear priests invoke the spirits and the loa rather than praying to the Holy Light of the human and dwarven churches. Ken'jai emphasizes maintaining favor and harmony with these unseen entities.",al={"troll priest lore","horde priests","spirits vs light"}},{q="Where is the Den?",a="The Den is a hollowed cave settlement nestled in the Valley of Trials in southern Durotar, serving as a hub for trainers and trial-masters overseeing new Horde recruits.",al={"the den durotar","where is the den","kenjai location"}},{q="Can orcs become priests through this quest?",a="No. In the Valley of Trials, only Darkspear trolls possess the spiritual traditions necessary to train as priests under Ken'jai. Orcish culture relies instead on shamanism and warlock magic.",al={"orc priests","can orcs be priests","orc hallowed tablet"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="This quest marks the transition from mundane valley trials to formal spiritual instruction under Ken'jai outside the Den.",["race:Troll"]="The tablet emphasizes Darkspear spiritual traditions, turning to ancestral spirits and the loa rather than the dogmatic philosophies of foreign priesthoods.",["faction:Horde"]="As the Horde settles Durotar, mystical practitioners ensure that spiritual rites and the will of the spirits remain central to the new nation's growth."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","gornek","hallowed tablet","ken'jai","priest","spirits","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:cutting-teeth","npc:gornek","subzone:valley-of-trials","quest:1089","zone:durotar"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Ken'jai",level="1",faction="Horde",id=3085},src={"Hallowed Tablet (quest)"}}
E["quest:3086"] = {t="quest",n="Glyphic Tablet",z="durotar",s="Glyphic Tablet is an introductory class quest in the Valley of Trials directed at novice Horde mages. Dispatched via Gornek after proving one's strength, it directs young spellcasters to Mai'ah, a troll mage trainer stationed outside the Den.",h="Glyphic Tablet is an introductory class quest in the Valley of Trials directed at novice Horde mages.",sec={{t="A Message in Inscribed Stone",b="After proving their basic mettle against the local wildlife in the Valley of Trials, fledgling mages are presented with an inscribed tablet passed along by Gornek. The missive originates from Mai'ah, the valley's resident mage trainer, bidding the initiate to seek her out by the entrance to the Den when they are ready to pursue their formal arcane studies.",sp=0},{t="The Dangers of the Unseen",b="When greeted, Mai'ah wastes little time on formalities, cutting straight to the sober reality of arcane power. While acknowledging that mages wield world-shaping potential, she warns that their greatest threat is neither rival warriors nor enemy races, but the unseen corrupting lure of magic itself. She counsels humility and patience, cautioning that unchecked sorcery easily tricks a practitioner into overestimating their own mastery.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who delivers the Glyphic Tablet to the player?",a="Gornek, the valley's initial questgiver, passes the tablet to you once you have completed your preliminary task of clearing mottled boars in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who gives glyphic tablet","where do i get glyphic tablet","glyphic tablet starter"}},{q="Who is Mai'ah?",a="Mai'ah is a Darkspear troll mage trainer stationed just outside the entrance of the Den in the Valley of Trials. She instructs beginning Horde mages in early spells and offers strict warnings about the perils of arcane corruption.",al={"who is maiah","mai'ah lore","troll mage trainer"}},{q="Where is Mai'ah located?",a="Mai'ah stands just outside the entrance to the Den, to the right of the tunnel mouth, in the northern section of the Valley of Trials.",al={"where is maiah","maiah location","find maiah"}},{q="What warning does Mai'ah give about magic?",a="Mai'ah warns that magic has an inherent corrupting influence that cannot be easily stopped. She emphasizes that mages should fear the unseen temptations and delusions of power brought by the arcane rather than physical enemies like orcs, elves, or dwarves.",al={"maiah warning","magic corruption lore","what does maiah say"}},{q="Do other classes receive the Glyphic Tablet?",a="No. The Glyphic Tablet is designated strictly for novice mages. Other classes receive distinct introductory summons—such as runes, scrolls, or sigils—tailored to their respective trainers.",al={"can other classes get glyphic tablet","is glyphic tablet mage only"}},{q="What prerequisite must be met to receive this tablet?",a="You must first complete the opening quest 'Cutting Teeth' for Gornek by slaying mottled boars across the red dirt flats of the Valley of Trials.",al={"glyphic tablet requirements","prereq for glyphic tablet"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="This quest marks your formal welcome into the ranks of Horde mages, introducing you to the valley's trainer and emphasizing the disciplined mindset needed to control raw magic.",["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls taking up the arcane path, receiving instruction from Mai'ah reflects the tribe's growing adaptation of formalized spellcasting alongside their traditional spiritual rites.",["race:Orc"]="Orcish mages are non-existent in traditional orc culture, making this training an opportunity for other Horde races like Darkspear trolls to hone their craft within Durotar's training grounds."},kw={"arcane","durotar","glyphic tablet","gornek","mage","mai'ah","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:mai-ah","npc:gornek","quest:cutting-teeth","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:dwarf"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Mai'ah",level="1",faction="Horde",id=3086},src={"Glyphic Tablet (quest)"}}
E["quest:3087"] = {t="quest",n="Etched Parchment",z="durotar",s="Etched Parchment is an initiation quest directing young orc hunters in the Valley of Trials to their local class trainer, Jen'shan. Delivered through Gornek after an initiate's first blooding, the note opens the door to specialized wilderness training and survival skills in Durotar.",h="Etched Parchment is an initiation quest directing young orc hunters in the Valley of Trials to their local...",sec={{t="A Summons from the Wild",b="After proving their basic mettle against the local mottled boars, hunters starting in the Valley of Trials receive an etched parchment handled by Gornek. The missive originates from Jen'shan, a skilled Darkspear hunter who observes new arrivals from the edges of the encampment. The note serves as an official invitation to begin formal training, acknowledging that the initiate possesses the instincts required to master the untamed beasts and harsh landscape of Durotar.",sp=0},{t="The Hunter's Way",b="Reporting to Jen'shan marks the transition from common recruit to dedicated stalker. Jen'shan disabuses newcomers of the notion that the hunter's craft is simpler than the arcane arts or ancestral shamanism. Mastering Durotar's predators, maintaining ranged weaponry, and surviving off an unforgiving land demand relentless discipline. She directs her apprentices to aid the other denizens of the valley to test their abilities before returning to her for more advanced survival techniques.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Etched Parchment?",a="It is a written summons delivered by Gornek on behalf of the hunter trainer Jen'shan. It calls promising recruits to report to her for specialized martial and wilderness instruction in the Valley of Trials.",al={"what is this parchment","etched parchment note","hunter parchment"}},{q="Who delivers this summons to the player?",a="Gornek hands over the parchment after you complete your initial trial of slaying mottled boars in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who gives etched parchment","where do i get the quest"}},{q="Who is Jen'shan?",a="Jen'shan is a Darkspear troll hunter stationed in the Valley of Trials. She evaluates new orc and troll hunters, teaching them the foundational skills of ranged warfare, tracking, and beastcraft.",al={"jen'shan lore","who is jenshan"}},{q="Why does Jen'shan compare hunters to mages and shamans?",a="Jen'shan warns that many dismiss hunting as an easy path compared to wielding ancestral spirits or arcane magic. She emphasizes that mastering lethal marksmanship and wild beasts requires equal dedication and danger.",al={"why hunters not easy","jen'shan dialogue meaning"}},{q="What happens after reporting to Jen'shan?",a="Jen'shan introduces you to advanced hunter techniques and instructs you to aid the other inhabitants of the Valley of Trials to hone your newly acquired skills in practical survival.",al={"what next after etched parchment","hunter quest continuation"}},{q="Who can receive this quest?",a="This quest is exclusively offered to newly created orc hunters training in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who gets etched parchment","is this hunter only"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This note represents your first formal recognition as a hunter of the Horde, pointing you to Jen'shan to refine your aim and understand the wild.",["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear recruits, studying under Jen'shan keeps alive the ancient jungle tracking traditions carried over from the Echo Isles.",["race:Orc"]="Orcish hunters rely on mentors like Jen'shan to adapt traditional clan hunting methods to the arid crags and deadly beasts of Durotar.",["faction:Horde"]="Hunters scout the borders and feed the camps; introducing initiates to their craft early ensures the nascent nation of Durotar stays supplied and guarded."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","etched parchment","gornek","hunter trainer","jen'shan","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:jen-shan","npc:gornek","quest:cutting-teeth","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Jen'shan",level="1",faction="Horde",id=3087},src={"Etched Parchment (Classic)"}}
E["quest:3088"] = {t="quest",n="Encrypted Parchment",z="durotar",s="The Encrypted Parchment is a summons delivered to novice orc rogues who have proven their basic survival skills in the Valley of Trials. Written in cipher, it directs promising recruits into the shadowed depths of the Den to meet Rwag, an operative serving the interests of the Shattered Hand.",h="The Encrypted Parchment is a summons delivered to novice orc rogues who have proven their basic survival...",sec={{t="A Coded Summons",b="After proving their mettle against the local wildlife, novice orcs receive an encrypted parchment passed along by Gornek. While other trainers openly recruit pupils in the clearing, the rogue instructor Rwag prefers the discreet safety of cipher and stone. The parchment directs the initiate past the sunlit camp and deep into the cavern known as the Den.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Shadows",b="Upon deciphering the note and venturing inside, the novice discovers Rwag skulking within the rock. Suspicious of the warlocks lurking even deeper in the cave, Rwag wastes no time explaining his true allegiance: he watches recruits on behalf of the Shattered Hand. While orcish society champions overt honor and glory on the battlefield, the Shattered Hand acts as the Horde's silent network of spies, cutthroats, and intelligence gatherers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends the Encrypted Parchment?",a="The parchment is written by Rwag, the rogue trainer in the Valley of Trials. He has Gornek deliver the coded message to promising young orcs after they complete their initial trials.",al={"who wrote the parchment","who gave me encrypted parchment","who sent note"}},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="It serves as the introductory class quest for orc rogues, teaching them how to find Rwag within the Den so they can begin their formal training in stealth, lockpicking, and martial subterfuge.",al={"why do i need encrypted parchment","what does this quest do"}},{q="Where is Rwag located?",a="Rwag hides inside the Den, the dark cavern situated on the northern side of the Valley of Trials. He skulks in the shadows near the entrance, keeping a wary distance from the warlocks deeper inside.",al={"where is rwag","find rwag","rwag location"}},{q="Why is the parchment encrypted?",a="Rogues rely on secrecy and discretion. Using a cipher ensures that wandering brutes or curious outsiders cannot read the summons, while simultaneously testing the initiate's ability to decode covert communications.",al={"why cipher","why is note coded"}},{q="Who are the Shattered Hand?",a="Originally an infamous orc clan known for self-mutilation, the Shattered Hand within Thrall's Horde has evolved into an organization of scouts, assassins, and covert agents working from the shadows to protect Horde interests.",al={"shattered hand horde","what is shattered hand"}},{q="Why does Rwag distrust Nartok?",a="Nartok is a warlock trainer situated deeper in the Den. Rogues operate by stealth, but even Rwag finds it deeply unsettling that dark spellcasters openly conduct fel rituals in the deepest corners of the cave.",al={"rwag nartok","why does rwag hate warlocks"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="This parchment marks your formal induction into the covert apparatus of the Horde, introducing you to Rwag and your earliest professional training.",["race:Orc"]="Unlike typical orc warriors who seek open, bloodthirsty glory, orc rogues balance ancestral discipline with the quiet cunning demanded by the Shattered Hand.",["faction:Horde"]="Even an honorable warchief like Thrall recognizes the necessity of spies and scouts to protect the nascent lands of Durotar from hidden threats."},kw={"durotar","encrypted parchment","gornek","orc rogue","rwag","shattered hand","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:rwag","npc:gornek","quest:cutting-teeth","quest:1089","quest:1858","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","quest:3083"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Rwag",level="3",faction="Horde",id=3088,ri={"Encrypted Parchment"}},src={"Encrypted Parchment (quest)"}}
E["quest:3089"] = {t="quest",n="Rune-Inscribed Parchment",z="durotar",s="Rune-Inscribed Parchment is a missive delivered to fledgling Horde shamans beginning their journey in the Valley of Trials. Written by the trainer Shikrik, the parchment summons promising initiates to begin their formal tutelage in commune with the spirits and elements.",h="Rune-Inscribed Parchment is a missive delivered to fledgling Horde shamans beginning their journey in the...",sec={{t="A Summons from the Spirits",b="After proving their basic survival skills against the local wildlife, new orc shamans are handed a rune-inscribed parchment by Gornek, the overseer of the Valley of Trials. The parchment bears mystical writing from Shikrik, the valley's resident shaman trainer, requesting an audience with the newly arrived initiate.",sp=0},{t="The Path of the Shaman",b="Reporting to Shikrik marks the formal beginning of a shaman's sacred duty to the Horde. Shikrik reminds the young initiate that their calling is not merely martial; they are chosen to serve as conduits for the ancestral spirits and wielders of elemental wrath. Through Shikrik, new shamans learn to channel spiritual energies, mend wounds, and call upon the natural forces of Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Rune-Inscribed Parchment?",a="It is a written summons given by Gornek in the Valley of Trials to new shamans, bidding them to seek out their trainer, Shikrik, for formal instruction in the elements.",al={"what is this quest","parchment quest","shaman starter note"}},{q="Who sends the parchment?",a="The message was penned by Shikrik, the shaman trainer stationed near the dens in the Valley of Trials, awaiting individuals chosen to guide their people spiritually.",al={"who wrote the parchment","shikrik note","who is shikrik"}},{q="Where do I take the parchment?",a="You take it just a short walk away inside the Valley of Trials, where Shikrik stands ready under the red crags to train orc and troll shamans.",al={"where do i go","where is shikrik","turn in location"}},{q="Why was my character chosen to receive it?",a="According to Shikrik, those drawn to the shamanic path are chosen to act as conduits for the ancestors and speak directly with the elemental forces of the world.",al={"why shaman","why chosen","shaman calling lore"}},{q="What happens after presenting the parchment?",a="Shikrik accepts you as her student, introducing you to the path of elemental magic, ancestor commune, and the fundamentals of healing and combat.",al={"next step","what does shikrik do","after parchment"}},{q="Can any class complete this quest?",a="No. The Rune-Inscribed Parchment is specifically addressed to fledgling shamans. Other classes receive their own distinct summons to their respective trainers.",al={"is this shaman only","who gets this parchment","parchment for warriors"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="This parchment represents your earliest step along the spiritual journey, cementing your sacred covenant with the spirits and the raw elements of Durotar.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, returning to shamanism honors the ancestral traditions of Draenor that were nearly extinguished during the demonic corruption of the Old Horde.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear trolls answering this call weave their innate spiritual communion and ancestral reverence into the shared shamanic traditions of the new Horde."},kw={"ancestors","durotar","elements","gornek","rune-inscribed parchment","shaman","shikrik","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","npc:gornek","quest:cutting-teeth","zone:durotar"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Shikrik",level="1",faction="Horde",id=3089},src={"Rune-Inscribed Parchment (Classic)"}}
E["quest:5648"] = {t="quest",n="Garments of Spirituality",z="durotar",s="Garments of Spirituality is a rite of passage for fledgling Horde priests in Durotar, assigned by Tai'jin in Razor Hill. Initiates are sent into the field to locate and mend the wounds of an injured grunt standing vigil against Kul Tiras survivors. Completing the task earns a priest their first ceremonial vestments and formal recognition among the Horde's spiritual practitioners.",h="Garments of Spirituality is a rite of passage for fledgling Horde priests in Durotar, assigned by Tai'jin in...",sec={{t="A Healer's Trial",b="In the arid scrub south of Razor Hill, the Horde faces relentless skirmishes against remnants of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's forces. Rather than sending prospective priests into abstract rituals, the troll trainer Tai'jin tests their discipline in real combat triage. Initiates are charged with seeking out Grunt Kor'ja, a warrior critically injured while repelling human infiltrators, to tend her injuries and bolster her constitution before she succumbs.",sp=0},{t="Vestments of the Faithful",b="Restoring Kor'ja to fighting condition proves the young priest's readiness to bear the mantle of Horde spiritual tradition. In recognition of saving a frontline defender, Tai'jin bestows the Garments of Spirituality. For both orcish allies and Darkspear trolls, these robes signify that the wearer is not merely an apprentice studying incantations, but a reliable lifeline capable of keeping the Horde's warriors alive in battle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Grunt Kor'ja and why does she need healing?",a="Grunt Kor'ja is a Horde warrior posted just south of Razor Hill. She was wounded in a skirmish against surviving soldiers from Admiral Proudmoore's Kul Tiras expedition who still harass the Durotar coastline.",al={"grunt korja","who is korja","injured grunt south"},it="target"},{q="Where can I find Tai'jin?",a="Tai'jin is located in Razor Hill in Durotar. She serves as a spiritual mentor and priest trainer for young Horde adventurers leaving the Valley of Trials.",al={"taijin location","who gives garments of spirituality","priest trainer razor hill"},gp=true},{q="What powers are required to heal Kor'ja?",a="Priests must tend to Kor'ja's injuries using Lesser Heal and bolster her endurance with the blessing of Power Word: Fortitude before returning to Tai'jin.",al={"which spells to use","how to complete garments of spirituality","korja spells"},gp=true},{q="Why are Kul Tiras soldiers still fighting in Durotar?",a="Following Grand Admiral Proudmoore's invasion and defeat, remnants of his fleet dispersed along the eastern coast of Durotar. They continue to mount desperate raids and establish footholds like Tiragarde Keep.",al={"proudmoore troops durotar","why humans in razor hill","kul tiras remnants"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the significance of the garments awarded?",a="The robes awarded by Tai'jin mark an initiate's transition into an active healer of the Horde. Surviving this practical test earns the student the right to wear the vestments of their calling.",al={"garments reward lore","why give a robe","priest vestments razor hill"},it="item"},{q="What quest precedes Garments of Spirituality?",a="This trial follows 'In Favor of Spirituality', an introductory quest offered by Tai'jin once a priest attains sufficient foundational training in Razor Hill.",al={"prerequisite quest","before garments of spirituality","how to start garments"},gp=true},{q="Why does Tai'jin want Kor'ja healed?",a="Tai'jin sees this trial as both practical defense and spiritual duty. Grunt Kor'ja took heavy wounds defending the settlement from Daelin Proudmoore's lingering Kul Tiras remnants, and without healing, she cannot survive to guard Razor Hill. For you, the task serves as your first true test: by mending her body and bestowing ancestral blessings, you prove your mastery of the priestly arts and demonstrate that you are ready to advance along the spiritual path.",al={"why does taijin help korja","taijin motive","why heal korja"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Tai'jin send you instead of tending to Kor'ja himself?",a="Tai'jin remains in Razor Hill to guide aspiring priests, and Kor'ja's plight offers the perfect trial to assess your growth. A priest's true worth is proven outside comfortable sanctuaries, in the dust where blood is spilled and frontline defenders falter. By tasking you to mend Kor'ja and fortify her spirit, Tai'jin requires you to demonstrate that your faith and training can endure the harsh realities facing the Horde.",al={"why send me","why doesnt taijin heal korja","why must i heal korja"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Priest"]="This rite of passage is the defining early test for Horde priests in Durotar, validating their field triage skills and granting their first vestments.",["race:Troll"]="Tai'jin's mentorship weaves troll ancestral spirituality into practical battlefield duty, ensuring young Darkspear wield their faith to protect their allies.",["faction:Horde"]="Grunt Kor'ja's survival directly bolsters the defense of Razor Hill against lingering Kul Tiras human aggressors entrenched nearby."},kw={"durotar","fortitude","garments of spirituality","grunt kor'ja","lesser heal","proudmoore","razor hill","tai'jin"},rel={"quest:5649","npc:tai-jin","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:human"},m={start="Tai'jin",level="4",faction="Horde",id=5648},src={"Garments of Spirituality"}}
E["quest:5649"] = {t="quest",n="In Favor of Spirituality",z="durotar",s="\"In Favor of Spirituality\" is a foundational rite of passage for young Darkspear priests departing the Valley of Trials. Directed by Ken'jai to report to the priest trainer Tai'jin in Razor Hill, initiates take their first real steps beyond the secluded training den into the wider challenges of Durotar. The journey highlights the delicate balance the Darkspear strike between honoring their ancestral troll heritage and integrating into the newly forged Horde.",h="\"In Favor of Spirituality\" is a foundational rite of passage for young Darkspear priests departing the Valley...",sec={{t="Leaving the Red Canyon",b="After mastering their basic rites under Ken'jai in the secluded Valley of Trials, Darkspear acolytes are ready to leave the training grounds behind. The winding paths out into Durotar lead directly to the crossroads settlement of Razor Hill. For a young priest, this journey represents a major milestone: transitioning from basic survival drills in the dirt to shouldering spiritual and cultural responsibilities for the tribe.",sp=0},{t="Old Faiths and New Alliances",b="Ken'jai is candid about the Darkspear's position within Thrall's Horde. While the trolls deeply value the orcs' loyalty and lessons of honor, not every ancestral tradition fits smoothly under the eyes of their allies. Darkspear spiritual leaders instruct their pupils to quietly preserve their heritage, holding fast to their identity while continuing to serve the Horde. Tai'jin at Razor Hill welcomes these acolytes into that deeper understanding, guiding them toward self-sufficiency and communal strength.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest In Favor of Spirituality?",a="The quest is given by Ken'jai, the troll priest trainer stationed inside the Den in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who starts in favor of spirituality","quest giver in favor of spirituality","kenjai priest quest"},gp=true},{q="Where can I find Tai'jin?",a="Tai'jin resides in the barracks at Razor Hill, situated east of the center of town along the main road of Durotar.",al={"tai'jin location","where is tai jin","find tai'jin"},gp=true},{q="What classes can accept this quest?",a="This quest is exclusively offered to troll priests beginning their journey in Durotar.",al={"is this quest priest only","who can take in favor of spirituality","priest class quest razor hill"},gp=true},{q="Why does Ken'jai emphasize keeping some traditions secret?",a="Ken'jai recognizes that while the orcs are loyal comrades who value honor, they do not look kindly on every ancient troll ritual or custom. He teaches young priests to honor their ancestral heritage discreetly to maintain harmony within the Horde.",al={"why secret troll traditions","orc troll friction religion","why practice in secret"},it="motive"},{q="What does Tai'jin teach the young priest upon arrival?",a="Tai'jin explains that the Darkspear have grown stronger by adapting to life in the Horde. Rather than waiting to consume strength directly from fallen foes, the tribe now prepares itself beforehand, entering battle already empowered.",al={"taijin speech","what does tai jin say","darkspear adaptation"},it="purpose"},{q="What quest immediately follows In Favor of Spirituality?",a="Upon turning in this quest, Tai'jin offers 'Garments of Spirituality', which sends the acolyte to assist a wounded Horde soldier in the field.",al={"what comes after in favor of spirituality","in favor of spirituality follow up","next priest quest after taijin"},it="next_step",gp=true}},ang={["class:Priest"]="This quest marks your transition out of the novice canyon to receive formal training and vestments from Tai'jin in Razor Hill.",["race:Troll"]="The mission illustrates the tension the Darkspear navigate every day, balancing their loyalty to the Horde with the preservation of ancient tribal spirituality.",["faction:Horde"]="It demonstrates how diverse cultures coordinate within Durotar, bridging the wild traditions of the Echo Isles with the martial outpost of Razor Hill."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","in favor of spirituality","ken'jai","priest","razor hill","tai'jin","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:tai-jin","quest:5648","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","npc:ukor","quest:2161","topic:horde"},m={start="Ken'jai",["end"]="Tai'jin",level="4",faction="Horde",id=5649},src={"In Favor of Spirituality"}}
E["quest:6062"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="durotar",s="This trial marks a young Horde hunter's first step into the art of beast taming. Guided by the veteran Thotar in Razor Hill, aspiring hunters use an enchanted taming rod to subdue and bond with a vicious dire mottled boar.",h="This trial marks a young Horde hunter's first step into the art of beast taming.",sec={{t="A Hunter's Rite of Passage",b="For orc and Darkspear troll hunters coming of age in Durotar, surviving alone in the wilderness is only half the battle. A true master of the wilds must learn to project authority over nature itself, turning hostile beasts into loyal allies. Hunter trainer Thotar entrusts novices with an enchanted taming rod, challenging them to face down a fierce wild boar without resorting to a lethal arrow.",sp=0},{t="The Boars of Durotar",b="Dire mottled boars roam the arid brush surrounding Razor Hill. Though brutish and ill-tempered, their resilience and ferocity make them ideal introductory subjects for taming. Withstanding their charges and enduring their aggression while channeling the rod's power requires patience and iron resolve—virtues essential for any tracker of the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this trial?",a="It serves as the first practical test for young hunters in Durotar, teaching them how to channel their will through a taming rod to subdue a wild creature rather than simply slaying it.",al={"why do this quest","boar taming quest reason","taming the beast point"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Thotar, the hunter trainer stationed in Razor Hill, offers this assignment once you have proven your basic survival skills across Durotar.",al={"quest giver","who gives taming the beast","where to get boar quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the dire mottled boars found?",a="Dire mottled boars can be found wandering the dry scrublands just outside the palisades of Razor Hill in central Durotar.",al={"boar location","where is dire mottled boar","where to find boar"},gp=true},{q="Do you keep the boar permanently after this quest?",a="No. The boar tamed during this initial exercise serves only as practice. It departs once returned to Thotar, as you must continue your training with other creatures before forming a lasting bond.",al={"do i keep the boar","is the boar my permanent pet","keep dire mottled boar"},gp=true},{q="What comes after this task?",a="Once you return to Thotar, he will test your command over other deadly predators found in Durotar, including surf crawlers and armored scorpid beasts.",al={"next quest","what after boar taming","taming chain next step"},it="next_step"},{q="Why use a taming rod instead of pure instinct?",a="Novice hunters lack the refined spiritual and physical discipline required to bond with beasts directly. The enchanted taming rod acts as a focus, helping novices project authority over a wild beast's spirit until they master the art permanently.",al={"why taming rod","what does the rod do","lore of taming rod"},it="power"},{q="Why does Thotar want you to tame a dire mottled boar?",a="Thotar is preparing you to become a true hunter of the Horde. In his eyes, commanding authority over nature and harnessing the inherent strength of wild beasts is essential to your discipline. He starts you with a local dire mottled boar so you can prove your determination and learn how to fight alongside a companion before moving on to fiercer predators.",al={"thotar motive","why tame boar thotar","why does thotar send you"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What are dire mottled boars?",a="Dire mottled boars are rugged, aggressive swine indigenous to the dry plains of Durotar. Known for their thick hides, stubborn temperaments, and vicious tusks, they roam the crags and ravines near Razor Hill scavenging for food. Their stubborn nature makes them sturdy first partners for a novice hunter learning the art of beast mastery.",al={"dire mottled boar","what is a dire mottled boar","mottled boars durotar"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Thotar send you on this trial instead of handling it himself?",a="This is not an errand or an emergency for Razor Hill's defenders; it is your personal initiation as a hunter. Gaining control over a beast requires direct willpower, practice, and personal determination that no mentor or scout can perform on your behalf. Thotar's role is to guide your training, but mastering the wild is a burden you must shoulder alone.",al={"why me thotar","why do i have to tame it","why doesn't thotar tame it"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This rite of passage bridges the gap between a simple marksman and a true master of beasts, unlocking the hunter's defining bond with animal companions.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, commanding a beast reflects strength of will and authority over the harsh wilderness of their new home in Durotar.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear hunters use this training to attune their spirits to the rugged wildlife of Kalimdor, continuing their ancient stalking traditions."},kw={"dire mottled boar","durotar","hunter quest","pet taming","razor hill","taming rod","thotar"},rel={"npc:thotar","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:6065","quest:6061","quest:6081","topic:troll"},m={start="Thotar",["end"]="Thotar",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6062},src={"Taming the Beast (Orc and Troll 1)"}}
E["quest:6068"] = {t="quest",n="The Hunter's Path",z="durotar",s="The Hunter's Path is a rite of passage directing young orc and troll hunters to Razor Hill. Under the guidance of master hunter Thotar, fledgling trackers learn the vital discipline of binding wild predators to their will.",h="The Hunter's Path is a rite of passage directing young orc and troll hunters to Razor Hill.",sec={{t="A Hunter's Awakening",b="Up to this point, an apprentice hunter in Durotar relies solely on their own bow and cunning. Tracking prey through red clay canyons and harsh scrubland teaches patience, but true mastery in the Horde requires bonding with the untamed fauna of the land. Class trainers recognize when a student has grown capable enough to walk this road, directing them straight to Razor Hill.",sp=0},{t="The Master at Razor Hill",b="Waiting at Razor Hill is Thotar, a veteran hunter steeped in the wild lore of Durotar. Thotar serves as the mentor who instructs novitiates in the perilous ritual of subduing ferocious beasts without breaking their spirit. Meeting him is the first step toward walking the wilderness with a loyal companion at one's side.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of The Hunter's Path?",a="It serves as the introductory summons that sends orc and troll hunters to Razor Hill so they can begin their beast taming training.",al={"why do hunters path","hunter path quest purpose","what does this quest do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Thotar?",a="Thotar is a seasoned hunter located in Razor Hill who oversees the trials required for young Horde trackers to bond with and command wild beasts.",al={"thotar who is he","who is thotar","thotar razor hill"},it="identity"},{q="Why can't young hunters tame pets immediately?",a="Controlling a dangerous predator requires deep discipline, patience, and specialized taming techniques. Until a hunter demonstrates basic survival skills, attempting to bind a wild beast would result in mauling or death.",al={"why no pet at level 1","why must hunters wait for pets","when do hunters get pets"},it="why_here"},{q="Which races undertake this specific trial?",a="This particular version of the path is meant for orcs and Darkspear trolls coming of age in Durotar, while tauren hunters undertake a similar trial in Mulgore.",al={"who gets this quest","is this for orcs and trolls only","what races do this"},it="people"},{q="What happens after reporting to Thotar?",a="Thotar immediately tasks the hunter with tracking down and subjugating various native predators across Durotar to prove their taming prowess.",al={"what comes next","after hunters path","next quest after thotar"},it="next_step"},{q="Where does this training take place?",a="The trial centers around Razor Hill, the primary settlement in central Durotar situated between the Valley of Trials and Orgrimmar.",al={"where is razor hill","thotar location","where to go"},it="place"},{q="Why does the trainer send you to Thotar?",a="Your initial class trainers recognize that you have developed the basic archery and survival skills necessary to handle greater responsibilities. To advance as a true hunter of the Horde, you must bond with a beast companion, and Thotar in Razor Hill is the master entrusted with guiding promising orcs and trolls through the sacred trials of taming.",al={"why see thotar","why thotar","trainer reason thotar"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This summons marks the most defining threshold in your journey: moving from a lone marksman to a true master of beasts.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, partnering with a ferocious companion echoes ancient traditions that stretch back to the wolf riders of Draenor.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear hunters regard learning to tame local raptors and boars as essential for securing their footing in Durotar's treacherous wilds.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde relies on its scouts and trackers to tame regional predators, turning the unforgiving ecology of Durotar into an asset."},kw={"durotar","hunter trainer","hunter's path","pet quest","razor hill","tame beast","thotar"},rel={"npc:thotar","quest:6061","quest:6081","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},m={["end"]="Thotar",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6068},src={"The Hunter's Path (Orc and Troll)"}}
E["quest:6081"] = {t="quest",n="Training the Beast",z="durotar",s="Training the Beast is the culminating rite of passage for young orc and troll hunters in Durotar. After demonstrating mastery over the wild beasts of the plains, hunters are sent from Razor Hill to Orgrimmar to study under veteran master hunter Ormak Grimshot. Completing this journey teaches the novice how to care for, feed, and hone the skills of their lifelong animal companion.",h="Training the Beast is the culminating rite of passage for young orc and troll hunters in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Journey Beyond the Wilderness",b="In the arid canyon lands of Durotar, mastering a bow and surviving the harsh elements is only half of a hunter's duty. After proving their resilience by taming Durotar's fierce boars, crab scavengers, and armored scorpid stalkers, young hunters are ready for the true responsibility of stewardship. Thotar, stationed in Razor Hill, dispatches them north through the red clay gulches straight to the fortified gates of Orgrimmar.",sp=0},{t="The Valley of Honor",b="Within the bustling capital, aspiring track-masters must seek out the Valley of Honor, an enclave where warrior spirits and veteran stalkers hone their craft. There dwells Ormak Grimshot, one of the Horde's most revered master hunters. Ormak looks past raw youth to see whether a hunter possesses the patience required not just to command a beast, but to sustain and nurture it through famine, battle, and loss.",sp=0},{t="Bonding with the Wild",b="A beast won through force of will remains wild until an understanding is forged between hunter and companion. Ormak imparts the sacred traditions required to maintain that bond: the knowledge of which foods nourish each creature's spirit, the discipline needed to teach them lethal techniques, and the spiritual focus required to revive a fallen beast should it collapse in the line of duty.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest Training the Beast?",a="Thotar, the hunter trainer situated outside the barracks in Razor Hill, offers this task once you have successfully subdued all three test creatures across Durotar.",al={"quest giver","who gives training the beast","where to start training the beast"},gp=true},{q="Where can I find Ormak Grimshot?",a="Ormak Grimshot resides in the Valley of Honor, an eastern district within the capital city of Orgrimmar, alongside other veteran hunter and warrior mentors.",al={"ormak grimshot location","find ormak grimshot","where is ormak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What skills does Ormak Grimshot teach you?",a="Ormak teaches you how to train your companion with active and passive abilities, how to feed your pet to keep it loyal and content, and how to revive it if it dies in combat.",al={"what do i learn","quest reward skills","hunter pet abilities"},it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Why do orc and troll hunters have to visit Orgrimmar for this?",a="Local trainers like Thotar can teach basic wilderness survival, but advanced beast mastery is preserved by the Horde's elder scouts and venerated trackers like Ormak Grimshot in the capital.",al={"why go to orgrimmar","why orgrimmar","valley of honor visit"},it="purpose"},{q="Do other Horde races undertake this exact quest?",a="No. This specific rite is designed for orc and troll hunters starting in Durotar. Tauren hunters undertake a parallel ritual in Mulgore under their own tribal masters.",al={"can tauren do this","is this orc only","undead hunter"},gp=true},{q="What happens if a hunter neglects to complete this training?",a="Without finishing this instruction, a hunter cannot feed, properly train, or resurrect their companion, rendering any captured beast unhappy, weak, and ultimately prone to abandoning them.",al={"do i need to do this","can i skip training the beast"},gp=true},{q="Why does Thotar send you to Ormak Grimshot?",a="Thotar guided you through the rites of taming Durotar's wild beasts, but knowing how to bond with a creature is only half the hunter's art. A beast captured in the wild will starve or abandon you if neglected. Thotar sends you onward to Ormak Grimshot so a veteran of the Valley of Honor can teach you how to feed, care for, and discipline your new companion properly.",al={"why does thotar want this done","thotar motive training the beast","why visit ormak"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This quest marks the moment your pet becomes a permanent, dependable ally rather than a fleeting summon, unlocking the essential Feed Pet and Revive Pet arts.",["race:Orc"]="Orcs view the bond with their hunting companion as a matter of martial honor and duty, a partnership tested in battle across the harsh frontiers of Durotar.",["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls carving out a new home in Kalimdor, learning to commune with Durotar's savage creatures is vital for scouting and surviving in unfamiliar soil.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde relies on its scouts and beasts to secure the fragile borders of Durotar and the Barrens against centaur, quilboar, and Alliance incursions."},kw={"durotar","hunter pet","orgrimmar","ormak grimshot","razor hill","thotar","training the beast","valley of honor"},rel={"quest:6061","quest:6065","npc:ormak-grimshot","npc:thotar","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-honor","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},m={start="Thotar",["end"]="Ormak Grimshot",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6081},src={"Training the Beast (Orc and Troll)"}}
E["quest:6082"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="durotar",s="This quest marks the final trial in a young Horde hunter's basic rites of passage in Durotar. Guided by the veteran hunter Thotar in Razor Hill, an aspiring tracker must confront and tame a dangerous armored scorpid. Conquering this armored predator proves mastery over wild beasts and unlocks the lifelong ability to tame, call, and dismiss a true companion.",h="This quest marks the final trial in a young Horde hunter's basic rites of passage in Durotar.",sec={{t="The Final Trial",b="Before a hunter is permitted to roam Kalimdor with a loyal animal companion, they must prove they can command the harshest wildlife Durotar has to offer. Razor Hill's hunter trainer, Thotar, sends trainees to subdue three distinct creatures with an enchanted taming rod. Having previously tested their mettle against dire boars and swift surf crawlers, hunters are tasked with facing the armored scorpid—a venomous, heavily plated predator that embodies resilience and lethal speed.",sp=0},{t="Bonding with the Wild",b="Subduing an armored scorpid is not an act of mere slaughter, but a demonstration of focus and dominance while under relentless assault. Thotar urges hunters to emulate the beast's quick, confident strikes. Returning to Razor Hill after successfully charming the venomous arachnid proves that the hunter possesses the calm will necessary to maintain control. With the taming rod returned, Thotar imparts the innate techniques of the wild, allowing the hunter to seek out and bind a permanent companion of their own choosing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creature do I need to tame for this trial?",a="You must seek out an armored scorpid roaming the arid red crags of Durotar and use Thotar's taming rod to pacify and control it.",al={"what beast to tame","target beast","scorpid quest"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Do I get to keep the armored scorpid after finishing the quest?",a="No. The armored scorpid tamed during the trial is temporary and vanishes once the training rod is handed back. Completing the task, however, teaches you the permanent ability to tame whichever wild beast you desire.",al={"keep scorpid","do i keep the pet","scorpid permanent"},gp=true},{q="Who initiates this rite of passage?",a="Thotar, the hunter trainer situated in Razor Hill within central Durotar, oversees this rite of passage for young orc and troll hunters.",al={"quest giver","who gives taming the beast","thotar location"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why does Thotar want hunters to tame an armored scorpid specifically?",a="Thotar considers the armored scorpid an ideal creature to emulate due to its confident, swift strikes and natural resilience. Mastering such a dangerous predator proves a hunter is ready to command any beast in the wild.",al={"why scorpid","purpose of scorpid"},it="motive"},{q="What skills do you learn upon completing this quest?",a="Completing this trial grants the foundational abilities of a seasoned beast master: Tame Beast, Call Pet, and Dismiss Pet.",al={"rewards","what spells do i get","taming skills unlocked"},it="power",gp=true},{q="What comes after this trial?",a="Once you have learned how to tame and call your own companion, Thotar directs you toward training that pet, sending you on the follow-up quest 'Training the Beast' to master feeding and commanding your ally.",al={"next quest","what's next","after taming 3"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Thotar make you tame beasts yourself rather than doing it for you?",a="This is a rite of passage every burgeoning hunter must endure alone. Thotar's role in Razor Hill is to guide and instruct you, but mastering communion with the wild cannot be granted through words alone. Taming an aggressive, venomous creature like an armored scorpid proves you possess the will, patience, and resolve required to bend a fierce predator to your command before you are entrusted with a permanent companion.",al={"why must I tame the beast","why doesn't thotar tame it","why me thotar scorpid"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This rite of passage is the defining milestone of a hunter's early journey, granting permanent access to the core techniques of taming, calling, and commanding animal companions.",["faction:Horde"]="Orc and troll youths in Durotar must survive the barren land's most vicious predators to earn their place as true scouts and providers for the Horde.",["race:Orc"]="Subduing Durotar's scorpids honors the orcish philosophy of overcoming harsh terrain through unyielding willpower and martial discipline.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear hunters draw upon their keen instincts and deep connection to wild spirits to pacify venomous predators that would strike others down."},kw={"armored scorpid","durotar","hunter trial","pet quest","razor hill","tame beast","taming rod","thotar"},rel={"npc:thotar","quest:6081","quest:6061","quest:6065","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},m={start="Thotar",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6082},src={"Taming the Beast (Orc and Troll 3)"}}
E["quest:6083"] = {t="quest",n="Taming the Beast",z="durotar",s="The second trial in a young hunter's rite of mastery in Durotar, directed by the trainer Thotar in Razor Hill. Aspiring orc and troll hunters are sent to the coastline near the Echo Isles to pacify a surf crawler, expanding their bond beyond terrestrial beasts to coastal wildlife.",h="The second trial in a young hunter's rite of mastery in Durotar, directed by the trainer Thotar in Razor Hill.",sec={{t="Bonding with the Coast",b="Having successfully mastered a dire mottled boar, a fledgling hunter is tasked by Thotar to turn their attention toward the sea. Durotar's harsh environment includes jagged coasts and shallow reefs teeming with armored crustaceans. Facing a surf crawler requires patience and fortitude, as these armored crabs resist intrusion into their coastal domain.",sp=0},{t="The Extension of Will",b="Thotar teaches that any beast a hunter binds must become an extension of their own strength. By subduing an aquatic creature like the surf crawler with the taming rod, the hunter learns to adapt their commanding presence across different temperaments and environments, proving their readiness for permanent companions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are surf crawlers found?",a="Surf crawlers skitter along the eastern shores of Durotar, specifically in the shallows across from Sen'jin Village near the waters leading out toward the Echo Isles.",al={"surf crawler location","where is surf crawler","crab location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of taming a surf crawler?",a="Thotar assigns the surf crawler to teach hunters how to command diverse beasts. Learning to tame an armored aquatic creature broadens a hunter's control, proving they can master animals from water as easily as those from dry land.",al={"why tame crab","surf crawler quest purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Do I keep the surf crawler permanently?",a="No. The beasts tamed during these initial trials are temporary practice subjects subdued through the magic of Thotar's taming rod. Only after completing the entire trial series will you learn the permanent taming skill.",al={"do i keep the crab","is surf crawler permanent"},gp=true},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Thotar, the hunter trainer situated in Razor Hill, offers this trial after you prove your ability to tame a dire mottled boar.",al={"quest giver","who starts taming the beast 2"},it="identity"},{q="What comes after taming the surf crawler?",a="Upon returning the rod to Thotar, he will test you with a third and final trial, tasking you to track down and tame an Armored Scorpid before teaching you permanent beast mastery.",al={"next quest","what's next in the chain"},it="next_step"},{q="Why use a taming rod instead of natural skills?",a="Novice hunters have not yet cultivated the innate spiritual authority required to bond wild beasts permanently. The taming rod acts as a conduit, allowing beginners to safely practice channeling their will before learning the true technique.",al={"why taming rod","what is taming rod"},it="item"},{q="Why does Thotar want me to tame a surf crawler?",a="Thotar is training you in the essential arts of being a hunter. Gaining control over beasts turns them into an extension of your own strength, granting you a distinct advantage over rivals. After testing you against land beasts, he wants you to turn toward the waters to broaden your command and prove you can master spirited aquatic creatures as well.",al={"thotar motive","why tame surf crawler","why does thotar want this"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What are surf crawlers?",a="Surf crawlers are spirited, hardy crabs native to the shallows along Durotar's eastern coast, frequently found scuttling in the waters between Sen'jin Village and the Echo Isles. Their armored carapaces and aquatic nature make them an ideal test for expanding a novice hunter's mastery beyond the terrestrial beasts of the plains.",al={"what is a surf crawler","surf crawlers durotar","about surf crawlers"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="This trial instills the foundational discipline required to command defensive beasts, demonstrating how a creature's natural armor and tenacity complement a ranged marksman.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs carving out a permanent home in Durotar, subduing the shoreline's hardy fauna reinforces their mastery over the rugged landscape.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear trolls are deeply familiar with the waters near the Echo Isles and Sen'jin Village, making this trial an encounter with the familiar wildlife of their coastal refuge."},kw={"durotar","echo isles","pet taming","razor hill","sen'jin village","surf crawler","taming rod","thotar"},rel={"npc:thotar","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:echo-isles","zone:durotar","quest:6061","quest:6081","quest:6065"},m={start="Thotar",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6083},src={"Taming the Beast (Orc and Troll 2)"}}
E["quest:784"] = {t="quest",n="Vanquish the Betrayers",z="durotar",s="Vanquish the Betrayers is a Horde military strike ordered by Gar'Thok in Razor Hill to reclaim Tiragarde Keep from human invaders. Kul Tiran forces under Lieutenant Benedict have reoccupied the stronghold, directly violating the fragile peace between Durotar and Theramore. Eliminating their garrison is critical to securing the eastern coast of the orcish homeland.",h="Vanquish the Betrayers is a Horde military strike ordered by Gar'Thok in Razor Hill to reclaim Tiragarde Keep...",sec={{t="A Shattered Truce",b="When Thrall led the Horde across the Great Sea to Kalimdor, he formed an uneasy alliance with Lady Jaina Proudmoore to vanquish the Burning Legion at Mount Hyjal. That peace was shattered when Jaina's estranged father, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore, arrived with the formidable navy of Kul Tiras. Blaming all orcs for the atrocities of the Old Horde, the Admiral invaded Durotar and seized coastal footholds, including Tiragarde Keep. Though Daelin was eventually slain at Theramore, remnants of his fleet refuse to honor any pact or surrender their hatred.",sp=0},{t="Benedict's Resurgence",b="Following the fall of the Grand Admiral, Tiragarde Keep was briefly broken, but Kul Tiras reserves under Lieutenant Benedict have since retaken the fortress. From this fortified redoubt between Razor Hill and Sen'jin Village, the sailors and marines harass travelers and threaten the eastern sea approaches. Gar'Thok views their entrenched position as an immediate danger to the security of Durotar, calling upon Horde warriors to strike directly at Benedict's command.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are Kul Tiran humans attacking Durotar?",a="They are remnants of the expeditionary fleet commanded by Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore. The Admiral refused to accept peaceful coexistence between humans and orcs, seeking to eradicate Durotar entirely. Even after his death, his loyalists continue to occupy coastal redoubts like Tiragarde Keep in defiance of the Horde.",al={"why are humans in durotar","kul tiras attacking","tiragarde keep humans lore"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Lieutenant Benedict?",a="Lieutenant Benedict is the commanding officer of the Kul Tiran reserves currently holding Tiragarde Keep. Following the defeat of Grand Admiral Proudmoore, Benedict rallied the surviving marines and sailors to retake the coastal fortification and mount persistent operations against the orcs.",al={"who is benedict","lieutenant benedict lore","leader tiragarde keep"},it="leader"},{q="Does Jaina Proudmoore support these humans?",a="No. Jaina made a pact of mutual survival with Warchief Thrall and actively opposed her father's aggressive crusade to preserve peace. The troops holding Tiragarde Keep are rogue remnants of Kul Tiras who reject Theramore's diplomacy and view Jaina's truce as an act of treason.",al={"does jaina support them","theramore kul tiras alliance","jaina proudmoore tiragarde"},it="ties"},{q="Why are they called 'betrayers'?",a="Gar'Thok considers them betrayers because their invasion directly violated the diplomatic understanding forged between Thrall and Jaina Proudmoore to defeat Archimonde in the Third War. Their continued military presence in sovereign Horde territory defies the post-war boundaries established on Kalimdor.",al={"why betrayers","who betrayed who","betrayers meaning"},it="name"},{q="Where is Tiragarde Keep located?",a="Tiragarde Keep is situated on the eastern coastline of Durotar, south of Razor Hill and just northeast of Sen'jin Village. Its high stone walls overlook the coastal waters, providing the invaders a strategic base close to Horde settlements.",al={"tiragarde keep location","where is tiragarde keep","where to find benedict"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Gar'Thok want Tiragarde Keep cleared?",a="Gar'Thok oversees the defense of Razor Hill and eastern Durotar. The reoccupation of Tiragarde Keep by hostile Kul Tiran forces directly threatens the security of the orcish homeland, defying the peace struck between Thrall and Jaina Proudmoore. Allowing an armed human fortress to fester on Durotar's coastline places nearby settlements and supply lines at immediate risk of invasion.",al={"gar'thok motive","why clear tiragarde keep","gar thok why attack humans"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are you being sent to eliminate at Tiragarde Keep?",a="You are tasked with breaking the surviving Kul Tiran naval forces occupying Tiragarde Keep: sailors, marines, and their commanding officer, Lieutenant Benedict. These soldiers represent the remnants of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's fleet, maintaining an unauthorized armed beachhead deep within sovereign Horde territory.",al={"who to kill tiragarde keep","who are the targets","vanquish targets"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Kul Tiran occupation of Tiragarde Keep is an ongoing act of war right on Durotar's threshold. Removing Benedict's forces demonstrates that the Horde can defend its newly settled home from foreign fleets.",["race:Orc"]="Orcs honor the truce struck with Jaina at Mount Hyjal, but Kul Tiras brings back bitter memories of the Second War. Fighting off Benedict's marines is a matter of survival and ancestral pride.",["race:Troll"]="Tiragarde Keep lies uncomfortably close to the Darkspear settlement of Sen'jin Village. Clearing out these hostile sailors directly protects the trolls' vulnerable new home."},kw={"daelin proudmoore","durotar","gar'thok","kul tiras","lieutenant benedict","marines","razor hill","sailors","tiragarde keep","vanquish the betrayers"},rel={"subzone:tiragarde-keep","npc:gar-thok","quest:825","quest:830","subzone:razor-hill","topic:kul-tiras","npc:jaina-proudmoore","zone:durotar"},m={start="Gar'Thok",level="7",faction="Horde",id=784},src={"Vanquish the Betrayers"}}
E["quest:786"] = {t="quest",n="Thwarting Kolkar Aggression",z="durotar",s="Thwarting Kolkar Aggression is a vital Horde defense mission handed out by the scout Lar Prowltusk near Sen'jin Village. Players are tasked with infiltrating Kolkar Crag to destroy three sets of coordinated invasion plans before the centaur clan can strike the fledgling settlements of Durotar.",h="Thwarting Kolkar Aggression is a vital Horde defense mission handed out by the scout Lar Prowltusk near...",sec={{t="A Looming Invasion",b="While scouting western Durotar, the troll tracker Lar Prowltusk slipped into Kolkar Crag under cover of night. What he discovered was alarming: the Kolkar centaurs were not merely mounting disorganized coastal raids, but coordinating an ambitious, three-pronged invasion aimed squarely at the orc and Darkspear homelands. The centaur warlords divided their battle strategies among three distinct leaders, intending to strike the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, and the gates of Orgrimmar itself.",sp=0},{t="Striking the Canyons",b="To avert catastrophic fighting across the dry red canyons of Durotar, recruits are sent deep into Kolkar Crag to cut the head off the serpent. Infiltrating the dusty encampment and burning the three attack scrolls disrupts the centaurs' chain of command. While Lar Prowltusk remains confident that the Horde would inevitably crush any full invasion, destroying these documents spares Durotar's defenders costly bloodshed while their young nation is still finding its footing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Thwarting Kolkar Aggression?",a="The quest is given by Lar Prowltusk, a Darkspear troll scout stationed just outside Sen'jin Village along the southern bluffs of Durotar.",al={"quest giver","who gives quest","lar prowltusk location"}},{q="What targets are the Kolkar centaur planning to attack?",a="The Kolkar battle plans outline a coordinated, three-tiered offensive targeting the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, and the Horde capital of Orgrimmar.",al={"centaur targets","what are attack plans","three targets"}},{q="Where is Kolkar Crag located?",a="Kolkar Crag is a sunbaked canyon complex tucked just west over the rocky ridges from Sen'jin Village in southern Durotar.",al={"kolkar crag location","where is the crag","centaur village durotar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where are the attack plans found inside the crag?",a="The three scrolls containing the invasion blueprints are kept in the hands of three separate Kolkar leaders guarding different campsites throughout the crag.",al={"attack plan locations","where are scrolls","centaur leaders"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the Kolkar want to invade Durotar?",a="The Kolkar are an aggressive, expansionist centaur clan native to the dry lands of Kalimdor. They view the arriving orcs and Darkspear trolls as intruders infringing upon their territory and hunting grounds.",al={"why are centaur attacking","centaur motive","kolkar lore"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after the plans are destroyed?",a="Destroying the documents prevents a coordinated siege, throwing the Kolkar's tactical offensive into disarray and protecting Durotar's fragile settlements from sudden devastation.",al={"quest aftermath","does centaur attack stop"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Lar Prowltusk want the attack plans destroyed?",a="Lar Prowltusk scouted Kolkar Crag and discovered the centaur are preparing a three-pronged invasion targeting Sen'jin Village, the Valley of Trials, and Orgrimmar itself. While the Horde would ultimately crush such an assault, Prowltusk wants their operational plans burned to stop the invasion before it starts, sparing Durotar's defenders unnecessary bloodshed and disruption.",al={"why destroy attack plans","lar prowltusk motive","why thwart kolkar aggression"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are the Kolkar centaur in Kolkar Crag?",a="The Kolkar are a brutal clan of centaur who have established a stronghold in the crags along Durotar's western ridge. Fierce and territorial, they harbor deep hatred for the newly arrived orcs and Darkspear trolls, regularly launching raids from their encampment and scheming to drive the Horde completely out of the region.",al={"who are the kolkar here","kolkar crag centaur","why are kolkar in durotar"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Stopping the Kolkar offensive prevents the fledgling Horde from having to fight an exhausting, multi-front territorial war right at the threshold of its new home.",["race:Troll"]="Having already lost their ancient island home, the Darkspear trolls cannot afford to let Sen'jin Village be overwhelmed by marauding centaurs.",["race:Orc"]="The Valley of Trials is where young orcs undergo their rites of adulthood, making centaur aggression there an existential insult to orcish warrior culture."},kw={"durotar","kolkar","kolkar crag","lar prowltusk","orgrimmar","sen'jin village","thwarting kolkar aggression","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:lar-prowltusk","subzone:kolkar-crag","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},m={start="Lar Prowltusk",level="8",faction="Horde",id=786},src={"Thwarting Kolkar Aggression"}}
E["quest:787"] = {t="quest",n="The New Horde",z="durotar",s="The New Horde is an introductory task in the Valley of Trials given by the veteran warrior Eitrigg. It directs fresh recruits to report to Gornek within the Den to begin their training. Through this brief summons, Eitrigg shares his personal journey and Thrall's guiding vision for a redeemed Horde.",h="The New Horde is an introductory task in the Valley of Trials given by the veteran warrior Eitrigg.",sec={{t="A Veteran's Return",b="Eitrigg stands in the Valley of Trials under orders from Warchief Thrall to evaluate and mentor the newest hopefuls of the Horde. Having abandoned the Old Horde after the Second War, disillusioned by its corruption by the Burning Legion, Eitrigg lived in quiet exile until captured by humans. Rescued by Thrall, he chose to return after learning of the young Warchief's dream: an honorable Horde rooted in ancestral shamanism, entirely severed from demonic masters.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to the Den",b="Before any recruit can venture beyond the harsh canyons of the Valley of Trials, they must prove their mettle. Eitrigg sends newcomers into the shaded cavern known as the Den to speak with Gornek. Though Gornek rarely minces words about the crude state of incoming aspirants, his oversight ensures that only those who master discipline and survival are permitted into the wider reaches of Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Eitrigg?",a="Eitrigg is an aging orc veteran who witnessed firsthand the corruption of the Old Horde under the influence of the Burning Legion. Disillusioned, he withdrew into self-imposed exile in Lordaeron. After being captured by humans and subsequently liberated by Thrall, he swore loyalty to Thrall's newly reformed Horde and now helps oversee recruit training in the Valley of Trials.",al={"who is eitrigg","eitrigg backstory","eitrigg lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Eitrigg talk about the 'New Horde'?",a="The original Horde was manipulated and enslaved by demonic bloodlust under the sway of the Burning Legion. Thrall's New Horde was forged to cast aside demonic control, resurrect traditional shamanistic ways, and build an honorable, autonomous future for orcs and their allies in Kalimdor.",al={"what is the new horde","difference between old and new horde","new horde meaning"},it="origin"},{q="Where is Gornek located?",a="Gornek is stationed just inside the entrance of the Den, the prominent cave hollowed out in the northern rock wall of the Valley of Trials.",al={"where is gornek","find gornek","gornek location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting to Gornek?",a="Gornek accepts you as one of Eitrigg's trainees and gives you your initial field assignments, putting you to work defending the valley and testing your readiness to serve the Horde.",al={"next quest after the new horde","what does gornek do","gornek quest"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why was Eitrigg exiled?",a="Eitrigg abandoned the Horde because he was disgusted by the demonic corruption and senseless slaughter orchestrated by warlocks serving the Burning Legion during the earlier wars.",al={"why did eitrigg leave","eitrigg exile reason","eitrigg demon corruption"},it="history"},{q="Why are recruits trained in the Valley of Trials?",a="The Valley of Trials provides a secluded, rugged environment in Durotar where young orcs and allied newcomers can face dangerous beasts and scorpids under the watchful eye of veteran trainers before setting out into the wider world.",al={"why valley of trials","purpose of the valley of trials","valley of trials training"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Eitrigg send you to Gornek?",a="Warchief Thrall charged Eitrigg with overseeing the training of all new recruits who arrive in the Valley of Trials. While Eitrigg greets newcomers and instills the ideals of a Horde freed from demonic corruption, Gornek handles the practical, hands-on tasks needed to test and harden you. Eitrigg sends you to him so your trial and training can officially begin.",al={"why see gornek","eitrigg motive","why report to gornek"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="This task encapsulates the founding ethos of Thrall's regime: a complete break from demonic servitude in favor of honor, survival, and ancestral identity.",["race:Orc"]="For young orcs stepping into the Valley of Trials, Eitrigg represents the living memory of their people's tragic past and their redemption under Thrall.",["race:Troll"]="The Darkspear trolls train alongside the orcs in the Valley of Trials, having embraced Thrall's vision of mutual survival and honor."},kw={"burning legion","durotar","eitrigg","gornek","new horde","the den","thrall","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:eitrigg","npc:gornek","quest:1089","npc:thrall","topic:horde","zone:durotar","topic:burning-legion"},m={level="1",faction="Horde",id=787},src={"The New Horde (quest)"}}
E["quest:791"] = {t="quest",n="Carry Your Weight",z="durotar",s="Carry Your Weight is an introductory task offered by Furl Scornbrow atop the watchtower overlooking Razor Hill. Too old to fight on the front lines, the scarred veteran asks young Horde adventurers to salvage canvas from local human and centaur hostiles so he can fashion supplies to aid their journey.",h="Carry Your Weight is an introductory task offered by Furl Scornbrow atop the watchtower overlooking Razor...",sec={{t="A Veteran's Calling",b="Furl Scornbrow is a veteran of the Third War who marched alongside Warchief Thrall during the pioneering of Durotar and the desperate defense at Mount Hyjal. Now slowed by age and old injuries, he no longer wields his axe in battle. Instead, he maintains a steady vigil from the Razor Hill watchtower, sounding the alarm against incursions while supporting the next generation of defenders.",sp=0},{t="Scavenged Canvas",b="With signal horn alerts growing less frequent as the Horde's grip on the region tightens, Furl passes his hours crafting practical gear. Sturdy canvas is hard to come by in the arid canyons of Durotar, but it is carried in abundance by both the Kul Tiran interlopers along the eastern shore and the nomadic Kolkar centaur roaming the plains. Scavenging scraps from these hostile forces provides Furl the cloth needed to stitch utility bags for active scouts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Furl Scornbrow?",a="Furl Scornbrow is an aging orc veteran stationed in the watchtower above Razor Hill. He fought alongside Thrall during the founding of Durotar and stood in the combined ranks that brought down Archimonde at Mount Hyjal. No longer able to fight on the front lines, he serves as a lookout and uses his downtime to craft field equipment for young Horde warriors.",al={"who is furl","furl scornbrow lore","who gives carry your weight"},it="identity"},{q="Where can canvas scraps be found in Durotar?",a="Canvas scraps are gathered from the Kul Tiran humans occupying Tiragarde Keep along Durotar's coast and from the Kolkar centaur encamped across the plains. Both factions carry heavy woven materials that can be salvaged from their camps and belongings.",al={"where to get canvas scraps","who drops canvas scraps","canvas scrap locations"},gp=true},{q="Where is the watchtower where Furl is located?",a="Furl's watchtower is perched on the high rocky bluffs directly northwest of Razor Hill. A winding path behind the settlement leads up to the summit where the wooden lookout structure stands.",al={"where is furl scornbrow","razor hill watchtower location","find razor hill watchtower"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Furl craft with the canvas scraps?",a="Furl stitches the gathered canvas scraps into a rugged utility bag. For young adventurers journeying across Durotar, having extra carrying capacity for provisions, rations, and salvaged arms is essential for surviving the harsh wilderness.",al={"what does furl make","what is the canvas used for","canvas scraps reward"},it="item"},{q="Why is an old warrior crafting bags instead of fighting?",a="Decades of relentless combat have taken their toll on Furl's body, leaving him unable to match the speed and strength demanded in the field. Rather than lamenting his retirement, he finds honor in keeping watch over Razor Hill and manufacturing gear that directly empowers younger fighters to defend the realm.",al={"why is furl crafting","why does furl stay in the tower","why isn't furl fighting"},it="motive"},{q="What war did Furl fight in?",a="Furl fought under Warchief Thrall during the Third War, taking part in the settlement of Durotar and the climactic Battle of Mount Hyjal against the Burning Legion. He proudly recalls answering the battlecry during the temporary, necessary truce formed between the Horde, the night elves, and the Alliance to defeat Archimonde.",al={"furl battle history","what did furl do before","archimonde furl"},it="history"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Every young soldier in Durotar relies on seasoned veterans like Furl Scornbrow, who remind newcomers that honoring the Horde means doing whatever duty the homeland requires, whether guarding an outpost or sewing canvas.",["race:Orc"]="Furl embodies the older generation of orcs who broke free from demonic corruption, crossed the sea with Thrall, and now dedicate their final years to nurturing the future of their fledgling nation.",["profession:Tailoring"]="Furl demonstrates practical, rugged frontier tailoring, turning discarded heavy canvas from human invaders and centaur raiders into durable wilderness survival gear."},kw={"canvas scraps","carry your weight","durotar","furl scornbrow","kolkar","razor hill","razor hill watchtower","tiragarde"},rel={"npc:furl-scornbrow","subzone:razor-hill-watchtower","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:784","quest:786","topic:centaur","topic:horde"},m={start="Furl Scornbrow",level="7",faction="Horde",id=791,ri={"Canvas Scraps"}},src={"Carry Your Weight"}}
E["quest:792"] = {t="quest",n="Vile Familiars",z="durotar",s="Vile Familiars is an early task given by Zureetha Fargaze to newly arrived champions in the Valley of Trials. While monitoring the valley's trials, Zureetha discovered an insidious coven of the Burning Blade hiding in a nearby cavern. To check their sudden spread, recruits are sent to hunt down the demonic familiars creeping out into the red dirt of Durotar.",h="Vile Familiars is an early task given by Zureetha Fargaze to newly arrived champions in the Valley of Trials.",sec={{t="A Shadow in the Valley",b="The Valley of Trials is meant to be a proving ground where young orcs and Darkspear trolls demonstrate their strength, discipline, and loyalty to Thrall's Horde. It was intended to test recruits against native predators like scorpids and boars, not demonic corruption. Yet, hidden in a cave to the northeast, agents calling themselves the Burning Blade have established a secret coven right under the watchful gaze of the valley's overseers.",sp=0},{t="Culling the Imps",b="Zureetha Fargaze, an instructor sent to guide newcomers near the Den, noticed the subtle taint before it could overrun the canyon. Minor demonic creatures known as Vile Familiars have begun pouring from the cave's mouth, hurling fire and menacing anyone who wanders too close. Before the Horde can root out the masters hiding in the shadows, young recruits are tasked with cutting down these lesser servants to keep the valley secure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Vile Familiars?",a="Zureetha Fargaze gives the quest. She is stationed just outside the entrance to the Den in the center of the Valley of Trials.",al={"vile familiars quest giver","who gives vile familiars","where to pick up vile familiars"},it="identity"},{q="What are Vile Familiars?",a="Vile Familiars are small, imp-like demonic creatures summoned and bound by the Burning Blade cultists. They serve as minor minions and pets, wielding fire to harass intruders.",al={"what are vile familiars","vile familiar lore","vile familiars mob type"},it="target"},{q="Where is the Burning Blade Coven located?",a="The coven is nestled within a cave in the northeastern reaches of the Valley of Trials, past the roaming Mottled Boars and Scorpid Workers.",al={"burning blade coven location","where is burning blade coven","cave in valley of trials"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Burning Blade in the Valley of Trials?",a="The Burning Blade is a covert cult dedicated to undermining Thrall's new Horde and spreading demonic corruption. Infiltrating the Valley of Trials allows them to lurk in secret and threaten the Horde's newest generation of fighters.",al={"why is burning blade here","burning blade motives","what does burning blade want"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after completing Vile Familiars?",a="Once the familiars outside the cavern are thinned out, Zureetha Fargaze directs you to delve inside the cave to face the cultist leader and recover a Burning Blade Medallion.",al={"vile familiars follow up","what comes after vile familiars","burning blade medallion quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Do I have to go deep into the cave to find the familiars?",a="No. While they dwell inside the cavern, plenty of Vile Familiars swarm around the entrance and the canyon floor just outside the cave mouth.",al={"are vile familiars inside cave","where to kill vile familiars","farm vile familiars"},gp=true},{q="Why does Zureetha Fargaze want the Vile Familiars slain?",a="Zureetha Fargaze came to the Valley of Trials to guide new recruits, but discovered a growing corruption right at the Horde's doorstep. The covert Burning Blade cult has established a hidden coven in the nearby caves, and their summoned imps are spilling out across the valley. To protect the trial grounds and purge the demonic taint before it spreads further, she needs their vanguard eliminated.",al={"why kill vile familiars","zureetha fargaze motivation","why does zureetha want vile familiars dead"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why does Zureetha send you instead of dealing with the familiars herself?",a="You are in the Valley of Trials to prove yourself worthy of serving the Horde. While Zureetha coordinates the response against the covert cultists and keeps watch outside the Den, dispatching you serves a dual purpose: it curtails the demonic infestation threatening the valley while serving as a vital baptism of fire against the darker powers undermining your people.",al={"why send me","why doesn't zureetha fight","why do i have to kill familiars"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For orcs striving to honor Thrall's rejection of demonic slavery, encountering fel taint in their sacred training grounds is a bitter reminder that the legacy of the Shadow Council still festers.",["faction:Horde"]="The Burning Blade represents one of the most immediate internal threats to Durotar, seeking to rot the young Horde from within before it can firmly establish its sovereignty.",["class:Warlock"]="Orc and troll warlocks must face the reality of rogue shadowcasters who abuse demonic pacts for destruction rather than bending fel energies toward the Horde's survival."},kw={"burning blade","burning blade coven","durotar","imps","the den","valley of trials","vile familiars","zureetha fargaze"},rel={"npc:zureetha-fargaze","subzone:burning-blade-coven","subzone:valley-of-trials","quest:1089","zone:durotar","topic:horde","topic:troll"},m={start="Zureetha Fargaze",level="4",faction="Horde",id=792},src={"Vile Familiars (Classic)"}}
E["quest:794"] = {t="quest",n="Burning Blade Medallion",z="durotar",s="Assigned by the warlock Zureetha Fargaze, this task sends young Horde initiates deep into the Burning Blade Coven cave in the Valley of Trials. There, players must confront a hidden cultist and recover an artifact of dark magic known as the Burning Blade Medallion. The mission reveals that demonic corruption is actively taking root right under the Horde's nose.",h="Assigned by the warlock Zureetha Fargaze, this task sends young Horde initiates deep into the Burning Blade...",sec={{t="A Hidden Threat in the Valley",b="While young orcs and trolls undergo basic trials of combat and survival in the Valley of Trials, an insidious menace lurks in the shadows. Through her divinations, the warlock Zureetha Fargaze senses that the vile familiars infesting the northern bluffs are merely the vanguard of a darker presence. Deep within a nearby cavern, the Burning Blade cult has established a hidden coven, practicing dark arts and harboring dangerous relics of demonic power.",sp=0},{t="Confronting Yarrog Baneshadow",b="The medallion itself is held in the clutches of Yarrog Baneshadow, an orc warlock acting as an agent of the Burning Blade. Tucked away on an elevated ledge deep within the subterranean den, Yarrog commands fel beasts and dark magic away from the watchful eyes of the Valley's overseers. Striking him down and seizing the medallion disrupts the cult's local leadership before their rituals can expand further into the heart of Durotar.",sp=1},{t="The Lingering Shadow",b="Securing the talisman confirms Zureetha Fargaze's worst fears. While the coven in the Valley of Trials has been dismantled, the medallion is proof that the Burning Blade operates with organization and intent. The cult's reach extends well beyond the initiation grounds, signaling that the nascent Horde will face far broader demonic conspiracies across Durotar.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do I find the Burning Blade Coven?",a="The Burning Blade Coven is located inside a cave tucked into the bluffs to the north and west of The Den in the Valley of Trials, surrounded by imp-like vile familiars.",al={"coven cave location","where is the cave","burning blade cave valley of trials"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is carrying the Burning Blade Medallion?",a="The medallion is carried by Yarrog Baneshadow, a rogue orc cultist found deep within the cavern, positioned on an elevated rock ledge beyond a shallow pool of water.",al={"who drops the medallion","yarrog baneshadow","medallion mob"},it="target"},{q="What is the Burning Blade?",a="The Burning Blade is a treacherous cult of fel-corrupted orcs and warlocks devoted to demonic powers, actively scheming against Thrall's new Horde from hidden dens and encampments.",al={"who are burning blade","burning blade cult","what is burning blade"},it="threat"},{q="Why is the medallion so important to Zureetha Fargaze?",a="Zureetha scried the medallion through her divinations. It serves as an item of power that fuels the cult's dark rituals and provides undeniable proof that demonic agents are infiltrating the Valley of Trials.",al={"why does zureetha want it","what is the medallion","zureetha fargaze medallion"},it="motive"},{q="Does defeating Yarrog finish off the cult in Durotar?",a="No. While Yarrog's demise cleanses the cave in the Valley of Trials, Zureetha warns that this coven is only a small cell and that the Burning Blade has much larger ambitions across Durotar.",al={"is the burning blade destroyed","are they gone","after burning blade medallion"}},{q="What happens after turning in the medallion?",a="Having proven your worth by slaying Yarrog and recovering the relic, you are deemed ready to leave the Valley of Trials and directed to report to Sen'jin Village on Durotar's southern coast.",al={"next quest","what comes next","after this quest"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Burning Blade Medallion for?",a="Through her divinations, Zureetha Fargaze identified the medallion as a potent item of black magic harbored deep within the Burning Blade Coven. Possessed by Yarrog Baneshadow, it serves as an artifact of demonic power and an emblem of the shadow council's lingering influence right on the Horde's doorstep.",al={"burning blade medallion purpose","what does burning blade medallion do","why is medallion powerful"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Recovering the tainted relic aids Zureetha Fargaze in exposing demonic corruption that defiles the earth of Durotar.",["race:Orc"]="Hunting down Yarrog Baneshadow highlights the internal struggle of the new Horde to purge the lingering demonic taint of the old ways right in their training grounds.",["class:Warlock"]="Confronting Yarrog serves as a stark reminder of the perils of rogue demonic worship outside the sanctioned, carefully hidden pacts forged under Thrall's rule.",["faction:Horde"]="The mission represents the final trial for young recruits, marking their readiness to venture into the broader wilds of Durotar to defend the young nation."},kw={"burning blade","coven","durotar","medallion","the den","valley of trials","warlock","yarrog baneshadow","zureetha fargaze"},rel={"npc:zureetha-fargaze","subzone:burning-blade-coven","quest:792","subzone:valley-of-trials","quest:1089","zone:durotar"},m={start="Zureetha Fargaze",level="5",faction="Horde",id=794,ri={"Burning Blade Medallion"}},src={"Burning Blade Medallion (Classic)"}}
E["quest:804"] = {t="quest",n="Sarkoth",z="durotar",s="Having avenged the wounded troll Hana'zua by slaying the monstrous scorpid Sarkoth, an adventurer must carry word of his plight back to the Den. Gornek must be alerted so that rescue can reach the stricken scout before his venomous wounds claim his life.",h="Having avenged the wounded troll Hana'zua by slaying the monstrous scorpid Sarkoth, an adventurer must carry...",sec={{t="A Scout's Plight",b="Stranded upon the high bluffs of the Valley of Trials, the Darkspear scout Hana'zua found himself venom-struck and unable to return down the treacherous paths unassisted. Though vengeance was delivered upon Sarkoth—the dread scorpid that felled him—pride alone cannot carry an envenomed warrior across the arid stones. Bound to his rock, he relies on a passing initiate to bring word back down to the training encampment.",sp=0},{t="Honor in the Den",b="Returning to Gornek at the Den concludes the trial. Gornek immediately recognizes the menace of Sarkoth and swiftly organizes aid for Hana'zua. In the eyes of the Horde commanders, stepping aside from one's personal training to vindicate and rescue a fallen stranger embodies true honor, proving an initiate's worth long before they march out into Durotar proper.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Hana'zua and why is he stranded?",a="Hana'zua is a young Darkspear troll scout who ventured into the high reaches of the Valley of Trials and was ambushed and poisoned by the monstrous scorpid Sarkoth. Too weak to make the climb down on his own, he requires rescue.",al={"hanazua","who is hanazua","why is the troll hurt"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Gornek?",a="Gornek is an orc overseer stationed at the Den in the Valley of Trials. He evaluates new recruits, assigns survival tasks, and coordinates aid when initiates encounter deadly threats within the ravine.",al={"gornek","where is gornek","den leader"},it="identity"},{q="What is Sarkoth?",a="Sarkoth is a notorious, overgrown scorpid residing in the rocky bluffs above the Valley of Trials. Its venom and sheer ferocity make it a legendary hazard among the trials of young orcs and trolls.",al={"sarkoth beast","what kind of monster is sarkoth"},it="target"},{q="Does Hana'zua survive his wounds?",a="Yes. Upon hearing your report, Gornek sends a rescue party immediately up the bluffs to tend to his venom and escort him safely back to camp.",al={"does the troll live","is hanazua okay","hanazua saved"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Gornek praise this deed so highly?",a="Surviving the trials is expected, but setting aside your own tasks to fight for a stranger's honor and ensure their survival exemplifies the core values the new Horde seeks to forge in its warriors.",al={"why does gornek care","gornek honor speech"}},{q="Where is the Den located?",a="The Den is the central training cave and staging ground located at the heart of the Valley of Trials in southwestern Durotar.",al={"where is the den","den location durotar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Hana'zua ask you to report to Gornek?",a="Though avenging his defeat against Sarkoth has steeled Hana'zua's resolve to survive, his grievous wounds leave him completely immobilized in the valley. He cannot make the trek back to the Den on his own strength. By sending you with word of his predicament, he hopes Gornek will dispatch aid before he succumbs to his injuries or the elements.",al={"why send to gornek","hanazua motive","why tell gornek"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why can't Hana'zua return to the Den himself?",a="Hana'zua was battered and left for dead by Sarkoth during his trial. He lacks the strength to stand, let alone crawl across the scorching canyon floor back to safety unassisted. With no other warriors nearby to assist him, you are his sole lifeline to relay word to Gornek before it is too late.",al={"why does hanazua need help","why cant hanazua walk","why me hanazua"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Orcish culture values personal strength, but standing up to defend an incapacitated ally's honor proves the heart of a true warrior.",["race:Troll"]="The fledgling alliance between the Darkspear tribe and Thrall's orcs is strengthened through acts of brotherhood such as saving Hana'zua from a slow, venomous death.",["faction:Horde"]="The new Horde is built on mutual survival in a harsh, unforgiving land; leaving no comrade behind is a foundational principle taught from an initiate's first steps."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","gornek","hana'zua","sarkoth","scorpid","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:hana-zua","npc:gornek","quest:1089","zone:durotar"},m={start="Hana'zua",["end"]="Gornek",level="5",faction="Horde",id=804},src={"Sarkoth (2)"}}
E["quest:805"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Sen'jin Village",z="durotar",s="Report to Sen'jin Village marks the moment young Horde initiates leave the secluded Valley of Trials behind to alert the Darkspear trolls of demonic cult activity. Entrusted by Zureetha Fargaze, messengers carry word of the Burning Blade to Master Gadrin, discovering that shadow magic already threatens the nearby coasts.",h="Report to Sen'jin Village marks the moment young Horde initiates leave the secluded Valley of Trials behind...",sec={{t="Leaving the Den",b="After proving their combat mettle and recovering dark medallions from the Burning Blade Coven within the Valley of Trials, novices are declared ready for the wider world. Zureetha Fargaze recognizes that the demonic presence within the sacred proving grounds is no isolated nuisance, but a symptom of a creeping blight across Durotar. She directs young adventurers east past the ravine's mouth and south toward the coast to warn the Darkspear tribe.",sp=0},{t="Shadows over the Coast",b="Arriving at the coastal settlement of Sen'jin Village, travelers deliver their warning to Master Gadrin, the elder witch doctor guiding the Darkspear in exile. While Gadrin confirms that the Burning Blade itself has not marched on the village sands, he reveals that dark magic has taken seed nearby on the Echo Isles. The report exposes how fragile the young Horde's foothold remains: even as allies rush to defend one another, ancient tribal betrayals and fel corruption strike at their flanks simultaneously.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Zureetha Fargaze sending people away from the Valley of Trials?",a="Having uncovered demonic activity inside the Valley of Trials, Zureetha Fargaze fears that the Burning Blade cult poses an organized threat to all of Durotar. She sends proven initiates beyond the valley to warn allied settlements and determine how far the cult's influence has spread.",al={"why leave valley","why go to senjin","zureetha fargaze orders"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Master Gadrin?",a="Master Gadrin is an elder witch doctor and spiritual leader of the Darkspear trolls residing in Sen'jin Village. He acts as an advisor to chieftain Vol'jin and oversees tribal matters while dealing with the threats looming over their temporary coastal refuge.",al={"master gadrin lore","who is gadrin"},it="identity"},{q="Has the Burning Blade attacked Sen'jin Village?",a="No, the Burning Blade has not directly attacked Sen'jin Village. However, Master Gadrin notes that kindred dark magics and betrayal have taken root nearby on the Echo Isles, meaning the trolls face imminent danger of their own.",al={"is burning blade in senjin","cult in senjin"},it="threat"},{q="Where is Sen'jin Village located?",a="Sen'jin Village lies east through the main canyon exit of the Valley of Trials, followed by a southward turn at the road's fork along the southeastern coast of Durotar.",al={"how to get to senjin","senjin village direction"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threat does Master Gadrin mention on the Echo Isles?",a="Master Gadrin is concerned with the dark betrayal of Zalazane, a fellow troll witch doctor who used insidious hexes to enslave his brethren and seize control of the Echo Isles, driving the surviving Darkspear onto the mainland shores.",al={"echo isles trouble","what happened at echo isles"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after reporting to Master Gadrin?",a="After listening to your report and detailing the trolls' own plight, Gadrin asks you to lend aid against the perils threatening the coastline, while further orders send you northwest to Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill.",al={"next quest after report to senjin","what to do after gadrin"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Zureetha Fargaze send you to Master Gadrin instead of a guard?",a="You have personally confronted the Burning Blade inside their coven in the Valley of Trials and recovered proof of their presence. Having proved your loyalty and strength through your trials, you are the most qualified messenger to provide Master Gadrin with an eyewitness account of the cult's infiltration.",al={"why send me","why me zureetha","why not send a runner to senjin"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="This task demonstrates the vital cooperation between the founding races of Thrall's Horde, exchanging intelligence to protect each other's young settlements.",["race:Troll"]="Returning to Sen'jin Village brings Darkspear adventurers face to face with the displacement of their people and the ongoing struggle to reclaim the Echo Isles.",["race:Orc"]="For young orcs, leaving the Valley of Trials to aid the Darkspear is an early test of honor and solidarity toward the allies who stood beside Thrall across the Great Sea."},kw={"burning blade","darkspear","durotar","echo isles","master gadrin","sen'jin village","valley of trials","zureetha fargaze"},rel={"npc:zureetha-fargaze","npc:master-gadrin","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:valley-of-trials","quest:823","subzone:burning-blade-coven","subzone:echo-isles","zone:durotar"},m={start="Zureetha Fargaze",["end"]="Master Gadrin",level="5",faction="Horde",id=805},src={"Report to Sen'jin Village (Classic)"}}
E["quest:806"] = {t="quest",n="Dark Storms",z="durotar",s="Dark Storms is a critical task assigned by Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill to strike down a rogue warlock corrupting the land. A goblin named Fizzle Darkstorm has entrenched himself in Thunder Ridge on behalf of the insidious Burning Blade cult. Eliminating him is vital to safeguarding Durotar from demonic resurgence before the cultists spread further.",h="Dark Storms is a critical task assigned by Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill to strike down a rogue warlock...",sec={{t="A Threat in the Ridge",b="While young Horde defenders patrol the borders of Durotar, internal corruption festers right under their watch. Orgnil Soulscar, conducting inquiries from Razor Hill, discovered that Thunder Ridge to the northwest has fallen under the sway of dark magic. The ravine is crawling with Burning Blade cultists who bring ruin and chaos to the local wildlife and land.",sp=0},{t="Fizzle Darkstorm",b="Directing the cultist activity within the ridge is Fizzle Darkstorm, an opportunistic goblin warlock allied with the Burning Blade. Rather than serving commerce or cartel interests, Fizzle wields fel power directly in service of the cult's subversive agenda. Slaying him and claiming his twisted claw proves to Orgnil that the cult's immediate leadership in the ravine has been broken.",sp=0},{t="Rooting Out the Cult",b="The Burning Blade represents everything Thrall's new Horde fights to leave behind: demonic servitude, reckless corruption, and bloodthirsty madness. Striking down Fizzle removes an active conspirator from Durotar's interior, but it also signals that the shadow over the orcish homeland runs far deeper than isolated encampments.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Fizzle Darkstorm?",a="Fizzle Darkstorm is a goblin warlock operating on behalf of the Burning Blade cult. He and his cultist followers have taken refuge in Thunder Ridge, spreading demonic chaos across the ravine until Orgnil Soulscar calls for his execution.",al={"who is fizzle","fizzle darkstorm lore","fizzle goblin"},it="target"},{q="Where is Thunder Ridge located?",a="Thunder Ridge is a rugged canyon situated in northwestern Durotar, north of Razor Hill and just southwest of Orgrimmar. It is notoriously overrun by lightning-infused beasts and encampments of Burning Blade cultists.",al={"where is thunder ridge","thunder ridge location","how to find thunder ridge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the Burning Blade in Durotar?",a="The Burning Blade seeks to undermine Thrall's Horde and re-establish demonic dominance over the orcs. They operate secretly out of hidden ravines, caves, and canyons across Durotar to sow corruption from within.",al={"burning blade in durotar","why are cultists in durotar","burning blade motives"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Orgnil Soulscar want Fizzle's claw specifically?",a="Orgnil requires unmistakable proof that the warlock has been terminated. Bringing back Fizzle's claw confirms that the head of the cultist cabal in Thunder Ridge can no longer direct operations.",al={"why fizzle claw","fizzle's claw meaning","proof of death fizzle"},it="item"},{q="What happens after Fizzle is slain?",a="Defeating Fizzle clears the immediate threat in Thunder Ridge, leading Orgnil Soulscar to send you on to the shaman Margoz, who knows more of the Burning Blade's corruption, to root out further Burning Blade conspiracies.",al={"what comes after dark storms","dark storms follow up","next quest after dark storms"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why would a goblin work for the Burning Blade?",a="While many goblins seek gold through trade cartels, some are enticed by the raw power, influence, and dark arts offered by shadow magic. Fizzle embraced fel witchcraft and lent his ruthless cunning directly to the cultists.",al={"goblin in burning blade","why is fizzle with the cult","fizzle warlock"}},{q="Why does Orgnil Soulscar want Fizzle Darkstorm eliminated?",a="Orgnil fears that if the Burning Blade is allowed even a small foothold in Durotar, their corruption and demonic influence will spread uncontrollably. Fizzle Darkstorm and his coven have entrenched themselves in Thunder Ridge, actively sowing chaos right on the doorstep of the fledgling orc homeland. Striking them down immediately prevents a full-scale demonic infiltration from taking root.",al={"why kill fizzle darkstorm","orgnil soulscar motive","why dark storms quest"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="The Burning Blade represents the dark past the orcs fight every day to overcome. Eliminating cultist infiltrators like Fizzle is essential to preserving Thrall's free nation.",["class:Warlock"]="Fizzle Darkstorm demonstrates the reckless danger of uncontrolled fel devotion, making him an embarrassment and a hazard that disciplined Horde practitioners cannot tolerate.",["faction:Horde"]="Ensuring the heart of Durotar remains secure from demonic subversion allows the nascent Horde to direct its defenses outward rather than collapsing from inside.",["class:Shaman"]="The dark rites practiced by Fizzle and his minions disrupt the natural spirits of Thunder Ridge, agitating its beasts and demanding elemental balance be restored."},kw={"burning blade","dark storms","durotar","fizzle darkstorm","fizzle's claw","orgnil soulscar","razor hill","thunder ridge"},rel={"npc:orgnil-soulscar","subzone:thunder-ridge","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","quest:823","topic:goblin"},m={start="Orgnil Soulscar",level="12",faction="Horde",id=806,ri={"Fizzle's Claw"}},src={"Dark Storms (quest)"}}
E["quest:808"] = {t="quest",n="Minshina's Skull",z="durotar",s="Master Gadrin of Sen'jin Village is haunted by the desperate cries of his deceased brother, Minshina. Slain and subjected to dark magic by the rogue witch doctor Zalazane on the Echo Isles, Minshina's soul remains bound inside his own severed skull. Freeing the fallen troll requires infiltrating Zalazane's ritual grounds to reclaim the relic and release his spirit from eternal torment.",h="Master Gadrin of Sen'jin Village is haunted by the desperate cries of his deceased brother, Minshina.",sec={{t="A Plea from the Shadows",b="Master Gadrin serves as one of the Darkspear tribe's spiritual anchors in Sen'jin Village, but his mind is tormented by dark visions. His brother Minshina fell victim to Zalazane's betrayal when the mad warlock seized control of the Echo Isles. Minshina perished during the conflict, but in troll tradition and voodoo mysticism, physical death does not always grant peace. Minshina's tormented voice speaks into Gadrin's dreams, pleading for salvation from a fate worse than death.",sp=0},{t="Zalazane's Circle of Power",b="Zalazane does not simply kill his former brethren; he ensnares their souls to fuel his dark sorcery. Minshina's essence was ritually bound to his own skull, which now rests amidst a blasphemous circle of power on the largest of the Echo Isles. Guarded by hexed trolls and bathed in candlelit ritual, the skull serves as a focal point for the traitor's twisted mojo. So long as it sits within the circle, Minshina remains an eternal captive to Zalazane's will.",sp=0},{t="Freedom in Death",b="To save Minshina, a brave champion must cross the waters east of Sen'jin Village to the southern reaches of the Echo Isles, break into the ritual ring, and extract the skull from the witch doctor's influence. Returning the remains to Master Gadrin severs the dark bindings, allowing Minshina's grateful spirit to briefly materialize, bow in reverence, and finally depart for the realm of the ancestors.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was Minshina?",a="Minshina was the brother of Master Gadrin, the prominent witch doctor and elder residing in Sen'jin Village. He was murdered during the uprising on the Echo Isles by Zalazane, who then desecrated his remains with dark sorcery.",al={"minshina identity","who is minshina","gadrin brother"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Minshina's spirit trapped in his skull?",a="Zalazane uses dark voodoo and warlock magic to enslave the spirits of slain Darkspear trolls. By binding Minshina's soul directly to his physical skull and placing it within a ritual circle of power, Zalazane denied him passage to the afterlife and harnessed his spirit.",al={"why trap skull","zalazane soul trap","minshina soul"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where is the circle of power located?",a="The ritual site is located atop a hill on the southernmost and largest of the Echo Isles, off the southeastern coast of Durotar. It is recognizable by ritual candles, dancing hexed trolls, and displays of skulls.",al={"where is skull","circle of power location","minshina skull spot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens when the skull is brought back to Sen'jin Village?",a="Once Master Gadrin receives the skull, the necromantic bindings shatter. Minshina's ghostly form appears before his brother and the adventurer, bows in gratitude, and vanishes to rest peacefully with the ancestors.",al={"quest turn in","what happens to minshina","does minshina appear"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is Zalazane and why did he do this?",a="Zalazane was once a respected witch doctor alongside Gadrin and Vol'jin. Driven mad by lust for power, he turned on his tribe, used hexes to mind-control his brothers and sisters, and drove the remaining Darkspear refugees onto the mainland of Durotar.",al={"who is zalazane","why zalazane evil","zalazane lore"},it="threat"},{q="Why can't Gadrin retrieve the skull himself?",a="Master Gadrin is crucial to holding Sen'jin Village together. Between guiding the young Darkspear leadership, advising chieftain Vol'jin, and actively countering Zalazane's expanding hexes across the coast, Gadrin cannot leave the settlement unprotected.",al={"why doesn't gadrin go","gadrin duties"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Master Gadrin want this done?",a="Master Gadrin is tormented by the cries of his brother, Minshina, calling out to him in his dreams. Minshina was slain by the traitorous witch doctor Zalazane on the Echo Isles, but death offered no peace. Zalazane bound Minshina's soul directly to his severed skull, ensnaring him in dark magic. Gadrin cannot bear to leave his brother's spirit condemned to eternal slavery, and he desperately needs someone to break the warlock's hold and grant Minshina eternal rest.",al={"why does gadrin need minshina skull","master gadrin motive","why free minshina"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is Minshina's Skull used for?",a="Minshina's Skull serves as a magical vessel holding the trapped essence of Master Gadrin's murdered brother. Zalazane placed it within a ritual circle of power on the largest of the Echo Isles, using vile sorcery to enslave Minshina's spirit even beyond death. Removing the skull from the dark altar disrupts the warlock's binding magic, allowing Gadrin to finally free his brother's soul once you deliver it safely back to Sen'jin Village.",al={"what is minshina skull","purpose of minshinas skull","minshinas skull item"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For a Darkspear troll, recovering Minshina's skull is a sacred duty to family and tribe, striking a blow against Zalazane's perversion of ancestral voodoo traditions.",["class:Priest"]="Priests understand the deep sanctity of the departed soul and recognize the horror of ritual necromancy that binds a fallen brother from finding eternal peace.",["class:Shaman"]="Shaman revere the spirits of the ancestors; breaking Zalazane's circle to release a tortured soul restores balance between the spirit world and the living.",["faction:Horde"]="Assisting Master Gadrin honors the bond between the new Horde and the Darkspear tribe, proving that an ally's grief is shared by all."},kw={"circle of power","darkspear","echo isles","gadrin","minshina","sen'jin village","skull","voodoo","zalazane"},rel={"npc:master-gadrin","subzone:echo-isles","subzone:sen-jin-village","quest:826","topic:troll","zone:durotar","quest:817","subzone:razor-hill"},m={start="Master Gadrin",level="9",faction="Horde",id=808,ri={"Minshina's Skull"}},src={"Minshina's Skull (quest)"}}
E["quest:812"] = {t="quest",n="Need for a Cure",z="durotar",s="Stranded along the rugged cliffs of northwestern Durotar, the Darkspear troll Rhinag lies poisoned by a venomtail scorpid. With precious little time before the toxin finishes him, he relies on a courier to sprint to Orgrimmar and retrieve a cure from Kor'ghan.",h="Stranded along the rugged cliffs of northwestern Durotar, the Darkspear troll Rhinag lies poisoned by a...",sec={{t="A Scorpid's Sting",b="The arid canyons of Durotar are crawling with venomtail scorpids, aggressive predators whose sting carries a swift, debilitating neurotoxin. Rhinag made the mistake of dropping his guard while battling the beasts near the borderlands. Knowing that the venom coursing through his veins will kill him in under an hour, he is unable to walk the distance to the city gates himself and must place his survival in the hands of whoever passes his remote camp.",sp=0},{t="Secrets in the Shadows",b="Rather than trusting an ordinary apothecary or shaman, Rhinag directs travelers deep beneath Orgrimmar into the shadowy subterranean caverns of the Cleft of Shadow. There dwells Kor'ghan, an enigmatic practitioner familiar with the harsh poisons of Durotar's wastes. Kor'ghan possesses the knowledge required to brew an effective counter-agent, though he rarely gives his aid freely to those who have not proven their mettle.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rhinag?",a="Rhinag is a Darkspear troll adventurer found clinging to life along the northwestern cliffs of Durotar. Stung by a venomtail scorpid, he fears both imminent death and the mockery he would face from his kin in Sen'jin Village if he were to return in such a humbled state.",al={"rhinag lore","who is rhinag","rhinag the troll"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Kor'ghan in the Cleft of Shadow?",a="Kor'ghan makes his home in the Cleft of Shadow, the shadowy cavern beneath Orgrimmar where warlocks, rogues, and other practitioners of dark arts ply their trades away from the eyes of Thrall's honored warriors. His understanding of venomous brews and grueling trials fits the Cleft's subterranean environment.",al={"where is korgan","who is korghan","kor'ghan location"}},{q="Why doesn't Rhinag just seek a shaman or healer in Sen'jin Village?",a="Rhinag admits that his own pride holds him back. He fears that returning to Sen'jin Village in such a careless, venom-stricken condition would earn him nothing but mockery from fellow trolls, preferring instead to seek a discreet remedy from Kor'ghan.",al={"why not go to senjin","why rhinag avoids senjin"},it="why_me"},{q="What happens after Rhinag receives the antidote?",a="Rhinag drinks the antidote and recovers, though his troubles do not end there. Knowing Kor'ghan, the curer will demand that Rhinag prove himself through further grueling trials—slaying boars and harvesting scorpid tails—before he is fully back in the practitioner's good graces.",al={"does rhinag survive","rhinag aftermath"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Where can Rhinag be found?",a="He is located in the rugged bluffs of northwestern Durotar, nestled near the border passes leading westward toward the Barrens.",al={"rhinag location","where is rhinag"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is there such an urgent rush for this cure?",a="The venomtail scorpid's poison is exceptionally potent, giving an untreated victim less than an hour before the venom overwhelms their vital organs.",al={"why is it timed","rhinag poison timer"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Venomtail Antidote for?",a="The antidote counteracts the lethal poison of the venomtail scorpids lurking in northwestern Durotar. Rhinag was stung deeply during a careless skirmish with the beasts, and the toxin courses through his blood rapidly. Without this specific draught brewed by Kor'ghan in Orgrimmar, Rhinag has less than an hour before the venom claims his life.",al={"what is the antidote for","venomtail antidote use","why need venomtail antidote"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Rhinag's dread of returning to Sen'jin Village underscores the harsh pride of the Darkspear tribe, where carelessness in basic wilderness survival invites harsh mockery from kin.",["faction:Horde"]="Durotar's rocky terrain is harsh and unforgiving, serving as an unrelenting trial by fire for newly arrived defenders of Thrall's young realm."},kw={"antidote","cleft of shadow","durotar","kor'ghan","need for a cure","orgrimmar","rhinag","scorpid","venomtail"},rel={"npc:rhinag","npc:kor-ghan","quest:813","subzone:cleft-of-shadow","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Rhinag",level="9",faction="Horde",id=812,ri={"Venomtail Antidote"}},src={"Need for a Cure"}}
E["quest:813"] = {t="quest",n="Finding the Antidote",z="durotar",s="Finding the Antidote is an urgent task undertaken for Kor'ghan in Orgrimmar to brew a cure for the poisoned hunter Rhinag. Facing a strict deadline before the venom proves fatal, an adventurer must gather venomtail poison sacs from scorpids outside the city walls. It highlights the unforgiving nature of Durotar's wildlife and the necessity of wilderness preparation.",h="Finding the Antidote is an urgent task undertaken for Kor'ghan in Orgrimmar to brew a cure for the poisoned...",sec={{t="A Race Against the Venom",b="While hunting throughout Durotar, a Darkspear troll named Rhinag made the perilous mistake of engaging native venomtail scorpids without bringing along an antidote. Stung and succumbing rapidly to their potent toxins, he was forced to send for immediate aid. The task falls to Kor'ghan, an experienced hunter residing in Orgrimmar, to mix a restorative draught before the poison finishes its work.",sp=0},{t="Crafting the Cure",b="Creating an antidote requires harvesting the source of the affliction itself: the venom sacs of mature venomtails lurking outside the gates of Orgrimmar. Kor'ghan notes that chastising Rhinag for his lack of preparation must wait, as every moment counts. Once the sacs are quickly retrieved and brought back into the city, Kor'ghan synthesizes the draught so it can be rushed straight to the dying hunter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rhinag?",a="Rhinag is a Darkspear troll hunter in Durotar who was badly stung by native venomtails while out tracking beasts. Lacking an antidote in the field, he was left incapacitated and reliant on couriers to retrieve a remedy from Orgrimmar before succumbing to the poison.",al={"rhinag lore","who is poisoned","who needs the antidote"},it="people"},{q="Who is Kor'ghan?",a="Kor'ghan is an experienced Darkspear troll hunter based in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow. He understands the natural beasts of Durotar intimately and possesses the alchemical knowledge required to brew an effective counter-venom using raw venomtail poison sacs.",al={"kor'ghan","who is korphan","korgan orgrimmar"},it="identity"},{q="Where do the required venom sacs come from?",a="The poison sacs are harvested directly from venomtail scorpids that prowl the rocky arid plains just outside the primary southern and eastern entrances of Orgrimmar.",al={"where are venomtails","poison sac location","venomtail scorpid sacs"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why is there an active time limit on this task?",a="The urgency is driven by Rhinag's failing health in the field. Because venomtail toxins are exceptionally virulent and fast-acting, Kor'ghan must receive the ingredients and distill the cure before the hunter perishes from systemic poisoning.",al={"why is there a timer","need for a cure timer","timed quest"},it="danger"},{q="What lesson does Kor'ghan emphasize during this hunt?",a="Kor'ghan warns that every hunter must carefully study the habits and lethal dangers of their quarry prior to engaging it. Entering the wilderness without proper preparation or countermeasures is an oversight that can easily cost a warrior their life.",al={"kor'ghan lesson","hunting lesson","kor'ghan advice"}},{q="How does this task fit with 'Need for a Cure'?",a="'Need for a Cure' is the foundational errand that sets the emergency in motion and starts the timer. 'Finding the Antidote' is the intermediary step where the player gathers the raw components for Kor'ghan to brew the finished concoction.",al={"need for a cure connection","prerequisite quest","how does it connect"}},{q="Why does Kor'ghan want this done?",a="Kor'ghan recognizes that Rhinag made a foolish mistake by hunting Durotar's deadliest scorpids unprepared, but he refuses to let one of the Darkspear die for poor judgment. To Kor'ghan, preserving the life of one of their own comes before reprimands. He wants to brew an antidote immediately so Rhinag survives the lethal envenomation.",al={"why help rhinag","kor'ghan motive","why does kor'ghan care"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Venomtail Poison Sac for?",a="Kor'ghan needs the fresh venom sacs to distill an antidote for Rhinag. By extracting the toxic components directly from Durotar's venomtail scorpids, he can concoct a counter-agent potent enough to neutralize the fast-acting venom coursing through the poisoned hunter's blood.",al={"venomtail sac use","what are venomtail poison sacs used for","why gather poison sacs"},it="item",add=true},{q="What are the venomtails near Orgrimmar?",a="Venomtails are predatory scorpids indigenous to the arid wastes of Durotar, prowling the rocky crags outside Orgrimmar. Known among orcish hunters as some of the deadliest creatures in the region, their toxic stings can kill quickly if untreated, making them dangerous beasts that demand caution and respect.",al={"what are venomtails","venomtail scorpid","why kill venomtails"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Kor'ghan serves as a stern reminder to all hunters: knowledge of a beast's venom and carrying appropriate remedies is just as critical as your bow and tracking skills.",["race:Orc"]="Survival in Durotar tests the endurance of the newly settled orcs, demonstrating that even a seasoned scout can fall to the land's native hazards if careless.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde in Durotar looks after its own, ensuring that isolated rangers and scouts on the perimeter can rely on the stronghold of Orgrimmar for aid."},kw={"antidote","durotar","kor'ghan","orgrimmar","poison","rhinag","scorpid","venomtail"},rel={"quest:812","npc:kor-ghan","npc:rhinag","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:cleft-of-shadow"},m={start="Kor'ghan",level="9",faction="Horde",id=813,ri={"Venomtail Poison Sac"}},src={"Finding the Antidote"}}
E["quest:816"] = {t="quest",n="Lost But Not Forgotten",z="durotar",s="Lost But Not Forgotten is a somber quest given by Misha Tor'kren at her homestead northwest of Razor Hill. Desperate for closure, she asks travelers to search the dangerous banks of the Southfury River for any trace of her headstrong son, Kron.",h="Lost But Not Forgotten is a somber quest given by Misha Tor'kren at her homestead northwest of Razor Hill.",sec={{t="A Mother's Dread",b="Northwest of Razor Hill, tucked away in the arid red wastes of Durotar, sits the humble Tor'kren farmstead. Here lives Misha Tor'kren, an orc mother paralyzed by sorrow and anxiety. Days earlier, her son Kron declared he was heading west toward the Southfury River on the border of the Barrens to hunt the river's ferocious crocolisks. Despite her warnings about the deadly beasts, Kron's stubborn pride drove him to storm off to prove his mettle. He has not been seen since.",sp=0},{t="A Grim Confirmation",b="Misha asks passing adventurers to comb the shores of the Southfury River for any sign of Kron's fate, even suggesting they look inside the bellies of the crocolisks. Tragically, her darkest instincts prove true. Slaying the vicious Dreadmaw crocolisks along the water reveals Kron's swallowed amulet. Returning the keepsake to Misha extinguishes any lingering hope that her boy survived, but finally grants a grieving mother the closure she needs to begin mourning.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Misha Tor'kren?",a="Misha Tor'kren is an orcish farm mother living at a secluded homestead northwest of Razor Hill in Durotar. Plagued by grief and worry, she asks wanderers to seek out any trace of her missing son, Kron.",al={"misha torkren","who gives lost but not forgotten","kron mother"},it="identity"},{q="Who was Kron?",a="Kron was Misha Tor'kren's headstrong son. Seeking to prove his strength, he ignored his mother's cautions and left to hunt dangerous crocolisks near the Southfury River, where he met his untimely death.",al={"who is kron","what happened to kron","misha son"},sp=1,it="identity"},{q="Where did Kron go missing?",a="Kron traveled west across Durotar toward the border of the Barrens to hunt along the banks of the Southfury River.",al={"where is kron","where to look for kron","kron location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How do you prove Kron's fate to Misha?",a="You find Kron's swallowed amulet among the remains of Dreadmaw crocolisks prowling the waters of the Southfury River. Bringing this recovered heirloom back to Misha confirms his death.",al={"krons amulet","sign of krons fate","crocolisk stomach"},sp=1,it="item",gp=true},{q="What reward does Misha give?",a="Misha gives you a gift she had originally prepared for Kron to celebrate his triumphant return from the hunt. Unable to bear looking at it after learning of his death, she passes it to the adventurer who brought her closure.",al={"lost but not forgotten reward","misha gift"},sp=1,it="for_you",gp=true},{q="Why did Kron leave in the first place?",a="Kron was driven by stubborn pride and a desire to prove his hunting prowess. When his mother warned him that the crocolisks were far too vicious and dangerous, he grew furious and stormed out to hunt them anyway.",al={"why did kron hunt","kron pride"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Misha Tor'kren want this done?",a="Misha is tormented by not knowing what became of her son. Kron stormed off days ago after an argument, determined to prove himself against dangerous beasts. While she fears the worst, she cannot begin to mourn or find closure until she has definite proof of his fate.",al={"why does misha need help","misha tor'kren motive","why look for kron"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is Kron's Amulet for?",a="Kron's Amulet was a personal possession carried by Misha's son when he left to hunt. Recovered from the stomach of a river beast, it serves as grim, undeniable proof to his mother that Kron was slain along the Southfury River.",al={"krons amulet lore","what is the amulet","kron amulet purpose"},sp=1,it="item",add=true},{q="What are the crocolisks along the Southfury River?",a="Dreadmaw crocolisks are aggressive, powerful reptiles native to the waterways and muddy banks separating Durotar from the Barrens. Vicious and opportunistic, they will devour any prey reckless enough to venture alone into their feeding grounds along the river.",al={"southfury crocolisks","why kill crocolisks","dreadmaw crocolisks"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Kron's fate is a tragic reminder that while pride and martial glory are core to orcish culture, reckless arrogance without respect for dangerous beasts leads to an unheroic death.",["class:Hunter"]="For hunters, Kron serves as a cautionary tale of a tracker who failed to assess the ferocity of his prey and ended up as their meal.",["faction:Horde"]="Life in early Durotar is harsh and unyielding, where everyday families struggle against the unforgiving landscape and the deadly predators that roam its borders."},kw={"amulet","crocolisk","dreadmaw","kron","misha","razor hill","southfury","tor'kren"},rel={"npc:misha-tor-kren","subzone:southfury-river","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","zone:barrens"},m={start="Misha Tor'kren",level="11",faction="Horde",id=816,ri={"Kron's Amulet"}},src={"Lost But Not Forgotten (Classic)"}}
E["quest:817"] = {t="quest",n="Practical Prey",z="durotar",s="Practical Prey is a hunting task given by the leatherworker Vel'rin Fang in Sen'jin Village. Facing a growing population and dwindling stockpiles, the Darkspear tribe must harvest durable tiger hides from the neighboring Echo Isles to craft essential shelters, clothing, and gear.",h="Practical Prey is a hunting task given by the leatherworker Vel'rin Fang in Sen'jin Village.",sec={{t="A Matter of Survival",b="Life along the arid coast of Durotar is harsh, and the Darkspear trolls exiled to Sen'jin Village must make full use of every resource. Tiger pelts are among the most versatile materials available, essential for stitching together tents, heavy blankets, and reinforced armor. As the settlement swells with refugees and returning scouts, stockpiles have worn thin, compelling craftspeople like Vel'rin Fang to commission new hunts.",sp=0},{t="Balance and the Hunt",b="The Darkspear maintain a deliberate relationship with the predators of their territory. Rather than overhunting the native Durotar tigers, the trolls generally allow the prowlers to thrive unmolested, culling them only when tribal stores require replenishment. Venturing across the water to the Echo Isles to stalk these predators serves both practical necessity and a traditional test of patience, discipline, and wilderness skill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Vel'rin Fang?",a="Vel'rin Fang is a Darkspear troll artisan based in Sen'jin Village who works with pelts and leather. He directs hunters to gather essential hides to keep the tribe clothed, sheltered, and equipped.",al={"vel'rin fang","who gives practical prey","velrin fang"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Sen'jin Village need tiger furs?",a="The growing population of Sen'jin Village has strained its existing reserves. Tiger pelts provide durable materials for warm blankets, sturdy tents, and leather armor to protect the villagers against the harsh elements.",al={"why tiger pelts","practical prey purpose","what are furs used for"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the Durotar tigers found?",a="The tigers stalk the wilderness across the Echo Isles, the archipelago situated just off the southeastern coastline of Durotar.",al={"where are the tigers","tiger location","echo isles tigers"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why don't the trolls hunt all the tigers nearby?",a="Vel'rin explains that the Darkspear deliberately balance their needs with the local ecology. They allow the predators to thrive so the population remains sustainable, stepping in to cull them only when the village's material demands outpace their supplies.",al={"why let tigers thrive","culling the flock"}},{q="Is hunting tigers significant to Darkspear culture?",a="Yes. Stalking a tiger is viewed as a rite of patience and cunning. Vel'rin fondly recounts waiting nearly an entire day motionless in the foliage of the Echo Isles before claiming his first major hunting victory.",al={"tiger hunt tradition","first tiger hunt"}},{q="Why must hunters travel to the Echo Isles if Zalazane holds them?",a="While the traitor witch doctor Zalazane and his hexed minions occupy much of the archipelago, the wild beasts of the islands remain abundant. Scavenging and hunting along the outer shores remains a necessary risk for the Darkspear.",al={"tigers on echo isles","why go to echo isles"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the Durotar Tiger Fur used for?",a="The Darkspear craft the furs into essential goods to shelter and sustain their growing settlement. Vel'rin Fang uses the pelts to fashion sturdy leather armor, warm blankets, and weather-resistant tents, ensuring the villagers in Sen'jin Village remain protected and do not freeze as the seasons turn.",al={"durotar tiger fur use","what is tiger fur for","tiger fur practical prey"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the exiled Darkspear, hunting across the Echo Isles is a bitter reminder of their lost home, where providing for the clan requires treading ground stolen by Zalazane.",["class:Hunter"]="Vel'rin's tale of enduring a full day of silent tracking before springing the trap speaks directly to the core virtues of patience and precision taught to all young hunters.",["faction:Horde"]="Supporting the fledgling Darkspear enclave with essential trade goods helps anchor the Horde's southern flank along the Great Sea."},kw={"darkspear","durotar tiger","echo isles","hunting","leatherworking","practical prey","sen'jin village","tiger fur","vel'rin fang"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:echo-isles","zone:durotar","quest:808","subzone:razor-hill"},m={start="Vel'rin Fang",level="8",faction="Horde",id=817,ri={"Durotar Tiger Fur"}},src={"Practical Prey"}}
E["quest:818"] = {t="quest",n="A Solvent Spirit",z="durotar",s="Master Vornal of Sen'jin Village tests fledgling adventurers by demanding reagents to compensate for his failing eyesight. He sends prospective pupils to harvest makrura eyes and crawler mucus along the coast of Durotar. While he scoffs at the idea of taking an apprentice, the task serves as a deliberate trial of patience and resolve.",h="Master Vornal of Sen'jin Village tests fledgling adventurers by demanding reagents to compensate for his...",sec={{t="A Master's Fading Sight",b="Master Vornal sits in Sen'jin Village, burdened by age and diminishing vision. Where primal magic once flowed naturally to his fingertips, he now leans heavily on alchemy to sharpen his perceptions and weave his arts. Despite his mounting physical decline, the stubborn troll refuses to take on an apprentice, claiming neither the Darkspear nor the orcs of Durotar have produced anyone worthy of his tutelage.",sp=0},{t="Testing the Unproven",b="Rather than straightforward instruction, Vornal demands raw materials from the harsh coastline: intact makrura eyes and vials of crawler mucus. Sourcing undamaged eyes from the armored, snapping makrura requires delicate strikes, while gathering sufficient mucus tests an adventurer's willingness to endure tedious, menial work. To Vornal, hunting these littoral beasts is less about the reagents and more about weeding out those who lack focus.",sp=0},{t="A Measure of Will",b="For Master Vornal, time and patience are the ultimate measures of strength. He expects brash youths to give in to frustration or abandon the chore entirely. Returning to Sen'jin Village with pristine ingredients demonstrates not only survival skills along the dangerous reefs of the Echo Isles channel, but the discipline necessary to master the subtle arts of alchemy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Master Vornal?",a="Master Vornal is an elderly troll alchemist and spellcaster dwelling in Sen'jin Village. His physical sight is failing him with age, forcing him to turn to alchemical solvents and brews to perform magic that once came easily.",al={"master vornal","who is vornal","vornal lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Vornal need makrura eyes and crawler mucus?",a="Vornal relies on alchemical concoctions to aid his magic and compensate for his waning eyesight. The mucus and intact makrura eyes serve as reagents for his mixtures, while also functioning as an initiation test for prospective apprentices.",al={"why crawler mucus","why makrura eyes","what does vornal make"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is Vornal so reluctant to teach an apprentice?",a="Vornal possesses high standards and little tolerance for arrogance. He believes no troll or orc has demonstrated the genuine dedication and patience required to learn from him, viewing most aspiring pupils as overly proud and easily discouraged.",al={"vornal apprentice","why no apprentice","is vornal looking for a student"},it="motive"},{q="Where are these creatures found around Sen'jin Village?",a="Crawlers and makrura roam the shallows along Darkspear Strand and inhabit the waterways separating the mainland from the Echo Isles just offshore.",al={"where are makrura","where are crawlers","darkspear strand beasts"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do the makrura eyes need to be intact?",a="Alchemical brews that sharpen perception require undamaged sensory organs. Brutal strikes during combat risk crushing the makrura's delicate eyes, demanding precision and restraint from the hunter.",al={"intact eye","makrura intact eyes","why intact eyes"},it="item"},{q="What lesson is Vornal trying to teach?",a="Vornal believes that patience is the true test of character. By assigning a repetitive and dirty harvesting chore along the surf, he aims to see whether a novice will succumb to weakness and haste or maintain the calm focus of an alchemist.",al={"vornal lesson","meaning of the quest","patience test"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Master Vornal need an adventurer rather than gathering the reagents himself?",a="Master Vornal admits his eyesight is failing him with age, making dangerous fieldwork along the coast ill-advised. More importantly, he uses the chore as a deliberate test. Vornal has long refused to take on an apprentice, believing no troll or orc worthy has crossed his path. By sending you to harvest delicate reagents from hostile coastal wildlife, he measures your patience, strength, and will to see if your deeds match your confidence.",al={"why me vornal","why does vornal need me","why send an adventurer"},it="why_me",add=true},{q="What are the makrura and surf crawlers threatening the Durotar coast?",a="Makrura are aggressive, crustacean humanoids native to the waters and shores of Durotar, while surf crawlers are wild, territorial crabs scuttling along the beaches and shallows near the Echo Isles. Both inhabit the waters off the Darkspear Strand, making the coast perilous for local fishers and gathering. For Master Vornal, however, they are valuable sources of specialized alchemical reagents needed to compensate for his failing senses.",al={"what are makrura","makrura durotar","surf crawlers senjin"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For the Darkspear rebuilding at Sen'jin Village, proving yourself to elder practitioners like Master Vornal is vital to carrying forward the tribe's mystical and alchemical traditions.",["race:Orc"]="Vornal openly doubts whether orcs possess the quiet discipline needed for alchemy, making the task a chance to prove Horde solidarity extends to scholarly patience.",["faction:Horde"]="Coastal Durotar remains perilous for the fledgling Horde; clearing aggressive makrura and surf crawlers secures the fishing shores around Sen'jin Village."},kw={"alchemy","crawler mucus","darkspear strand","durotar","intact makrura eye","makrura","master vornal","sen'jin village"},rel={"npc:master-vornal","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:darkspear-strand","subzone:echo-isles","zone:durotar","topic:troll","quest:99141"},m={start="Master Vornal",level="7",faction="Horde",id=818},src={"A Solvent Spirit"}}
E["quest:823"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Orgnil",z="durotar",s="Report to Orgnil is an early Horde quest dispatched by Master Gadrin from Sen'jin Village. It directs fledgling adventurers northward to Razor Hill to warn Orgnil Soulscar about the insidious reach of the Burning Blade cult. This dispatch helps coordinate Durotar's scattered defense against demonic corruption brewing right in the orcs' homeland.",h="Report to Orgnil is an early Horde quest dispatched by Master Gadrin from Sen'jin Village.",sec={{t="A Coordinated Defense",b="While Sen'jin Village grapples with its own local woes—most notably Zalazane's treachery on the Echo Isles—Master Gadrin recognizes that reports of the Burning Blade cult represent a far wider danger. Whispers of demonic corruption were uncovered in the Valley of Trials, and the Darkspear witch doctor knows these threats cannot be handled in isolation. He dispatches traveling heroes north along the dusty road to Razor Hill, where the local orc authorities maintain a broader watch over Durotar.",sp=0},{t="Orgnil Soulscar",b="Stationed in the military encampment of Razor Hill, Orgnil Soulscar is an orc charged with rooting out domestic evils and safeguarding the central heartlands. When adventurers deliver Gadrin's warning, Orgnil wastes no time integrating the reports from both the Valley of Trials and Sen'jin Village. Recognizing that the shadow of the Burning Blade looms dangerously close, he quickly mobilizes forces to dismantle the cultists before their dark rituals can unseat the young nation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Report to Orgnil?",a="Master Gadrin, the Darkspear witch doctor and spiritual leader residing in Sen'jin Village, gives you this task after you assist the trolls with their initial local struggles.",al={"who gives report to orgnil","where to get report to orgnil","quest giver report to orgnil"},gp=true},{q="Where is Orgnil Soulscar located?",a="Orgnil Soulscar is located in Razor Hill, the fortified settlement situated north of Sen'jin Village in central Durotar.",al={"where is orgnil soulscar","orgnil soulscar location","find orgnil soulscar"},gp=true},{q="Why does Master Gadrin send you to Razor Hill?",a="Master Gadrin realizes that demonic cult activity discovered in the Valley of Trials and around Durotar poses a threat to everyone, not just the trolls. He directs you to Orgnil Soulscar, the orc responsible for policing the region against the Burning Blade.",al={"why report to orgnil","why go to razor hill","purpose of report to orgnil"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Burning Blade mentioned in the quest?",a="The Burning Blade is a treacherous cult of demon worshippers operating in the shadows of Durotar and beyond. Their covert presence in nearby canyons and caves threatens the safety and stability of the nascent Horde.",al={"who are the burning blade","burning blade cult","what is burning blade"},it="threat"},{q="What quest follows Report to Orgnil?",a="Upon turning in the report to Orgnil Soulscar in Razor Hill, he immediately assigns you the quest Dark Storms to investigate and combat the gathering cultist threat.",al={"next quest after report to orgnil","report to orgnil followup","what comes after report to orgnil"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What prerequisite must be completed before receiving this quest?",a="It naturally follows your arrival in Sen'jin Village via the quest Report to Sen'jin Village, linking early Valley of Trials discoveries with the wider Durotar campaign.",al={"prereq report to orgnil","how to unlock report to orgnil","previous quest report to orgnil"},gp=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="This task marks the vital communication and cooperation between the newly allied Darkspear trolls and the orcs of Durotar as they face shared threats.",["race:Troll"]="Though the Darkspear are absorbed in their battle against Zalazane, Master Gadrin demonstrates the trolls' commitment to the Horde by alerting orc leaders to regional dangers.",["race:Orc"]="Orgnil Soulscar represents the frontline defense of your new homeland, ensuring demonic taint does not take root within Durotar's borders."},kw={"burning blade","durotar","master gadrin","orgnil soulscar","razor hill","report to orgnil","sen'jin village"},rel={"npc:master-gadrin","npc:orgnil-soulscar","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","subzone:valley-of-trials"},m={start="Master Gadrin",["end"]="Orgnil Soulscar",level="7",faction="Horde",id=823},src={"Report to Orgnil"}}
E["quest:825"] = {t="quest",n="From The Wreckage....",z="durotar",s="Gar'Thok of Razor Hill directs Horde scouts to scavenge the sunken remains of Grand Admiral Proudmoore's fleet off the Scuttle Coast. By recovering advanced Gnomish Tools from the watery wreckage, the Horde hopes to dissect Alliance engineering and turn that technological advantage to its own benefit.",h="Gar'Thok of Razor Hill directs Horde scouts to scavenge the sunken remains of Grand Admiral Proudmoore's...",sec={{t="Echoes of the Fleet",b="When Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore brought the naval might of Kul Tiras to Kalimdor, his vessels choked the shoreline near Tiragarde Keep. Following his defeat, shattered hulls settled along the Scuttle Coast. While the surviving Kul Tiran soldiers fortify the keep itself, the remnants of their armada lie broken on the shoals, slowly rotting beneath the tide.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Contraptions",b="Orcish warfare traditionally relies on raw strength, iron, and blood, but the Horde recognizes the dangerous edge provided by Alliance ingenuity. Gnomish technicians accompanied the expeditionary fleets, outfitting the Alliance vessels with complex machinery and precision gear. Gar'Thok seeks to recover these submerged tools so the Horde can unravel the mechanics behind them.",sp=0},{t="Destined for Orgrimmar",b="The salvaged tools are not meant to remain gathering dust in Razor Hill. Gar'Thok arranges for them to be transported by caravan directly to Orgrimmar. By reverse-engineering gnomish instruments, Horde craftspeople and tacticians aim to better counter Alliance devices in coming conflicts while bolstering their own emerging industries.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Horde salvaging tools from these wrecks?",a="The Horde wants to understand the advanced technology utilized by the Alliance. Gnomes build intricate machinery for human forces, and by studying their tools, Horde tacticians can figure out how to counter Alliance devices while adopting useful mechanics for their own craftspeople.",al={"why get gnomish tools","why salvage wreck","gar'thok reason for tools"},it="motive"},{q="Whose ships are wrecked off the Scuttle Coast?",a="The sunken vessels belonged to Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's Kul Tiras fleet. After landing on the shores of Durotar to wage war against Thrall's newly founded nation, several ships were destroyed along the coastline just east of Tiragarde Keep.",al={"whose ships are these","who wrecked ships durotar","proudmoore fleet wreckage"},it="origin"},{q="Where do the recovered tools go after Razor Hill?",a="Gar'Thok sends the recovered Gnomish Tools on the next caravan bound for Orgrimmar. There, engineers and craftsmen can study the contraptions thoroughly to help strengthen the capital's defenses and industry.",al={"what happens to tools","where do gnomish tools go","who gets the salvage"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are gnomish tools found on human warships?",a="The gnomes are close allies of the humans within the Grand Alliance, frequently providing naval expeditions with mechanical expertise, siege gear, and precision maintenance tools to keep war fleets operational.",al={"why gnomes with humans","gnomes on proudmoore ships","alliance gnomish tech"},it="item"},{q="What is the Scuttle Coast?",a="The Scuttle Coast is the eastern shoreline of Durotar running past Tiragarde Keep. It is named for the half-submerged and sunken vessels littering the shallow waters following the battles against Proudmoore's expedition.",al={"where is scuttle coast","scuttle coast location","durotar sunken ships area"},it="place"},{q="How does this task relate to the threat at Tiragarde Keep?",a="After clearing out Kul Tiran marines during the assault on Tiragarde Keep, Gar'Thok uses the opportunity to loot the remaining Alliance resources. Stripping the nearby shipwrecks ensures the Horde profits from the enemy's defeat before scavengers or tides take everything.",al={"tiragarde keep connection","vanquish the betrayers link","why do this after tiragarde"},it="conflict"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="For tinkers, the recovery of Gnomish Tools highlights the early technological friction between Alliance mechanical precision and the burgeoning craft industries of the Horde.",["faction:Horde"]="Gar'Thok views every scrap of Alliance metal as a dual prize: knowledge to defeat future invasions and material to help build the nascent nation of Durotar.",["race:Gnome"]="Though small in stature, gnomes leave their mark everywhere the Alliance sails; their sophisticated gear is respected enough by the Horde to warrant dedicated recovery missions."},kw={"durotar","gar'thok","gnomish tools","proudmoore","razor hill","salvage","scuttle coast","tiragarde keep","wreckage"},rel={"npc:gar-thok","quest:784","subzone:scuttle-coast","subzone:tiragarde-keep","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:gnome"},m={start="Gar'Thok",level="8",faction="Horde",id=825,ri={"Gnomish Tools"}},src={"From The Wreckage...."}}
E["quest:826"] = {t="quest",n="Zalazane",z="durotar",s="Master Gadrin of Sen'jin Village tasks Horde champions with traveling to the Echo Isles to end the treachery of the witch doctor Zalazane. Driven mad by dark magic, Zalazane enslaved his fellow tribesmen and seized the Darkspear trolls' rightful home, forcing them into exile on Durotar's coast.",h="Master Gadrin of Sen'jin Village tasks Horde champions with traveling to the Echo Isles to end the treachery...",sec={{t="Betrayal on the Isles",b="When the Darkspear tribe fled their sunken island home and followed Thrall across the Great Sea, they established a settlement on the Echo Isles just off Durotar's southeast coast. Zalazane, a respected and potent witch doctor of the tribe, fell prey to a lust for power. Harnessing mind-enslaving hexes, he subjugated many of his kin and launched a violent uprising. The remaining free Darkspear, led by Vol'jin, were driven from their ancestral camps across the water, forced to build a temporary refuge at Sen'jin Village.",sp=0},{t="A Tribe's Torment",b="Zalazane was not content merely driving the tribe away. From his hilltop redoubt on the central Echo Isle, he regularly sends raiding parties across the channel to snatch more Darkspear and drag them into his thrall. Those afflicted become mindless voodoo and hexed thralls, utterly lost to the tribe. Master Gadrin views this not merely as an occupation of land, but as an existential threat: until Zalazane's severed head is brought before the elders, no Darkspear can ever truly be safe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zalazane?",a="Zalazane was once a prominent witch doctor among the Darkspear trolls. Corrupted by a hunger for dark power, he turned on his brethren, using mind-controlling voodoo to enslave fellow tribespeople and conquer the Echo Isles for himself.",al={"zalazane lore","who is the boss on echo isles","witch doctor zalazane"},it="target"},{q="Why did the Darkspear flee the Echo Isles?",a="Zalazane staged a surprise coup d'etat on the islands, turning brothers and sisters into mindless thralls through foul sorcery. Vol'jin and the surviving free Darkspear lacked the numbers to stand against their enchanted kin and retreated to mainland Durotar, founding Sen'jin Village as a temporary refuge.",al={"why are trolls in sen'jin village","echo isles backstory","how did trolls lose echo isles"},it="history"},{q="What happens to the trolls under Zalazane's control?",a="The trolls under his sway have their minds completely fractured by powerful hexes. They act purely as Zalazane's mindless servants, patrolling the islands and staging mainland raids to capture more victims. Master Gadrin considers them entirely lost to the tribe, leaving execution as the only mercy.",al={"hexed trolls","voodoo trolls","can zalazane's thralls be cured"},it="threat"},{q="Where is Zalazane located?",a="Zalazane makes his lair on the largest island of the Echo Isles chain, just east off the southern coast of Durotar. He patrols between the high summit of the central hill down into the cluster of troll huts directly beneath it.",al={"zalazane location","find zalazane","where is zalazane"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who gives the quest to kill Zalazane?",a="Master Gadrin, the tribal elder situated in Sen'jin Village on Durotar's southern shore, offers the quest after you complete introductory tasks dealing with local threats and arrive from the Valley of Trials.",al={"who starts zalazane","where to get zalazane quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Vol'jin not lead the assault himself?",a="While Vol'jin rules the tribe and coordinates the Darkspear's defense alongside Warchief Thrall in Orgrimmar, Sen'jin Village remains under the local guidance of elders like Master Gadrin. Gadrin coordinates day-to-day survival and enlists capable adventurers to strike back at the treacherous witch doctor.",al={"where is vol'jin","why isn't vol'jin fighting zalazane"},it="leader"},{q="Why does Master Gadrin want Zalazane killed?",a="Zalazane is not content with stealing the Echo Isles; he continually dispatches his enthralled trolls across the water to raid the mainland, enslaving more Darkspear to bolster his ranks. Master Gadrin knows that Sen'jin Village will never be safe as long as the rogue witch doctor lives to torment and abduct their people.",al={"gadrin zalazane why","why kill zalazane","why does master gadrin want this"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is Zalazane's Head for?",a="Master Gadrin demands Zalazane's severed head as undeniable proof of the witch doctor's demise. Only by seeing the head with his own eyes can Gadrin be certain that Zalazane's dark influence is broken and that the Darkspear tribe can finally sleep in peace.",al={"zalazanes head purpose","why bring zalazanes head","zalazane head quest item"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For a Darkspear troll, slaying Zalazane is a deeply personal act of vengeance and duty, punishing the betrayer who stole your people's rightful home and enslaved your brothers.",["faction:Horde"]="The conflict represents one of the young Horde's first major tests of unity, proving that allies from across Durotar will rally to defend the displaced Darkspear tribe.",["class:Shaman"]="Zalazane perverts the spiritual crafts and primal powers practiced by troll shamans and witch doctors, turning binding magics against his own brethren."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","echo isles","hexed troll","master gadrin","sen'jin village","vol'jin","voodoo troll","zalazane"},rel={"npc:master-gadrin","subzone:echo-isles","subzone:sen-jin-village","quest:808","topic:darkspear-tribe","npc:vol-jin","zone:durotar","quest:817"},m={start="Master Gadrin",level="10",faction="Horde",id=826,ri={"Zalazane's Head"}},src={"Zalazane (quest)"}}
E["quest:827"] = {t="quest",n="Skull Rock",z="durotar",s="Assigned by the hermit Margoz, this task directs Horde adventurers into the cavern of Skull Rock just east of Orgrimmar. The cave has been overrun by the Burning Blade cult, who use painful demonic devices to bind themselves to dark magic. Securing these cursed artifacts allows Margoz to study the cult's presence right on the capital's doorstep.",h="Assigned by the hermit Margoz, this task directs Horde adventurers into the cavern of Skull Rock just east of...",sec={{t="A Den of Shadows",b="Skull Rock is a forbidding sea cave nestled along the craggy eastern coastline of Durotar. While seemingly isolated, it sits distressingly close to the mighty gates of Orgrimmar. Rather than housing wild beasts or mere outlaws, the caverns harbor a cell of the Burning Blade—the shadowy demonic cult that has long plagued orcish society. Within these dim tunnels, cultists conduct unholy rituals under the nose of the Warchief's scouts.",sp=0},{t="Demonic Attunement",b="The cultists operating within Skull Rock wear Searing Collars, torcs designed to scorch and brand their own flesh. According to Margoz, this self-inflicted torment is far from mindless cruelty; the searing agony and fel sorcery embedded in the metal serve to attune the wearers to demonic power. By recovering these artifacts, Margoz intends to unravel the exact spells and bindings empowering the Burning Blade's ranks.",sp=0},{t="The Looming Threat",b="Uncovering the secret behind the collars confirms that the cult's presence in Durotar is deliberate and organized. The Burning Blade does not simply operate as scattered brigands; their sorceries run deep and pose an active, insidious threat to the newly established Horde territories. Analyzing the collars sets off a chain of inquiries that leads directly into the shadowy circles of Orgrimmar itself.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Skull Rock located?",a="Skull Rock is a coastal cavern located in northeastern Durotar, tucked along the shoreline east of Orgrimmar and north of Sen'jin Village. It is identified by the craggy cliffside framing the entrance.",al={"skull rock location","where is skull rock","skull rock cave durotar"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is the Burning Blade?",a="The Burning Blade is a dangerous cult of orcs and fel-worshipers dedicated to demonic entities and dark magic. Though the modern Horde broke away from demonic servitude, splinter groups like the Burning Blade continue to practice forbidden rituals to corrupt the Horde from the shadows.",al={"what is burning blade","who are burning blade cultists","burning blade lore"},it="threat"},{q="What do the cultists use the Searing Collars for?",a="The cultists wear the fiery metal bands around their necks to burn their own flesh. Margoz suspects that this ritualistic pain and demonic enchantment allows them to channel and attune themselves to dark fel energies.",al={"searing collars purpose","why wear searing collars","what are searing collars"},it="item"},{q="Who is Margoz?",a="Margoz is an orcish hermit dwelling in a small camp atop the bluffs of Durotar, near Skull Rock. He keeps a watchful eye on cultist movements along the coast and works to dismantle the Burning Blade's dark operations.",al={"who is margoz","margoz durotar","margoz questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Horde allow the cult so close to Orgrimmar?",a="They do not knowingly tolerate it. The cult operates in deep secrecy, hiding within sea caves and desolate ravines where regular patrols rarely reach. Adventurers are sent to investigate precisely because the cultists manage to conceal their footholds until their dark rituals begin.",al={"why is skull rock near orgrimmar","orgrimmar burning blade nearby"},it="conflict"},{q="What happens after Margoz examines the collars?",a="Margoz casts an investigative spell over the gathered collars to divine their origin and magical signature. The magical backlash and revealed secrets urge him to send you into Orgrimmar to seek out others knowledgeable in fel sorcery.",al={"next quest after skull rock","where do collars lead","margoz spell"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Margoz want the Searing Collars?",a="Margoz believes that by burning their flesh with these collars, the cultists attune themselves to demonic forces. He needs a collection of intact collars to study and inspect with his magic, hoping to uncover the dark secrets behind the Burning Blade and expose how deep their demonic corruption runs.",al={"why does margoz need collars","margoz searing collars motive","why collect searing collars"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are you sent against in Skull Rock?",a="You are dispatched against the cultists of the Burning Blade hiding inside Skull Rock, a cavern east of Orgrimmar. They have gathered there beneath the Horde's nose to perform vile rituals, bind themselves to demonic masters, and plot against the safety of Durotar.",al={"who is in skull rock","skull rock enemies","burning blade cultists skull rock"},it="target",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="The Burning Blade represents the dark past the orcs fight every day to leave behind; purging them from the rocks of Durotar is a matter of survival and honor.",["class:Warlock"]="The Searing Collars demonstrate crude but potent fel bindings, offering dark practitioners a glimpse into how the cult channels demonic sacrifice into raw power.",["faction:Horde"]="A demonic cult festering just outside the walls of Orgrimmar threatens the very heart and security of the young Horde."},kw={"burning blade","cultists","demonic","durotar","fel","margoz","orgrimmar","searing collar","skull rock"},rel={"quest:828","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Margoz",level="12",faction="Horde",id=827,ri={"Searing Collar"}},src={"Skull Rock (Classic)"}}
E["quest:828"] = {t="quest",n="Margoz",z="durotar",s="Margoz is a Horde quest tasking adventurers with seeking out an isolated orc shaman who watches over the northern reaches of Durotar. Following the confrontation with fel corruption in the canyon, Orgnil Soulscar directs champions to consult Margoz before assaulting a nearby cultist stronghold. The wise hermit provides crucial counsel regarding the growing shadow cast by the Burning Blade.",h="Margoz is a Horde quest tasking adventurers with seeking out an isolated orc shaman who watches over the...",sec={{t="A Hermit's Vigil",b="After discovering the depths of fel taint at Thunder Ridge, Orgnil Soulscar recognizes that brute strength alone will not suffice to cleanse Durotar. He directs his champions toward Margoz, an experienced orc shaman who keeps a lonely camp in the crags northeast of Razor Hill. Positioned between the jagged heights of Drygulch Ravine and the eastern sea, Margoz keeps watch over dark omens that the bustling warriors of Orgrimmar often overlook.",sp=0},{t="The Threat of Skull Rock",b="Margoz possesses crucial intelligence regarding the Burning Blade's true power base in northern Durotar: a concealed cavern system known as Skull Rock, carved directly into the mountain cliffs outside Orgrimmar's southern gates. By conferring with Margoz, travelers learn that the cultists operate far closer to Thrall's capital than the Warchief's guards realize. The shaman ensures that anyone sent to purge the coven does not walk blindly into demonic ambush.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Margoz?",a="Margoz is a wise orc shaman loyal to the Horde who lives in a secluded camp in northeastern Durotar. He studies the movements of dark magic and monitors the demonic corruption spreading through the region.",al={"margoz lore","who is margoz","margoz npc"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find Margoz?",a="Margoz is camped out in the rugged hills of northeastern Durotar, situated between Drygulch Ravine and the eastern coastline, just southeast of Orgrimmar.",al={"margoz location","find margoz","where is margoz"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Orgnil Soulscar send me to Margoz?",a="Orgnil recognizes that Margoz has spent extensive time studying the local Burning Blade cultists. Before sending you to assault their stronghold, Orgnil wants you to receive Margoz's spiritual wisdom and practical counsel.",al={"why speak with margoz","orgnil soulscar margoz"},it="motive"},{q="What is Skull Rock?",a="Skull Rock is a hidden mountain cave just south of Orgrimmar's eastern walls. It serves as a fortified coven for the Burning Blade, where demon-worshiping cultists conduct rituals right under the Horde's nose.",al={"skull rock lore","what is skull rock"},it="place"},{q="What happens after finding Margoz?",a="Once you report to Margoz, he acknowledges your growing strength and immediately tasks you with entering Skull Rock to slay the cultists and recover their corrupted insignia.",al={"next quest after margoz","margoz follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Is Margoz part of the Burning Blade?",a="No. Margoz is a devoted Horde shaman dedicated to purging demonic influence and keeping young champions grounded on an honorable, uncorrupted path.",al={"is margoz evil","is margoz a cultist"},it="side"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Margoz represents the old, patient wisdom of shamanism, taking watch on the wilderness margins to sense spiritual corruption before it boils over into war.",["faction:Horde"]="Margoz's warning highlights the vulnerability of Orgrimmar, proving that demon cults lurk within striking distance of the Horde's heart.",["race:Orc"]="Meeting Margoz reminds orcish warriors of the lingering temptation of fel power, urging the new generation to walk a pure and honorable path."},kw={"burning blade","drygulch ravine","durotar","margoz","orgnil soulscar","orgrimmar","shaman","skull rock"},rel={"npc:orgnil-soulscar","quest:827","zone:durotar","subzone:drygulch-ravine","zone:orgrimmar"},m={start="Orgnil Soulscar",["end"]="Margoz",level="12",faction="Horde",id=828},src={"Margoz (Classic)"}}
E["quest:830"] = {t="quest",n="The Admiral's Orders",z="durotar",s="Recovered from a locked strongbox atop Tiragarde Keep, these weathered papers bear the personal seal of the late Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore. The recovered orders reveal that the Kul Tiran human garrison along Durotar's coast is far more entrenched and organized than simple shipwreck survivors. Delivering them to Gar'Thok in Razor Hill exposes lingering military plans threatening the fledgling Orc nation.",h="Recovered from a locked strongbox atop Tiragarde Keep, these weathered papers bear the personal seal of the...",sec={{t="A Sealed Legacy",b="Hidden inside a heavy chest on the upper floors of Tiragarde Keep, an aged envelope survives under the watch of Lieutenant Benedict. Sealed with the crest of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore, the parchment outlines direct naval commands issued during Kul Tiras's bloody invasion of Durotar. Even after the Grand Admiral fell at Theramore, his officers maintained their fortifications, clinging tightly to their mission to eradicate the Horde settlement.",sp=0},{t="Alarm in Razor Hill",b="Bringing the recovered documents to Gar'Thok, commander of Razor Hill, confirms the worst fears of the local defense force. The human forces entrenched along the eastern shoreline are not aimless castaways, but an established beachhead awaiting reinforcement. Gar'Thok immediately recognizes that dismantling the Tiragarde command structure is an urgent matter of survival for Durotar.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where are the Admiral's Orders found?",a="The orders are found inside an Aged Envelope stored within a locked chest on the third floor of Tiragarde Keep in Durotar. To open the chest, you must first defeat Lieutenant Benedict on the second floor to claim his key.",al={"orders location","where is aged envelope","find admirals orders"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Who was Admiral Proudmoore?",a="Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore was the ruler of Kul Tiras and supreme commander of the Alliance naval fleet during the Second War. Refusing to believe orcs could ever live peacefully, he sailed to Kalimdor to wage a war of extermination against Durotar before meeting his demise at Theramore.",al={"who is the admiral","daelin proudmoore lore","who issued orders"},it="identity"},{q="Why are Kul Tiran soldiers still in Tiragarde Keep?",a="When Daelin Proudmoore invaded Durotar, he established fortified coastal footholds like Tiragarde Keep. Following his defeat, surviving officers and marines under Lieutenant Benedict held their posts, determined to continue his campaign against the Horde.",al={"why are humans in durotar","tiragarde keep soldiers","kul tiras in durotar"},it="why_here"},{q="Why is Gar'Thok so concerned about these orders?",a="As military commander of Razor Hill, Gar'Thok is tasked with safeguarding central Durotar. Discovering organized naval orders proves that Tiragarde Keep poses an active, calculated military threat to the orcish homeland rather than disorganized, stranded survivors.",al={"gar'thok reaction","why does garthok care"},it="danger"},{q="Who holds the key to the Admiral's chest?",a="Lieutenant Benedict, the commanding Kul Tiran officer situated on the second level of Tiragarde Keep, carries the key required to unlock the strongbox containing the Aged Envelope.",al={"benedict key","who drops key"},it="in_charge",gp=true},{q="What happens after giving the orders to Gar'Thok?",a="Upon inspecting the orders, Gar'Thok recognizes the immediate strategic danger and commands further action to neutralize the remaining human leadership and dismantle their operations in Durotar.",al={"admirals orders follow up","next quest"},it="next_step"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Uncovering Proudmoore's orders proves that the Alliance presence on Durotar's shores was an orchestrated campaign of extermination, reinforcing why the Horde must defend its newfound home with vigilance.",["race:Orc"]="For the orcs fighting to build a future in Durotar, these documents are a stark reminder of Daelin Proudmoore's relentless hatred and the remnants who still seek their destruction."},kw={"admirals orders","aged envelope","daelin proudmoore","gar'thok","kul tiras","lieutenant benedict","razor hill","tiragarde keep"},rel={"npc:gar-thok","subzone:tiragarde-keep","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar"},m={start="Aged Envelope",["end"]="Gar'Thok",level="7",faction="Horde",id=830},src={"The Admiral's Orders"}}
E["quest:832"] = {t="quest",n="Burning Shadows",z="durotar",s="Recovered from the Burning Blade cultist Gazz'uz in the depths of Skull Rock, this mysterious glowing pendant whispers urgent warnings into the bearer's mind. The voice specifically threatens Gazz'uz with the wrath of Neeru Fireblade, an orc warlock residing in Orgrimmar.",h="Recovered from the Burning Blade cultist Gazz'uz in the depths of Skull Rock, this mysterious glowing pendant...",sec={{t="A Voice in the Stone",b="Upon slaying Gazz'uz deep within Skull Rock, an ominous pendant known as the Eye of Burning Shadow is retrieved from his remains. Rather than being an inert magical trinket, the stone vibrates with psychic communication. A demanding voice speaks directly into the mind of anyone holding it, demanding reports from Gazz'uz and warning him that his clandestine operations east of Orgrimmar have been compromised.",sp=0},{t="A Curious Threat",b="What catches any loyal Horde scout off guard is the voice's desperate ultimatum: respond, or Neeru Fireblade will be notified to hunt Gazz'uz down with swift brutality. Neeru Fireblade dwells openly in Orgrimmar's Cleft of Shadow, ostensibly practicing dark arts under Thrall's strict oversight. Delivering the talisman to Neeru prompts feigned surprise and curiosity, with the warlock marveling that his name was invoked as a boogeyman against the cult.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Eye of Burning Shadow?",a="The Eye of Burning Shadow is an enchanted pendant dropped by the Burning Blade leader Gazz'uz inside Skull Rock. It acts as a two-way telepathic relay between cult operatives and their unseen masters.",al={"eye of burning shadow","what is this pendant","gazz'uz eye"},it="item"},{q="Who is speaking through the pendant?",a="An unidentified superior within the Shadow Council or Burning Blade hierarchy is attempting to contact Gazz'uz, unaware that the cultist has already been slain in Skull Rock.",al={"who spoke to me","voice in the pendant","who talks through eye"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the voice threaten Gazz'uz with Neeru Fireblade?",a="The voice claims Neeru Fireblade will descend upon Gazz'uz with brutal force if he fails to report. On the surface, this frames Neeru as a feared loyal enforcer of Thrall, though the familiarity between the cult and Neeru suggests deeper undercurrents.",al={"why mention neeru","neeru fireblade threat","neeru connection"},it="purpose"},{q="Where do I take the Eye of Burning Shadow?",a="Bring the pendant to Neeru Fireblade, who can be found hovering over cauldrons and tomes deep within the Cleft of Shadow in Orgrimmar.",al={"where to turn in burning shadows","where is neeru fireblade"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="How does Neeru Fireblade react when given the eye?",a="Neeru claims ignorance, acting baffled that cultists would invoke his name. He takes the pendant ostensibly to study its magic and uncover why the Burning Blade bears a name so similar to his own clan identity.",al={"neeru reaction","what does neeru say"},sp=1},{q="Where is Gazz'uz located?",a="Gazz'uz lurks at the deepest point of Skull Rock, a cavern hidden along the crags on Durotar's eastern coastline just east of Orgrimmar.",al={"where is gazz'uz","gazz'uz location","skull rock boss"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the voice in the Eye of Burning Shadow want a report?",a="The voice whispering through the pendant is trying to contact Gazz'uz, a Burning Blade leader in Skull Rock. News has reached the cult hierarchy that their hidden enclave has been discovered by the Horde, and the unseen commander urgently seeks to rally Gazz'uz to prepare defenses before an inevitable assault wipes out their foothold.",al={"why does the pendant speak","why eye of burning shadow report","eye of burning shadow voice motive"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="For a warlock training in the Cleft of Shadow, witnessing another practitioner's name invoked by the Burning Blade serves as a stark reminder of how thin the line is between state-sanctioned fel study and open treason.",["faction:Horde"]="Uncovering whispers between cultists right outside the capital's gates reveals that the demonic corruption of the Old Horde still festers uncomfortably close to Durotar's heart.",["race:Orc"]="Orcs who fought alongside Thrall to purge the Legion's taint view the Burning Blade's presence in Durotar as an intolerable desecration of their new homeland."},kw={"burning blade","burning shadows","cleft of shadow","durotar","eye of burning shadow","gazz'uz","neeru fireblade","orgrimmar","skull rock"},rel={"quest:827","quest:829","zone:durotar"},m={start="Eye of Burning Shadow",["end"]="Neeru Fireblade",level="12",faction="Horde",id=832},src={"Burning Shadows"}}
E["quest:834"] = {t="quest",n="Winds in the Desert",z="durotar",s="Rezlak, an engineer contracted from Gazlowe's operations, needs help recovering crucial construction materials stolen by harpies in Durotar. A caravan bound for Orgrimmar was ambushed in Razorwind Canyon, scattering sacks of supplies among the cliffs.",h="Rezlak, an engineer contracted from Gazlowe's operations, needs help recovering crucial construction...",sec={{t="A Goblin on a Deadline",b="Rezlak was sent directly by Chief Engineer Gazlowe of Ratchet to assist the Horde with their ambitious construction projects across Durotar. Building fortifications in harsh, barren terrain is demanding enough without logistical disasters, but Rezlak's shipments keep disappearing before they reach the building sites. Without essential cargo, all progress grinds to a halt, leaving the irritable goblin supervisor stranded with nothing to build with.",sp=0},{t="Ambush in the Canyon",b="The latest vital supply run promised to Rezlak was intercepted by the Dustwind harpies inhabiting Razorwind Canyon. These winged scavengers roost along the high ravine cuts flanking the road between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar, swooping down on unsuspecting wagons. Instead of eating or destroying the freight, the harpies hoard the crates and sacks around their nesting sites, leaving the cargo intact for anyone brave enough to fight into their territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rezlak?",a="Rezlak is a goblin worker employed by Gazlowe, the boss of Ratchet. Gazlowe sent him to Durotar to assist the orcs with their ongoing construction efforts outside the gates of Orgrimmar.",al={"rezlak","who is rezlak","who gave this quest"},it="identity"},{q="Why are goblins helping build in Durotar?",a="Gazlowe and the Steamwheedle Cartel have an ongoing commercial and engineering partnership with Warchief Thrall. Goblin engineers and machines helped lay out the foundations of Orgrimmar, and Gazlowe continues to supply contracted labor and materials to the Horde.",al={"why are goblins helping orcs","gazlowe durotar","goblin horde cooperation"},it="purpose"},{q="Where did the supplies come from?",a="The supplies were transported via caravan through Durotar to support regional construction efforts, likely shipped overland through the Southfury river routes or brought north from merchant vessels docked at Ratchet.",al={"where are the supplies from","caravan origin"},it="origin"},{q="What are the harpies doing in Durotar?",a="The Dustwind harpies are aggressive, predatory scavengers that infest the cliffs and ravines of central Durotar. They harass travelers, raid trade lines through Razorwind Canyon, and scavenge anything bright or useful for their nests.",al={"why harpies in durotar","dustwind harpies lore","razorwind harpies"},it="threat"},{q="Where is Razorwind Canyon located?",a="Razorwind Canyon branches directly off the main southern gorge that connects Orgrimmar to Razor Hill. Ravines cut into both the eastern and western cliff walls, forming high roosts where the Dustwind harpies stash their stolen cargo.",al={"razorwind canyon location","where to find supplies","sacks of supplies location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why didn't the orc guards protect the caravan?",a="The young Horde's military resources are stretched thin across Durotar, dealing with threats from Centaur raiders, Bristleback quilboar, and Kul Tiras marines along the coast. Guard detachments are often too small to fend off sudden aerial strikes from cliff-dwelling harpies.",al={"why failed caravan","durotar security","orc caravans"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Rezlak want this done?",a="Rezlak was sent directly by Gazlowe to oversee engineering and construction work for the Horde in Durotar. Without these essential materials, his work has ground to a complete standstill, leaving him empty-handed and frustrated. He cannot fulfill his contract or finish his assigned projects until the cargo is recovered.",al={"rezlak motive","why does rezlak need supplies","why does rezlak care"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Sack of Supplies for?",a="These sacks contain engineering and building provisions intended for Horde construction across Durotar. Rezlak and his crew require them to complete their building projects for the orcs, but the material was scattered through Razorwind Canyon when Dustwind harpies intercepted the delivery caravan.",al={"sack of supplies use","what are the sacks of supplies","rezlak supply sacks"},it="item",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Every shipment lost to canyon beasts threatens the rapid expansion and fortification of the Horde's stronghold in Durotar.",["race:Orc"]="Orcs rely on goblin expertise and foreign supplies to turn the harsh, dry soil of Durotar into a fortified homeland.",["profession:Engineering"]="Rezlak represents the pragmatic ingenuity of Steamwheedle engineers, who care far more about keeping blueprints and deliveries on schedule than local wildlife troubles."},kw={"caravan","durotar","dustwind harpies","gazlowe","orgrimmar","ratchet","razorwind canyon","rezlak","supplies"},rel={"npc:rezlak","quest:835","subzone:razorwind-canyon","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:razor-hill"},m={start="Rezlak",faction="Horde",id=834,ri={"Sack of Supplies"}},src={"Winds in the Desert"}}
E["quest:835"] = {t="quest",n="Securing the Lines",z="durotar",s="Securing the Lines is a task given by Rezlak near Razorwind Canyon to protect vital goblin supply routes running through Durotar. Harpies roosting in Drygulch Ravine continuously intercept and plunder supply caravans, prompting the frustrated goblin to hire muscle to clear them out.",h="Securing the Lines is a task given by Rezlak near Razorwind Canyon to protect vital goblin supply routes...",sec={{t="A Route Plagued by Harpies",b="The dry valleys of Durotar are harsh enough without aggressive harpies swooping down on unsuspecting travelers. Operating on behalf of his boss Gazlowe, the goblin Rezlak watches over regional supply operations. Unfortunately, the Dustwind harpies inhabiting Drygulch Ravine have turned Razorwind Canyon into a hazard, routinely raiding caravans and seizing incoming shipments before they can reach their destinations.",sp=0},{t="Business and Bloodshed",b="Rezlak lives by the goblin maxim that you can get anything done if the price is right. Rather than personally entering the canyon, he hires adventurers to break the back of the roost by eliminating Dustwind Savages and Dustwind Storm Witches. Clearing these harpies keeps the trade corridors open, secures incoming shipments of engineering gadgets, and points helpful travelers toward greater opportunities in Ratchet.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Rezlak working for?",a="Rezlak works for Gazlowe, the chief engineer and boss of the neutral goblin port town of Ratchet. Gazlowe oversees extensive commerce and infrastructure projects throughout Durotar and the Barrens.",al={"rezlak boss","who does rezlak work for","rezlak employer"},it="ties"},{q="Why are the harpies attacking caravans?",a="The Dustwind harpies have established a substantial roost in Drygulch Ravine, which cuts directly alongside the primary transit routes of Razorwind Canyon. They fiercely attack any intruders and plunder the wagons and goods passing nearby.",al={"why do harpies attack","dustwind harpies motive","why drygulch ravine"},it="conflict"},{q="Where is Drygulch Ravine located?",a="Drygulch Ravine is nestled deep within the eastern reaches of Razorwind Canyon in northern Durotar, carved out into the arid crimson hills.",al={"drygulch ravine location","where is drygulch ravine","how to find drygulch"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after helping Rezlak?",a="With the Dustwind harpies culled and his supply route secured, Rezlak points adventurers toward Ratchet across the border in the Barrens, encouraging them to seek out Gazlowe for further profitable contracts.",al={"after securing the lines","rezlak follow up","what next after rezlak"},it="next_step"},{q="Why doesn't the Horde handle the harpies instead of goblins?",a="While the Horde maintains outposts in Durotar, their resources are stretched thin managing centaur, quilboar, and internal settlement needs. Goblin merchants like Rezlak often find it quicker and cheaper to hire independent adventurers directly to protect their private enterprise.",al={"why goblins hiring","why isn't orgrimmar handling this","horde and harpies"},it="why_me"},{q="What kinds of harpies reside in Drygulch Ravine?",a="The roost primarily consists of feral Dustwind Savages who attack in close combat and Dustwind Storm Witches who command wind and lightning against trespassing caravans.",al={"harpy types","dustwind harpy types","drygulch enemies"},it="target"},{q="Why does Rezlak want the harpies cleared out?",a="Rezlak is responsible for keeping cargo moving through Durotar, but the Dustwind harpies in Drygulch Ravine have been ambushing and raiding his supply caravans. Every lost wagon costs gold, delays vital materials, and jeopardizes upcoming shipments—including some specialized equipment he is personally awaiting from Ratchet.",al={"rezlak motive","why kill drygulch harpies","rezlak caravan problem"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Safeguarding Rezlak's shipments keeps cutting-edge goblin components moving from Ratchet into the hands of local tinkerers.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the harpy menace in eastern Razorwind Canyon preserves the flow of goods and reinforcements between Durotar's frontier outposts and the coastal trade hubs."},kw={"drygulch ravine","dustwind savage","dustwind storm witch","gazlowe","ratchet","razorwind canyon","rezlak","securing the lines"},rel={"npc:rezlak","subzone:drygulch-ravine","subzone:razorwind-canyon","subzone:ratchet","zone:durotar"},m={start="Rezlak",level="11",id=835},src={"Securing the Lines (Classic)"}}
E["quest:8358"] = {t="quest",n="Incoming Gumdrop",z="durotar",s="Incoming Gumdrop is a seasonal Hallow's End quest in Durotar where Kali Remik trades a sweet treat for a bit of playful humiliation. In order to obtain a Darkspear Gumdrop for an ailing orphan, adventurers must play along and mimic the sounds and motion of a steam train.",h="Incoming Gumdrop is a seasonal Hallow's End quest in Durotar where Kali Remik trades a sweet treat for a bit...",sec={{t="A Troll's Price for Candy",b="During the festive season of Hallow's End, heroes across Durotar collect traditional holiday sweets on behalf of a sick child in need of cheer. While Kali Remik in Sen'jin Village is happy to contribute a chewy Darkspear Gumdrop to the cause, she refuses to part with her confection without demanding the customary trick first.",sp=0},{t="Playing the Fool",b="Rather than demanding combat or dangerous trials, Kali asks visiting champions to drop their dignity and perform a train impression on command. Embracing the lighthearted revelry of Hallow's End, seasoned warriors and grim warlocks alike must make chugging engine noises and whistle blows to secure the sweet prize.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kali Remik?",a="Kali Remik is a Darkspear troll resident located in Sen'jin Village along the southern coast of Durotar. During Hallow's End, she holds the Darkspear Gumdrops needed for the holiday festivities.",al={"kali remik","who gives quest","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why do I need to make a train noise?",a="Hallow's End is built around tricks and treats. Even though the candy is collected for an ailing child, Kali insists on enjoying the holiday tradition by asking you to perform an absurd train impression before handing over the sweet.",al={"why train","train emote","what does she want"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Darkspear Gumdrop used for?",a="The Darkspear Gumdrop is one of several regional confections gathered across Horde lands to complete a festive assortment of treats intended to lift the spirits of a sick orphan.",al={"what does gumdrop do","darkspear gumdrop use","hallows end treats for spoops"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where does this quest fit into the holiday?",a="This quest is only available during the annual Hallow's End celebration, serving as one of the regional errand quests that send Horde players visiting various settlements.",al={"is this seasonal","hallows end quest","holiday event"},it="history"},{q="Can Alliance players complete this quest?",a="No, this quest is exclusive to the Horde. Kali Remik is situated in the Darkspear settlement of Sen'jin Village in Durotar and will not offer treats to Alliance adventurers.",al={"alliance version","can alliance do this"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Where is Kali Remik located?",a="She can be found in Sen'jin Village, situated along the southern coast of Durotar, south of Razor Hill.",al={"kali remik location","where is kali","durotar location"},it="place",gp=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="Visiting Kali Remik in Sen'jin Village gives Darkspear trolls a chance to share holiday revelry on their home shores before heading out to other Horde settlements.",["faction:Horde"]="Gathering seasonal sweets across Durotar, Mulgore, and Tirisfal Glades brings together the disparate cultures of the Horde in a shared, lighthearted tradition."},kw={"darkspear gumdrop","durotar","hallow's end","incoming gumdrop","kali remik","sen'jin village","spoops","train emote"},rel={"npc:kali-remik","zone:durotar"},m={start="Kali Remik",faction="Horde",id=8358},src={"Incoming Gumdrop (Horde)"}}
E["quest:8670"] = {t="quest",n="Runetotem the Elder",z="durotar",s="Runetotem the Elder is an encounter with an ancestral spirit during the Lunar Festival in Durotar. Found standing within Razor Hill under a pillar of heavenly light, she offers blessings and festival tokens to travelers who come to pay their respects to the past.",h="Runetotem the Elder is an encounter with an ancestral spirit during the Lunar Festival in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Spirit in Razor Hill",b="During the Lunar Festival, the spirits of ancient elders materialize across Azeroth to commune with the living. Elder Runetotem manifests inside Razor Hill, positioned just past the southern entrance. Bathed in a clear beam of starlight from above, she watches over the orcish settlement and welcomes adventurers who step aside from their travels to acknowledge the wisdom of those who came before.",sp=0},{t="Guidance Across the Lands",b="Approaching Elder Runetotem does more than honor an individual ancestor. In exchange for your homage, she rewards you with a festival token of fortune and shares word of where other spirits may be found, pointing wanderers toward Elder Darkhorn and Elder High Mountain across the continent.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Elder Runetotem located?",a="Elder Runetotem is located inside Razor Hill in Durotar, positioned just to the right immediately after entering through the southern entrance.",al={"elder runetotem location","where is elder runetotem","find elder runetotem"}},{q="Why is there a beam of light shining on her?",a="Like all the ancestral spirits who manifest during the Lunar Festival, Elder Runetotem is highlighted by a celestial shaft of light shining down from the sky, marking her as an honored elder.",al={"light beam elder","why is runetotem glowing","elder beam of light"}},{q="What do you receive for honoring Elder Runetotem?",a="Honoring Elder Runetotem rewards a festival token commemorating your respect for the ancestors, and she offers directions toward other wandering spirits like Elder Darkhorn and Elder High Mountain.",al={"runetotem reward","what does runetotem give","elder runetotem turn in"}},{q="Can Alliance players visit Elder Runetotem?",a="The Lunar Festival elders welcome homage from all mortals regardless of allegiance, though Razor Hill is a heavily guarded Horde outpost, making it perilous for Alliance travelers to approach her.",al={"alliance elder runetotem","can alliance talk to runetotem"}},{q="Which elders does Runetotem mention?",a="Elder Runetotem shares lore on the whereabouts of fellow ancestors, specifically giving guidance on finding Elder Darkhorn and Elder High Mountain.",al={"runetotem directions","who does runetotem tell you to find"}},{q="Is Elder Runetotem a living tauren or a ghost?",a="Elder Runetotem is an ancestral spirit who appears during the Lunar Festival season to bestow blessings upon those whose spirits burn with life.",al={"is runetotem dead","is runetotem a ghost"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Meeting a spirit bearing the revered Runetotem family name outside the plains of Mulgore serves as a potent reminder of your people's deep spiritual heritage across Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="Standing right inside the walls of Razor Hill, Elder Runetotem is one of the safest and most convenient ancestors for young Horde travelers to honor early in their journeys.",["faction:Alliance"]="Paying homage to Elder Runetotem requires slipping deep behind enemy lines into the heart of Durotar without drawing the wrath of Razor Hill's orcish guards."},kw={"durotar","elder darkhorn","elder high mountain","elder runetotem","lunar festival","razor hill","runetotem"},rel={"npc:elder-runetotem","subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:light"},m={start="Elder Runetotem",id=8670},src={"Runetotem the Elder"}}
E["quest:96652"] = {t="quest",n="The Adventurer",z="durotar",s="While exploring the rugged wastes of Durotar, travelers stumble across a plain, discarded journal chronicling the quiet travels of an unfamiliar figure. Its pages speak warmly of outdoor life and camping out under the stars, awaiting delivery to Brakk near Razor Hill.",h="While exploring the rugged wastes of Durotar, travelers stumble across a plain, discarded journal chronicling...",sec={{t="A Wanderer's Notes",b="Durotar is a harsh land where survival usually takes precedence over leisurely travel, making the discovery of a wandering chronicler's book an unusual sight. Found lying unattended in the red dirt, the modest journal contains the musings and exploits of someone completely unknown to the common heroes of the Horde. Rather than detailing bloody battles or grand campaigns, its pages dwell on the humble joys of sleeping under the open sky and making camp in the wild.",sp=0},{t="Delivery to Brakk",b="Whoever penned the entries left enough of an impression—or connection—to point toward Brakk, an orc stationed near the settlement of Razor Hill. Carrying the personal effects of lost travelers to local scouts and encampment hands is often the only way scattered wanderers are ever reunited with their belongings, or at least remembered by those watching the dusty roads.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the lost journal?",a="The book is remarkably ordinary, filled with day-to-day entries detailing the quiet exploits of an obscure adventurer. In particular, it repeatedly highlights the simple joys and fun of setting up camp in the wilderness.",al={"what does the journal say","lost journal contents","journal text"},it="item"},{q="Who wrote the journal?",a="The identity of the author remains unnamed in the recovered pages; it describes the life and travels of someone you have never heard of before encountering the book in the wilds.",al={"who is the adventurer","author of lost journal","who wrote this book"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Brakk?",a="Brakk is an orc located near Razor Hill in central Durotar who takes delivery of the lost journal.",al={"brakk razor hill","who is brakk","where is brakk"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the journal found?",a="The plain journal is discovered lying abandoned amidst the terrain of Durotar, waiting for a passing Horde traveler to recover it.",al={"where do i find the journal","lost journal location","adventurer quest start"},gp=true},{q="Why does Brakk care about this journal?",a="Positioned just outside Razor Hill along Durotar's active trails, Brakk serves as a key contact point for items, reports, and wandering business passing through central Horde territory.",al={"why bring it to brakk","brakk purpose","brakk journal"},it="motive"},{q="Is the adventurer who wrote it in danger?",a="The recovered pages give no indication of foul play, merely containing fond recollections of camping out. However, leaving behind one's travel journal in the red dust of Durotar suggests the writer either dropped it by mistake or moved on unexpectedly.",al={"is the author alive","did the adventurer die","lost adventurer status"},it="threat"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The arid trails of Durotar are walked by many new recruits; retrieving lost property and reporting back to scouts near Razor Hill helps maintain order along the central frontier.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunters who spend their lives surviving off the land can easily relate to the journal's fond, repeated entries on the joys of wilderness camping."},kw={"adventurer","brakk","camping","durotar","journal","lost journal","razor hill"},rel={"zone:durotar","subzone:razor-hill"},m={start="Object #654925",["end"]="Brakk",level="6",faction="Horde",id=96652},src={"The Adventurer (Durotar)"},fv=true}
E["quest:97279"] = {t="quest",n="Wayward Weapons",z="durotar",s="Wayward Weapons is an early training task in the Valley of Trials, issued by the overseer Gornek. With young warriors arriving in droves to serve the Horde, armaments are running thin. To prove their discipline and support the encampment, recruits scour the scrubland to salvage gear abandoned by less capable predecessors.",h="Wayward Weapons is an early training task in the Valley of Trials, issued by the overseer Gornek.",sec={{t="Arming the New Blood",b="The Valley of Trials is the forge where raw recruits are tested against the harsh red wastes of Durotar. With countless aspirants stepping forward to pledge their blades to the warchief, the encampment's weapon stocks are strained to their limit. Weaponsmith Kzan Thornslash struggles to keep pace with demand, especially when early lessons prove fatal or humiliating for the unready.",sp=0},{t="A Test of Resourcefulness",b="Overseer Gornek turns this shortage into a practical trial. Rather than wasting new metal, he directs fresh arrivals to recover the abandoned blades and blunt training weapons left behind by failed recruits who fell or fled in the dust. Delivering these recovered arms to Kzan allows the smith to repair and temper them for the next wave, teaching novitiates that survival in the Horde demands scavenging as well as swinging steel.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there so many abandoned training weapons lying around?",a="Not every hopeful who steps into the Valley of Trials possesses the strength or resolve required by the Horde. Faint-hearted or careless recruits routinely drop their gear in panic or fall to the local boars and scorpids, leaving their issued armaments scattered across the dirt.",al={"why are weapons on the ground","abandoned weapons durotar","failed recruits weapons"},it="origin"},{q="Who is Kzan Thornslash?",a="Kzan Thornslash is the resident weaponsmith stationed inside the Den in the Valley of Trials. He is responsible for outfitting new recruits, repairing battered training gear, and maintaining the Horde's martial supplies in the starting valley.",al={"kzan thornslash lore","who is kzan","weaponsmith kzan"},it="identity"},{q="Who issues this task?",a="Gornek, the overseer standing outside the Den, assigns this task. He watches over incoming aspirants, judging their basic potential and dispatching them to handle immediate needs around the trial grounds.",al={"who gives wayward weapons","gornek quest"},gp=true},{q="What will Kzan do with these salvaged weapons?",a="Kzan repairs, sharpens, and restores the battered practice weapons. Because resources in Durotar are sparse and recruits arrive constantly, salvaged iron and wood must be reused to train the next wave.",al={"what happens to the training weapons","repairing weapons kzan"},it="next_step"},{q="Where is this quest taking place?",a="It takes place in the Valley of Trials, an isolated canyon in southern Durotar where young orcs and Darkspear trolls begin their path as warriors for the Horde.",al={"valley of trials location","where is wayward weapons"},it="place"},{q="Why doesn't the Horde just forge entirely new weapons?",a="Durotar is a rugged, arid land with limited easily accessible iron deposits, and the young Horde cannot afford waste. Recycling practice blades from washouts ensures that raw metal is conserved for frontline troops.",al={"why salvage weapons","durotar metal shortage"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Gornek want the abandoned weapons collected?",a="A fresh influx of recruits into the Valley of Trials has strained the camp's armory. The weaponsmith, Kzan, is running short on practice gear, and Gornek needs to keep supplies moving to train the next wave. Asking you to scour the grounds solves the shortage while letting Gornek test your diligence and survival skills out in the valley.",al={"gornek motive","why does gornek want weapons","why collect abandoned training weapons"},it="motive",add=true},{q="What is the Abandoned Training Weapon for?",a="These crude blades and bludgeons were carried by past recruits who proved unworthy or perished before finishing their trials. Left scattered in the dirt, they are still sturdy enough to be restored. Once you deliver them to Kzan Thornslash, he repairs and sharpens them so future recruits have gear to fight with.",al={"abandoned training weapon use","what are abandoned weapons used for","purpose of abandoned training weapon"},it="item",add=true},{q="Why does Gornek send a recruit instead of guards?",a="The trial grounds exist to separate capable warriors from the weak. Sending seasoned guards to clean up after failed recruits wastes veteran manpower, whereas sending you serves a dual purpose: you cut your teeth hunting boars in the wilds while proving you can follow orders and maintain the camp's necessities.",al={"why not send guards","why me gornek","why send recruits for weapons"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["profession:Blacksmithing"]="Every scrap of metal counts in Durotar. Helping Kzan recover ruined gear reflects the smith's duty to reclaim iron and rework battered edges into usable tools of war.",["class:Warrior"]="Respecting weapons is foundational for any warrior. Recovering the arms tossed aside by failed recruits emphasizes discipline and self-reliance before true combat even begins.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde endures in Durotar through grit and resourcefulness, refusing to squander arms even when discarded by those unfit to carry them."},kw={"durotar","gornek","kzan thornslash","recruits","salvage","the den","training weapons","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:gornek","npc:kzan-thornslash","quest:1089","zone:durotar"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Kzan Thornslash",level="2",faction="Horde",id=97279,ri={"Abandoned Training Weapon"}},src={"Wayward Weapons"},fv=true}
E["quest:98576"] = {t="quest",n="Glyphic Parchment",z="durotar",s="Glyphic Parchment is an introductory summons directed to aspiring mages in the Valley of Trials. Delivered via Gornek, the written missive guides fledglings toward Mai'ah, a troll mage trainer stationed near the Den, to begin their arcane discipline.",h="Glyphic Parchment is an introductory summons directed to aspiring mages in the Valley of Trials.",sec={{t="A Summons to Study",b="While new recruits prove their physical mettle against the local pests of Durotar, those possessing an affinity for the arcane cannot rely purely on brute force. Gornek passes along a written notice scribed with runes, instructing novice spellcasters to seek out Mai'ah, who oversees the early magical instruction of the Horde's newest recruits.",sp=0},{t="The Way of the Arcane",b="Stationed just outside the entrance to the Den, Mai'ah tempers the ambitions of young spellweavers. Rather than recklessly hurling raw sorcery, she emphasizes patience, timing, and calculated intellect. Under her guidance, novices learn to view the cosmos as delicate strands to weave rather than an unruly tempest to unleash.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends the Glyphic Parchment?",a="The parchment is sent by Mai'ah, the mage trainer positioned near the Den in the Valley of Trials. Gornek holds the letter and hands it over once a fledgling mage begins their trials.",al={"who wrote glyphic parchment","who sent this","parchment author"}},{q="Where can Mai'ah be found?",a="Mai'ah is located in the Valley of Trials in Durotar, stationed right outside the entrance to the Den alongside other class mentors.",al={"where is maiah","mai'ah location","find mai'ah"}},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="It serves to introduce novice mages to their class trainer. Speaking with Mai'ah initiates your formal instruction in arcane arts, opening access to new spells and foundational training.",al={"what does glyphic parchment do","why do this quest","quest goal"}},{q="What is Mai'ah's philosophy on magic?",a="Mai'ah teaches that arcane magic requires intellect, restraint, and calculated patience. Rather than acting impulsively, an effective mage watches carefully and strikes at the precise moment with the appropriate response.",al={"what does maiah teach","mai'ah lore"}},{q="Why is a troll training mages in the Valley of Trials?",a="The Valley of Trials welcomes both young orcs and Darkspear trolls entering the Horde's ranks. Darkspear spellcasters like Mai'ah lend their wisdom and mastery of cosmic forces to tutor emerging practitioners.",al={"why troll mage","trolls and arcane","troll trainer in orc area"}},{q="Who delivers the parchment to the player?",a="Gornek, the primary trial overseer situated at the central camp of the Valley of Trials, delivers the parchment when you return to him during your early tasks.",al={"who gives glyphic parchment","gornek quest"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="This missive marks your formal recognition as a student of the arcane, directing you to Mai'ah to begin learning and expanding your spellbook.",["faction:Horde"]="Mentorship in the Valley of Trials ensures that even volatile arts like the arcane are cultivated with discipline to strengthen the Horde's future.",["race:Troll"]="Mai'ah represents the Darkspear's growing arcane traditions, offering her cosmic insights to guide both fellow trolls and allied recruits."},kw={"arcane","durotar","glyphic parchment","gornek","mage","mai'ah","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:mai-ah","npc:gornek","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","quest:1089"},m={start="Gornek",["end"]="Mai'ah",level="1",faction="Horde",id=98576},src={"Glyphic Parchment (Forever)"},fv=true}
E["quest:cutting-teeth"] = {t="quest",n="Cutting Teeth",z="durotar",s="Cutting Teeth is the initial trial given to fresh recruits arriving in the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Overseer Gornek assigns newcomers to thin the mottled boar population roaming the nearby cactus dirt farms, testing their basic combat readiness. Surviving this modest rite of passage proves an aspiring warrior or spellcaster possesses the backbone necessary to serve the Horde.",h="Cutting Teeth is the initial trial given to fresh recruits arriving in the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Measure of Backbone",b="The Valley of Trials does not indulge delusions of grandeur. While young recruits might dream of pursuing massive beasts across the Barrens or winning glory on battlefields, overseer Gornek begins their evaluation with far more grounded matters. Thinning the mottled boars around the valley farms serves as a baseline assessment: it ensures a recruit knows how to wield a weapon or cast a spell, can handle wild aggression, and possesses enough sense to survive their very first skirmish.",sp=0},{t="Taming the Red Dust",b="Beyond testing raw recruits, culling the mottled boars serves a practical domestic purpose for the red desert settlement. The feral swine roam the dirt farms north and northeast of the camp, rooting through cactus patches and threatening the scarce supplies cultivated in Durotar's harsh soil. By sending aspirants to clear them out, the camp keeps local pests in check while forging young orcs and trolls into competent defenders of the new nation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Gornek send recruits after boars instead of bigger beasts?",a="As Gornek himself admits, recruits are far more useful to the Horde alive than dead. While the Barrens hold mighty kodo and predators, sending an untried rookie against them would simply result in needless slaughter. Boars provide a reliable test of basic fighting ability without throwing away lives.",al={"why boars","why kill boars","gornek boar hunt"},it="motive"},{q="Where are the mottled boars located?",a="Mottled boars root through the scrub and dirt farms situated to the north and northeast of the central clearing in the Valley of Trials.",al={"boar location","where are boars","find mottled boars"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the significance of the phrase 'cutting teeth'?",a="The phrase refers to gaining one's very first practical experience in a craft or calling. For an aspiring defender of the Horde, it marks the transition from training dummies and idle talk to drawing blood in actual survival.",al={"what does cutting teeth mean","meaning of cutting teeth"},it="name"},{q="Who assigns this trial?",a="The task is assigned by Gornek, an overseer stationed at the heart of the Valley of Trials who evaluates and directs new recruits entering Durotar's training grounds.",al={"who gives cutting teeth","quest giver cutting teeth","gornek trial"},it="in_charge"},{q="Does this complete the training in the Valley of Trials?",a="No. Gornek warns that fighting boars is merely a warm-up. Completing this task leads immediately to more hazardous challenges, including confronting humanoid intruders and gathering vital valley resources.",al={"is this the last quest","what comes after cutting teeth"},it="next_step"},{q="Why do the boars pose a problem in the valley?",a="The feral boars aggressively wander the local dirt farms and brush patches, endangering workers and consuming the few resilient crops, like cactus fruit, that sustain the encampment.",al={"boar problem","valley of trials boars"},it="danger"},{q="Why does Gornek send me instead of the seasoned warriors?",a="The Valley of Trials exists solely to weed out the weak and forge green recruits into capable defenders of the Horde. Seasoned veterans have far more pressing duties safeguarding Durotar and fortifying Orgrimmar. For an untested novice, battling the local wildlife proves you possess the mettle and backbone required before anyone entrusts you with real military responsibility.",al={"why send me cutting teeth","why does gornek need recruits","why not seasoned guards"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Every young champion stepping into Durotar must start from the very dirt, proving that the Horde's future rests on blood and sweat rather than unearned prestige.",["race:Orc"]="Orcish culture values practical survival and martial honor above all else; even humble boar-culling acts as a sacred first step into adulthood and the service of Thrall's new nation.",["race:Troll"]="As the Darkspear tribe rebuilds alongside their orc allies, young troll scouts and mystics must also prove their self-reliance amidst Durotar's unforgiving predators."},kw={"barrens","boars","cutting teeth","durotar","gornek","horde","mottled boar","recruits","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:gornek","quest:your-place-in-the-world","zone:durotar","zone:barrens"},m={start="Gornek",faction="Horde",id=788,ri={"Mottled Boar"}},src={"Cutting Teeth"}}
E["quest:galgar-s-cactus-apple-surprise"] = {t="quest",n="Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise",z="durotar",s="Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise is a straightforward errand undertaken by young warriors and novices in the sun-baked Valley of Trials. Seeking relief from Durotar's punishing heat, the orc Galgar enlists travelers to gather wild cactus apples so he can prepare his famed refreshing treat. The task teaches fresh recruits how to forage and survive in an arid land.",h="Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise is a straightforward errand undertaken by young warriors and novices in the...",sec={{t="Surviving the Red Wastes",b="The crimson dirt of the Valley of Trials is notoriously merciless. Between rigorous combat drills and fierce trials against native beasts, exhaustion and dehydration set in quickly. For young orcs and Darkspear trolls taking their first steps as defenders of the Horde, learning how to subsist off the land is just as vital as swinging an axe. Cacti growing throughout the valley yield ripe, water-rich apples that offer immediate respite from the oppressive desert sun.",sp=0},{t="A Valley Delicacy",b="Galgar, stationed inside the training grounds, has turned local foraging into an art. His famous 'Cactus Apple Surprise' is legendary among the denizens of the valley for its ability to cool a person down faster than a plunge into river water. By contracting eager recruits to harvest the prickly fruit from nearby cacti, Galgar keeps his kitchen stocked while ensuring new wanderers never set out into Durotar with an empty belly.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Galgar?",a="Galgar is an orc resident stationed within the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Rather than overseeing formal combat drills, he spends his time preparing cooling provisions and delicacies like his famous Cactus Apple Surprise to help recruits withstand the desert heat.",al={"who is galgar","galgar lore","who gives cactus apple quest"},it="identity"},{q="What is Cactus Apple Surprise?",a="It is a popular local confection and refreshing snack crafted by Galgar using fresh cactus apples collected from wild desert cacti. It is prized among trainees for providing fast relief and vital hydration under the blistering sun of Durotar.",al={"cactus apple surprise food","what is the surprise","galgars recipe"},it="item"},{q="Where are cactus apples found?",a="Cactus apples grow in small clusters on the ground at the base of flowering cacti scattered throughout the red cliffs and canyons of the Valley of Trials.",al={"where are cactus apples","find cactus apples","how to get cactus apples"},gp=true},{q="Why does Galgar ask recruits to gather them?",a="The Valley of Trials is intensely hot, and Galgar is unable to leave his post to wander the desert himself. He offers to share portions of his prized treat with any passing novice willing to venture out into the brush and gather the raw ingredients for him.",al={"why gather cactus apples","why does galgar need apples"},it="why_me"},{q="Does this quest connect to a larger storyline?",a="No. It is a standalone foraging task designed to acquaint new recruits with gathering resources from the local environment while they complete their initial trials for the Horde.",al={"is there a chain","cactus apple follow up","what comes after cactus apple surprise"}},{q="Why is foraging important in the Valley of Trials?",a="Durotar is a harsh and unforgiving land carved out of arid rock and scrub. Horde leaders believe that surviving on Durotar's sparse natural resources is essential training for anyone wishing to endure the trials of the wider world.",al={"why forage","survival in durotar"}},{q="Why does Galgar want cactus apples gathered?",a="The sweltering heat of the Valley of Trials is relentless, and Galgar is looking for relief. He craves his signature recipe, cactus apple surprise, which he claims is the best treat to cool someone off under the blazing Durotar sun. By gathering the fruit, you allow him to prepare a batch to beat the heat and share the refreshing food with you.",al={"why does galgar want apples","galgar motive","why gather cactus apples"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Galgar's dish highlights the resourcefulness required to produce nourishing food and refreshing treats out of tough, prickly desert flora.",["race:Orc"]="Settling Durotar meant adapting to an arid landscape, and simple dishes made from native cacti represent the orcs' practical ability to thrive in their new home.",["faction:Horde"]="Every fresh recruit who steps foot into the Valley of Trials quickly learns that enduring Durotar's punishing sun is as much a part of their training as combat."},kw={"cactus","cactus apple","durotar","food","foraging","galgar","horde","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:galgar","subzone:valley-of-trials","quest:cutting-teeth","zone:durotar"},m={start="Galgar",faction="Horde",id=4402,ri={"Cactus Apple"}},src={"Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise"}}
E["quest:lazy-peons"] = {t="quest",n="Lazy Peons",z="durotar",s="Foreman Thazz'ril is fed up with the Valley of Trials' workforce falling asleep on the job. Entrusted with his weighted blackjack, young recruits are tasked with roaming the valley to discipline sleeping peons and ensure vital lumber continues flowing to Durotar's settlements.",h="Foreman Thazz'ril is fed up with the Valley of Trials' workforce falling asleep on the job.",sec={{t="Slacking in the Sun",b="Building a new home in the arid plains of Durotar demands vast amounts of timber, stone, and sheer physical toil. Much of that burden falls squarely upon the peon caste—orcs who lack martial prowess but form the industrious backbone of the Horde. Unfortunately for Foreman Thazz'ril, the baking heat and grueling labor of the Valley of Trials make it easy for these laborers to slip off to shady trees for unauthorized naps.",sp=0},{t="A Swift Wake-Up Call",b="Rather than allowing productivity to grind to a halt, Foreman Thazz'ril uses a rather direct management strategy: the Foreman's Blackjack. Entrusting incoming Horde recruits with this blunt disciplinary tool, he sends them across the valley floor to crack sleeping workers over the head. Startled awake, the dazed peons hastily return to chopping wood, reminded that idle hands have no place in the survival of Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the peons falling asleep?",a="Gathering heavy lumber under Durotar's punishing sun is brutal, exhausting work. Without a supervisor breathing down their necks, peons regularly slip away beneath the shade of large trees to rest.",al={"why are peons lazy","sleeping peons","peons sleeping on job"}},{q="Who is Foreman Thazz'ril?",a="Foreman Thazz'ril is an orc overseer stationed in the Valley of Trials. He manages the labor crews responsible for harvesting lumber and supplies needed for fledgling Horde construction.",al={"thazzril","who gives lazy peons","thazz'ril"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Foreman's Blackjack?",a="It is a heavy leather sap used by Foreman Thazz'ril to discipline slacking workers. A swift blow upside the head is just enough to wake a sleeping peon without causing permanent injury.",al={"blackjack","peon club","blackjack tool"},it="item"},{q="What role do peons have in the Horde?",a="Peons represent the laboring class of orcish society. While physically stout, they are considered unfit for military warfare, serving instead as builders, miners, and woodcutters to fuel the Horde's war machine and settlements.",al={"orc peons role","what are peons","peon caste"},it="people"},{q="Where do I find the sleeping peons?",a="They can be found throughout the Valley of Trials, both north and south of the Den. Look under the wide canopies of trees where the workers retreat to find shade.",al={"lazy peon locations","where are lazy peons","find sleeping peons"},it="target",gp=true},{q="What happens after the peons are awakened?",a="Once you return the blackjack to Foreman Thazz'ril, he sends you on another chore: recovering his lost mining pick from deep within a nearby cave.",al={"after lazy peons","what follows lazy peons","next quest after peons"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Foreman Thazz'ril want the peons awakened?",a="Foreman Thazz'ril is responsible for keeping the Valley of Trials supplied with timber, and construction demands constant labor. When the peons slack off and nap under the trees, lumber gathering grinds to a halt. Thazz'ril needs them disciplined and actively chopping wood so the Horde's encampment can maintain its supplies and fortifications.",al={"thazzril motive","why wake the peons","why hit peons"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Who are you sent after?",a="You are sent after the Valley of Trials' peons, the lowest-ranking laborers of the Horde assigned to harvest lumber from the valley's trees. Rather than working, many have abandoned their axes to nap in the shade. While essential to the valley's supply lines, their notorious lack of motivation requires a harsh reminder to keep them at their posts.",al={"who do I hit","who are lazy peons","target of lazy peons"},it="target",add=true},{q="Why does Foreman Thazz'ril need you to discipline the peons?",a="Foreman Thazz'ril oversees multiple operations across the Valley of Trials and cannot leave his post to scour every copse of trees for shirkers. With the valley's warrior trainers and guards busy training recruits or guarding against local threats, handing a blackjack to a capable young recruit like you is the quickest way to enforce order among the laborers.",al={"why me lazy peons","why doesn't thazzril hit them","why not guards"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For young orcs coming of age, disciplining your own kin's labor force is an early lesson in the harsh realities and practical discipline required to carve a nation out of the wilderness.",["race:Troll"]="Darkspear trolls training alongside their allies witness firsthand the peculiar combination of brute strength and managerial exasperation that defines orcish construction.",["faction:Horde"]="Every outpost in Durotar relies on timber harvested by these peons, making basic workforce discipline a matter of collective survival."},kw={"blackjack","durotar","foreman thazz'ril","lazy peons","lumber","peon","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:foreman-thazz-ril","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","quest:1089"},m={start="Foreman Thazz'ril",faction="Horde",id=5441},src={"Lazy Peons"}}
E["quest:sarkoth"] = {t="quest",n="Sarkoth",z="durotar",s="High on a southern plateau in the Valley of Trials lurks Sarkoth, an unusually vicious scorpid whose venomous sting has brought a young Darkspear hunter to death's door. Lying wounded beneath a tree, the dying troll Hana'zua pleads for a passing warrior to slay the beast and retrieve its mangled claw to salvage his honor.",h="High on a southern plateau in the Valley of Trials lurks Sarkoth, an unusually vicious scorpid whose venomous...",sec={{t="A Matter of Honor",b="The trials in the Valley are meant to temper aspiring warriors of the Horde, but the harsh desert rarely offers second chances. While stalking the valley's venomous native fauna, the young troll scout Hana'zua encountered a scorpid far larger and deadlier than the rest. Though he managed to strike a heavy blow that mangled one of its pincers, Sarkoth's tail plunged into Hana'zua's chest, leaving him bleeding out in the dry red dirt. Facing what seems to be the end of his life, his only remaining wish is that the beast does not outlive him.",sp=0},{t="The Plateau Terror",b="Sarkoth prowls the elevated mesa overlooking the southern reaches of the Valley of Trials. Marked by the shattered claw from Hana'zua's strike, the monstrous beast dominates the high ridge, striking at anyone bold enough to climb the rocky path. Slaying the creature and returning its scarred claw to Hana'zua offers the wounded scout some bitter solace—a tangible proof that his last desperate strike softened the monster enough to be brought down.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Sarkoth?",a="Sarkoth prowls atop the high plateau south of where Hana'zua lies wounded. To reach him, look for a dirt ramp winding up the canyon walls, where the large scorpid wanders the ridge.",al={"sarkoth location","where is sarkoth","how to get to sarkoth"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Hana'zua?",a="Hana'zua is a young Darkspear troll undertaking his hunting trials in the Valley of Trials. Mauled and envenomed by Sarkoth, he lies slumped beneath a tree, desperately seeking an adventurer to avenge him before he succumbs to his wounds.",al={"hanazua","dying troll valley of trials","quest giver sarkoth"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Hana'zua want Sarkoth's claw?",a="During their fight, Hana'zua landed a fierce strike that shattered Sarkoth's claw before he was stung. Retrieving that mangled claw serves as proof of the monster's death and gives Hana'zua pride knowing his final fight was not completely in vain.",al={"why sarkoths claw","mangled claw proof","hanazua honor"},it="item"},{q="Does Hana'zua die from the venom?",a="Though gravely wounded and bitter about his perceived failures, bringing down Sarkoth gives Hana'zua enough hope to send you to the Den in search of medical aid rather than resigning himself to death beneath the tree.",al={"does hanazua survive","hanazua fate","is hanazua dead"},sp=1,it="history"},{q="What makes Sarkoth different from other scorpids?",a="Unlike the common scorpid workers skittering across the lower valley floor, Sarkoth is significantly larger, more aggressive, and bears the distinctive marks of recent battle, including a damaged claw.",al={"sarkoth differences","why is sarkoth special","scorpid boss durotar"},it="target"},{q="What is the follow-up task after killing Sarkoth?",a="Once you return Sarkoth's claw to Hana'zua, he urges you to hurry back to the Den to inform the camp leaders of his plight and bring assistance before his venomous wound proves fatal.",al={"quest after sarkoth","next step hanazua","back to the den quest"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Hana'zua want Sarkoth dead?",a="Hana'zua believes his life is fading beneath the scorpid's venom, and he refuses to die in disgrace. His father always told him he would amount to little, and perishing alone in the dirt without slaying his opponent would prove those bitter words true. Avenging his defeat is his final chance to uphold his warrior's honor and ensure his last enemy does not outlive him.",al={"why kill sarkoth","hanazua motive","why does hanazua want sarkoth dead"},it="motive",add=true},{q="Why can't Hana'zua kill Sarkoth himself?",a="Hana'zua is severely crippled and bleeding out beneath a tree. In their clash atop the southern plateau, he managed to strike Sarkoth's claw, but the beast drove its stinger deep into his chest. Poisoned and too weak to stand or return to the Den for aid, he relies entirely on you to finish the hunt before his life seeps away.",al={"why does hanazua need me","why can't hanazua fight","why me sarkoth"},it="why_me",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For a fellow Darkspear, answering Hana'zua's plea is a solemn duty of kinship, ensuring a tribe member's honorable stand is recognized rather than lost to the sands of Durotar.",["race:Orc"]="Orcs understand the agony of dying without victory; avenging Hana'zua grants an untested scout the warrior's satisfaction of seeing his foe brought low.",["faction:Horde"]="In the unforgiving environment of the Valley of Trials, coming to the aid of fallen comrades defines the communal strength Thrall's Horde strives to foster."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","hana'zua","mangled claw","sarkoth","scorpid","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:hana-zua","quest:804","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},m={start="Hana'zua",faction="Horde",id=790,ri={"Sarkoth's Mangled Claw"}},src={"Sarkoth (quest)"}}
E["quest:your-place-in-the-world"] = {t="quest",n="Your Place In The World",z="durotar",s="This simple rite of passage marks the moment an aspiring young champion steps forward to serve the Horde. Given by Kaltunk in the Valley of Trials, it sends untested recruits straight to Gornek to begin their basic combat training. It represents the very first step toward earning honor and survival in the harsh lands of Durotar.",h="This simple rite of passage marks the moment an aspiring young champion steps forward to serve the Horde.",sec={{t="Coming of Age in Durotar",b="In the arid canyon of the Valley of Trials, young orcs and darkspear trolls must prove their worth before they can ever set foot in the wider world. Life under Warchief Thrall demands strength, vigilance, and discipline. Kaltunk evaluates every eager recruit, temperately dampening their dreams of wrestling demons and dragons to redirect them toward realistic duties. Every legendary hero of the Horde begins right here, learning humility before claiming glory.",sp=0},{t="Reporting to Gornek",b="Just steps away from Kaltunk sits Gornek, a gruff veteran stationed beside the camp fire. Gornek evaluates the fresh arrivals with a skeptical eye, often grumbling about the meager stock arriving at the camp. Yet, it is his responsibility to harden these fledgling fighters through rigorous trials, beginning with culling the local vermin threatening the encampment's supplies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="It serves as the introductory rite of passage for young recruits in the Valley of Trials. It officially enlists you into service under the Horde and introduces you to Gornek, who assigns your first real combat duties.",al={"why do this quest","first horde quest","what is your place in the world"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Kaltunk?",a="Kaltunk is an orc overseer stationed at the entrance of the Valley of Trials. He greets coming-of-age recruits, looks them over, and directs them toward proper trainers and leadership within the camp.",al={"kaltunk role","who gives this quest"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Gornek?",a="Gornek is an experienced Horde trainer seated near the campfire in the Valley of Trials. He is tasked with testing incoming recruits and hardening them into capable soldiers before allowing them to leave the canyon.",al={"gornek role","where is gornek"},it="identity"},{q="Where does this quest lead next?",a="Reporting to Gornek leads immediately into the trial 'Cutting Teeth', where recruits are sent into the dirt to cull mottled boars and prove their basic martial prowess.",al={"what quest is next","next after your place in the world"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are recruits kept in the Valley of Trials?",a="The Valley of Trials is a secluded, protected canyon within Durotar designed to train, evaluate, and weed out recruits before they encounter the far deadlier beasts, quillboar, and enemy scouts of the wider territory.",al={"why valley of trials","why start here"},it="why_here"},{q="Does this quest differ between orcs and trolls?",a="Both young orcs and Darkspear trolls begin their training together in the Valley of Trials and receive this same introductory call to arms from Kaltunk.",al={"troll intro quest","orc intro quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Kaltunk send you to Gornek?",a="You have finally come of age to fight for the Horde and win glory for Warchief Thrall. While Kaltunk sees potential in you, he knows eager recruits often dream of slaying dragons before learning the basics. He directs you to Gornek so you can be tested with duties appropriate for a novice, ensuring you survive long enough to become a true asset to the Valley.",al={"why does kaltunk want this done","kaltunk motive","why kaltunk sends you"},it="motive",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Every young Horde recruit in Durotar must prove they possess the grit to defend their fledgling nation before taking up arms in the Warchief's name.",["race:Orc"]="For orcs, reaching age and reporting for duty in the Valley of Trials is a deeply cultural milestone centered on personal honor and martial readiness.",["race:Troll"]="Having settled in Durotar alongside their orc allies, the Darkspear trolls train alongside their brethren here to forge unity and mutual survival."},kw={"cutting teeth","durotar","gornek","horde","kaltunk","recruits","valley of trials","warchief"},rel={"npc:kaltunk","npc:gornek","quest:cutting-teeth","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},m={start="Kaltunk",["end"]="Gornek",faction="Horde",id=4641},src={"Your Place In The World"}}
E["subzone:bladefist-bay"] = {t="subzone",n="Bladefist Bay",z="durotar",s="Bladefist Bay is the rugged stretch of coast lining eastern Durotar just outside the gates of Orgrimmar. Named in honor of Kargath Bladefist, the bay serves as a natural harbor facing the Great Sea, shadowed by craggy bluffs and the nearby southern shores of Azshara.",h="Bladefist Bay is the rugged stretch of coast lining eastern Durotar just outside the gates of Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Harbor on the Great Sea",b="Stretching along the northeastern edge of Durotar, Bladefist Bay opens directly into the vast waters of the Great Sea. Flanked by rocky cliffs and treacherous surf, it functions as a primary maritime threshold for the Horde capital of Orgrimmar. The tides frequently deposit driftwood, ocean refuse, and flotsam onto the coastline, earning it a reputation among locals as a natural collection point for ocean debris. Directly north, the ancient red cliffs and ruins of Azshara loom across the water, making the bay a vital maritime boundary for Durotar.",sp=0},{t="Shadow of the Shattered Hand",b="The bay honors Kargath Bladefist, the famed chieftain of the Shattered Hand clan who severed his own hand to replace it with a blade during the old Horde's trials on Draenor. The proximity of the bay to places like Skull Rock—where cultists and hidden rogue networks operate in the shadows—echoes the fierce and ruthless legacy of the clan whose chieftain gave the waters their name.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bladefist Bay named after?",a="The bay is named after Kargath Bladefist, the legendary chieftain of the Shattered Hand clan known for replacing his severed hand with a lethal scythe blade.",al={"who is bladefist","bladefist namesake","kargath bladefist bay"},it="name"},{q="Where is Bladefist Bay located?",a="It lies along the northeastern coast of Durotar, directly east of Orgrimmar's main gates and south across the water from Azshara.",al={"bladefist bay location","where is bladefist bay","how to get to bladefist bay"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What threats lurk around Bladefist Bay?",a="The shoreline is situated right beside Skull Rock, a cavern infamous for harboring warlocks, demons, and members of the sinister Burning Blade cult.",al={"bladefist bay danger","dangers at bladefist bay","enemies in bladefist bay"},it="danger"},{q="Why is the bay sometimes called a midden heap?",a="Ocean currents from the Great Sea routinely sweep sea detritus, wreckage, and rubble straight onto its shores, giving it a reputation as a dumping ground for the sea's refuse.",al={"midden heap","bladefist flotsam","ocean trash bay"}},{q="What is Bladefist Bay?",a="Bladefist Bay is a coastal inlet of the Great Sea along the northeastern shores of Durotar, sitting east of Orgrimmar and south of Azshara. It serves as an eastern anchorage and docking area for Horde vessels navigating the open waters, though its shores are often littered with sea debris and flotsam carried in by the ocean tides.",al={"what is bladefist bay","bladefist bay durotar","about bladefist bay"},it="place",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="The bay bears the proud and brutal name of Kargath Bladefist, serving as a reminder of the trials of the Shattered Hand clan on Draenor.",["class:Rogue"]="The Shattered Hand operates within Orgrimmar's shadows as the Horde's guild of thieves and assassins, giving this coast quiet resonance for covert operatives."},kw={"bay","bladefist","durotar","great sea","kargath","orgrimmar","shattered hand","skull rock"},rel={"zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","quest:827","zone:azshara","quest:1858"},src={"Bladefist Bay"}}
E["subzone:burning-blade-coven"] = {t="subzone",n="Burning Blade Coven",z="durotar",s="Tucked into the northern cliffs of the Valley of Trials, the Burning Blade Coven is an infested cave network threatening the Horde's newest recruits. Corrupted cultists and summoned demons lurk within, turning an old mineral cavern into a staging ground for dark magic right on Durotar's doorstep.",h="Tucked into the northern cliffs of the Valley of Trials, the Burning Blade Coven is an infested cave network...",sec={{t="A Shadow Over the Proving Grounds",b="The dusty red mountains rimming the Valley of Trials were once simply a testing wilderness for young orcs and Darkspear trolls taking their first steps in service to the Horde. In recent days, however, dark rituals have taken hold of the northern caves. Imps and lesser fiends spill from the cavern mouth, stirring chaos and threatening recruits. Led by the shadowy warlock Yarrog Baneshadow, the Burning Blade cult has entrenched itself deep inside, turning what was once a routine training ground into an active battleground against demonic corruption.",sp=0},{t="Corruption in the Rocks",b="Before the demons took root, the caves attracted the attention of local overseers hoping to harvest raw materials for the settlement. Foreman Thazz'ril ventured deep inside on a mineral survey, only to be driven out in haste, leaving valuable equipment behind as the cultists made their presence known. Now, driving back Baneshadow's coven serves as the ultimate proving trial for aspiring warriors, rogues, and spellcasters before they are deemed ready to venture out into greater Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Burning Blade Coven located?",a="The cave is embedded in the high red rock ridges directly along the northern edge of the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",al={"coven location","where is burning blade coven","valley cave location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who leads the cultists here?",a="The coven is led by a warlock named Yarrog Baneshadow, who directs the local rituals and commands the summoned demons.",al={"coven leader","who leads burning blade coven","yarrog"},it="leader"},{q="What kinds of enemies lurk inside?",a="The cave is infested with rogue imps, minor demonic servitors, and mortal acolytes aligned with the shadowy Burning Blade cult.",al={"what mobs are in the cave","coven monsters","demons in valley of trials"},it="threat"},{q="Why do new recruits go into the cave?",a="Braving the dark depths of the cave, recovering lost tools like Foreman Thazz'ril's pick, and slaying Yarrog Baneshadow serves as the final initiation rite for new orc and troll adventurers before leaving the valley.",al={"why go to coven","coven purpose","coven final test"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Burning Blade Coven?",a="The Burning Blade Coven is a dark cavern carved into the northern red mountains of the Valley of Trials. Once an abandoned cave surveyed for minerals, it has been claimed by demonic cultists who threaten the very proving grounds of the Horde.",al={"what is burning blade coven","burning blade coven lore","what is this cave"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is the Burning Blade Coven dangerous?",a="It poses a severe threat to the Valley of Trials. Mischievous imps and dangerous demons have begun spilling out from the cave's mouth, and sinister members of the Burning Blade lurk within its depths. Venturing into the cavern to face these perils serves as the final trial for aspiring orc and troll adventurers before they are permitted to journey into Durotar.",al={"is burning blade coven dangerous","how dangerous is the coven","is it safe here"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Burning Blade Coven?",a="The cavern takes its name from the Burning Blade cult whose members have secretly occupied its tunnels. They use its secluded hollows as a coven to consort with demonic entities and plot against the young Horde right under the noses of its mentors.",al={"why is it called burning blade coven","burning blade coven name origin","who named burning blade coven"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The demonic imps and dark rituals here are an early, cautionary glimpse into what happens when fel power is wielded recklessly in open defiance of the Horde.",["race:Orc"]="The presence of the Burning Blade cult so close to the Valley of Trials is an intolerable insult to Thrall's new Horde and a stark reminder of the demon worship the orcs fought to leave behind."},kw={"burning blade coven","demon","durotar","imps","thazz'ril","valley of trials","yarrog baneshadow"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Burning Blade Coven"}}
E["subzone:darkspear-strand"] = {t="subzone",n="Darkspear Strand",z="durotar",s="Darkspear Strand is the stretch of coastline in southern Durotar where the Darkspear trolls washed ashore following their exile from the Echo Isles. Located directly beside Sen'jin Village, this beach marks the bitter beginning of the tribe's mainland refuge under Vol'jin's leadership.",h="Darkspear Strand is the stretch of coastline in southern Durotar where the Darkspear trolls washed ashore...",sec={{t="A Shore of Exile",b="When the witch doctor Zalazane went mad and seized control of the Echo Isles, the surviving Darkspear trolls were forced to abandon their offshore home. Desperate refugees crossed the narrow waters and landed along this sun-bleached coast. Rather than scatter into the hostile red wastes of Durotar, the survivors banded together just yards inland from the shoreline to construct Sen'jin Village. Today, the strand serves as a quiet reminder of their displacement, looking out across the surf toward the islands they still hope to reclaim.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened at Darkspear Strand?",a="This coastline is where the Darkspear trolls made landfall after fleeing the Echo Isles. When Zalazane turned his dark magic against his own people, the survivors evacuated across the water and came ashore here, immediately gathering nearby to establish Sen'jin Village.",al={"why is it called darkspear strand","darkspear strand lore","what is this beach"},it="history"},{q="Why did the Darkspear leave the Echo Isles?",a="The witch doctor Zalazane betrayed his kin and used dark voodoo to enslave the minds of his fellow tribesfolk. Chief Vol'jin led the remaining uncorrupted Darkspear off the islands to escape total subjugation, landing on this strand.",al={"why did trolls leave echo isles","zalazane exile","echo isles evacuation"},it="origin"},{q="What settlement is located next to Darkspear Strand?",a="Sen'jin Village sits just yards inland from the beach. It was established by the refugees immediately after landing on the strand and serves as the primary Darkspear outpost and spiritual center in Durotar.",al={"village near darkspear strand","town next to beach","sen'jin village location"}},{q="What is Darkspear Strand?",a="Darkspear Strand is the stretch of Durotar's coastline situated directly opposite the Echo Isles, lying just outside Sen'jin Village. It serves as the primary shore where the Darkspear trolls washed ashore and regrouped after their tragic retreat from their island home.",al={"what is darkspear strand","darkspear strand lore","about darkspear strand"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is it called Darkspear Strand?",a="The shoreline bears the name of the Darkspear tribe, honoring their landing here during their evacuation from the Echo Isles. It marks the first safe ground the tribe reached on Kalimdor's mainland after fleeing the treacherous coup of Zalazane.",al={"why darkspear strand","how did darkspear strand get its name","darkspear strand name origin"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, stepping onto this shore carries the sting of Zalazane's betrayal and the bittersweet memory of escaping with their lives to found Sen'jin Village.",["faction:Horde"]="The strand marks the southern coast where the Darkspear cemented their place on the Kalimdor mainland beside their Orc allies after losing their island settlement."},kw={"darkspear","darkspear strand","durotar","echo isles","sen'jin village","vol'jin","zalazane"},rel={"subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:echo-isles","zone:durotar","topic:troll"},src={"Darkspear Strand"}}
E["subzone:deadeye-shore"] = {t="subzone",n="Deadeye Shore",z="durotar",s="Deadeye Shore is a windswept stretch of coastline along Durotar's eastern edge, directly east of Drygulch Ravine. Named in memory of the legendary Bleeding Hollow chieftain Kilrogg Deadeye, the barren sands are roamed primarily by wild raptors, scorpids, and feral boars.",h="Deadeye Shore is a windswept stretch of coastline along Durotar's eastern edge, directly east of Drygulch...",sec={{t="A Shoreline of the Bleeding Hollow",b="Stretching beneath the red bluffs of central Durotar, Deadeye Shore takes its name from Kilrogg Deadeye, the one-eyed chieftain of the Bleeding Hollow clan who fought in the First and Second Wars. From high above, the sand and rocky outcrops faintly mirror the shape of a skull with a missing eye socket. While lacking major settlements or military outposts, the shoreline is far from peaceful: aggressive wildlife dominates the sands, and shadowy cultists from the Burning Blade have been known to prowl down toward the water from their nearby hideouts in the ravines.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is it called Deadeye Shore?",a="The shoreline is named after Kilrogg Deadeye, the famed chieftain of the Bleeding Hollow clan. The natural coastal terrain also resembles a skull missing an eye, echoing the chieftain's own blinded socket.",al={"who is deadeye","why deadeye shore","origin of name"},it="name"},{q="Who lives along Deadeye Shore?",a="No permanent settlements stand on Deadeye Shore. The stretch of coast is inhabited primarily by native wildlife like raptors, scorpids, and boars, though fishermen and travelers occasionally pass through—sometimes running afoul of hidden Burning Blade cultists.",al={"who is here","settlements deadeye shore","npcs deadeye"},it="residents"},{q="What threats are found around Deadeye Shore?",a="Beyond aggressive local beasts, the greatest danger comes from the neighboring Drygulch Ravine. Cultists belonging to the Burning Blade occasionally wander down from the rocky canyons toward the coast, ambushing unwary travelers and fishermen.",al={"dangers deadeye shore","enemies here","burning blade deadeye"},it="danger"},{q="What is Deadeye Shore?",a="Deadeye Shore is a rugged stretch of coastline on the eastern edge of Durotar, sitting directly east of Drygulch Ravine. It is characterized by its stark, sun-bleached sands and rocky bluffs looking out over the Great Sea, largely isolated from the settled settlements of the Horde.",al={"what is deadeye shore","deadeye shore overview","where is deadeye shore"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Deadeye Shore?",a="Beyond receiving its name in honor of Kilrogg Deadeye, chieftain of the Bleeding Hollow clan, this stretch of coastline has seen little recorded history. However, its isolation makes it dangerous for wanderers; an orc fisherman named Byrok was notably ambushed along these sands by cultists of the insidious Burning Blade.",al={"deadeye shore history","what happened here","deadeye shore events"},it="history",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For orcs establishing their new nation in Durotar, the shore honors Kilrogg Deadeye, reminding them of the old chieftains who shaped the Horde's history during the wars on Azeroth."},kw={"bleeding hollow","deadeye shore","drygulch ravine","durotar","kilrogg deadeye"},rel={"zone:durotar","subzone:drygulch-ravine"},src={"Deadeye Shore"}}
E["subzone:drygulch-ravine"] = {t="subzone",n="Drygulch Ravine",z="durotar",s="Drygulch Ravine is a rugged, hidden gorge tucked into the rocky bluffs of eastern Durotar. Accessible only through an obscure cave passage from Razorwind Canyon or a perilous drop from above, this craggy trench is overrun by nesting Dustwind harpies who menace nearby supply caravans.",h="Drygulch Ravine is a rugged, hidden gorge tucked into the rocky bluffs of eastern Durotar.",sec={{t="A Bandit Haven in the Red Rocks",b="Carved deep into the crags east of Orgrimmar, Drygulch Ravine is almost entirely cut off from casual travel. Its only ground-level access is a cramped natural tunnel connected to Razorwind Canyon. Fed by a modest river, this sheltered depression once saw peaceful orc habitation, but wild beasts and roosting Dustwind harpies have turned it into a lawless pocket of Durotar. The winged scavengers use the steep cliff faces to nest their broods and stockpile stolen goods taken from Horde supply trains passing along the regional trails.",sp=0},{t="A Thorn in Durotar's Side",b="Life in Drygulch Ravine has long been precarious. Not long after the Third War, escaped thunder lizards from Thunder Ridge threatened the area, prompting warnings to Warchief Thrall in Orgrimmar. Today, the harpies pose the immediate danger. Their matriarchs fiercely defend clutches of eggs tucked along the high ledges, and Horde scouts frequently dispatch young warriors to cull the flock, recover plundered trade crates, and break the harpies' grip on the ravine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you get into Drygulch Ravine?",a="Unless you survive a leap from the high cliffs above, the only ground route is through a small cave entrance tucked within neighboring Razorwind Canyon.",al={"drygulch entrance","how to enter drygulch","where is the cave to drygulch"},gp=true},{q="What creatures live in Drygulch Ravine?",a="The ravine is dominated by Dustwind harpies who build their nests, lay eggs, and stash looted caravan supplies along the craggy rock shelves.",al={"drygulch mobs","what is in drygulch ravine","who lives in drygulch"},it="residents"},{q="Why does the Horde care about this ravine?",a="The Dustwind harpies raid Durotar's vital trade trails, hoarding stolen cargo in the gorge. Horde authorities in Razor Hill regularly send recruits to recover provisions and cull the flock.",al={"why kill harpies drygulch","drygulch ravine quests","horde interest in drygulch"},it="purpose"},{q="Did thunder lizards once attack the ravine?",a="Yes. A few years after the Third War, agitated thunder lizards broke out of nearby Thunder Ridge and threatened Drygulch Ravine, forcing local orcs to seek military aid from Warchief Thrall in Orgrimmar.",al={"thunder lizards drygulch","drygulch history lizards"},it="history"},{q="What is Drygulch Ravine?",a="Drygulch Ravine is a secluded, steep-sided canyon nestled within the rugged crags of Durotar. Fed by an inland river and accessed primarily through a narrow cave opening off Razorwind Canyon, it offers a sheltered crevasse away from the open plains. While orcs once inhabited the gorge, it has recently become a secluded roost for nesting creatures, isolated from the major settlements of the Horde.",al={"what is drygulch ravine","drygulch ravine lore","drygulch ravine info"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is Drygulch Ravine dangerous?",a="Drygulch Ravine is perilous for unescorted travelers and supply caravans. The high cliffs are dominated by the aggressive Dustwind harpies, who swoop down from their roosts to attack intruders and raid passing Horde transports. Navigating the sheer drops and tight crevices invites ambush, especially near their high nests where the fiercest harpies aggressively guard their brood.",al={"is drygulch ravine dangerous","drygulch ravine threats","how dangerous is drygulch"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the ravine's roosts and recovering stolen supplies helps secure Durotar's internal trade routes against constant banditry.",["race:Orc"]="Drygulch Ravine stands as a test of frontier endurance, where young orcs prove their mettle against the ferocious harpies perched on the homeland's rocky bluffs."},kw={"drygulch ravine","durotar","dustwind harpies","harpy nests","orgrimmar","razorwind canyon","stolen supplies","thunder ridge"},rel={"subzone:razorwind-canyon","subzone:thunder-ridge","quest:834","quest:835","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","npc:thrall","topic:third-war"},src={"Drygulch Ravine"}}
E["subzone:dustwind-cave"] = {t="subzone",n="Dustwind Cave",z="durotar",s="Dustwind Cave is a secluded hollow perched atop the cliffs of Razorwind Canyon, just northeast of Razor Hill. It serves as an active training ground and covert sanctuary for initiates of the nefarious Burning Blade cult operating within Durotar.",h="Dustwind Cave is a secluded hollow perched atop the cliffs of Razorwind Canyon, just northeast of Razor Hill.",sec={{t="A Shadow in the Cliffs",b="Overlooking Razorwind Canyon, Dustwind Cave is one of the closest and most perilous threats to Razor Hill. While many assume demonic cultists gather only in deep subterranean depths, here the Burning Blade trains fresh recruits right under the noses of the Horde authorities. Shadowy cultists tutor initiates in forbidden dark magics and demonology, preparing them to undermine the young orcish realm from within Durotar's own borders.",sp=0},{t="Tainted Bloodlines",b="Those who trespass into the cave risk exposure to the cultists' dangerous corruptions. Practitioners inside channel volatile dark arts such as felblood afflictions, demonstrating how deeply the Burning Blade clings to the demonic legacy Thrall fought so hard to banish. Eliminating the cabal here is vital for maintaining the precarious peace of Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Dustwind Cave located?",a="Dustwind Cave is situated high along the clifftops of Razorwind Canyon, directly northeast of Razor Hill in Durotar.",al={"dustwind cave location","where is dustwind cave","how to find dustwind cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who occupies Dustwind Cave?",a="The cave is occupied by cultists and initiates of the Burning Blade, a shadowy demonic cult dedicated to spreading fel corruption and destabilizing the Horde.",al={"who is in dustwind cave","dustwind cave enemies","mobs in dustwind cave"},it="residents"},{q="Why is the Burning Blade operating here?",a="The Burning Blade uses Dustwind Cave as a secluded training outpost where seasoned cultists instruct new recruits in demonic arts away from the immediate gaze of the Orgrimmar and Razor Hill guards.",al={"why are cultists in dustwind cave","burning blade purpose durotar"},it="motive"},{q="Why does the Horde want this cave cleared?",a="Having demon-worshiping cultists lurking just steps away from Razor Hill poses an unacceptable security risk to traveling recruits and the overall defense of Durotar.",al={"why clear dustwind cave","horde threat dustwind cave"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Dustwind Cave?",a="Dustwind Cave is a small cavern carved into the high cliffs above Razorwind Canyon, sitting just northeast of Razor Hill. Hidden away from the watchful eyes of Orgrimmar's grunts, it serves as a clandestine training ground and safe haven for initiates of the shadow-worshiping Burning Blade cult.",al={"what is dustwind cave","dustwind cave lore","about dustwind cave"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is Dustwind Cave dangerous?",a="It is quite dangerous, particularly for unseasoned adventurers. The cavern crawls with fanatical Burning Blade cultists and their eager trainees. Beyond steel blades and ruthless ambush, these zealots wield corrupting shadow and demonic magic, seeking to spread their dark influence across Durotar.",al={"is dustwind cave safe","threats in dustwind cave","how dangerous is dustwind cave"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks of the Horde will recognize the dark rituals taking place within Dustwind Cave, though the Burning Blade wields their fel gifts toward rebellion rather than the service of Thrall's new order.",["faction:Horde"]="Dustwind Cave represents an embarrassing and dangerous internal breach, harboring demon cultists within shouting distance of Razor Hill."},kw={"burning blade","cultists","durotar","dustwind cave","felblood","razor hill","razorwind canyon"},rel={"subzone:razorwind-canyon","subzone:razor-hill","quest:827","zone:durotar"},src={"Dustwind Cave"}}
E["subzone:echo-isles"] = {t="subzone",n="Echo Isles",z="durotar",s="The Echo Isles are a cluster of tropical islands lying just off the southeastern coast of Durotar. Originally settled by the Darkspear trolls after fleeing their ancestral islands, the archipelago is currently lost to the rogue witch doctor Zalazane, who drove his people into exile with dark magic and enslaved minions.",h="The Echo Isles are a cluster of tropical islands lying just off the southeastern coast of Durotar.",sec={{t="A Fractured Sanctuary",b="Following their flight across the Great Sea alongside Thrall, the Darkspear tribe claimed the Echo Isles as their new home. Their peace was repeatedly shattered: first by the naval forces of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore during Kul Tiras' invasion of Durotar, and later from within. Shortly after the trolls drove back Proudmoore's fleet, one of their own witch doctors, Zalazane, seized dark arts to enslave the minds of his kin. Chieftain Vol'jin and the free Darkspears were forced to abandon the islands once more, seeking temporary refuge across the narrow strait at Sen'jin Village.",sp=0},{t="Zalazane's Grip",b="Today, the tropical cluster is overrun by aggressive predators, tainted wildlife, and the thralls of Zalazane. Using malevolent hexes, voodoo fetishes, and ju-ju heaps placed throughout the islands, the traitorous witch doctor bends beasts and captive trolls to his will. From their encampment at Darkspear Strand, Vol'jin's scouts and warriors mount frequent sorties into the islands, determined to recover the remains of their fallen and strike down the mad mystic who stole their home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why don't the Darkspear trolls live here right now?",a="The witch doctor Zalazane betrayed the tribe, using dark magic to strip his brethren of their free will and twist them into obedient servitors. Chieftain Vol'jin ordered an evacuation to the mainland coast of Durotar, founding Sen'jin Village as a staging ground while the tribe fights to reclaim their home.",al={"why abandoned","why did trolls leave","troll home"},it="ruin"},{q="Who is Zalazane?",a="Zalazane is a traitorous Darkspear witch doctor who turned on his tribe. Using powerful voodoo and dark magic, he placed hexes over the islands, corrupted the local wildlife, and enslaved fellow trolls into mindless thralls.",al={"who is zalazane","boss on echo isles","witch doctor zalazane"},it="in_charge"},{q="What threats are on the islands?",a="The archipelago is infested with wild raptors, tigers, and corrupted beasts, as well as Zalazane's voodoo heaps and his mind-controlled troll minions, including hexed and voodoo trolls.",al={"echo isles mobs","what is on the islands","echo isles dangers"},it="danger"},{q="How did the Darkspear tribe end up on these islands originally?",a="After Thrall and the Horde rescued the Darkspear tribe from a sinking island and hostile naga in the Great Sea, the trolls journeyed to Kalimdor and were granted the Echo Isles to settle alongside their orc allies.",al={"how did trolls get here","darkspear origin","echo isles history"},it="origin"},{q="What are the Echo Isles?",a="The Echo Isles are a tropical archipelago resting just off the southeastern shores of Durotar. Originally claimed by the Darkspear tribe as their new homeland in Kalimdor, the islands are now heavily contested, plagued by wild beasts, hexed trolls, and dark magic.",al={"what is echo isles","echo islands","where are the echo isles"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened to the Echo Isles?",a="After escaping their sinking homeland with Thrall's Horde, the Darkspear settled the Echo Isles. They were soon forced to evacuate when Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's fleet attacked. Though Proudmoore was eventually defeated and the trolls returned, the witch doctor Zalazane betrayed them, using dark sorcery to enslave his brethren and drive Vol'jin's people onto the Durotar coast.",al={"history of echo isles","echo isles lore","what happened at echo isles"},it="history",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="The Echo Isles represent both the promised home of the Darkspear in Kalimdor and the bitter sting of Zalazane's betrayal. Reclaiming them is a matter of tribal survival and personal honor.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing the Echo Isles is essential for stabilizing the southern coast of Durotar, protecting Sen'jin Village, and consolidating the young Horde's borders against naval threats and rogue mystics."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","echo isles","sen'jin village","trolls","vol'jin","voodoo","zalazane"},rel={"topic:darkspear-tribe","quest:826","npc:vol-jin","subzone:sen-jin-village","zone:durotar","subzone:darkspear-strand","quest:808","topic:kul-tiras"},src={"Echo Isles"}}
E["subzone:hidden-path"] = {t="subzone",n="Hidden Path",z="durotar",s="The Hidden Path is a secluded mountain trail winding through the crags above the Valley of Trials in Durotar. It serves as a rite of passage for aspiring shaman seeking the sacred Spirit Rock, while offering an overlooked vantage overlooking the rugged borders of the Barrens.",h="The Hidden Path is a secluded mountain trail winding through the crags above the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Sacred Ascent",b="Carved into the red peaks bordering the Valley of Trials, the Hidden Path is intentionally difficult to spot from the canyon floor. Young shaman are directed here by their mentors to prove their awareness and discipline before communing with the spirits at Spirit Rock. Along the trail's highest reaches, travelers are treated to expansive panoramic views stretching westward toward the rolling savannas of the Barrens.",sp=0},{t="Strategic Vulnerability",b="Beyond its spiritual importance, the path cuts a precarious breach through the natural fortifications enclosing the valley. A low pass along the route provides a direct back door toward Ratchet and the road to Orgrimmar. Because it circumvents the standard canyon checkpoints, vigilant defenders fear that bold Alliance infiltrators could exploit this quiet trail to slip directly into the Horde's primary proving grounds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Hidden Path lead?",a="The path ascends from the Valley of Trials up into the crags to Spirit Rock, a sacred site where shaman commune with the elements. It also winds along mountain passes that connect toward the Barrens and the coastline.",al={"hidden path destination","where does hidden path go","hidden path leads to"},it="place"},{q="Why is the path significant to shaman?",a="Initiate shaman in the Valley of Trials are tasked with locating this secluded trail as part of their early elemental trials. Climbing the path allows them to reach the Spirit Rock and drink the Sapta required to commune with the spirits.",al={"shaman path valley of trials","spirit rock path","shaman quest path"},it="purpose"},{q="Could enemies use the Hidden Path to attack the Valley of Trials?",a="Yes. The low gaps along the path bypass the standard guarded entrances to the valley. A cunning Alliance strike force coming from Ratchet or the coast could theoretically use the trail to bypass Horde scouts and enter the training grounds undetected.",al={"hidden path alliance invasion","is valley of trials vulnerable","valley of trials back door"},it="threat"},{q="What can you see from the top of the path?",a="At its highest point, the trail offers a clear, elevated view looking west toward the vast plains of the Barrens, as well as sweeping views across the red canyons of Durotar.",al={"hidden path view","lookout point hidden path"}},{q="What is the Hidden Path?",a="The Hidden Path is a secluded mountain trail winding through the crags bordering the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Kept largely out of plain sight, it serves as a secret passage leading up to Spirit Rock, a sacred site where fledgling shaman commune with the elemental spirits. From its higher ridges, it overlooks the rugged frontier stretching toward the Barrens.",al={"hidden path durotar","what is hidden path","about hidden path"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Hidden Path?",a="The path earns its name from its obscurity. Tucked into the crags framing the Valley of Trials, it is not an obvious road or marked route, but a concealed way through the rocky barrier. Finding it is traditionally part of an initiate's trial, testing their perception before they reach Spirit Rock.",al={"why called hidden path","hidden path name meaning","hidden path name origin"},it="name",add=true},{q="Is the Hidden Path dangerous?",a="The path itself is quiet and free of permanent settlements or monster camps, but its isolation poses a strategic concern. Because a lower gap along the trail provides unmonitored passage out toward the coast, Ratchet, or even northward toward Orgrimmar, it represents an unguarded flank where Alliance infiltrators could theoretically slip into the Valley of Trials.",al={"is hidden path safe","hidden path danger","enemies hidden path"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="The Hidden Path is your first true physical and spiritual climb, testing your perception before you commune with the earth spirits at Spirit Rock.",["faction:Horde"]="Though sacred to shaman, this unfortified passage represents a security blind spot above the Valley of Trials that warrants a watchful eye."},kw={"barrens","durotar","hidden path","shaman","spirit rock","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:spirit-rock","subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","zone:barrens","subzone:ratchet","topic:alliance","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Hidden Path"}}
E["subzone:jaggedswine-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Jaggedswine Farm",z="durotar",s="Jaggedswine Farm is a modest livestock steading situated in northern Durotar, just south of the main entrance to Orgrimmar. Comprising a timber storage shed, a sprawling pen, and a muddy watering hole, it serves as a critical food source raising hardy swine for the nearby Horde capital.",h="Jaggedswine Farm is a modest livestock steading situated in northern Durotar, just south of the main entrance...",sec={{t="Provisions for the Capital",b="Carved out of Durotar's unforgiving, sunbaked earth, Jaggedswine Farm represents the harsh reality of sustaining an urban stronghold like Orgrimmar. The red soil of the region yields sparse agriculture, making robust livestock essential to feeding thousands of orcish warriors and laborers. The farm centers on a timber storehouse, a wide wooden pen, and a natural watering pond where swine are herded, bred, and butchered to keep the Horde's granaries stocked.",sp=0},{t="A Quiet Frontier",b="Though quiet and often appearing half-tended under the dry heat, the farm is a regular stomping ground for local swineherds and patrolling Orgrimmar Grunts. Wild and mature swine roam both inside and outside the enclosures, occasionally testing the patience of nearby guards. Sitting right on the threshold of the capital's valley approach, the plot remains an unassuming yet indispensable outpost in the daily logistics of Durotar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Jaggedswine Farm?",a="The farm raises and maintains swine to provide meat and lard for the Horde, particularly to feed the population and garrison of nearby Orgrimmar.",al={"what is jaggedswine farm","why is there a pig farm in durotar","jaggedswine farm purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where exactly is Jaggedswine Farm located?",a="It lies in northern Durotar, sitting just outside the southern approach and grand gates that lead into the Valley of Strength in Orgrimmar.",al={"where is jaggedswine farm","how to get to jaggedswine farm","pig farm durotar location"},gp=true},{q="Why does the farm look somewhat deserted?",a="Orcish livestock farming in Durotar is utilitarian and unglamorous. Between free-roaming boars and sparse timber structures, the steading lacks grand homesteads, but it remains actively used by Horde supply lines.",al={"is jaggedswine farm abandoned","who lives at jaggedswine farm","why no farmers"},it="ruin"},{q="Are the pigs here dangerous to travelers?",a="While the domesticated swine inside the pens are docile, wild and mature boars roaming the outskirts can be aggressive if startled by young travelers or careless foragers.",al={"are swine hostile","do pigs attack here","swine dangerous"},it="danger"},{q="What is Jaggedswine Farm?",a="Jaggedswine Farm is one of several swine-breeding homesteads situated just south of the gates of Orgrimmar in northern Durotar. Established to supply essential provisions to the Orcish capital, the modest settlement consists of an enclosure for livestock, a storage house, and a nearby watering pond. While practical for the Horde's sustenance, it stands exposed in the harsh, dry terrain outside the city walls.",al={"what is jaggedswine farm","jaggedswine farm info","tell me about jaggedswine farm"},it="place",add=true},{q="Why is it called Jaggedswine Farm?",a="The farm takes its name from the distinctive, bristled swine raised here to feed the growing population of Orgrimmar. Like much of the wildlife surviving in Durotar's unforgiving landscape, these hardy beasts sport rugged hides and sharp features suited to the barren clay and rock of the canyon plains.",al={"why called jaggedswine","jaggedswine farm name origin","why jaggedswine"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="For Horde cooks learning their trade in Durotar, the abundant swine around Jaggedswine Farm make it a primary local source for tender ribs, pork cuts, and cooking grease.",["faction:Horde"]="Establishing stable meat supplies in the arid wastes of Durotar is a matter of survival, making outposts like Jaggedswine vital to sustaining Orgrimmar's military strength."},kw={"boars","durotar","horde provisions","jaggedswine farm","orgrimmar","pig pen","pigs","swine"},rel={"zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:gates-of-orgrimmar","topic:horde"},src={"Jaggedswine Farm"}}
E["subzone:kolkar-crag"] = {t="subzone",n="Kolkar Crag",z="durotar",s="Kolkar Crag is a sunbaked, jagged gorge in southern Durotar claimed by the hostile Kolkar centaur. Led by Warlord Kolkanis, this enclave serves as a staging ground for coordinated raids against nearby Horde settlements.",h="Kolkar Crag is a sunbaked, jagged gorge in southern Durotar claimed by the hostile Kolkar centaur.",sec={{t="A Thorn in Durotar's Side",b="Tucked away in the rugged canyons of southern Durotar, Kolkar Crag is a base of operations for the aggressive Kolkar clan. Despite the arid and unforgiving terrain, these centaur have fortified the natural choke points of the gorge. From this ravine, their scouts and marauders keep close watch over the surrounding flats, probing for vulnerabilities across orc and Darkspear holdings. For young warriors training in the Valley of Trials or patrolling the southern coast, Kolkar Crag represents the nearest organized front of centaur hostility.",sp=0},{t="Schemes of Invasion",b="Under the command of Warlord Kolkanis, the centaur entrenched at the crag hold ambitions far beyond simple skirmishes. Recovered attack plans reveal plots targeting the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, Razor Hill, and daring strikes aimed directly toward the gates of Orgrimmar. Halting these plans requires decisive preemptive strikes deep into the ravine to assassinate Kolkanis and break their muster before their war parties can sweep through the valleys.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who lives in Kolkar Crag?",a="Kolkar Crag is held by the Kolkar centaur clan, led on-site by Warlord Kolkanis. They use the defensible canyon as a camp and raiding post against Horde outposts throughout Durotar.",al={"who is at kolkar crag","kolkar crag inhabitants","who owns kolkar crag"},it="residents"},{q="Why is the Horde concerned about this ravine?",a="The centaur within the gorge have drafted plans to launch coordinated assaults on Durotar's vital settlements, including the training grounds in the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, Razor Hill, and Orgrimmar itself.",al={"why care about kolkar crag","is kolkar crag dangerous","kolkar threat"},it="threat"},{q="Who leads the centaur here?",a="The encampment is commanded by Warlord Kolkanis, a ferocious centaur warlord who directs their scouting maneuvers and formulates battle plans against the orcs and trolls.",al={"kolkar crag boss","who leads kolkar crag","warlord kolkanis"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is Kolkar Crag?",a="Kolkar Crag is a rugged, craggy gorge located in southern Durotar. It serves as an entrenched stronghold for the hostile Kolkar centaur, who have carved out a base within its natural canyons dangerously close to vital Horde settlements.",al={"kolkar crag location","what is kolkar crag","kolkar crag overview"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Kolkar Crag?",a="Following the Third War, Kolkar centaur fortified themselves within this ravine, using it as a staging ground to plan coordinated attacks against Durotar settlements, including Sen'jin Village, Razor Hill, the Valley of Trials, and Orgrimmar itself. Word of massing orc forces in response to the centaur threat even prompted Theramore to reinforce nearby Northwatch Hold.",al={"kolkar crag history","history of kolkar crag","events at kolkar crag"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Kolkar Crag dangerous?",a="Yes, it is exceptionally dangerous. The gorge is teeming with aggressive Kolkar centaur led by Warlord Kolkanis, all organized and preparing raids against nearby settlements. Unwary travelers wandering into the ravine will quickly find themselves ambushed and outnumbered.",al={"how dangerous is kolkar crag","is kolkar crag safe"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called Kolkar Crag?",a="The ravine takes its name directly from the Kolkar clan of centaur that claimed and established their stronghold within the rocky gorge.",al={"kolkar crag name meaning","why kolkar crag"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="The presence of centaur so close to the Valley of Trials threatens the initiation of young orcs, making the pacification of Kolkar Crag an urgent matter of territorial defense.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing southern Durotar against centaur incursions protects the supply lines running between Sen'jin Village and the road to Orgrimmar."},kw={"centaur","durotar","kolkanis","kolkar","kolkar crag","sen'jin village","valley of trials","warlord kolkanis"},rel={"quest:786","topic:centaur","zone:durotar","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:razor-hill","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Kolkar Crag"}}
E["subzone:orgrimmar"] = {t="subzone",n="Orgrimmar",z="durotar",s="Orgrimmar is the formidable warrior capital of the New Horde, carved into the winding red canyons of northern Durotar. Founded by Warchief Thrall and named in memory of Orgrim Doomhammer, it serves as the beating heart of orcish renewal and intertribal survival on Kalimdor.",h="Orgrimmar is the formidable warrior capital of the New Horde, carved into the winding red canyons of northern...",sec={{t="A Stronghold in the Stone",b="Following the Third War and the victory at Mount Hyjal, Warchief Thrall brought his surviving people south to establish a permanent homeland in Durotar. Nestled into a natural barrier of sheer mountain crags, Orgrimmar was engineered to withstand siege, boasting spiked timber palisades, stone watchtowers, and deep mountain-carved caverns. Built in cooperation with the Darkspear trolls, tauren stonemasons, and goblin engineers, the fortress turned a desolate wilderness into an unassailable bastion of strength.",sp=0},{t="Heart of the New Horde",b="Free of the demonic bloodlust that once bound them, the orcs built Orgrimmar as a beacon of honor, community, and survival. Today in 25 ADP, the city houses not only orcs and Darkspear trolls, but also welcomes emissaries from the tauren of Mulgore and emissaries from the newly allied Forsaken. Within its fortified canyons, shamans instruct the next generation in ancestral balance, while veterans clash in gladiatorial rings to hone the army that shields the fragile peace of Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Orgrimmar named after?",a="Warchief Thrall named the city in honor of his mentor and predecessor, the legendary orc Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer. Doomhammer fell in the Eastern Kingdoms during the liberation of the orc internment camps, bestowing his iconic warplate and battle hammer onto Thrall.",al={"orgrimmar name origin","why called orgrimmar","who was orgrimmar named for"},it="name"},{q="Who helped build the city?",a="The capital was raised rapidly through the joint effort of orcs, the Darkspear trolls, the tauren, hired goblin sappers and engineers, and the wandering champion Rexxar. Its natural stone walls were excavated and fortified to provide swift, defensible shelter in the harsh terrain of Durotar.",al={"who built orgrimmar","how was orgrimmar made","orgrimmar builders"},it="origin"},{q="Which races call Orgrimmar home?",a="Orgrimmar is primarily inhabited by the orcs and Sen'jin's Darkspear trolls, who share its districts. Tauren travelers frequently reside in the city as steadfast allies, and envoys of the recently accepted Forsaken have begun establishing a quiet foothold alongside them.",al={"who lives in orgrimmar","orgrimmar residents","races in orgrimmar"},it="residents"},{q="Where does Warchief Thrall reside?",a="Thrall presides over the New Horde from Grommash Hold, a central stronghold located in the Valley of Wisdom within Orgrimmar, named to honor his fallen friend, Grom Hellscream.",al={"where is thrall","thrall location orgrimmar","warchief seat"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is Orgrimmar?",a="Orgrimmar is the mighty capital city of the orcs and the primary seat of the entire Horde. Carved deep into the jagged red-rock canyons on the northern border of Durotar, it stands as an imposing warrior fortress guarded by towering wooden ramparts, iron gates, and natural mountain barriers. For travelers and heroes of the Horde, it serves as the beating heart of trade, training, and leadership.",al={"what is orgrimmar","about orgrimmar","orgrimmar overview"},it="place",add=true},{q="What is the history behind the founding of Orgrimmar?",a="Following the Third War and the Battle of Mount Hyjal, Warchief Thrall led the orcs to Kalimdor to claim a new homeland free of demonic corruption. Aided by the tauren, the Darkspear trolls, and Rexxar, the Horde rapidly carved the fortress city into the rocky valleys of Durotar. Despite violent skirmishes with native centaur, harpies, and quilboar, the stronghold endured and established the Horde's enduring presence on the continent.",al={"orgrimmar history","how was orgrimmar founded","founding of orgrimmar"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is Orgrimmar dangerous?",a="For loyal members of the Horde, Orgrimmar is a secure and welcoming sanctuary, fiercely guarded by seasoned warriors and Kor'kron protectors. However, any Alliance trespasser foolish enough to step near its gates will be hunted down and slain on sight. Beyond its outer walls, the surrounding canyons of Durotar also harbor lurking threats like hostile quilboar, harpies, and rogue cultists.",al={"is orgrimmar dangerous","orgrimmar threats","threats in orgrimmar"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As the supreme seat of Horde leadership, Orgrimmar is the central staging ground for military campaigns, clan alliances, and diplomatic relations across Kalimdor and beyond.",["race:Orc"]="For the orcs, Orgrimmar is the realization of their redemption, where they cast off the legacy of the demonic curse to build an honorable, independent future."},kw={"darkspear","doomhammer","durotar","grommash hold","new horde","orgrimmar","tauren","thrall"},rel={"zone:durotar","npc:thrall","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","subzone:grommash-hold","subzone:drag","topic:new-horde","topic:darkspear-tribe","topic:tauren"},src={"Orgrimmar"}}
E["subzone:razor-hill"] = {t="subzone",n="Razor Hill",z="durotar",s="Razor Hill is the principal Horde settlement in central Durotar, nestled at the strategic crossroads between the Valley of Trials, the Barrens, and Orgrimmar. Centered around a prominent fortified barracks, it serves as the staging ground and training center for young orc and troll warriors testing their mettle in the harsh wilderness.",h="Razor Hill is the principal Horde settlement in central Durotar, nestled at the strategic crossroads between...",sec={{t="Heart of Durotar",b="Built at a vital geographical junction, Razor Hill connects northern Durotar with the coastal settlements to the south and the sprawling plains of the Barrens across the Southfury River. Dominated by its stone-and-timber barracks and classic orcish burrows, the settlement was established early in the founding of Durotar. Shortly after the Third War, human forces from Kul Tiras lured the Horde into an ambush here under the guise of an emissary summit, an assault thwarted when Rexxar went in Thrall's stead. Today, the outpost stands fully fortified against further coastal incursions.",sp=0},{t="Watch on the Frontier",b="Under the command of veteran officers like Gar'Thok, Razor Hill coordinates local defense against several looming threats. Human marine remnants still hold Tiragarde Keep along the eastern shoreline, while aggressive quilboar and harpy tribes harass local supply lines. Far more insidious is the presence of the Burning Blade cult, whose shadowy rituals and corrupted agents in the nearby crags are closely tracked and stamped out by investigators like Orgnil Soulscar.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Razor Hill's purpose in Durotar?",a="Razor Hill serves as the main administrative and defensive outpost in central Durotar. It connects the southern shores and the Valley of Trials to Orgrimmar in the north and the Barrens to the west, while providing supplies and training for young adventurers.",al={"why is razor hill here","razor hill purpose","what is razor hill"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened here during the Kul Tiras invasion?",a="Following the Third War, forces loyal to Kul Tiras offered a peaceful summit with Warchief Thrall at Razor Hill. Suspecting treachery, the champion Rexxar went in Thrall's place, uncovered an ambush, and defeated the human assassins.",al={"kul tiras ambush","rexxar razor hill","what happened at razor hill summit"},it="history"},{q="Who commands the settlement?",a="The settlement's garrison is commanded by the orc veteran Gar'Thok from within the town's barracks, overseeing patrols against human remnants and local wild beasts.",al={"razor hill leader","who runs razor hill","gar'thok"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Burning Blade doing near Razor Hill?",a="The shadowy demonic cult has infiltrated hidden crags and canyons around central Durotar. Horde scouts, directed by Orgnil Soulscar, work out of Razor Hill to uncover their covens and eliminate their influence.",al={"burning blade durotar","orgnil soulscar","cultists near razor hill"},it="threat"},{q="What is Razor Hill?",a="Razor Hill is the principal orcish settlement in central Durotar. Built around a major crossroads, it connects the road north to Orgrimmar, south to Sen'jin Village and the Valley of Trials, and west toward the Barrens. Dominated by its stout military barracks and watchtower, the fortified outpost serves as both a thriving civic hub for local orc laborers and farmers and a vital defensive bulwark defending the heart of Durotar.",al={"about razor hill","razor hill overview","what kind of town is razor hill"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is Razor Hill dangerous?",a="Within its walls, Razor Hill is well defended by Horde guards and watchful grunts, making it a safe haven for weary travelers. However, the surrounding territory is fraught with peril. Human marine scouts from Tiragarde Keep frequently probe near the roads, foul cultists of the Burning Blade lurk in nearby canyons, and venomous wildlife like scorpid and raptors prowl just outside the town's perimeter.",al={"is razor hill safe","threats to razor hill","razor hill danger"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As the first true town encountered after leaving the training grounds, Razor Hill serves as the launchpad for young Horde soldiers proving their loyalty to Thrall's new nation.",["race:Orc"]="Razor Hill stands as a testament to the new life orcs have carved out in Durotar, trading demonic servitude for sturdy burrows and hard-won survival."},kw={"barracks","burning blade","durotar","gar'thok","kul tiras","orgnil soulscar","razor hill"},rel={"zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:tiragarde-keep","npc:gar-thok","npc:orgnil-soulscar","zone:barrens"},src={"Razor Hill"}}
E["subzone:razor-hill-watchtower"] = {t="subzone",n="Razor Hill Watchtower",z="durotar",s="Perched on the red stone bluffs overlooking Razor Hill, this sturdy outpost serves as an early warning post for the heart of Durotar. Sentries stationed here keep a vigilant eye across the dusty plains and toward the coast, safeguarding the settlement below from encroaching threats.",h="Perched on the red stone bluffs overlooking Razor Hill, this sturdy outpost serves as an early warning post...",sec={{t="Eyes Over Durotar",b="Constructed from thick timber and iron framing, the Razor Hill Watchtower guards the settlement of Razor Hill and the surrounding canyons. Durotar faces relentless threats from Kul Tiras marines along the eastern shore, quillboar raiders prowling the scrublands, and Burning Blade cultists lurking in nearby crags. From this elevated vantage point atop the ridgeline, Horde sentries can spot approaching warbands, smoke signals, and incursions long before they reach the settlement gates.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Razor Hill Watchtower?",a="The watchtower serves as the primary lookout post for Razor Hill and central Durotar. Its high elevation allows scouts to monitor the trails, watch for hostile beasts, and detect any troop movements from nearby Alliance encampments or centaur raiding parties.",al={"why is the watchtower here","watchtower purpose","razor hill tower"},it="purpose"},{q="Who guards the watchtower?",a="Horde sentries and scouts are stationed here on rotation from Razor Hill. They keep watch over the surrounding red ravines and stand ready to sound the alarm if the town below is threatened.",al={"who is at the tower","watchtower guards"},it="in_charge"},{q="What threats can be seen from up here?",a="Scouts primarily keep watch for aggressive quillboar from the Razormane tribes, human infiltrators from Tiragarde Keep along the eastern coast, and wild beasts roaming the dry valleys.",al={"threats to razor hill","what are they looking for"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Razor Hill Watchtower?",a="Perched on the red bluffs high above the settlement of Razor Hill, this wooden Horde fortification commands a sweeping view across Durotar. It serves as an early warning post for the nearby crossroads, letting sentries monitor the dusty canyon roads, the southern coastline, and any movement of hostile quilboar, centaur, or Alliance infiltrators creeping inland from the Great Sea.",al={"what is razor hill watchtower","razor hill tower","watchtower razor hill"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is the Razor Hill Watchtower dangerous?",a="For Horde travelers, the watchtower is entirely secure, manned by loyal warriors keeping vigil over the surrounding cliffs. However, members of the Alliance who wander up these bluffs will find watchful sentries ready to sound the alarm and strike down any trespassers encroaching upon Durotar's heartland.",al={"is razor hill watchtower safe","danger razor hill watchtower"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For young warriors and scouts emerging from the Valley of Trials, the watchtower is a reassuring landmark signaling the safety and strength of the fledgling Horde.",["class:Hunter"]="The high vantage point offers an unobstructed view of the surrounding crags, ideal for spotters tracking quarry and tracking beast movements across Durotar."},kw={"durotar","lookout","razor hill","razor hill watchtower","sentry","watchtower"},rel={"subzone:razor-hill","zone:durotar","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Razor Hill Watchtower"}}
E["subzone:razormane-grounds"] = {t="subzone",n="Razormane Grounds",z="durotar",s="The Razormane Grounds form the forward encampment of the Razormane quilboar pushing eastward from the Barrens into central Durotar. Choked with sharp briars and the stripped carcasses of wild game, this bristling outpost serves as the frontline in the quilboars' unending clash with the orcs of Orgrimmar.",h="The Razormane Grounds form the forward encampment of the Razormane quilboar pushing eastward from the Barrens...",sec={{t="A Thorn in Durotar's Side",b="Sprawling beneath the red cliffs of central Durotar, the Razormane Grounds mark the furthest eastern reach of quilboar expansion out of the Barrens. Entangled within thick brambles and surrounded by bleached bones, the encampment poses a constant danger to travelers along the Southfury River. The camp is led by figures such as Captain Flat Tusk of the Battleguard and Geolord Mottle, who orchestrate raids against neighboring orc settlements and passing supply lines. Despite regular patrols dispatched from Razor Hill and nearby outposts, the Razormane replenish their ranks tirelessly, sprouting from the briars faster than the Horde can clear them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Razormane Grounds?",a="It is a fortified quilboar encampment in central Durotar, acting as a forward base for the Razormane tribe as they expand eastward from the Barrens.",al={"razormane grounds","quilboar camp durotar","where are razormane"},it="place"},{q="Why are the quilboar attacking Durotar?",a="The Razormane quilboar view all neighboring territories as rightfully theirs, seeking to expand their thorny thickets and hunting lands at the expense of the new Horde settlements.",al={"why quilboar attack","why are razormane here","quilboar invasion"},it="conflict"},{q="Who leads the quilboar at the Razormane Grounds?",a="The encampment is commanded by Captain Flat Tusk, leader of the Razormane Battleguard, alongside the earth-shaping geomancer Geolord Mottle.",al={"razormane bosses","who leads the razormane grounds","captain flat tusk"},it="leader"},{q="Why are there so many bones around the camp?",a="The Razormane are aggressive scavengers and hunters who strip the local wildlife down to the bone to feed their raiders, leaving the carcasses behind to mark their territory.",al={"bones in camp","razormane animal carcasses","why dead animals"}},{q="What happened at the Razormane Grounds?",a="When the orcs founded Durotar, the Razormane quilboar pushed eastward out of the Barrens to expand their territory. The Razormane Grounds became the front line of that invasion. The orcs have fought relentlessly to hold them back from Durotar's heartland, but for every quilboar slain among the brambles, more seem to emerge from the thickets to press the assault.",al={"razormane grounds history","what happened at razormane grounds","razormane invasion durotar"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who lives at the Razormane Grounds?",a="The encampment is home to an aggressive war band of Razormane quilboar pushing into Durotar. The camp is commanded by Captain Flat Tusk, who leads their battleguard, alongside the geomancer Geolord Mottle, who commands earth magic among the brambles.",al={"who lives at razormane grounds","razormane grounds inhabitants","who is at razormane grounds"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is the Razormane Grounds dangerous?",a="Yes. It serves as an active forward war camp crawling with hostile quilboar warriors and geomancers. The Razormane fiercely butcher intruders and local wildlife alike, littering the area with stripped bones, and the dense thorn brambles make any retreat perilous.",al={"is razormane grounds dangerous","danger razormane grounds","how dangerous are razormane grounds"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Razormane Grounds?",a="The grounds are named after the Razormane tribe of quilboar, who established this sprawling encampment as a staging area for their territorial push into Durotar.",al={"why is it called razormane grounds","razormane grounds name meaning","where did razormane grounds get its name"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="For the orcs of Durotar, the Razormane Grounds are a persistent threat right in the heart of their new homeland, requiring young warriors to prove their mettle by culling the quilboar.",["faction:Horde"]="Keeping the Razormane Grounds suppressed is vital to securing travel and supply lines between the Barrens and the Horde capital of Orgrimmar."},kw={"captain flat tusk","durotar","geolord mottle","quilboar","raggaran","razormane","razormane grounds"},rel={"zone:durotar","topic:quilboar","zone:barrens"},src={"Razormane Grounds"}}
E["subzone:razorwind-canyon"] = {t="subzone",n="Razorwind Canyon",z="durotar",s="Razorwind Canyon is a winding, rocky gulch split across the main road between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar. Infested by the aggressive Dustwind harpies, the canyon poses a persistent danger to travelers moving north toward the Horde's capital.",h="Razorwind Canyon is a winding, rocky gulch split across the main road between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Threat on the High Road",b="Razorwind Canyon flanks the central artery linking Razor Hill to Orgrimmar, carving paths into both the eastern bluffs and the western scrublands toward Tor'kren Farm. The canyon is the nesting ground of the Dustwind harpies, territorial creatures that strike without hesitation at travelers who stray too close to their roosts. Their presence so near the capital's trade routes makes clearing out these gullies an ongoing necessity for the defenders of Durotar.",sp=0},{t="Passages and Ravines",b="Beyond serving as harpy nests, the twists of Razorwind Canyon function as hidden routes through Durotar's red rock hills. The eastern branch tunnels deeply into the crags, providing a passage through a cavern into Drygulch Ravine. Because the harpies roost on the high perches and descend in flocks, unwary adventurers traversing these passes can easily find themselves surrounded and cut down.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Razorwind Canyon located?",a="Razorwind Canyon is located in central Durotar, flanking both sides of the main road running between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar. Entrances lead into it north of Razor Hill, near Tor'kren Farm, and through a cave connecting to Drygulch Ravine.",al={"razorwind canyon location","where is razorwind canyon","how to find razorwind canyon"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures inhabit Razorwind Canyon?",a="The canyon is heavily inhabited by the Dustwind harpies. These aggressive, avian creatures nest in large clutches throughout the gullies and rocky outcroppings, preying on unwary travelers.",al={"razorwind mobs","what lives in razorwind canyon","harpy canyon durotar"},it="residents"},{q="Why is the Horde concerned about this canyon?",a="Razorwind Canyon borders the primary trade and travel route between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar. The nesting harpies frequently harass couriers, supply caravans, and travelers passing along the central road.",al={"why care about razorwind","orgrimmar threat razorwind"},it="threat"},{q="Does Razorwind Canyon connect to other areas?",a="Yes. In addition to opening onto the main road, the canyon provides trails west toward Tor'kren Farm, as well as an eastern cavern leading into Drygulch Ravine.",al={"canyon connections","where does razorwind lead"},gp=true},{q="What is Razorwind Canyon?",a="Razorwind Canyon is a jagged canyon flanking the main road between Razor Hill and Orgrimmar in central Durotar. Split into eastern and western ravines, the crags serve as the primary nesting grounds for the savage Dustwind harpies, posing a constant danger to travelers journeying along the Horde's vital overland routes.",al={"razorwind canyon lore","about razorwind canyon","what is razorwind"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is Razorwind Canyon dangerous?",a="Yes, it is very dangerous. Razorwind Canyon swarms with aggressive Dustwind harpies who fiercely defend their nesting perches. Their overwhelming numbers and vicious nature make it easy for unwary travelers or lone wanderers to be swarmed, subdued, and killed if they venture off the road into the canyon depths.",al={"is razorwind dangerous","razorwind canyon danger","danger in razorwind"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the Dustwind harpies from Razorwind Canyon is vital to keeping the main thoroughfare between Razor Hill and the capital of Orgrimmar safe for couriers and fresh recruits.",["race:Orc"]="The harpies nesting right along Durotar's central roadway are an insult to the security of the orcish homeland, requiring young warriors to cull their numbers."},kw={"drygulch ravine","durotar","dustwind harpies","razor hill","razorwind canyon","tor'kren farm"},rel={"zone:durotar","subzone:razor-hill","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:drygulch-ravine","subzone:tor-kren-farm","quest:835","quest:834"},src={"Razorwind Canyon"}}
E["subzone:rocktusk-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Rocktusk Farm",z="durotar",s="Rocktusk Farm is a small swine ranch situated in northern Durotar just down the road outside the gates of Orgrimmar. Tucked near the fortified approaches of the capital, the stead supplies vital meat and provisions to the city's inhabitants.",h="Rocktusk Farm is a small swine ranch situated in northern Durotar just down the road outside the gates of...",sec={{t="Provisions for the Capital",b="Carved out of the arid soil of Durotar, Rocktusk Farm is dedicated to raising hardy swine suited to the rough desert climate. Due to Durotar's notoriously dry and stony ground, raising crops is difficult, making domestic swine farms an essential lifeline for feeding Orgrimmar's burgeoning population. Nestled close to the capital's fortified perimeter, the homestead enjoys a degree of safety rarely found in the harsh wilds of the red canyonlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Rocktusk Farm used for?",a="Rocktusk Farm is a domestic pig farm. It raises swine to supply fresh meat and provisions to the neighboring capital of Orgrimmar, where arable land is scarce.",al={"what is this place","rocktusk farm purpose","why are there pigs here"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Rocktusk Farm located?",a="The farm sits in northern Durotar, located just southwest down the road from the main gates of Orgrimmar and nestled along the rocky bluffs.",al={"where is rocktusk farm","rocktusk farm location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is the farm safe from wild beasts?",a="Its close proximity to Orgrimmar and nearby Horde military patrols keeps it safer than most outlying homesteads in Durotar, though wild beasts and roaming pests still prowl the outskirts.",al={"is rocktusk farm safe","dangers at rocktusk farm"},it="danger"},{q="What is Rocktusk Farm?",a="Rocktusk Farm is a swine-breeding homestead situated along the western road just outside the gates of Orgrimmar in Durotar. Operating in the rugged shadow of the capital's defenses, the farm raises pigs to help provide vital sustenance and provisions for the growing Horde.",al={"what is rocktusk farm","rocktusk farm durotar","about rocktusk farm"},it="place",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Settled just outside the capital, the swine reared here are critical sustenance for the warriors and laborers stationed in Orgrimmar.",["profession:Cooking"]="The pigs raised on the farm are prized by Horde cooks searching for fresh pork, ribs, and savory cuts to roast."},kw={"durotar","horde provisions","orgrimmar","pig farm","rocktusk farm","swine"},rel={"zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar","topic:horde","subzone:gates-of-orgrimmar"},src={"Rocktusk Farm"}}
E["subzone:scuttle-coast"] = {t="subzone",n="Scuttle Coast",z="durotar",s="The Scuttle Coast is the wave-battered eastern shoreline of Durotar, situated between Razor Hill and Tiragarde Keep. The rocky beach is strewn with sunken wreckage from Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's Kul Tiras fleet, making it an active scavenging ground for the Horde and a lingering reminder of recent naval warfare.",h="The Scuttle Coast is the wave-battered eastern shoreline of Durotar, situated between Razor Hill and...",sec={{t="Wreckage of the Fleet",b="Running along Durotar's eastern edge out to the Great Sea, the Scuttle Coast earned its grim character during the invasion led by Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore. When the Kul Tiras fleet assaulted the fledgling nation of Durotar, fierce battles with the Horde drove many human warships against the jagged shoals, smashing them into splintered hulks. Today, the shoreline is choked with barnacle-encrusted timber, broken rigging, and salvaged cargo barrels. For the nearby encampments of Razor Hill, the coast represents both a lingering security hazard and a valuable source of recovered provisions and abandoned Alliance mechanisms.",sp=0},{t="Scavengers and Tides",b="The name Scuttle Coast refers not only to the sunken warships deliberately scuttled or grounded during the fighting, but also to the swarms of crabs and makrura that pick through the rotting detritus. While shoreline wildlife and dangerous tides keep casual travelers away, Horde scavengers periodically comb through the wreckage to retrieve valuable equipment, including gnomish technical components abandoned in the cargo holds of the sunken ships.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where did all these shipwrecks come from?",a="The shattered ships belonged to the naval fleet of Kul Tiras under Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore. They were smashed against Durotar's rocky shallows during the admiral's failed military campaign against the newly founded Horde.",al={"why are there ships here","who owns the wrecked ships","sunken ships durotar"},it="history"},{q="Why is it called the Scuttle Coast?",a="The name carries a double meaning. It refers directly to the warships scuttled along the coastline during naval combat, as well as the numerous makrura and crabs that scuttle across the rocky sands.",al={"why is it called scuttle coast","scuttle coast name origin"},it="name"},{q="What is the Horde looking for along the coast?",a="Horde scouts and scavengers search the broken holds for salvageable tools, supplies, and discarded gnomish technology left behind by the Alliance forces.",al={"what are orcs salvaging","horde salvage scuttle coast"},it="purpose"},{q="Is the Scuttle Coast safe to travel?",a="No. Aside from treacherous waves and jagged rocks, hostile coastal beasts like makrura prowl the surf, and armed Kul Tiras survivors remain entrenched just to the south at Tiragarde Keep.",al={"scuttle coast dangers","is scuttle coast dangerous"},it="danger"},{q="What is Scuttle Coast?",a="The Scuttle Coast is the rocky eastern shoreline of Durotar, facing the Great Sea just southeast of Razor Hill and north of Tiragarde Keep. It is a windswept stretch of beach and jagged shoals infamous for maritime disasters and treacherous waters.",al={"what is scuttle coast","scuttle coast lore","tell me about scuttle coast"},it="place",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The broken hulls littering this beach stand as stark monuments to Durotar's defense against Daelin Proudmoore's invading navy.",["profession:Engineering"]="The sunken Alliance holds along the shore contain abandoned gnomish gadgets, scrap metal, and intricate machinery ripe for reverse-engineering."},kw={"daelin proudmoore","durotar","kul tiras","makrura","razor hill","scuttle coast","shipwrecks","tiragarde keep"},rel={"zone:durotar","subzone:tiragarde-keep","subzone:razor-hill","topic:kul-tiras","npc:jaina-proudmoore","topic:gnome","topic:alliance"},src={"Scuttle Coast"}}
E["subzone:sen-jin-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Sen'jin Village",z="durotar",s="Sen'jin Village is a coastal settlement on the southern shores of Durotar, serving as a sanctuary for the Darkspear trolls. Established by Chieftain Vol'jin after his people were driven from their ancestral home on the Echo Isles, the hamlet honors his fallen father, the witch doctor Sen'jin. Today, it stands as a fragile haven focused on survival, herbalism, and reclaiming what was stolen.",h="Sen'jin Village is a coastal settlement on the southern shores of Durotar, serving as a sanctuary for the...",sec={{t="A Refugee Shore",b="When the dark witch doctor Zalazane betrayed the Darkspear and seized control of the Echo Isles, Chieftain Vol'jin was forced to lead the survivors across the strait to the mainland of Durotar. There, nestled beneath coastal cliffs and looking out over the water, they raised crude huts and established Sen'jin Village. The settlement carries the name of Vol'jin's father, the venerable elder who sacrificed himself during the Third War to save their people from coastal murlocs. Despite their close alliance with Thrall's Horde, the trolls here live under the shadow of exile, staring daily across the shallows at the home they lost.",sp=0},{t="Eyes on the Isles",b="Daily life in Sen'jin Village revolves around preparation and defense. Between local Centaur raids, aggressive sea beasts, and Zalazane's hexes reaching across the sea, the villagers rely heavily on herbal remedies and brewing potent alchemical spirits. While Vol'jin coordinates broader tribal defense from the Horde capital, local shamans, hunters, and scouts gather here to recruit fresh wanderers stepping out of the Valley of Trials. Their aim is clear: to gather resources, protect Durotar's southern flank, and plot the eventual downfall of the traitor Zalazane.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why did the Darkspear build Sen'jin Village here?",a="The Darkspear fled across the strait to the Durotar coastline after the witch doctor Zalazane went mad and took control of their home on the Echo Isles. Sen'jin Village was established by Vol'jin as a temporary refuge and staging ground just across the water from their stolen land.",al={"why is senjin village here","why are trolls in durotar","why did trolls leave echo isles"},it="origin"},{q="Who was Sen'jin?",a="Sen'jin was a respected witch doctor and chieftain of the Darkspear tribe, as well as the father of Vol'jin. During the Third War, he foresaw Thrall's arrival and sacrificed his life while saving his tribe and the young Horde from fanatical sea murlocs in the South Seas.",al={"who was senjin","who is senjin named after","senjin lore"},it="name"},{q="Why are there so many herbalists and alchemists here?",a="The local witch doctors and medicine men rely heavily on Durotar's coastal flora and scorpok venoms to concoct charms, antidotes, and rituals. These botanical brews sustain the wounded and offer wards against the dark hexes drifting over from the Echo Isles.",al={"senjin village trainers","professions in senjin village","why alchemy here"}},{q="Can you reach the Echo Isles from Sen'jin Village?",a="The Echo Isles sit directly across the eastern water from the village. Adventurers often swim or wade across the shallow channel to strike back at Zalazane's voodoo cultists, recover stolen artifacts, or gather resources for the village defenders.",al={"how to get to echo isles","isles off senjin coast","swimming to echo isles"},gp=true},{q="What is Sen'jin Village?",a="Sen'jin Village is a coastal fishing settlement on the southern shore of Durotar, serving as the primary mainland refuge for the Darkspear trolls. Founded after the tribe was driven from the Echo Isles, it is a modest cluster of huts, docks, and raptor pens where troll refugees, witch doctors, and scouts maintain a watch over their lost homeland.",al={"what is senjin village","senjin village overview","sen'jin village lore"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Sen'jin Village?",a="When the witch doctor Zalazane betrayed the Darkspear tribe and seized control of the Echo Isles with dark voodoo, Vol'jin led the surviving trolls across the water to Durotar's southern coast. There, they raised this village as a temporary sanctuary and military foothold, naming it in honor of Vol'jin's fallen father while plotting to reclaim their home.",al={"sen'jin village history","history of senjin village","how was senjin village founded"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who lives in Sen'jin Village?",a="The settlement is populated almost entirely by exiled Darkspear trolls. Local hunters, shadow hunters, herbalists, and alchemists work out of its huts and docks, defending the coast and gathering resources to support the broader Darkspear war effort under Chieftain Vol'jin's leadership.",al={"who lives in senjin village","who runs senjin village","sen'jin village leader"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is Sen'jin Village dangerous?",a="The village itself is heavily guarded by Sen'jin axe throwers and shamans, offering safety within its borders. However, danger lies just beyond: Zalazane's mind-controlled trolls inhabit the nearby Echo Isles, while the surrounding shores are plagued by aggressive wildlife and encroaching sea creatures.",al={"is sen'jin village safe","threats to senjin village","senjin village dangers"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls emerging from the Valley of Trials, this refuge is the beating heart of their displaced people, holding memories of their lost chieftain and the enduring sting of Zalazane's betrayal.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The village is a vital starting center for natural medicine, surrounded by coastal Peacebloom, Silverleaf, and Earthroot used by local witch doctors to treat venom and curses."},kw={"darkspear","durotar","echo isles","sen'jin village","senjin","vol'jin","zalazane"},rel={"topic:darkspear-tribe","subzone:echo-isles","npc:vol-jin","quest:826","zone:durotar","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:razor-hill","topic:third-war"},src={"Sen'jin Village"}}
E["subzone:shrine-of-the-dormant-flame"] = {t="subzone",n="Shrine of the Dormant Flame",z="durotar",s="Perched atop the highest peak northwest of the Valley of Trials, the Shrine of the Dormant Flame is a secluded sanctuary revered by Horde shaman. Guided by its solitary keeper, Telf Joolam, initiates make the treacherous climb to commune with the element of fire and prove their spiritual mastery.",h="Perched atop the highest peak northwest of the Valley of Trials, the Shrine of the Dormant Flame is a...",sec={{t="A Summit of Trial and Flame",b="Reaching the Shrine of the Dormant Flame requires braving a narrow, winding trail that begins along the Southfury River at the southwestern edge of the Southfury Watershed. High above the red cliffs of Durotar, the mountain summit offers a commanding view of the surrounding lands, though a single misstep along the precipice means certain death. In this quiet refuge wanders Telf Joolam, a solitary hermit tasked with overseeing sacred rites. For aspiring orc and troll shaman undertaking the ritual Call of Fire, the shrine's brazier serves as the crucible where they must ignite slumbering coals using the ember of a vanquished elemental, proving their power to commune with and respect the destructive spirits of flame.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you reach the Shrine of the Dormant Flame?",a="The path begins along the Southfury River on the southwestern edge of the Southfury Watershed, just northwest of the Valley of Trials. A narrow mountain trail spirals around the peak, leading directly up to the summit.",al={"how to get to shrine of the dormant flame","path to dormant flame","climb dormant flame mountain"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Why is this shrine important to shaman?",a="The shrine is a sacred site where aspiring Horde shaman learn to understand and command the element of fire. As part of their Call of Fire journey, initiates must travel to this summit to prepare a ritual draft and kindle the dormant brazier.",al={"shrine of dormant flame purpose","why do shaman go here","call of fire shrine"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Telf Joolam?",a="Telf Joolam is a solitary troll hermit who serves as the keeper of the shrine. He guides young shaman through their trials, concocting a draught of fire to awaken their spiritual sight and testing their resolve.",al={"who is telf joolam","dormant flame npc","shrine keeper"},it="in_charge"},{q="What happens when you kindle the brazier?",a="Shaman who have gathered the required ritual components and defeated a hostile fire elemental place its burning ember into the brazier. This acts as an offering to prove they have the strength and discipline to tame the volatile spirit of flame.",al={"brazier of dormant flame","igniting the flame","shrine brazier quest"},gp=true},{q="What is the Shrine of the Dormant Flame?",a="Perched atop the highest mountain peak northwest of the Valley of Trials, the Shrine of the Dormant Flame is a sacred place of communion for Horde shaman. Reached only by a winding, narrow trail above the Southfury River, it is where initiates prove their spiritual authority over elemental fire by kindling its sacred brazier.",al={"what is shrine of the dormant flame","what is dormant flame shrine","shrine of dormant flame durotar"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at the Shrine of the Dormant Flame?",a="For generations since the Horde settled Durotar, young orc and troll shaman have climbed to this windswept peak to undergo their trials. Here, aspirants bring captured embers won from defeated fire elementals to ignite the mountain's ceremonial brazier, proving their mastery over the primal flame and earning their fire totems under the watch of its keeper.",al={"history of shrine of dormant flame","shrine of dormant flame past","what happened at dormant flame shrine"},it="history",add=true},{q="Is the Shrine of the Dormant Flame dangerous?",a="The shrine itself is peaceful, but the journey to reach it is treacherous. The spiral path clinging to the mountain's cliffs is narrow and dizzying, and a single misstep can send you plunging to your death on the rocks far below. Additionally, summoning and binding elemental fire upon the peak requires absolute focus to avoid being consumed.",al={"danger shrine of dormant flame","is dormant flame shrine safe","is it dangerous up here"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called the Shrine of the Dormant Flame?",a="The peak takes its name from the sacred brazier that rests cold and quiet until a worthy shaman awakens it. The flame remains asleep—dormant—waiting to be kindled by an ember won from elemental combat, bursting to life only when invoked during the trials of fire.",al={"why dormant flame","shrine dormant flame name origin","why is it called shrine of the dormant flame"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Every young orc and troll shaman must make the arduous trek up this crag to kindle their spiritual connection with fire and earn their Fire Totem.",["faction:Horde"]="Tucked away in the mountains above Durotar, this isolated shrine preserves ancient elemental rites vital to the spiritual heart of the new Horde."},kw={"call of fire","dormant flame","durotar","fire totem","shrine","southfury watershed","telf joolam","valley of trials"},rel={"quest:1524","npc:telf-joolam","subzone:southfury-river","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:merchant-coast","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Shrine of the Dormant Flame"}}
E["subzone:skull-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Skull Rock",z="durotar",s="Skull Rock is a cavern tucked into the eastern coastal cliffs of Durotar, just east of Orgrimmar. It serves as a fortified coven for the demonic Burning Blade cult right under the capital's nose.",h="Skull Rock is a cavern tucked into the eastern coastal cliffs of Durotar, just east of Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="A Den of Cultists",b="Hidden beneath the crags of northeastern Durotar, Skull Rock is one of the most perilous strongholds of the Burning Blade cult in the region. Dark cultists, fel-worshipping orcs, and summoners gather deep within the winding tunnels to practice demonic arts and weave conspiracies against the nascent Horde. The cell is led by the dangerous warlock Gazz'uz, whose operations pose an imminent threat to the nearby gates of Orgrimmar and travelers traversing the eastern shoreline.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Skull Rock?",a="Skull Rock is a cave system situated in northeastern Durotar along the coast. It is occupied by cultists of the Burning Blade who use its natural cover to plot against Thrall's Horde.",al={"skull rock cave","where is skull rock","what is in skull rock"},it="place"},{q="Who controls Skull Rock?",a="The cavern is infested by the Burning Blade cult, led by the orc warlock Gazz'uz from the deepest chamber of the cave.",al={"who leads skull rock","who runs skull rock","skull rock boss"},it="residents"},{q="Why does the Horde care about this cave?",a="Its proximity to Orgrimmar makes it a severe security hazard. The Burning Blade actively seeks to undermine Thrall's new realm and plunge the orcs back into demonic servitude.",al={"why clear skull rock","why is skull rock dangerous"},it="danger"}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The dark arts practiced within Skull Rock showcase the unchecked spread of demonic influence that Thrall's Horde seeks to root out and control.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the cultists from Skull Rock is vital to securing the coastal approaches to Durotar and protecting Orgrimmar from subversion from within."},kw={"burning blade","cultists","durotar","gazz'uz","orgrimmar","skull rock"},rel={"quest:827","zone:durotar","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Skull Rock"}}
E["subzone:spirit-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Spirit Rock",z="durotar",s="Spirit Rock is a sacred crag perched in the rugged bluffs above the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Reached by a winding trail known as the Hidden Path, it serves as a secluded holy site where initiates commune directly with the elemental forces of the land.",h="Spirit Rock is a sacred crag perched in the rugged bluffs above the Valley of Trials in Durotar.",sec={{t="A Sanctuary of the Elements",b="Overlooking the red canyon where young Horde warriors and scouts begin their training, Spirit Rock stands as an altar of communion. Isolated from the clatter of the Valley of Trials, it is approached only via the Hidden Path winding up the rocky ridgeline. Aspiring shaman make pilgrimages to this desolate outcrop to drink the traditional sapta, piercing the veil of the physical world to hear the rumblings and whisperings of the earth itself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Spirit Rock used for?",a="Spirit Rock is a sacred site used primarily by Horde shaman initiates. By consuming a specialized draught known as an Earth Sapta at the rock, novices gain the spiritual vision required to commune directly with the spirits of the earth.",al={"spirit rock purpose","what happens at spirit rock","spirit rock use"},it="purpose"},{q="How do you reach Spirit Rock?",a="Spirit Rock sits high in the cliffs above the Valley of Trials in southwestern Durotar. It is accessible by ascending the Hidden Path, a narrow, unmarked trail that winds out of the canyon floor into the rugged hills.",al={"how to get to spirit rock","path to spirit rock","spirit rock location"},gp=true},{q="What is a sapta?",a="A sapta is a ceremonial elemental brew prepared by shaman trainers. Drinking it alters the seeker's perception, allowing them to perceive elemental manifestations that remain invisible to ordinary senses.",al={"earth sapta","what is sapta","sapta drink"},it="item"},{q="What is Spirit Rock?",a="Spirit Rock is a secluded sanctuary perched high in the rocky bluffs overlooking the Valley of Trials in Durotar. Reached by a winding, hidden path up the hills, it serves as a sacred gathering ground where aspiring shaman seek communion with the spirits of the world.",al={"what is spirit rock","spirit rock durotar","about spirit rock"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is Spirit Rock dangerous?",a="The rock itself is a place of solemn spiritual reflection rather than a den of monsters. However, the path leading up into the jagged crags borders the rough wilderness of Durotar, and communing directly with elemental spirits carries its own trials for the unprepared.",al={"spirit rock danger","is spirit rock safe","enemies at spirit rock"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called Spirit Rock?",a="It earned its name because it is a consecrated natural focal point where the veil between the physical realm and the elemental spirits is thin. It is here that shaman drink specially prepared saptas to perceive and speak with the spirits of the earth.",al={"why spirit rock","spirit rock name origin"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Spirit Rock is a vital rite of passage for young orc and troll shaman, who venture up the Hidden Path to drink the Earth Sapta and forge their first bond with the spirits of stone and soil."},kw={"call of earth","durotar","earth spirits","hidden path","sapta","shaman","spirit rock","valley of trials"},rel={"subzone:hidden-path","subzone:valley-of-trials","quest:1520","zone:durotar","topic:horde"},src={"Spirit Rock"}}
E["subzone:the-den"] = {t="subzone",n="The Den",z="durotar",s="The Den is the sheltered cave at the heart of the Valley of Trials in southwestern Durotar. Serving as the primary base of operations for young orc and troll adventurers, it provides martial and magical training before they set out into the wider world.",h="The Den is the sheltered cave at the heart of the Valley of Trials in southwestern Durotar.",sec={{t="Cradle of the Horde",b="Tucked into the red canyon walls of the Valley of Trials, the Den serves as an austere proving ground. Within its carved, shadowy interior, novice fighters, spellcasters, and hunters report to veterans like Gornek and Zureetha Fargaze. It is here that fledglings receive their foundational combat instruction, supplies, and initial rites of passage, hardening them for the harsh realities of Durotar and the greater struggles facing the new Horde.",sp=0},{t="A Watchful Outpost",b="Beyond housing class trainers and provisions, the Den functions as an active field redoubt. Between dispatching new recruits to cull the local beasts and aggressive quillboars, the overseers maintain a strict, vigilant watch over the valley.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Den?",a="The Den serves as the central command post and training sanctuary within the Valley of Trials. Here, novice orcs and Darkspear trolls gather to learn basic class techniques, purchase provisions, and receive assignments that prove their loyalty and combat readiness to the Horde.",al={"what is the den","why is the den here","purpose of the den"},it="purpose"},{q="Who runs things inside the Den?",a="The encampment is supervised by veteran overseers such as Gornek and Foreman Thazz'ril, along with spiritual and magical mentors like Zureetha Fargaze and Canaga Earthcaller, all working together to instruct the newest generation of warriors and mystics.",al={"who leads the den","who is in charge","den overseer"},it="in_charge"},{q="Can you learn primary professions here?",a="No. The Den only hosts basic class trainers and general equipment merchants. New adventurers must travel north to Razor Hill or on to Orgrimmar to study primary trade skills such as Blacksmithing, Leatherworking, or Mining.",al={"profession trainers den","can i learn blacksmithing here","train mining in den"},gp=true},{q="What is the Den?",a="The Den is the cavernous base of operations in the Valley of Trials, nestled in the southwestern corner of Durotar. It serves as the primary muster camp for young orc novices seeking to prove themselves worthy of the Horde. Inside, trainers teach the basics of various arts, merchants sell essential supplies, and local leaders hand out trials to test incoming recruits before they venture into the wider world.",al={"what is the den","the den durotar","about the den"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is the Den dangerous?",a="The Den itself is heavily guarded and quite safe for members of the Horde, protected by Den Grunts and experienced overseers. The real dangers lie outside, where beasts and quilboar roam the Valley of Trials.",al={"is the den dangerous","is it safe in the den","the den threats"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Every young orc begins their journey at the Den, shedding the complacency of internment camps and blood haze to earn their place through discipline and labor.",["race:Troll"]="Following the devastation of the Darkspear Isles, young Darkspear trolls train in the Den alongside their orc allies, proving their mettle under the Horde's banner."},kw={"durotar","gornek","starting cave","the den","trainers","valley of trials","zureetha fargaze"},rel={"subzone:valley-of-trials","zone:durotar","npc:gornek","npc:zureetha-fargaze","subzone:razor-hill","npc:magga","npc:mai-ah","topic:troll"},src={"The Den"}}
E["subzone:thunder-ridge"] = {t="subzone",n="Thunder Ridge",z="durotar",s="Thunder Ridge is a rugged canyon in western Durotar, situated just southwest of Orgrimmar along the banks of the Southfury River. Once a lush grove of ancient trees inhabited by herds of thunder lizards, the canyon has suffered severe deforestation from human lumber operations and dark sorcery. Today, the agitated beasts and lingering cultists pose an ongoing threat to nearby settlements.",h="Thunder Ridge is a rugged canyon in western Durotar, situated just southwest of Orgrimmar along the banks of...",sec={{t="A Scarred Sanctuary",b="Not long ago, Thunder Ridge was a rare green haven in arid Durotar, sustained by ancient trees and watched over by the spirit Owa'nohe. Its tranquil balance shattered shortly after the Third War when human interlopers from Kul Tiras began felling its timber, driving the native thunder lizards into a frenzy. Later, fel sorcery wielded by the Burning Blade finished the destruction, stripping the canopy and leaving behind a barren, exposed gorge where angry lightning-spewing beasts now roam unrestrained.",sp=0},{t="Cultists and Tests of Strength",b="The denizens of Orgrimmar keep a wary eye on the ridge. The Burning Blade maintains a pocket of cultists here under the warlock Fizzle Darkclaw, who uses demonic magic to sow further chaos across Durotar. Horde veterans like Orgnil Soulscar task scouts with hunting down the cabal, while warrior trainers such as Uzzek send aspiring fighters into the crags to test their resilience against the enraged thunder lizards.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What happened to the trees in Thunder Ridge?",a="Thunder Ridge was once a dense woodland, but it suffered two waves of destruction. First, lumber operations run by Kul Tiran forces aggressively felled its ancient timber shortly after Durotar was founded. Later, the Burning Blade used dark, demonic magic to raze the surviving groves, wiping out the forest entirely.",al={"why is thunder ridge barren","thunder ridge forest","deforestation thunder ridge"},it="ruin"},{q="Why are the thunder lizards so aggressive here?",a="The thunder lizards lived peacefully among the ridge's ancient trees until outside intrusion ruined their habitat. The noise and destruction of human logging, combined with lingering fel corruption from the Burning Blade cultists, drove the herds into an agitated madness that makes them attack anyone who ventures into the canyon.",al={"angry lizards thunder ridge","thunder lizards durotar"},it="conflict"},{q="Who is Fizzle Darkclaw?",a="Fizzle Darkclaw is a leader within the Burning Blade cult who established an encampment within Thunder Ridge. From this staging ground, he and his followers direct dark rituals to destabilize the region, prompting Horde leaders like Orgnil Soulscar to place a bounty on his head.",al={"fizzle darkclaw lore","who is darkclaw","burning blade thunder ridge"},it="threat"},{q="Did Rexxar fight in Thunder Ridge?",a="Yes. Shortly after Durotar was founded, the Champion of the Horde Rexxar traveled here to gather shimmerweed for the farseer Drek'Thar. While in the canyon, Rexxar discovered the human lumber camp driving the lizards wild, forcing him to cull the frenzied beasts and salvage their eggs for Drek'Thar to study.",al={"rexxar thunder ridge","drek'thar thunder ridge"}},{q="What is Thunder Ridge?",a="Thunder Ridge is a deep, deforested gorge nestled in northwestern Durotar, located just southwest of Orgrimmar. Once a flourishing ancient forest watched over by nature spirits, it served as a traditional sanctuary for massive herds of thunder lizards. Today, its lush canopy is gone, replaced by barren cliffs, roaming beasts, and encroaching dark cultists.",al={"what is thunder ridge","thunder ridge durotar","where is thunder ridge"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Thunder Ridge?",a="Shortly after Durotar was founded, humans from Kul Tiras established an illegal logging operation here, cutting down the ancient timber and enraging the thunder lizards until Rexxar and Drek'Thar intervened. Later, demonic corruption wielded by the Burning Blade cult severed the remaining trees, stripping the valley bare and agitating the native beasts into a violent frenzy.",al={"history of thunder ridge","thunder ridge lore","what happened here thunder ridge"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who lives in Thunder Ridge?",a="No peaceful settlement exists within the ridge. Aside from herds of agitated thunder lizards and lightning hides, a coven of Burning Blade cultists led by the warlock Fizzle Darkclaw has established a camp in the ravine, using dark magic to sow chaos across Durotar.",al={"who lives in thunder ridge","thunder ridge inhabitants","thunder ridge factions"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is Thunder Ridge dangerous?",a="Yes. The native thunder lizards are naturally territorial, and recent dark meddling has driven them into an erratic, hostile fury capable of shocking intruders with lightning. In addition, the Burning Blade cultists lurking in the gorge will readily strike down anyone investigating their ritual sites.",al={"how dangerous is thunder ridge","thunder ridge hazards","is thunder ridge safe"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="Warrior mentors like Uzzek send their trainees into Thunder Ridge to test their defensive prowess against the sheer physical force and lightning shocks of the wild thunder lizards.",["faction:Horde"]="Nestled just outside Orgrimmar's western bluffs, the ridge must be kept clear of Burning Blade agents like Fizzle Darkclaw to prevent demonic subversion at the capital's doorstep."},kw={"burning blade","durotar","fizzle darkclaw","orgnil soulscar","rexxar","southfury river","thunder lizards","thunder ridge","uzzek"},rel={"zone:durotar","quest:806","quest:1498","npc:orgnil-soulscar","npc:uzzek","subzone:southfury-river","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:drygulch-ravine"},src={"Thunder Ridge"}}
E["subzone:tiragarde-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Tiragarde Keep",z="durotar",s="Tiragarde Keep is a fortified human stronghold situated along Durotar's Scuttle Coast, south of Razor Hill. Originally built during Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's invasion, the ruined citadel remains garrisoned by hostile Kul Tiran marines under Lieutenant Benedict. It serves as a defiant, permanent thorn in the Horde's side right on their home territory.",h="Tiragarde Keep is a fortified human stronghold situated along Durotar's Scuttle Coast, south of Razor Hill.",sec={{t="Proudmoore's Bastion",b="Erected during Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's campaign to eradicate Thrall's newly founded realm, Tiragarde Keep provided the Kul Tiran fleet an entrenched beachhead on the red shores of Durotar. Although the Horde eventually broke the siege and killed Proudmoore at Theramore Isle, the keep was never fully abandoned. Resupply forces under Lieutenant Benedict reclaimed the shattered stone walls, following the late Admiral's standing orders to wage an unyielding war against the orcs, entirely refusing the peace forged by Lady Jaina Proudmoore.",sp=0},{t="A Thorn in Durotar's Flank",b="Today, the keep's gleaming white battlements stand in harsh contrast against Durotar's crimson cliffs. Well-trained Kul Tiras sailors and marines patrol the ramparts and launch raids targeting supply lines near Razor Hill. For the Horde, Tiragarde Keep is an ongoing security crisis and a live proving ground. Orc and troll commanders constantly task young warriors with assaulting the fortress and cutting down Benedict's soldiers, seeking to contain the garrison before the humans can mount a deeper inland offensive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there humans in Durotar?",a="These humans are Kul Tiras sailors and marines who arrived with Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore during his invasion following the Third War. They reject peace with the Horde and maintain this garrison to harass the orcs.",al={"why are alliance here","who are the humans in tiragarde","human soldiers durotar"},it="why_here"},{q="Are these humans part of Jaina's forces in Theramore?",a="No. While Jaina Proudmoore rules Theramore Isle and maintains an uneasy truce with Thrall, these soldiers follow the orders of her late father, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore. They consider any peace with orcs unacceptable treason.",al={"is tiragarde theramore","are they jaina proudmoore's men","theramore soldiers here"},it="ties"},{q="Who commands Tiragarde Keep?",a="The stronghold is commanded by Lieutenant Benedict, a Kul Tiran officer acting on posthumous invasion orders left by Admiral Proudmoore to secure the coast and attack the Horde.",al={"tiragarde boss","who leads tiragarde keep","lieutenant benedict"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why hasn't the Horde simply wiped them out?",a="The keep is fortified and manned by disciplined, well-armed Kul Tiran troops. While the defenders from Razor Hill frequently skirmish with the garrison and use it as a proving ground for new recruits, launching a full-scale siege would draw heavy casualties and divert vital resources away from securing the rest of Durotar.",al={"why not destroy tiragarde","why is the keep still here"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Tiragarde Keep?",a="Tiragarde Keep is an Alliance coastal fortification situated along the Scuttle Coast in southeastern Durotar. Built out of pale stonework that clashes sharply with the surrounding red canyons, it serves as a fortified beachhead for human forces hostile to the Horde. Even in its battered condition, the keep provides Kul Tiras soldiers a fortified base to harass nearby settlements like Razor Hill.",al={"tiragarde keep what is it","what is this keep","tell me about tiragarde keep"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Tiragarde Keep?",a="Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore hastily constructed the keep during his invasion of Durotar to wage war against the nascent Horde. The Horde struck back, assaulting and battering the fortress until it fell. Although Proudmoore was later slain, reserve forces under Lieutenant Benedict were dispatched to reclaim the ruined keep and carry on the fallen Admiral's campaign.",al={"tiragarde keep history","what happened here","battle of tiragarde keep"},it="history",add=true},{q="Why is Tiragarde Keep ruined?",a="The fortress lies in ruins because the Horde stormed and shattered it during Grand Admiral Proudmoore's initial invasion of Durotar. While Lieutenant Benedict and his Kul Tiran reinforcements successfully reoccupied the site, they hold it as a crumbling, patched stronghold rather than a pristine castle, constantly under siege and pressure from nearby orcish outposts.",al={"why is tiragarde keep destroyed","why is the keep damaged","who destroyed tiragarde keep"},it="ruin",add=true},{q="Is Tiragarde Keep dangerous?",a="Yes, deeply so for members of the Horde. The keep is occupied by well-trained Kul Tiras Marines and Sailors who carry deep hatred for orcs and strike at travelers along the coast. They launch raids toward Razor Hill and fiercely defend their ramparts against any Horde warriors sent to dislodge them.",al={"is tiragarde keep safe","tiragarde keep danger","are the humans in tiragarde keep dangerous"},it="danger",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="Tiragarde Keep is a blatant Alliance invasion base right on Durotar's doorstep; raiding its ramparts and eliminating Lieutenant Benedict is a rite of passage for young soldiers serving Razor Hill.",["race:Human"]="The garrison represents the unbending, vengeful legacy of Kul Tiras and Admiral Proudmoore, fighting a stubborn guerrilla war in defiance of Jaina Proudmoore's diplomacy."},kw={"daelin proudmoore","durotar","kul tiras","lieutenant benedict","razor hill","scuttle coast","tiragarde keep"},rel={"zone:durotar","subzone:scuttle-coast","subzone:razor-hill","quest:784","topic:kul-tiras","subzone:theramore-isle","npc:jaina-proudmoore","npc:thrall"},src={"Tiragarde Keep"}}
E["subzone:tor-kren-farm"] = {t="subzone",n="Tor'kren Farm",z="durotar",s="Tor'kren Farm is a quiet, struggling swine farm nestled in northwestern Durotar, tucked between Thunder Ridge and the Southfury Watershed. It is maintained solely by Misha Tor'kren, an aging orc widow whose life has been weighed down by grief and the harsh frontier.",h="Tor'kren Farm is a quiet, struggling swine farm nestled in northwestern Durotar, tucked between Thunder Ridge...",sec={{t="A Lonely Homestead",b="Carving out a living from the dry, unforgiving red dirt of Durotar is never simple, but Tor'kren Farm has had a harder time than most. Situated southeast of Thunder Ridge, the homestead focuses on raising pigs in a rugged climate where feed and water are scarce. Unlike the bustling trade posts or heavily defended barracks of the Horde, the farm stands isolated and quiet, producing meager yields in the shadow of nearby bluffs.",sp=0},{t="A Mother's Loss",b="The farm's greatest burden is not poor soil, but tragedy. Misha Tor'kren once worked these pens alongside her beloved son, Kron. That life ended when Kron journeyed down to the Southfury River to hunt the ferocious crocolisks lurking along the banks and never returned. Left to carry on alone, Misha tends the swine by herself, holding fast to her homestead and clinging to the memory of her fallen child.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Tor'kren Farm located?",a="Tor'kren Farm lies in northwestern Durotar, situated southeast of the canyon known as Thunder Ridge and just north of the Southfury Watershed.",al={"tor'kren farm location","where is torkren farm","find tor'kren farm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who lives at Tor'kren Farm?",a="The farm is tended solely by Misha Tor'kren, an elderly orc widow who raises pigs on the homestead by herself.",al={"who runs tor'kren farm","tor'kren farm npcs","who is misha tor'kren"},it="residents"},{q="What happened to Misha's son?",a="Misha's son, Kron, was killed while hunting crocolisks along the nearby Southfury River several years ago, leaving his mother to manage the farm on her own.",al={"misha son","kron tor'kren death","who is kron"},it="history"},{q="What does Tor'kren Farm produce?",a="It operates as a swine farm, though harsh terrain and isolation keep its profits far leaner than other livestock operations in Durotar.",al={"torkren farm business","what kind of farm is torkren","tor'kren pigs"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Tor'kren Farm?",a="Tor'kren Farm is a modest homestead situated in northwestern Durotar, tucked between Thunder Ridge and the Southfury Watershed. It serves as a working pig farm, though it struggles to achieve the success and profit of other settlements in the region. Maintained under the harsh desert sun, it represents the quiet, grinding effort of everyday orcs trying to carve out a livelihood on Durotar's unforgiving frontier.",al={"what is torkren farm","torkren farm lore","about torkren farm"},it="place",add=true},{q="Is Tor'kren Farm dangerous?",a="The farmstead itself offers relative safety, but its surroundings are fraught with peril. It lies near the Southfury River and its watershed, waters infested with vicious crocolisks that have claimed lives in the past. In addition, the rugged terrain nearby harbors aggressive wildlife, meaning travelers and workers must always keep their guard up when venturing beyond the homestead's immediate perimeter.",al={"is torkren farm safe","torkren farm threats","danger at torkren farm"},it="danger",add=true},{q="Why is it called Tor'kren Farm?",a="The farm takes its name from the Tor'kren family who built and maintain it. Misha Tor'kren settled the land to raise swine alongside her son Kron, lending their family name to the small, enduring patch of farmland.",al={"why is it called torkren farm","torkren farm name origin","who is torkren"},it="name",add=true}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The quiet tragedy at Tor'kren Farm reveals the everyday sacrifices made by ordinary Horde settlers striving to tame Durotar's wild frontier.",["class:Hunter"]="The fate of Kron serves as a grim warning to young hunters about the deadly predators lurking along the Southfury River."},kw={"durotar","kron","misha tor'kren","pig farm","southfury river","southfury watershed","thunder ridge","tor'kren farm"},rel={"npc:misha-tor-kren","subzone:southfury-river","subzone:thunder-ridge","zone:durotar"},src={"Tor'kren Farm"}}
E["subzone:valley-of-trials"] = {t="subzone",n="Valley of Trials",z="durotar",s="Tucked away behind the rugged red cliffs of southern Durotar, the Valley of Trials serves as the testing ground for new recruits of the Horde. Young orcs and their Darkspear troll allies come here to prove their strength and earn their place among the warriors of Kalimdor. Those who survive the valley's harsh wildlife and hidden threats depart ready to defend their fledgling nation.",h="Tucked away behind the rugged red cliffs of southern Durotar, the Valley of Trials serves as the testing...",sec={{t="A Crucible of Sand and Stone",b="The Valley of Trials is designed to weed out the weak before they ever set foot in the broader reaches of Durotar. Overseen by chieftains and trainers stationed in the carved cliffside shelter known as The Den, young fighters are thrust into the sun-scorched gulch to hunt scorpids, culled aggressive boars, and enforce discipline among lazy peons harvesting scarce timber. The trial is uncompromising: those who prove their mettle earn the right to venture forth as true soldiers of the Horde, while those who fail are left to bleach beneath the desert sun.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow in the North",b="What was once an isolated training ground has recently taken on a far more sinister edge. In the natural caves along the northern cliffs, cultists of the Burning Blade have taken root, summoning minor demonic familiars into the valley. While trainers treat these interlopers as live-combat practice for fresh recruits, the presence of fel magic so close to Orgrimmar's threshold fuels dark rumors that the Shadow Council is actively attempting to sink its claws back into the orcish people.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Valley of Trials?",a="It is the traditional proving ground for recruits of the Horde, primarily young orcs and Darkspear trolls. Within its sheltered canyons, new adventurers complete rigorous tasks to demonstrate their martial skill, survival instinct, and loyalty before being permitted to leave for the rest of Durotar.",al={"why are orcs here","what is this place","valley of trials purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="What is The Den?",a="The Den is a cave carved into the cliffs roughly in the center of the valley. It houses class trainers, vendors, and overseers like Gornek who direct new recruits, equip them, and monitor their progress during their initial trials.",al={"the den","cave in valley of trials","who is in the den"},it="place"},{q="Why are there demons in a beginner's training ground?",a="Cultists belonging to the Burning Blade have established a secret coven in the northern caves. Although trainers use their weak familiars to test recruits, the cult's presence suggests shadowy forces like the Shadow Council are seeking a foothold right on Durotar's doorsteps.",al={"why demons in valley of trials","burning blade in durotar","demons north cave"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Sarkoth?",a="Sarkoth is an unusually large, venomous scorpid residing in the rocky heights of the valley. Due to his aggression and lethality, instructors task promising recruits with hunting him down to test their courage and bring back his mangled claw as proof.",al={"sarkoth lore","giant scorpid","sarkoth quest"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Valley of Trials?",a="The Valley of Trials is a rugged, canyon-sheltered proving ground in southern Durotar. Surrounded by towering red cliffs, it serves as the essential proving ground for young orcs and Darkspear trolls seeking to earn their place in the Horde. Here, recruits endure trials of combat, survival, and discipline under harsh sun and craggy rocks before stepping beyond the valley walls into the wider world.",al={"where am i","what is this place","valley of trials lore"},it="place",add=true,nx={6,7}},{q="Why is it called the Valley of Trials?",a="It takes its name from the strict rites of passage held within its walls. Every aspiring recruit must prove their strength, resolve, and loyalty to the Horde by completing dangerous trials against the land's beasts and threats. Those who prove worthy are granted passage out into Durotar; those who fail and fall in the attempt are left to bake in the scorching desert sun.",al={"why valley of trials","meaning of valley of trials name","why is it named valley of trials"},it="name",add=true},{q="Is the Valley of Trials part of Durotar?",a="Yes, it lies in the southern reaches of Durotar. Durotar itself is a dry, rocky realm on the eastern coast of Kalimdor, founded and named by Thrall in memory of his father, Durotan. The Valley of Trials is the protected staging ground where recruits prepare before entering the harsher wilds of the broader territory.",al={"is this in durotar","is valley of trials part of durotar","valley of trials durotar"},it="place",add=true},{q="Who is in charge here?",a="The valley's trials and training are managed locally by Horde veteran taskmasters and class trainers. Taskmaster Gornek directs the new arrivals and evaluates their progress, ensuring every novice proves their worth to the New Horde before they are allowed to venture into greater Durotar.",al={"who leads the valley of trials","who runs the valley of trials","who is the boss here"},it="in_charge",add=true,nx={9}},{q="Who is Gornek?",a="Gornek is an orc taskmaster stationed right in front of The Den in the Valley of Trials. He oversees recruits from the moment they report for duty, issuing foundational trials to test your mettle, culling wild beasts, and directing proven warriors and spellcasters to their respective trainers.",al={"gornek","who is gornek","what does gornek do"},it="leader",add=true},{q="What is the New Horde?",a="The New Horde is a coalition of disparate cultures founded by Warchief Thrall upon principles of survival, honor, and freedom. Bound together by an alliance of mutual protection in a hostile world, it stands centered on the orcs, joined by allies like the Darkspear trolls and the tauren, dedicated to building a future free from demonic corruption.",al={"new horde","what is the horde","thrall's horde"},it="purpose",add=true},{q="Why are orcs living in a desert now?",a="After escaping human captivity in the Eastern Kingdoms and crossing the Great Sea, Thrall brought the orcs to Kalimdor to claim a land of their own. Durotar's cracked red soil, rugged canyons, and arid heat remind the orcs of their ancient homeworld of Draenor, offering a harsh beauty where their strength can endure.",al={"why durotar","why are orcs in the desert","why did orcs settle durotar"},it="arrival",rc="Orc",add=true},{q="Why is my troll starting in an orc camp?",a="The Darkspear tribe owes their very survival to Thrall, who helped rescue them when their island home was lost during the exodus to Kalimdor. Allied in gratitude and friendship, young Darkspear trolls train shoulder-to-shoulder with orc recruits in the Valley of Trials to prove their shared devotion to the Horde.",al={"why do trolls start in valley of trials","troll starting area","why are trolls with orcs"},it="arrival",rc="Troll",add=true,nx={13}},{q="What happened to the Darkspear tribe?",a="Driven from their ancestral islands in the Great Sea after fighting murlocs and a sea witch, the Darkspear followed Thrall to Kalimdor and colonized the Echo Isles off Durotar's coast. However, the treachery of the witch doctor Zalazane and attacks by human forces drove them from the isles, forcing them onto the Durotar mainland at Sen'jin Village.",al={"darkspear history","what happened to darkspear","echo isles darkspear"},it="history",rc="Troll",add=true},{q="Who are the Burning Blade?",a="The Burning Blade is a dark cult associated with demonic corruption and whispers of the treacherous Shadow Council. Rather than seeking honor under Thrall's Horde, their warlocks and followers traffic with fel powers and harbor sinister designs against the safety of Durotar.",al={"burning blade","who is the burning blade","burning blade cult"},it="threat",add=true,nx={15}},{q="Why are the Burning Blade in the valley?",a="Members of the cult have secretly moved into the natural cavern network along the valley's northern cliffs, now known as the Burning Blade Coven. Led by the warlock Yarrog Baneshadow, their presence allows demonic imps to spill into the training grounds, testing recruits who must eradicate the corruption before departing.",al={"why is burning blade here","burning blade in valley of trials","why are they in the coven"},it="why_here",add=true},{q="What is Sen'jin Village and why am I being sent there?",a="Sen'jin Village is a Darkspear troll settlement established along the southern coast of Durotar on Darkspear Strand. Founded by Vol'jin after Zalazane seized the Echo Isles, it serves as the tribe's staging post and your natural destination once you prove yourself worthy of leaving the Valley of Trials.",al={"sen'jin village","why go to sen'jin village","what is senjin village"},it="next_step",add=true},{q="How did I end up in Valley of Trials?",a="You arrived here to test yourself. Tucked away within the southern crags of Durotar, the Valley of Trials serves as the proving ground for new recruits of the Horde. Whether answered out of a sense of duty, tribal tradition, or the raw urge to fight for your people, all who wish to serve Thrall's realm must first brave this arid gorge. You entered on foot, reporting to the recruiters and taskmasters of The Den to begin your rite of passage.",al={"how did i get here","how did i end up here","why did i wake up here"},it="arrival",add=true},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Valley of Trials?",a="You are here to prove your strength and earn your place among the Horde. Under the harsh sun, Taskmaster Gornek and the valley's mentors demand that you toughen yourself by slaying local beasts, harvesting vital supplies, and honing your combat craft. As your final challenge, you must face the growing corruption brewing in the northern caverns. Once your instructors judge you capable of surviving Durotar's perils, you will be permitted to pass through the northern gate and journey deeper into the wild lands beyond.",al={"what should i do here","what am i doing here","why am i here"},it="purpose",add=true},{q="Why does a new Orc start here, in Valley of Trials?",a="For an orc, coming to the Valley of Trials is an essential rite of passage. In this new homeland that Thrall carved from the dust and named after his father, Durotan, old traditions live on in a new form. Every aspiring orc must undergo these trials to demonstrate honor, discipline, and battle readiness before they can join the grunts guarding Orgrimmar or roam the frontier. You were sent here to prove that you possess the spirit needed to defend the New Horde.",al={"why do orcs start here","why are orcs in the valley","why do i start in the valley of trials as an orc"},it="arrival",rc="Orc",add=true},{q="Why does a new Troll start here, in Valley of Trials?",a="Your people, the Darkspear tribe, recently suffered a bitter betrayal. Driven from your home on the Echo Isles by the traitor Zalazane and his hexed minions, the survivors gathered along the coast at Sen'jin Village. Lacking proper proving grounds of your own, your chieftain Vol'jin relies on his alliance with Thrall, sending eager Darkspear youth here to Durotar's valley alongside the orcs. By proving your strength in this harsh canyon, you prepare to serve the Horde and eventually help reclaim your home.",al={"why do trolls start here","why is a troll in an orc camp","why am i here as a troll"},it="arrival",rc="Troll",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="The valley represents a rite of passage for every young orc seeking honor, echoing the warrior traditions of Draenor in a newly forged homeland.",["race:Troll"]="Having lost their home on the Echo Isles to Zalazane, the Darkspear trolls train alongside their orc allies in this canyon to earn their place in the Horde."},kw={"burning blade coven","durotar","gornek","orcs","peons","sarkoth","the den","valley of trials"},rel={"npc:gornek","zone:durotar","quest:1089","subzone:burning-blade-coven","subzone:echo-isles","topic:horde","topic:darkspear-tribe","topic:shadow-council"},src={"Valley of Trials"}}
E["topic:grommash-hellscream"] = {t="topic",n="Grommash Hellscream",z="durotar",s="Grommash Hellscream was the legendary chieftain of the Warsong clan, a close brother-in-arms to Warchief Thrall, and the first orc to drink the blood of Mannoroth. Though his thirst for battle once bound his people to the Burning Legion, he redeemed the orcish race by slaying the demon lord in Ashenvale at the cost of his own life.",h="Grommash Hellscream was the legendary chieftain of the Warsong clan, a close brother-in-arms to Warchief...",sec={{t="The First Drink and the Iron Will",b="Before the Dark Portal ever bridged worlds, Grom Hellscream led the Warsong clan with unyielding ferocity, distinguished by his pitch-black tattooed jaw and the deadly sweep of his two-handed axe, Gorehowl. When Gul'dan and the Shadow Council offered the chalice of demonic strength on Draenor, Grom was the first chieftain to drink the blood of the pit lord Mannoroth. That fateful draught doomed the orcish race to demonic subservience and a burning bloodlust. Yet unlike many chieftains who perished or succumbed entirely, Grom possessed an iron will that kept his fierce spirit intact, surviving the horrors of the old Horde while harboring an unspoken ache for what his people had surrendered.",sp=0},{t="A Brotherhood in the Wilds",b="Kept behind on Draenor during the Second War, Grom later crossed through the Dark Portal only to be stranded when the rift was shattered. For nearly fifteen years, Grom and his surviving Warsong warriors evaded the Alliance of Lordaeron, enduring the lethargy and despair that fell upon the orcs after the demon blood faded. Hope rekindled when a young fugitive named Thrall sought him out in the wilderness. Recognizing Thrall's strength and noble heart, Grom mentored him in the proud heritage of their people. Alongside Orgrim Doomhammer, the two rallied their disparate clans, broke open the human internment camps, and ignited the birth of the New Horde.",sp=0},{t="Fall and Final Redemption",b="Upon arriving in Kalimdor during the Third War, Grom's unquenched aggression resurfaced in the ancient forests of Ashenvale. Beset by the night elves and the demigod Cenarius, Grom succumbed once more, drinking from a corrupted fountain infused with Mannoroth's blood to save his clan. Enslaved anew by the demon lord, Grom turned against his own people until Thrall and Jaina Proudmoore captured and cleansed his corrupted spirit with ancient shamanic and arcane rites. Fully restored to his senses and burdened by immense guilt, Grom pursued Mannoroth into Demon Fall Canyon. In a desperate final strike, he drove Gorehowl into the demon lord's chest, severing the demonic curse forever as hellfire claimed his life.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Grommash Hellscream?",a="Grommash 'Grom' Hellscream was the chieftain of the Warsong clan and Thrall's trusted lieutenant. He was famous for his razor-sharp axe, Gorehowl, and infamous as the first orc to accept the demonic pact by drinking Mannoroth's blood. He later redeemed his legacy by slaying Mannoroth in Kalimdor, freeing the entire orcish race from the Blood Curse.",al={"who is grom","who was hellscream","grom hellscream backstory"},it="identity"},{q="How did Grom die?",a="Grom died in Demon Fall Canyon within Ashenvale alongside Thrall. Confronting the pit lord Mannoroth, Grom launched himself into the air and cleaved the demon's chest with Gorehowl. The fatal strike shattered the demon's heart, but the ensuing burst of demonic hellfire fatally wounded Grom, who died declaring that he had finally freed himself and his people.",al={"grom death","how did grom hellscream die","who killed grom"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Grom's connection to Thrall?",a="When Thrall escaped the internment camp of Durnholde, Grom was the first clan chieftain he encountered. Grom took the young orc under his wing, teaching him orcish traditions, language, and culture. Thrall came to view Grom as an older brother and spiritual guide, while Grom saw Thrall as the visionary who could lead their shattered race back to honor.",al={"thrall and grom","how did thrall know grom","were thrall and grom friends"},it="ties"},{q="Why was Grom's jaw tattooed black?",a="Upon his ascension to chieftain of the Warsong clan on Draenor, Grom ritually tattooed his lower jaw a solid shade of pitch-black. It served as a distinct emblem of his authority and iron will throughout his life, making his ferocious war cries instantly recognizable on the battlefield.",al={"grom black jaw","why is groms jaw black","grom tattooed lower jaw"},it="origin"},{q="Why did Grom drink demon blood a second time?",a="While harvesting lumber in Ashenvale, Grom's clan was decimated by the night elves and the demigod Cenarius, whose divine nature made him nearly invincible to mortal weapons. Desperate to ensure his clan's survival, Grom discovered a pool of water corrupted by Mannoroth's blood. Despite knowing the dreadful cost, he drank from it to gain the demonic fury needed to defeat Cenarius.",al={"why did grom drink again","grom chaos orcs","grom drank blood twice"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Grommash buried?",a="Grom rests in Demon Fall Canyon in southeastern Ashenvale, the exact ground where he struck down Mannoroth. A stone monument stands over his burial site, inscribed with an epitaph authored by Thrall celebrating his courage and ultimate sacrifice for the Horde.",al={"grom grave","grom monument","where is groms tomb"},it="place"},{q="What is the history of Grommash Hellscream?",a="Grommash rose to lead the Warsong clan on Draenor and became the first chieftain to drink the blood of the demon Mannoroth, binding the orcs to the Burning Legion. Kept on Draenor during the Second War, he later led his clan across the Dark Portal and survived fifteen years in hiding in Lordaeron's wilds, fighting the demonic lethargy that gripped his people. When he met Thrall, Grom helped spark the rebellion that liberated the captive orcs from human internment camps, eventually sailing west with Thrall to Kalimdor.",al={"grom hellscream backstory","grom history","where did grom come from"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who was allied with Grommash Hellscream?",a="Grom was the devoted chieftain of the Warsong clan and the greatest lieutenant and close brother-in-arms to Warchief Thrall. Together with Orgrim Doomhammer and Thrall's Frostwolf clan, Grom allied his warriors to liberate the orcish internment camps in Lordaeron and forge the new Horde. He fought side by side with Thrall through the crossing to Kalimdor and the founding of their new home until his ultimate sacrifice against Mannoroth.",al={"grom allies","who did grom fight for","who was grom hellscream allied with"},it="allies",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Orcs revere Grommash as their ultimate savior. His sacrifice in Ashenvale broke the demonic Blood Curse that held the race in thrall for generations, allowing the New Horde to walk with pride and free will.",["faction:Horde"]="To the Horde, Grom represents the tragic arc of their founding: a fierce warrior whose reckless temper led them into darkness, but whose unyielding courage bought their survival and freedom in Kalimdor.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elves view Grom's memory with lingering bitterness, remembering him as the demon-crazed invader who defiled Ashenvale's sacred groves and murdered the demigod Cenarius.",["class:Warrior"]="Warriors study Grom's battlefield prowess and mastery of Gorehowl as the pinnacle of martial aggression, seeing in him the terrible cost of unchecked rage and the sheer power of an indomitable fighting spirit."},kw={"ashenvale","blood curse","cenarius","gorehowl","grom","grommash","hellscream","mannoroth","thrall","warsong"},rel={"npc:thrall","topic:warsong-clan","topic:new-horde","zone:ashenvale","topic:third-war","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","topic:burning-legion","npc:jaina-proudmoore"},src={"Grommash Hellscream"}}
E["zone:durotar"] = {t="zone",n="Durotar",z="durotar",s="Durotar is the arid, red-rock homeland founded by Warchief Thrall following the Third War, named in honor of his father, Durotan. Bounded by the Southfury River and the Great Sea, it serves as the heartland of the New Horde and the proving ground for young orcs and Darkspear trolls. Within its harsh canyons lie fortified settlements like Razor Hill, the sprawling warrior city of Orgrimmar, and entrenched hostile holdouts ranging from quilboar tribes to stranded Alliance troops.",h="Durotar is the arid, red-rock homeland founded by Warchief Thrall following the Third War, named in honor of...",sec={{t="A Harsh New Home",b="When Thrall led his people across the Great Sea to Kalimdor, he deliberately sought an untamed frontier where the orcs could carve out an honest existence through labor and grit rather than conquest. Durotar's cracked red soil, baked gullies, and towering red-rock spires remind the orcs deeply of Draenor before its destruction. While the climate is unforgiving, offering little arable land and sparse water, the Horde embraced the landscape's natural defense and austere majesty. Bordered to the west across the Southfury River by the open Barrens and to the north by the ruined wilderness of Azshara, Durotar stands as living proof that the orcs have forged their own destiny.",sp=0},{t="Enemies on the Frontier",b="Though Durotar is firmly under Horde dominion, securing it remains an active war. Razormane quilboar, pushed out during the nation's founding, relentlessly raid settlements and farms from the western crags. Farther south, remnants of Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's Kul Tiras fleet still hold the crumbling garrison of Tiragarde Keep under Lieutenant Benedict, refusing to surrender. Worse still, demonic remnants of the Burning Blade coven lurk within hidden ravines and deep sea caves, subtly seeking to re-corrupt young orcs with promises of fel power.",sp=0},{t="The Trials of the Darkspear",b="Along the southern coast lies Sen'jin Village, the staging ground for the exiled Darkspear trolls. Led by Master Gadrin, the Darkspear were forced from their home on the nearby Echo Isles when the witch doctor Zalazane lost his mind and used dark voodoo to enslave his kin. Unable to reclaim their islands alone, the Darkspear rely on newly trained orc and troll warriors stepping forth from the Valley of Trials to break Zalazane's hold and secure the coast.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why did Thrall settle the Horde in such a barren desert?",a="Thrall chose this unforgiving territory intentionally. The red earth and rugged mesas reminded the orcs of their ancestral world of Draenor, while its harsh conditions served as penance and a forge for discipline. Thrall believed his people needed to earn their survival through honest hardship rather than claiming fertile lands by conquest, ensuring they would not slide back into bloodthirsty complacency.",al={"why settle here","why durotar","why durotar barren"},it="motive"},{q="Who was Durotar named after?",a="The land was named in honor of Durotan, Thrall's late father and the former chieftain of the Frostwolf clan. Durotan had opposed the demonic corruption of the orcish clans and was murdered on the orders of the warlock Gul'dan.",al={"who is durotar named for","durotan","origin of durotar name"},it="name"},{q="Why are there human soldiers inside Tiragarde Keep?",a="The soldiers at Tiragarde Keep are surviving Kul Tiran marines under Lieutenant Benedict, left over from Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's invasion fleet. Even after Proudmoore was slain, these troops refused to surrender or withdraw, maintaining an entrenched hostile outpost right on Durotar's southern coast.",al={"why humans in durotar","tiragarde keep humans","proudmoore troops durotar"},it="hostile"},{q="What is the conflict on the Echo Isles?",a="The Darkspear trolls originally established their Kalimdor home on the Echo Isles. However, a powerful witch doctor named Zalazane succumbed to madness and turned his dark magic against his brethren, enslaving their minds. The survivors fled to the mainland to establish Sen'jin Village, from which they launch raids to break his hold.",al={"what happened to echo isles","why sen'jin village","zalazane lore"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Burning Blade doing in Durotar?",a="The Burning Blade is a subversive demonic cult loyal to the Shadow Council and the Burning Legion. Operatives lurk in secluded spots like Skull Rock and the Burning Blade Coven, attempting to undermine Thrall's leadership and tempt impressionable orcs back into demonic servitude.",al={"burning blade durotar","skull rock cultists","demons in durotar"},it="threat"},{q="What connects Durotar to other regions?",a="A bridge over the Southfury River leads west into the Barrens, while a path through northern Orgrimmar crosses into Azshara. Outside Orgrimmar, twin zeppelin towers provide transcontinental air travel directly to Tirisfal Glades and Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"how to leave durotar","durotar travel","durotar exits"},it="place"},{q="What is Durotar?",a="Durotar is the rocky, sun-baked realm on Kalimdor's eastern shore, serving as the proud homeland of the Horde. Founded by Warchief Thrall following the Third War, its red dirt, jagged canyons, and harsh climate intentionally reflect Draenor, the ancestral world of the orcs. Bordered by the Southfury River to the west and the Great Sea to the south and east, Durotar houses the capital city of Orgrimmar and shelters both orcs and Darkspear trolls.",al={"about durotar","durotar info","where is durotar"},it="place",add=true},{q="What happened at Durotar?",a="Originally roaming grounds held loosely by quilboar tribes, Durotar became the destination of Thrall's exodus across the Great Sea. After allied forces pushed back native beast-tribes and triumphed over the Burning Legion at Mount Hyjal, Thrall formally established Durotar as a sovereign orcish nation. Shortly after its founding, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore's fleet invaded its eastern coast, though the Horde repelled the armada, driving human remnants into Tiragarde Keep.",al={"durotar history","history of durotar","past of durotar"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who lives in Durotar?",a="Durotar is ruled as a tribal chiefdom by Warchief Thrall from the seat of Orgrimmar. Orcs make up the grand majority of its population, accompanied by exiled Darkspear trolls centered near Sen'jin Village. Tauren allies and visiting Forsaken ambassadors frequently traverse the region, while hostile pockets of quilboar, centaur, harpies, and Kul Tiras marines dispute borders across the outer crags.",al={"who runs durotar","durotar population","durotar inhabitants"},it="residents",add=true},{q="Is Durotar dangerous?",a="Yes. Beyond the fortified roads and gates of settlements like Razor Hill and Orgrimmar, Durotar remains largely untamed. Poisonous scorpids, predatory raptors, and crocolisks prowl the wilderness. Worse, entrenched enemies harass Horde travelers constantly: Razormane quilboar strike from northern canyons, Kolkar centaurs raid watering holes, human marines garrison the Scuttle Coast, and covert warlocks of the Burning Blade lurk in nearby shadow.",al={"is durotar safe","durotar threats","dangers of durotar"},it="danger",add=true},{q="What is Razor Hill and why is it here?",a="Razor Hill is the principal fortified crossroads of central Durotar. Positioned directly at the junction connecting Sen'jin Village to the south, the Barrens across the Southfury River to the west, and Orgrimmar to the north, it anchors Horde logistics and defense. Heavily dominated by its military barracks and watchtower, the settlement coordinates border patrols and serves as the primary outpost protecting travelers from coast-dwelling marines and raiders.",al={"razor hill","about razor hill","why razor hill"},it="place",add=true,nx={12,13}},{q="Who built Razor Hill?",a="Razor Hill was built by Thrall's Horde shortly after their arrival on Kalimdor. Originally just a bare hill on the frontier—famously where Rexxar intercepted an ambush by Kul Tiras forces meant for Thrall—the site was fortified with a stout barracks and burrows to anchor Horde defense between the sea, the canyons, and the northern capital.",al={"who made razor hill","razor hill origins"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Is Razor Hill part of Orgrimmar?",a="It is not part of the city itself, but it falls directly under Orgrimmar's administration and military authority. Razor Hill functions as an outer garrison town and staging post in central Durotar, filtering arriving travelers, training recruits, and securing the southern approaches to the capital's towering northern gates.",al={"is razor hill in orgrimmar","razor hill orgrimmar"},it="place",add=true},{q="Was anyone living in Durotar before the Horde?",a="The quilboar claimed the land long before the Horde arrived. Bristled tribes, particularly the Razormane, occupied the crags and riverbanks of what was considered part of the greater Barrens. Decisive campaigns led by Thrall drove them into remote canyons and westward across the Southfury River, though they still fight ferociously to retake their ancestral territory.",al={"who lived here first","durotar natives"},it="history",add=true},{q="Who is in charge around Razor Hill?",a="Local defense and military operations in Razor Hill fall under seasoned veterans like Gar'Thok, while orc officials such as Orgnil Soulscar spearhead counterintelligence and internal investigations. Together, they manage town defenses, organize hunting expeditions, and task promising recruits with defending central Durotar.",al={"razor hill leader","who leads razor hill"},it="in_charge",add=true},{q="Who are these Kul Tiras sailors and why are they on our coast?",a="They are remnants of the grand armada commanded by the late Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore of Kul Tiras. Proudmoore refused to accept peace with the orcs and established Tiragarde Keep along the eastern shoreline as a foothold to wage war. Even after the Admiral was slain at Theramore, his surviving officers entrenched themselves inside the ruins, continuing their unyielding crusade against the Horde.",al={"kul tiras sailors","why are humans in durotar","tiragarde keep sailors"},it="threat",add=true,nx={17}},{q="Who is Lieutenant Benedict?",a="Lieutenant Benedict is the surviving Kul Tiras officer commanding the hostile garrison inside Tiragarde Keep. Following Admiral Proudmoore's death, Benedict rallied the remaining soldiers and marines under standing orders, maintaining a fortified human bastion in Durotar that regularly harries orc settlements and caravans.",al={"lieutenant benedict","benedict tiragarde","who is benedict"},it="identity",add=true},{q="What is Sen'jin Village?",a="Sen'jin Village is a coastal fishing settlement on the southern shore of Durotar, serving as the provisional home of the Darkspear trolls. Established by Chieftain Vol'jin, the village boasts alchemists, hunters, and shaman working to secure the mainland coast while guarding against aquatic monsters and traitorous kin across the waters.",al={"senjin village","what is sen'jin","senjin"},it="place",add=true,nx={19,20}},{q="Who was Sen'jin?",a="Sen'jin was the venerable shadow hunter and chieftain of the Darkspear tribe on their ancestral islands in the Great Sea. During the Third War, he foresaw Thrall's arrival and the liberation of his people, but gave his life defending the tribe from frenzied murlocs and sea witches before they could escape.",al={"who is senjin","sen'jin lore"},it="identity",add=true},{q="Why do trolls live in Durotar?",a="The Darkspear tribe owes their survival to Thrall, who rescued them when their original island home began sinking under aquatic onslaughts. Pledging loyalty to the Horde, they accompanied the orcs to Kalimdor and were given the offshore Echo Isles to inhabit, maintaining close cultural and military bonds with Orgrimmar.",al={"why are trolls here","darkspear in durotar"},it="origin",add=true},{q="Where does your journey lead after Razor Hill?",a="Once you have proven your strength around Razor Hill, orders will direct you either north into the grand gates of Orgrimmar to meet higher military leadership, or westward across the Southfury River into the sprawling expanse of the Barrens, where larger battles against quilboar, centaur, and Alliance encroachers await.",al={"after razor hill","where to go after razor hill","next zone after razor hill"},it="next_step",add=true},{q="How did I end up in Durotar?",a="If you are an orc, this rugged red land is your people's new sovereign home, carved out by Warchief Thrall after the exodus from the Eastern Kingdoms. You came of age here, sent to the secluded Valley of Trials to test your strength under the desert sun before earning your place in the Horde. If you are a Darkspear troll, your people fled across the Great Sea alongside Thrall and settled the coast after being driven from the nearby Echo Isles by the traitorous witch doctor Zalazane.",al={"how did i get here","why am i in durotar","how did i arrive here"},it="arrival",add=true},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Durotar?",a="You are here to prove your worth to the Horde and secure the survival of a fledgling nation. Durotar remains a harsh frontier beset on all sides: Razormane quilboar raid settlements, human remnants from Kul Tiras cling tenaciously to Tiragarde Keep, and the insidious Burning Blade cult schemes in shadowed ravines. By aiding local outposts like Razor Hill and Sen'jin Village, you help tame the crags, protect vulnerable settlements, and earn your place among the champions walking the grand streets of nearby Orgrimmar.",al={"what should i do in durotar","what is my purpose here","what am i doing here"},it="purpose",add=true}},ang={["race:Orc"]="Durotar is your people's new promised land, won through sweat and blood after years of demonic lethargy and internment. Proving your worth in the Valley of Trials is the first rite of passage for every new champion of the Horde.",["race:Troll"]="After escaping the sea witch in the Great Sea, the Darkspear found refuge alongside Thrall in Durotar, but the traitor Zalazane took the Echo Isles from within. Retaking the isles and defending Sen'jin Village is personal.",["faction:Alliance"]="Durotar is the beating heart of the Horde's military strength. Any Alliance traveler found wandering its sun-scorched canyons will be hunted down on sight by aggressive patrols and native beasts alike.",["class:Shaman"]="The arid terrain is steeped in raw elemental spirits. Young shamans visit sacred sites like the Spirit Rock and the Shrine of the Dormant Flame to attune themselves to earth and fire.",["class:Warlock"]="Thrall strictly polices dark magic, forcing the Shadow Council's covens into hiding within places like Skull Rock and beneath the city in the winding caverns of Ragefire Chasm."},kw={"durotan","durotar","echo isles","orgrimmar","razor hill","sen'jin village","skull rock","southfury river","thrall","tiragarde keep","valley of trials","zalazane"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","subzone:valley-of-trials","subzone:razor-hill","subzone:sen-jin-village","subzone:echo-isles","subzone:tiragarde-keep","zone:barrens","zone:ragefire"},m={levels="1-10"},src={"Durotar (Classic)","Durotar"}}
